{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_0","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"schema_version\":\"ruler_chapter_judgment_v1\",\"job_key\":\"chapter-judge:2022-top20-hybrid-v2-judges-v1:2022:1B\",\"run_key\":\"2022-top20-hybrid-v2-judges-v1\",\"chapter_id\":\"1B\",\"target_year\":2022,\"rubric_version\":\"chapter_1b_v4\",\"calibration_batch_id\":\"chapter-judge:2022-top20-hybrid-v2-judges-v1:2022:1B\",\"evaluations\":[{\"dossier_job_key\":\"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:BGD:17068\",\"iso3\":\"BGD\",\"ruler_id\":\"2992\",\"ruler_year_id\":17068,\"ruler_name\":\"Sheikh Hasina\",\"period_start_year\":2022,\"period_end_year\":2022,\"chapter_id\":\"1B\",\"rubric_version\":\"chapter_1b_v4\",\"calibration_batch_id\":\"chapter-judge:2022-top20-hybrid-v2-judges-v1:2022:1B\",\"calibrated_against\":[\"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:RUS:15706\",\"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:USA:15810\",\"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:JPN:16638\"],\"score_1_to_10\":4.5,\"insufficient_evidence_reason\":null,\"confidence_score\":45,\"plausible_score_range\":{\"lower\":4,\"upper\":5},\"decisive_positive_evidence\":[{\"evidence_id\":\"E0005\",\"explanation\":\"Hasina's 2022 UNGA speech is the only direct ruler-attributed nuclear-risk action in the file and it is explicitly pro-disarmament and nonproliferation.\"}],\"decisive_negative_evidence\":[],\"inherited_baseline_and_constraints\":\"Bangladesh is a non-nuclear state with a peaceful treaty baseline already in place; the 2022 record shows restraint rhetoric, not a hard nuclear-risk decision. The available evidence is sparse and mostly declaratory.\",\"ruler_attribution\":\"The only direct 2022 ruler-attributed fact is Hasina's UNGA statement. It supports a restrained posture, but it does not show a concrete command, custody, or crisis decision.\",\"supported_lenses\":[\"1B.1\",\"1B.2\",\"1B.4\",\"1B.10\"],\"missing_or_weak_lenses\":[\"1B.3\",\"1B.5\",\"1B.6\",\"1B.7\",\"1B.8\",\"1B.9\"],\"contrary_evidence\":[{\"evidence_id\":\"E0005\",\"explanation\":\"The same item is rhetorical and does not demonstrate concrete risk-reducing implementation in 2022.\"}],\"source_mix\":\"Official/state-media speech text with no independent outcome audit; the file is narrow and mostly declaratory, with no local priors available.\",\"structured_prior_summary\":\"Structured local priors were not collected for this experiment; all lens rows are marked not_available.\",\"chapter_rationale\":\"Sheikh Hasina earns a mildly positive score because the record contains a direct 2022 anti-nuclear statement at the UN General Assembly and a standing treaty posture consistent with restraint. That said, the chapter is not about applause for disarmament language alone: the dossier does not show a ruler-attributed command, safety, or crisis-management decision that materially lowered existential risk in 2022. The evidence is therefore supportive of a restrained posture but too thin and too declaratory to justify a higher score.\",\"lower_anchor_rejected\":\"A lower score would underrate the only direct 2022 ruler-attributed evidence, which is explicitly pro-disarmament rather than escalatory.\",\"higher_anchor_rejected\":\"A materially higher score would require concrete risk-bearing conduct or demonstrated safety improvement, which the dossier does not show.\",\"manual_review_required\":false,\"manual_review_reason_type\":null,\"manual_review_reason\":null,\"chapter_specific\":[{\"field\":\"exposure_profile\",\"value\":\"limited_exposure_with_choices\"},{\"field\":\"inherited_risk_posture\",\"value\":\"Peaceful, non-nuclear baseline with existing disarmament commitments.\"},{\"field\":\"trajectory\",\"value\":\"slightly positive but very sparse\"},{\"field\":\"end_posture\",\"value\":\"Still restrained and non-escalatory by the end of 2022.\"},{\"field\":\"ruler_authority_and_attribution\",\"value\":\"Direct speech attribution exists, but no 2022 nuclear command or safety governance act is shown.\"},{\"field\":\"crisis_and_command_safety_assessment\",\"value\":\"No crisis or command-safety episode is documented; the record is posture, not implementation.\"}]},{\"dossier_job_key\":\"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:BRA:19646\",\"iso3\":\"BRA\",\"ruler_id\":\"3413\",\"ruler_year_id\":19646,\"ruler_name\":\"Jair Bolsonaro\",\"period_start_year\":2022,\"period_end_year\":2022,\"chapter_id\":\"1B\",\"rubric_version\":\"chapter_1b_v4\",\"calibration_batch_id\":\"chapter-judge:2022-top20-hybrid-v2-judges-v1:2022:1B\",\"calibrated_against\":[\"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:RUS:15706\",\"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:USA:15810\",\"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:JPN:16638\"],\"score_1_to_10\":6.5,\"insufficient_evidence_reason\":null,\"confidence_score\":74,\"plausible_score_range\":{\"lower\":6,\"upper\":7},\"decisive_positive_evidence\":[{\"evidence_id\":\"E0009\",\"explanation\":\"The ANSN law created an autonomous nuclear-safety regulator, a concrete institutional safeguard attributable to Bolsonaro's signing of the law.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0010\",\"explanation\":\"The 2022 decree implemented ANSN's structure and its monitoring, regulation, and inspection mandate.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0011\",\"explanation\":\"Promulgation of the physical-protection amendment is a formal nuclear-security step in the target year.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0008\",\"explanation\":\"ABACC's safeguards mission and coordination framework reinforce Brazil's peaceful nuclear posture.\"}],\"decisive_negative_evidence\":[{\"evidence_id\":\"E0006\",\"explanation\":\"Brazil's TPNW status is only a signature, not ratification, so the nonproliferation posture is real but not maximal.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0014\",\"explanation\":\"Civil nuclear reactors are a safety-governed context, but not evidence of broader weapons-risk leadership or realized risk reduction.\"}],\"inherited_baseline_and_constraints\":\"Brazil entered 2022 with a strong treaty and safeguards baseline, plus a civil nuclear sector rather than a weapons program. Bolsonaro's sphere of responsibility was mostly regulatory and institutional, not crisis-driven nuclear command.\",\"ruler_attribution\":\"The strongest 2022 items are formal executive/legal acts under Bolsonaro's presidency. They do not prove perfect implementation, but they are concrete risk-bearing choices rather than mere rhetoric.\",\"supported_lenses\":[\"1B.1\",\"1B.3\",\"1B.4\",\"1B.6\",\"1B.7\",\"1B.9\",\"1B.10\"],\"missing_or_weak_lenses\":[\"1B.2\",\"1B.5\",\"1B.8\"],\"contrary_evidence\":[{\"evidence_id\":\"E0006\",\"explanation\":\"Signature without ratification is weaker than full treaty commitment.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0014\",\"explanation\":\"The civil-reactor profile is safety context, not evidence of a broader existential-risk breakthrough.\"}],\"source_mix\":\"Official legal texts and official institutional pages dominate, with some current-profile context; no local priors were available, but the evidence base is stronger than mere rhetoric because it includes enacted law and decree language.\",\"structured_prior_summary\":\"Structured local priors were not collected for this experiment; all lens rows are marked not_available.\",\"chapter_rationale\":\"Bolsonaro's 2022 record is meaningfully positive because it includes concrete, ruler-attributable nuclear-safety institution building: the ANSN framework, the 2022 implementing decree, and a physical-protection amendment. The limits are equally clear: the dossier is about civil nuclear governance and formal compliance, not a dramatic crisis intervention or a major arms-control advance. That keeps the score below the top bands, but above a merely mixed assessment, because the state did put in place real safeguards under his presidency.\",\"lower_anchor_rejected\":\"A lower score would miss the concrete legal and regulatory actions that improved Brazil's nuclear safety architecture in 2022.\",\"higher_anchor_rejected\":\"A materially higher score would require evidence of more consequential command, crisis, or implementation gains than the file actually shows.\",\"manual_review_required\":false,\"manual_review_reason_type\":null,\"manual_review_reason\":null,\"chapter_specific\":[{\"field\":\"exposure_profile\",\"value\":\"limited_exposure_with_choices\"},{\"field\":\"inherited_risk_posture\",\"value\":\"Peaceful civil-nuclear baseline with treaty and safeguards constraints.\"},{\"field\":\"trajectory\",\"value\":\"improving institutional safeguards\"},{\"field\":\"end_posture\",\"value\":\"Safer and more formalized nuclear regulation by year-end.\"},{\"field\":\"ruler_authority_and_attribution\",\"value\":\"Direct executive and legal attribution exists for the law and decree, though not for day-to-day safety performance.\"},{\"field\":\"crisis_and_command_safety_assessment\",\"value\":\"No crisis episode is shown, but the safety architecture was strengthened in formal terms.\"}]},{\"dossier_job_key\":\"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:CHN:15832\",\"iso3\":\"CHN\",\"ruler_id\":\"1432\",\"ruler_year_id\":15832,\"ruler_name\":\"Xi Jinping\",\"period_start_year\":2022,\"period_end_year\":2022,\"chapter_id\":\"1B\",\"rubric_version\":\"chapter_1b_v4\",\"calibration_batch_id\":\"chapter-judge:2022-top20-hybrid-v2-judges-v1:2022:1B\",\"calibrated_against\":[\"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:RUS:15706\",\"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:USA:15810\",\"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:JPN:16638\"],\"score_1_to_10\":3,\"insufficient_evidence_reason\":null,\"confidence_score\":87,\"plausible_score_range\":{\"lower\":2.5,\"upper\":3.5},\"decisive_positive_evidence\":[{\"evidence_id\":\"E0001\",\"explanation\":\"The January P5 statement is a real restraint signal, but it is declaratory rather than operational.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0014\",\"explanation\":\"China's formal no-first-use and minimum-force language is a restraint claim, though self-reported.\"}],\"decisive_negative_evidence\":[{\"evidence_id\":\"E0002\",\"explanation\":\"Xi publicly linked Chinese power to stronger strategic deterrence and a world-class military build-up.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0007\",\"explanation\":\"The Taiwan drills and missile launches sharply increased miscalculation risk.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0010\",\"explanation\":\"U.S. analysis projected a major nuclear build-up trajectory tied to Xi's deterrent signal.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0016\",\"explanation\":\"The Party Constitution revision tightened political loyalty and central control over the military, reducing internal challenge.\"}],\"inherited_baseline_and_constraints\":\"China entered 2022 as a nuclear-armed great power with strong centralized party control. That gives the ruler meaningful existential-risk authority, but the file shows that authority being used in a more coercive and militarized direction than in a safety-maximizing one.\",\"ruler_attribution\":\"Many items are direct Xi statements or party-state acts under his leadership. The restraint language exists, but it is outweighed by stronger evidence of deterrent build-up, centralization, and coercive Taiwan signaling.\",\"supported_lenses\":[\"1B.1\",\"1B.2\",\"1B.3\",\"1B.4\",\"1B.5\",\"1B.6\",\"1B.7\",\"1B.8\",\"1B.10\"],\"missing_or_weak_lenses\":[\"1B.9\"],\"contrary_evidence\":[{\"evidence_id\":\"E0001\",\"explanation\":\"The P5 statement points toward restraint, but it is a joint declaration without proof of later operational moderation.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0014\",\"explanation\":\"No-first-use and minimum-force language are declared positions, not verified implementation outcomes.\"}],\"source_mix\":\"Official Chinese texts, official UN records, and Reuters-based reporting produce a broad but polarized picture: the file contains both restraint language and vivid escalation evidence.\",\"structured_prior_summary\":\"Structured local priors were not collected for this experiment; all lens rows are marked not_available.\",\"chapter_rationale\":\"Xi Jinping receives a low score because the 2022 record mixes declaratory restraint with stronger, more consequential escalation: strategic deterrence build-up, centralization of military control, aggressive Taiwan drills, and a growing nuclear-force trajectory. The dossier does not show actual near-use or a nuclear detonation, so it does not fall into the extreme floor bands. But it does show more than ordinary tension: the year ends with a more militarized and less reassuring posture than it began with.\",\"lower_anchor_rejected\":\"A score of 2 would understate how much of the file is about sustained escalation, not just isolated rhetoric.\",\"higher_anchor_rejected\":\"A score of 4 would overstate the restraint value of the declaratory material and ignore the stronger coercive facts.\",\"manual_review_required\":false,\"manual_review_reason_type\":null,\"manual_review_reason\":null,\"chapter_specific\":[{\"field\":\"exposure_profile\",\"value\":\"material_exposure\"},{\"field\":\"inherited_risk_posture\",\"value\":\"Established nuclear power with centralized party-military control.\"},{\"field\":\"trajectory\",\"value\":\"deteriorating overall, despite restraint rhetoric\"},{\"field\":\"end_posture\",\"value\":\"More coercive and more centralized than at the start of 2022.\"},{\"field\":\"ruler_authority_and_attribution\",\"value\":\"Direct and indirect attribution is strong; the issue is not authorship but the direction of use.\"},{\"field\":\"crisis_and_command_safety_assessment\",\"value\":\"No nuclear near-use is shown, but the year contains serious miscalculation risk and tighter political control.\"}]},{\"dossier_job_key\":\"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:COD:16113\",\"iso3\":\"COD\",\"ruler_id\":\"2830\",\"ruler_year_id\":16113,\"ruler_name\":\"Félix Tshisekedi\",\"period_start_year\":2022,\"period_end_year\":2022,\"chapter_id\":\"1B\",\"rubric_version\":\"chapter_1b_v4\",\"calibration_batch_id\":\"chapter-judge:2022-top20-hybrid-v2-judges-v1:2022:1B\",\"calibrated_against\":[\"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:RUS:15706\",\"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:USA:15810\",\"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:JPN:16638\"],\"score_1_to_10\":null,\"insufficient_evidence_reason\":\"The dossier does not provide a defensible 2022 ruler-attributed nuclear or other catastrophic-risk choice by Tshisekedi. The material is mostly treaty status, cyber strategy, and peace-process context, which is too indirect for a chapter score.\",\"confidence_score\":20,\"plausible_score_range\":{\"lower\":1,\"upper\":10},\"decisive_positive_evidence\":[],\"decisive_negative_evidence\":[],\"inherited_baseline_and_constraints\":\"The file shows a non-nuclear state with treaty baseline and some cyber-policy activity, but not a judgeable existential-risk sphere. The evidence does not connect Tshisekedi to a concrete 2022 nuclear, launch-safety, or equivalent catastrophic-risk decision.\",\"ruler_attribution\":\"Attribution is mostly structural or indirect; the 2022 file does not reveal a ruler-specific existential-risk choice that can be scored.\",\"supported_lenses\":[],\"missing_or_weak_lenses\":[\"1B.1\",\"1B.2\",\"1B.3\",\"1B.4\",\"1B.5\",\"1B.6\",\"1B.7\",\"1B.8\",\"1B.9\",\"1B.10\"],\"contrary_evidence\":[],\"source_mix\":\"Official constitutional and treaty records, plus a few media and UN items, but no direct ruler-attributed catastrophic-risk decision; local priors were unavailable.\",\"structured_prior_summary\":\"Structured local priors were not collected for this experiment; all lens rows are marked not_available.\",\"chapter_rationale\":\"This chapter cannot be defensibly scored for Tshisekedi on the evidence provided. The file shows treaty ratification, cyber strategy drafting, and peace-process rhetoric, but it does not show a direct 2022 ruler-attributed choice in a nuclear or otherwise clearly catastrophic-risk domain. That leaves the record too indirect to separate responsible governance from mere institutional or diplomatic context.\",\"lower_anchor_rejected\":\"A numeric floor score would imply some judgeable catastrophic-risk action, which the dossier does not supply.\",\"higher_anchor_rejected\":\"A substantive positive score would require a concrete risk-bearing decision or outcome that is not present in the file.\",\"manual_review_required\":false,\"manual_review_reason_type\":null,\"manual_review_reason\":null,\"chapter_specific\":[{\"field\":\"exposure_profile\",\"value\":\"unknown_due_to_evidence_gap\"},{\"field\":\"inherited_risk_posture\",\"value\":\"Non-nuclear state with some treaty and cyber-policy context, but no documented 2022 catastrophic-risk choice.\"},{\"field\":\"trajectory\",\"value\":\"insufficient_data\"},{\"field\":\"end_posture\",\"value\":\"Judgment remains indeterminate from the embedded evidence.\"},{\"field\":\"ruler_authority_and_attribution\",\"value\":\"Mostly indirect or structural attribution; no direct judgeable risk-bearing act is recovered.\"},{\"field\":\"crisis_and_command_safety_assessment\",\"value\":\"No usable crisis or command-safety record for this chapter.\"}]},{\"dossier_job_key\":\"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:DEU:16984\",\"iso3\":\"DEU\",\"ruler_id\":\"2975\",\"ruler_year_id\":16984,\"ruler_name\":\"Olaf Scholz\",\"period_start_year\":2022,\"period_end_year\":2022,\"chapter_id\":\"1B\",\"rubric_version\":\"chapter_1b_v4\",\"calibration_batch_id\":\"chapter-judge:2022-top20-hybrid-v2-judges-v1:2022:1B\",\"calibrated_against\":[\"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:RUS:15706\",\"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:USA:15810\",\"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:JPN:16638\"],\"score_1_to_10\":6,\"insufficient_evidence_reason\":null,\"confidence_score\":72,\"plausible_score_range\":{\"lower\":5.5,\"upper\":6.5},\"decisive_positive_evidence\":[{\"evidence_id\":\"E0005\",\"explanation\":\"Germany publicly welcomed the P5 non-use statement and explicitly framed dialogue as a way to reduce escalation risk.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0006\",\"explanation\":\"Observer participation in the TPNW meeting signaled continued disarmament engagement while preserving NATO commitments.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0007\",\"explanation\":\"The NPDI statement supported NPT implementation and practical risk-reduction steps.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0008\",\"explanation\":\"The G7 statement on Ukraine emphasized physical integrity, safety systems, and protected communications at nuclear installations.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0009\",\"explanation\":\"Scholz's UN speech paired Ukraine support with an explicit warning about nuclear power and an international-order frame.\"}],\"decisive_negative_evidence\":[{\"evidence_id\":\"E0010\",\"explanation\":\"The F-35 procurement preserved NATO nuclear-sharing capability rather than reducing it.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0099\",\"explanation\":\"The Bundeswehr fund channeled major resources into procurement, including the nuclear-sharing successor aircraft, instead of a deeper disarmament shift.\"}],\"inherited_baseline_and_constraints\":\"Germany is a non-nuclear NATO member with alliance obligations that constrain how far a disarmament turn can go. The 2022 record sits inside that inherited posture and does not show a break from it, but it does show active risk-management choices.\",\"ruler_attribution\":\"The strongest items are direct Scholz statements or official government actions under his chancellorship. The posture is mixed because Germany kept nuclear-sharing while also pursuing diplomacy and safety messaging.\",\"supported_lenses\":[\"1B.1\",\"1B.2\",\"1B.4\",\"1B.6\",\"1B.7\",\"1B.8\",\"1B.10\"],\"missing_or_weak_lenses\":[\"1B.3\",\"1B.5\",\"1B.9\"],\"contrary_evidence\":[{\"evidence_id\":\"E0010\",\"explanation\":\"The F-35 decision preserves a nuclear-sharing role rather than reducing reliance on it.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0099\",\"explanation\":\"The Bundeswehr special fund emphasizes procurement and strategic hardening more than disarmament.\"}],\"source_mix\":\"Official government and parliamentary records dominate, with a Reuters-derived procurement item and no local priors. The evidence base is broad enough to judge as mixed, not so broad as to justify a higher band.\",\"structured_prior_summary\":\"Structured local priors were not collected for this experiment; all lens rows are marked not_available.\",\"chapter_rationale\":\"Scholz lands in the responsible-middle band because 2022 contains repeated, concrete German actions that reduce nuclear risk or manage it carefully: P5 non-use language, TPNW observer engagement, NPDI diplomacy, G7 nuclear-safety language, and Ukraine crisis communication. But the year also preserves Germany's nuclear-sharing posture through the F-35 procurement and the special fund, so this is not a clean disarmament turn. The overall picture is therefore responsible and serious, but clearly mixed rather than exceptional.\",\"lower_anchor_rejected\":\"A score below this would undercount the repeated official risk-reduction and de-escalation choices made under Scholz.\",\"higher_anchor_rejected\":\"A higher score would require a clearer break from nuclear-sharing or a more consequential improvement in Germany's existential-risk posture.\",\"manual_review_required\":false,\"manual_review_reason_type\":null,\"manual_review_reason\":null,\"chapter_specific\":[{\"field\":\"exposure_profile\",\"value\":\"limited_exposure_with_choices\"},{\"field\":\"inherited_risk_posture\",\"value\":\"Alliance-based nuclear-sharing posture with strong NATO constraints.\"},{\"field\":\"trajectory\",\"value\":\"mixed but somewhat safer on diplomacy and signaling\"},{\"field\":\"end_posture\",\"value\":\"Still inside nuclear-sharing, but with stronger risk-management messaging.\"},{\"field\":\"ruler_authority_and_attribution\",\"value\":\"Direct Scholz statements and government decisions exist, but the posture is still coalition- and alliance-bound.\"},{\"field\":\"crisis_and_command_safety_assessment\",\"value\":\"No command-safety breakdown is shown; the main tension is between deterrence maintenance and restraint rhetoric.\"}]},{\"dossier_job_key\":\"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:EGY:16232\",\"iso3\":\"EGY\",\"ruler_id\":\"2851\",\"ruler_year_id\":16232,\"ruler_name\":\"Abdel Fattah el-Sisi\",\"period_start_year\":2022,\"period_end_year\":2022,\"chapter_id\":\"1B\",\"rubric_version\":\"chapter_1b_v4\",\"calibration_batch_id\":\"chapter-judge:2022-top20-hybrid-v2-judges-v1:2022:1B\",\"calibrated_against\":[\"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:RUS:15706\",\"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:USA:15810\",\"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:JPN:16638\"],\"score_1_to_10\":null,\"insufficient_evidence_reason\":\"No admissible ruler-attributed evidence remained after review. The dossier supplies no 2022 Sisi-specific nuclear or catastrophic-risk decision that can be scored.\",\"confidence_score\":10,\"plausible_score_range\":{\"lower\":1,\"upper\":10},\"decisive_positive_evidence\":[],\"decisive_negative_evidence\":[],\"inherited_baseline_and_constraints\":\"The batch provides no judgeable 2022 existential-risk choice for Egypt. There is no usable record here of command, crisis, dual-use, or nuclear-safety conduct by Sisi.\",\"ruler_attribution\":\"No attributable 2022 fact is recovered beyond the absence of evidence.\",\"supported_lenses\":[],\"missing_or_weak_lenses\":[\"1B.1\",\"1B.2\",\"1B.3\",\"1B.4\",\"1B.5\",\"1B.6\",\"1B.7\",\"1B.8\",\"1B.9\",\"1B.10\"],\"contrary_evidence\":[],\"source_mix\":\"Empty evidence set with no local priors and no judgeable risk-bearing conduct.\",\"structured_prior_summary\":\"Structured local priors were not collected for this experiment; all lens rows are marked not_available.\",\"chapter_rationale\":\"There is no defensible chapter score for Sisi from the embedded material. The file contains no admissible 2022 ruler-attributed nuclear, safety, or other catastrophic-risk decision, so any numeric score would be invented rather than judged. The correct output is null.\",\"lower_anchor_rejected\":\"A numeric score wou