d is mildly positive because Vietnam consistently pushed peaceful nuclear use, denuclearization on the Korean Peninsula, and regional nonproliferation architecture. But the file remains mostly declaratory and institutional, with no direct 2022 ruler-attributed safety or crisis decision that would justify a higher band. So this is a steady, restrained middle score rather than a standout performance.\",\"lower_anchor_rejected\":\"A lower score would undervalue the consistent peace-oriented and nonproliferation posture visible in the 2022 file.\",\"higher_anchor_rejected\":\"A higher score would require direct existential-risk management or a more consequential implementation result than the evidence provides.\",\"manual_review_required\":false,\"manual_review_reason_type\":null,\"manual_review_reason\":null,\"chapter_specific\":[{\"field\":\"exposure_profile\",\"value\":\"limited_exposure_with_choices\"},{\"field\":\"inherited_risk_posture\",\"value\":\"Non-nuclear state with party-led foreign policy and limited civil-nuclear exposure.\"},{\"field\":\"trajectory\",\"value\":\"stable restraint and peaceful nuclear framing\"},{\"field\":\"end_posture\",\"value\":\"Still low-exposure, with incremental cooperative steps rather than breakthroughs.\"},{\"field\":\"ruler_authority_and_attribution\",\"value\":\"Direct attribution exists for some diplomacy, but much of the file is party-state context.\"},{\"field\":\"crisis_and_command_safety_assessment\",\"value\":\"No command crisis is shown; the record is mostly diplomacy and civil-nuclear cooperation.\"}]}],\"unavailable_dossiers\":[],\"batch_notes\":[\"Anchors used for calibration were Russia as the low end (direct operational brinkmanship without realized nuclear use), the United States and Japan as the high end (sustained 2022 restraint and diplomacy under real authority), and the null/edge cases of Egypt, Ethiopia, and the Philippines where the dossier does not supply a judgeable 2022 existential-risk choice.\",\"All d