{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_0","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"schema_version\":\"ruler_chapter_judgment_v1\",\"job_key\":\"chapter-judge:2022-top20-hybrid-v2-judges-v1:2022:2B\",\"run_key\":\"2022-top20-hybrid-v2-judges-v1\",\"chapter_id\":\"2B\",\"target_year\":2022,\"rubric_version\":\"chapter_2b_v3\",\"calibration_batch_id\":\"chapter-judge:2022-top20-hybrid-v2-judges-v1:2022:2B\",\"evaluations\":[{\"dossier_job_key\":\"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:BGD:17068\",\"iso3\":\"BGD\",\"ruler_id\":\"2992\",\"ruler_year_id\":17068,\"ruler_name\":\"Sheikh Hasina\",\"period_start_year\":2022,\"period_end_year\":2022,\"chapter_id\":\"2B\",\"rubric_version\":\"chapter_2b_v3\",\"calibration_batch_id\":\"chapter-judge:2022-top20-hybrid-v2-judges-v1:2022:2B\",\"calibrated_against\":[\"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:RUS:15706\",\"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:JPN:16638\",\"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:ETH:16782\"],\"score_1_to_10\":7.0,\"insufficient_evidence_reason\":null,\"confidence_score\":79,\"plausible_score_range\":{\"lower\":6.5,\"upper\":7.5},\"decisive_positive_evidence\":[{\"evidence_id\":\"E0012\",\"explanation\":\"Bangladesh explicitly called for an immediate cessation of hostilities in Ukraine and urged diplomacy and dialogue, a direct peace-oriented state position under Hasina.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0016\",\"explanation\":\"Bangladesh pressed Myanmar to speed Rohingya verification and facilitate safe return, showing regional diplomacy rather than coercion.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0018\",\"explanation\":\"Hasina's India visit produced a broad cooperative statement on sovereignty, security, border management, and cyber issues, reinforcing lawful bilateral management.\"}],\"decisive_negative_evidence\":[{\"evidence_id\":\"E0013\",\"explanation\":\"The March abstention on the first Ukraine resolution shows caution and hedging rather than forceful anti-aggression leadership.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0015\",\"explanation\":\"The later abstention on Russian reparations again shows mixed posture, not a fully consistent or decisive peace line.\"}],\"inherited_baseline_and_constraints\":\"Bangladesh was not an active belligerent in 2022; the baseline was cautious diplomacy with limited leverage over the Ukraine war and a long-running Rohingya crisis requiring regional management.\",\"ruler_attribution\":\"Most evidence is state-diplomatic rather than personal command, but it is still attributable to Hasina's government because it reflects the government's foreign-policy line and bilateral agenda.\",\"supported_lenses\":[\"2B.1 diplomacy and de-escalation\",\"2B.7 ceasefire and dialogue\",\"2B.10 more lawful regional relations\"],\"missing_or_weak_lenses\":[\"2B.2 war initiation and proxy conflict\",\"2B.4 civilian-harm conduct\",\"2B.8 militarization\"],\"contrary_evidence\":[{\"evidence_id\":\"E0013\",\"explanation\":\"March abstention can be read as diplomatic hedging rather than strong norm enforcement.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0022\",\"explanation\":\"The year combined peace language with mixed abstentions, so the record is restrained but not exceptional.\"}],\"source_mix\":\"Official UN and mission statements, local press reporting, and host-government transcripts dominate the dossier; local priors were unavailable in this experiment.\",\"structured_prior_summary\":\"Structured local priors were not collected in this experiment; judgment rests on the embedded chapter projection, cited evidence, and dossier-local counterevidence.\",\"chapter_rationale\":\"Sheikh Hasina's 2022 international conduct is best read as restrained, diplomacy-first statecraft. Bangladesh consistently supported dialogue and sovereignty language on Ukraine, advanced humanitarian and regional diplomacy on the Rohingya issue, and maintained cooperative bilateral management with India, but it also hedged at several UN votes and never produced a decisive peace breakthrough. The evidence shows a generally lawful and peace-oriented posture without the kind of strong, consequential conflict resolution needed for a higher score.\",\"lower_anchor_rejected\":\"A score of 6 is too low because the record includes repeated explicit peace language, humanitarian diplomacy, and cooperative regional management rather than mere non-aggression by default.\",\"higher_anchor_rejected\":\"A score of 8 is too high because the evidence is mostly diplomatic posture, with mixed abstentions and no demonstrated durable settlement or major restraint crisis personally resolved by Hasina.\",\"manual_review_required\":false,\"manual_review_reason_type\":null,\"manual_review_reason\":null,\"chapter_specific\":[{\"field\":\"trajectory\",\"value\":\"Mixed but restrained: repeated peace-oriented diplomacy and humanitarian engagement outweighed cautious abstentions.\"}]},{\"dossier_job_key\":\"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:BRA:19646\",\"iso3\":\"BRA\",\"ruler_id\":\"3413\",\"ruler_year_id\":19646,\"ruler_name\":\"Jair Bolsonaro\",\"period_start_year\":2022,\"period_end_year\":2022,\"chapter_id\":\"2B\",\"rubric_version\":\"chapter_2b_v3\",\"calibration_batch_id\":\"chapter-judge:2022-top20-hybrid-v2-judges-v1:2022:2B\",\"calibrated_against\":[\"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:RUS:15706\",\"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:JPN:16638\",\"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:ETH:16782\"],\"score_1_to_10\":5.0,\"insufficient_evidence_reason\":null,\"confidence_score\":73,\"plausible_score_range\":{\"lower\":4.0,\"upper\":6.0},\"decisive_positive_evidence\":[{\"evidence_id\":\"E0017\",\"explanation\":\"Bolsonaro publicly said Brazil would remain neutral and not take sides, which is restraint compared with open alignment in the Ukraine war.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0018\",\"explanation\":\"Brazil's UN statement urged diplomatic solutions and expressed grave concern about Russian military operations.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0021\",\"explanation\":\"Brazil used Bolsonaro's authority to provide humanitarian visas for Ukrainians and