e a war of aggression.\",\"ruler_attribution\":\"This is direct personal and command attribution: Putin authorized the invasion, presided over escalation, and controlled the nuclear-deterrence and annexation framework.\",\"supported_lenses\":[\"2B.2 war of choice and annexation\",\"2B.4 civilian harm and proportionality\",\"2B.8 militarization for coercive strength\"],\"missing_or_weak_lenses\":[\"2B.1 diplomacy\",\"2B.7 genuine peace settlement\",\"2B.9 accountability\"],\"contrary_evidence\":[{\"evidence_id\":\"E0017\",\"explanation\":\"Early compromise talk was tactical and did not change the underlying aggression.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0023\",\"explanation\":\"The grain deal was humanitarian but did not offset the invasion, annexation, or civilian harm.\"}],\"source_mix\":\"Official Kremlin material is corroborated by UN, Amnesty, Reuters, and other independent reporting; local priors were unavailable in this experiment.\",\"structured_prior_summary\":\"Structured local priors were not collected in this experiment; the judgment is driven by the embedded evidence of invasion, annexation, and civilian harm.\",\"chapter_rationale\":\"Vladimir Putin's 2022 Chapter 2B record is a clear floor case. He authorized the full-scale invasion of Ukraine, escalated it through civilian-harming operations, partial mobilization, and annexation moves, and did so under a framework that made the presidency the central authority for nuclear and war policy. Limited tactical talks and a grain deal do not change the basic picture: this is aggressive war, not lawful restraint.\",\"lower_anchor_rejected\":\"There is no lower score than 1 on the scale, and the realized record of invasion, annexation, and civilian harm fully meets the floor.\",\"higher_anchor_rejected\":\"A score of 2 is too high because the dossier is not just severe rhetoric or risky signaling; it is actual war of aggression with extensive unlawful conduct and escalation.\",\"manual_review_required\":false,\"manual_review_reason_type\":null,\"manual_review_reason\":null,\"chapter_specific\":[{\"field\":\"trajectory\",\"value\":\"Aggressive war and escalating coercion throughout the year, with only limited tactical negotiations.\"}]},{\"dossier_job_key\":\"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:THA:19649\",\"iso3\":\"THA\",\"ruler_id\":\"3414\",\"ruler_year_id\":19649,\"ruler_name\":\"Prayut Chan-o-cha\",\"period_start_year\":2022,\"period_end_year\":2022,\"chapter_id\":\"2B\",\"rubric_version\":\"chapter_2b_v3\",\"calibration_batch_id\":\"chapter-judge:2022-top20-hybrid-v2-judges-v1:2022:2B\",\"calibrated_against\":[\"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:RUS:15706\",\"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:JPN:16638\",\"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:ETH:16782\"],\"score_1_to_10\":6.0,\"insufficient_evidence_reason\":null,\"confidence_score\":70,\"plausible_score_range\":{\"lower\":5.0,\"upper\":6.5},\"decisive_positive_evidence\":[{\"evidence_id\":\"E0017\",\"explanation\":\"Prayut defused the Myanmar airspace breach as a limited incident rather than a crisis.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0020\",\"explanation\":\"Thailand hosted informal Myanmar talks aimed at a diplomatic path and the ASEAN five-point peace process.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0015\",\"explanation\":\"The UN Ukraine resolution provides the legal-diplomatic frame Thailand was responding to when it chose a cautious posture.\"}],\"decisive_negative_evidence\":[{\"evidence_id\":\"E0022\",\"explanation\":\"Thailand abstained on the annexation condemnation resolution, which weakened its public opposition to Russia's move.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0024\",\"explanation\":\"Thailand also abstained on the damage register resolution, again showing caution rather than strong accountability pressure.\"}],\"inherited_baseline_and_constraints\":\"Thailand inherited regional fragility on Myanmar and had limited leverage over the Ukraine war, so the score turns on whether Prayut used those constraints to promote calm or merely to hedge.\",\"ruler_attribution\":\"The evidence is partly Prayut's own public handling and partly government-hosted diplomacy; the cross-border posture is attributable to his administration even where ministries executed the details.\",\"supported_lenses\":[\"2B.1 crisis de-escalation\",\"2B.7 regional mediation\",\"2B.10 cautious lawful posture\"],\"missing_or_weak_lenses\":[\"2B.2 conflict initiation\",\"2B.4 civilian harm\",\"2B.5 proxy control\"],\"contrary_evidence\":[{\"evidence_id\":\"E0022\",\"explanation\":\"Abstentions on Ukraine accountability votes show caution rather than clear principle enforcement.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0024\",\"explanation\":\"The register vote repeated that caution and kept Thailand from the stronger accountability camp.\"}],\"source_mix\":\"Reuters, UN records, and Thai reporting form the core; local priors were unavailable in this experiment.\",\"structured_prior_summary\":\"Structured local priors were not collected in this experiment; the judgment uses the embedded dossier and counterevidence only.\",\"chapter_rationale\":\"Prayut Chan-o-cha's 2022 international-security conduct is cautious and somewhat mediation-oriented, but not strongly peace-leading. He downplayed a Myanmar airspace breach, hosted informal Myanmar talks, and generally kept Thailand on a legal-diplomatic line, yet he also abstained on key Ukraine accountability resolutions, which blunted the country's normative stance. That places him in the middle: restrained enough to avoid a low score, but too hedged and low-impact to merit a high one.\",\"lower_anchor_rejected\":\"A score of 5.0 is too low because Prayut's government did engage in mediation and de-escalatory handling of a live regional incident.\",\"higher_anchor_rejected\":\"A score of 6.5 is too high because Thailand's repeated abstentions and limited outcome record keep this from being a strong peace case.\",\"manual_review_required\":false,\"manual_review_reason_type\":null,\"manual_review_reason\":null,\"chapter_specific\":[{\"field\":\"trajectory\",\"value\":\"Cautious, mediator-leaning, but more hedged than decisive on major international crises.\"}]},{\"dossier_job_key\":\"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:TUR:15972\",\"iso3\":\"TUR\",\"ruler_id\":\"2813\",\"ruler_year_id\":15972,\"ruler_name\":\"Recep Tayyip Erdoğan\",\"period_start_year\":2022,\"period_end_year\":2022,\"chapter_id\":\"2B\",\"rubric_version\":\"chapter_2b_v3\",\"calibration_batch_id\":\"chapter-judge:2022-top20-hybrid-v2-judges-v1:2022:2B\",\"calibrated_against\":[\"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:RUS:15706\",\"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:JPN:16638\",\"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:ETH:16782\"],\"score_1_to_10\":3.0,\"insufficient_evidence_reason\":null,\"confidence_score\":88,\"plausible_score_range\":{\"lower\":2.5,\"upper\":4.0},\"decisive_positive_evidence\":[{\"evidence_id\":\"E0009\",\"explanation\":\"Turkey helped broker the Black Sea grain deal, a real but limited peace and humanitarian achievement.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0013\",\"explanation\":\"The Finland-Sweden NATO memorandum shows Erdoğan used bargaining to resolve a security dispute through an agreement.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0014\",\"explanation\":\"The later implementation mechanism shows the memorandum was being operationalized rather than immediately abandoned.\"}],\"decisive_negative_evidence\":[{\"evidence_id\":\"E0015\",\"explanation\":\"The UN commission said Erdoğan's announced incursion was followed by military escalation and mobilization.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0017\",\"explanation\":\"HRW said Turkey repeatedly struck northeast Syria in ways that aggravated humanitarian and displacement crises.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0018\",\"explanation\":\"Turkey's November air campaign hit 89 targets and was tied to retaliation, with civilian-harm allegations.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0019\",\"explanation\":\"Erdoğan said air operations were only the beginning and that a land operation would follow when convenient.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0020\",\"explanation\":\"Reuters reported Turkish drones targeted oil installations in northeast Syria, marking a systematic escalation.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0022\",\"explanation\":\"The U.S. human-rights report tied abuses by Turkey-supported groups to severe violations and no prosecution trail.\"}],\"inherited_baseline_and_constraints\":\"Turkey entered 2022 with existing cross-border entanglements in Syria and Iraq and a role in NATO bargaining, so the score turns on whether Erdoğan used that leverage for restraint or coercion.\",\"ruler_attribution\":\"The strongest evidence is directly Erdoğan's public threat language and Turkish-government military action, with independent rights and reporting corroboration.\",\"supported_lenses\":[\"2B.2 cross-border coercion\",\"2B.4 civilian-harm concerns\",\"2B.5 proxy and allied responsibility\"],\"missing_or_weak_lenses\":[\"2B.7 durable peace settlement\",\"2B.9 accountability\",\"2B.10 more peaceful regional order\"],\"contrary_evidence\":[{\"evidence_id\":\"E0009\",\"explanation\":\"The grain deal shows Turkey could still facilitate limited diplomacy.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0013\",\"explanation\":\"The NATO memorandum proves Erdoğan could strike bargains rather than only escalate.\"}],\"source_mix\":\"UN, HRW, Reuters, NATO, and official government material are all represented; local priors were unavailable in this experiment.\",\"structured_prior_summary\":\"Structured local priors were not collected in this experiment; the judgment uses the embedded dossier and counterevidence only.\",\"chapter_rationale\":\"Recep Tayyip Erdoğan's 2022 record is coercive and conflict-heavy, even though it includes one major diplomatic achievement in the grain deal and one important NATO bargain. The dominant pattern, however, is Turkish cross-border military action in Syria and Iraq, explicit threat language about a future land operation, and credible reporting of civilian-harm risks and proxy abuses. That places him firmly in the adverse range, though not at the absolute floor because he still demonstrated some negotiation capacity.\",\"lower_anchor_rejected\":\"A score of 2.5 is too low because Erdoğan did achieve real bargains, including the grain deal and the Finland-Sweden memorandum.\",\"higher_anchor_rejected\":\"A score of 4.0 is too high because the year is still dominated by repeated coercive military conduct and threatened escalation.\",\"manual_review_required\":false,\"manual_review_reason_type\":null,\"manual_review_reason\":null,\"chapter_specific\":[{\"field\":\"trajectory\",\"value\":\"Coercive cross-border posture with occasional bargaining success, but the year trended toward escalation.\"}]},{\"dossier_job_key\":\"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:USA:15810\",\"iso3\":\"USA\",\"ruler_id\":\"2782\",\"ruler_year_id\":15810,\"ruler_name\":\"Joe Biden\",\"period_start_year\":2022,\"period_end_year\":2022,\"chapter_id\":\"2B\",\"rubric_version\":\"chapter_2b_v3\",\"calibration_batch_id\":\"chapter-judge:2022-top20-hybrid-v2-judges-v1:2022:2B\",\"calibrated_against\":[\"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:RUS:15706\",\"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:JPN:16638\",\"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:ETH:16782\"],\"score_1_to_10\":7.0,\"insufficient_evidence_reason\":null,\"confidence_score\":83,\"plausible_score_range\":{\"lower\":6.5,\"upper\":7.5},\"decisive_positive_evidence\":[{\"evidence_id\":\"E0014\",\"explanation\":\"Biden said the diplomatic path to avoiding war was still open immediately before the invasion.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0016\",\"explanation\":\"NATO condemned Russia's invasion and called for withdrawal while describing allied measures as preventive and proportionate.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0020\",\"explanation\":\"The administration pursued war-crimes accountability and rejected Kremlin misinformation.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0025\",\"explanation\":\"The G7 statement condemned annexation, civilian killings, and accountability gaps.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0027\",\"explanation\":\"The State Department said the U.S. wanted a just peace based on the UN Charter and insisted that the war end through diplomacy.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0028\",\"explanation\":\"The Biden-Macron statement condemned the war, backed civilian resilience, and committed to accountability and support for as long as necessary.\"}],\"decisive_negative_evidence\":[{\"evidence_id\":\"E0017\",\"explanation\":\"Biden-directed lethal defensive assistance deepened U.S. involvement in the war effort.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0018\",\"explanation\":\"Treasury sanctions on the Russian central bank and wealth channels were lawful but still coercive escalation.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0023\",\"explanation\":\"Large security-assistance packages sustained the battlefield and prevented this from being a pure ceasefire record.\"}],\"inherited_baseline_and_constraints\":\"The United States inherited no direct war with Russia, but it had to balance allied defense, deterrence, and diplomatic pressure in a major external war.\",\"ruler_attribution\":\"The strongest evidence is directly Biden's own statements and executive direction, with official U.S. agencies implementing the policy line.\",\"supported_lenses\":[\"2B.1 diplomacy before and during crisis\",\"2B.7 accountability and negotiated peace posture\",\"2B.10 lawful alliance leadership\"],\"missing_or_weak_lenses\":[\"2B.2 conflict initiation\",\"2B.4 civilian protection inside the battlefield\",\"2B.5 proxy control\"],\"contrary_evidence\":[{\"evidence_id\":\"E0017\",\"explanation\":\"Military aid is supportive of defense but still prolongs the war effort.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0023\",\"explanation\":\"The U.S. repeatedly chose active support rather than a quick settlement, which limits the restraint ceiling.\"}],\"source_mix\":\"Primary U.S. presidential, Treasury, State Department, UN, and allied statements are combined with one independent rights report; local priors were unavailable in this experiment.\",\"structured_prior_summary\":\"Structured local priors were not collected in this experiment; the judgment relies on the embedded dossier and counterevidence.\",\"chapter_rationale\":\"Joe Biden's 2022 record is restraint-oriented but deeply involved in a major war. He kept diplomacy open before the invasion, led a sanctions-and-accountability coalition afterward, and repeatedly framed U.S. policy as defensive and lawful, but he also committed substantial military assistance that helped sustain the conflict. That places him in the positive middle-to-upper range: clearly not aggressive, yet not close to an exceptional peace score because the U.S. chose sustained war involvement rather than a quick settlement path.\",\"lower_anchor_rejected\":\"A score of 6.5 is too low because Biden repeatedly grounded policy in diplomacy, the UN Charter, and accountability rather than in coercive war aims.\",\"higher_anchor_rejected\":\"A score of 7.5 is too high because the scale of military assistance and prolonged wartime support prevents a stronger restraint reading.\",\"manual_review_required\":false,\"manual_review_reason_type\":null,\"manual_review_reason\":null,\"chapter_specific\":[{\"field\":\"trajectory\",\"value\":\"Defensive alliance leadership with substantial military support and persistent diplomacy.\"}]},{\"dossier_job_key\":\"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:VNM:19647\",\"iso3\":\"VNM\",\"ruler_id\":\"3411\",\"ruler_year_id\":19647,\"ruler_name\":\"Nguyễn Phú Trọng\",\"period_start_year\":2022,\"period_end_year\":2022,\"chapter_id\":\"2B\",\"rubric_version\":\"chapter_2b_v3\",\"calibration_batch_id\":\"chapter-judge:2022-top20-hybrid-v2-judges-v1:2022:2B\",\"calibrated_against\":[\"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:RUS:15706\",\"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:JPN:16638\",\"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:ETH:16782\"],\"score_1_to_10\":6.5,\"insufficient_evidence_reason\":null,\"confidence_score\":74,\"plausible_score_range\":{\"lower\":6.0,\"upper\":7.0},\"decisive_positive_evidence\":[{\"evidence_id\":\"E0012\",\"explanation\":\"Trọng described Vietnam's foreign policy as peaceful, cooperative, and multilateral, which is a clear restraint signal.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0014\",\"explanation\":\"He emphasized the UN as a major partner and peace/security cooperation as a foreign-policy priority.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0015\",\"explanation\":\"Vietnam called for self-restraint, peaceful settlement, and protection of Vietnamese citizens in Ukraine.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0016\",\"explanation\":\"Vietnam again urged dialogue and peaceful means after Russia's annexation moves.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0017\",\"explanation\":\"The China joint statement stressed peaceful handling of sea issues and maintaining peace and stability in the East Sea.\"}],\"decisive_negative_evidence\":[{\"evidence_id\":\"E0018\",\"explanation\":\"RFA described Hanoi's response as formulaic and passive, which limits the case for active peace leadership.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0019\",\"explanation\":\"The China visit reinforced close ties and strategic balancing rather than a clear conflict-resolution breakthrough.\"}],\"inherited_baseline_and_constraints\":\"Vietnam was a non-belligerent state with a strong institutional preference for balancing great powers and avoiding direct confrontation, so the question is whether Trọng's leadership kept that posture lawful and peaceful.\",\"ruler_attribution\":\"Much of the evidence is party-state rather than purely personal, but Trọng's own statements and visits make the attribution adequate for Chapter 2B.\",\"supported_lenses\":[\"2B.1 restraint and peaceful language\",\"2B.7 dialogue and peaceful settlement\",\"2B.10 stable multilateral posture\"],\"missing_or_weak_lenses\":[\"2B.2 direct conflict management\",\"2B.4 battlefield conduct\",\"2B.5 proxy restraint\"],\"contrary_evidence\":[{\"evidence_id\":\"E0018\",\"explanation\":\"Independent reporting suggests the response was passive and mostly formulaic rather than visibly decisive.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0019\",\"explanation\":\"The China visit mainly reinforced balancing strategy, not a concrete peace settlement.\"}],\"source_mix\":\"Vietnamese official statements and some independent RFA reporting provide the core evidence; local priors were unavailable in this experiment.\",\"structured_prior_summary\":\"Structured local priors were not collected in this experiment; judgment is based on the embedded dossier evidence and its counterevidence.\",\"chapter_rationale\":\"Nguyễn Phú Trọng's 2022 record is restraint-oriented and institution-friendly. Vietnam repeatedly called for self-restraint, peaceful settlement, and multilateral cooperation, while keeping its external posture careful and legalistic; the main limitation is that this mostly remained declaratory diplomacy rather than a demonstrable conflict-ending initiative. The score therefore lands above the middle but below the strongest peace cases, reflecting a consistently cautious and lawful posture without a major breakthrough.\",\"lower_anchor_rejected\":\"A score of 6.0 is too low because the dossier shows repeated, direct peace and restraint language from Trọng and his government.\",\"higher_anchor_rejected\":\"A score of 7.0 is too high because the record is mostly declaratory and balancing-oriented rather than decisively peace-producing.\",\"manual_review_required\":false,\"manual_review_reason_type\":null,\"manual_review_reason\":null,\"chapter_specific\":[{\"field\":\"trajectory\",\"value\":\"Restraint-oriented and multilateral, but mostly declaratory rather than outcome-changing.\"}]}],\"unavailable_dossiers\":[],\"batch_notes\":[\"Calibrated against Russia as the low anchor, Japan as a high-restraint anchor, and Ethiopia as a mixed war-to-peace transition case.\",\"The batch separates into a low coercive band (Russia, Iran, China, Turkey), a mixed middle band (Brazil, Congo, Ethiopia, India, Pakistan, Thailand), and a stronger restraint band (Bangladesh, Germany, Egypt, Indonesia, Japan, Mexico, Philippines, United States, Vietnam).\",\"Nigeria is a recoverable null because the provided dossier contains only inherited baseline context, not a 2022 target-period security decision attributable to Buhari.\"],\"run_profile\":{\"provider_profile\":\"gpt-5.4-mini\",\"provider\":\"openai\",\"model\":\"gpt-5.4-mini\",\"dossier_count\":20,\"unavailable_dossier_count\":0,\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":\"unknown_not_exposed_by_tool\",\"output_tokens\":\"unknown_not_exposed_by_tool\",\"total_tokens\":\"unknown_not_exposed_by_tool\",\"estimated_cost_usd\":\"unknown_not_exposed_by_tool\"}}}"}}
