{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_0","type":"agent_message","text":"{\n  \"schema_version\": \"ruler_chapter_judgment_v1\",\n  \"job_key\": \"chapter-judge:2022-top20-hybrid-v2-judges-v1:2022:5B\",\n  \"run_key\": \"2022-top20-hybrid-v2-judges-v1\",\n  \"chapter_id\": \"5B\",\n  \"target_year\": 2022,\n  \"rubric_version\": \"chapter_5b_v3\",\n  \"calibration_batch_id\": \"chapter-judge:2022-top20-hybrid-v2-judges-v1:2022:5B\",\n  \"evaluations\": [\n    {\n      \"dossier_job_key\": \"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:BGD:17068\",\n      \"iso3\": \"BGD\",\n      \"ruler_id\": \"2992\",\n      \"ruler_year_id\": 17068,\n      \"ruler_name\": \"Sheikh Hasina\",\n      \"period_start_year\": 2022,\n      \"period_end_year\": 2022,\n      \"chapter_id\": \"5B\",\n      \"rubric_version\": \"chapter_5b_v3\",\n      \"calibration_batch_id\": \"chapter-judge:2022-top20-hybrid-v2-judges-v1:2022:5B\",\n      \"calibrated_against\": [\n        \"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:RUS:15706\",\n        \"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:DEU:16984\",\n        \"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:VNM:19647\"\n      ],\n      \"score_1_to_10\": 6.5,\n      \"insufficient_evidence_reason\": null,\n      \"confidence_score\": 0.78,\n      \"plausible_score_range\": {\n        \"lower\": 6.0,\n        \"upper\": 7.0\n      },\n      \"decisive_positive_evidence\": [\n        {\n          \"evidence_id\": \"E0055\",\n          \"explanation\": \"Fast pandemic support showed the authorities using fiscal capacity for broad relief rather than pure extraction.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"evidence_id\": \"E0058\",\n          \"explanation\": \"The IMF program agreement signaled an active stabilization response to 2022 macro strain.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"evidence_id\": \"E0067\",\n          \"explanation\": \"The central-bank governor appointment shows direct executive action on monetary management.\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"decisive_negative_evidence\": [\n        {\n          \"evidence_id\": \"E0064\",\n          \"explanation\": \"Fuel-price hikes, high inflation, and reserve pressure show serious household stress and weak stabilization.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"evidence_id\": \"E0068\",\n          \"explanation\": \"Late-2022 macro indicators show inflation, balance-of-payments stress, and a multiple exchange-rate regime.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"evidence_id\": \"E0056\",\n          \"explanation\": \"IMF criticism of banking regulation and tax reform shows structural weaknesses that were not solved.\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"inherited_baseline_and_constraints\": \"Bangladesh entered 2022 with strong long-run growth and poverty reduction, but also with inflation pressure, reserve strain, weak banking quality, and pandemic-era fiscal demands.\",\n      \"ruler_attribution\": \"Attribution is reasonably strong for crisis response, fiscal design, and key economic appointments, but weaker for household-level execution and structural banking reform.\",\n      \"supported_lenses\": [\n        \"5B.1\",\n        \"5B.3\",\n        \"5B.6\",\n        \"5B.8\",\n        \"5B.9\",\n        \"5B.10\"\n      ],\n      \"missing_or_weak_lenses\": [\n        \"5B.2\",\n        \"5B.4\",\n        \"5B.5\",\n        \"5B.7\"\n      ],\n      \"contrary_evidence\": [\n        {\n          \"evidence_id\": \"E0064\",\n          \"explanation\": \"The economy was still under inflation and reserve pressure.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"evidence_id\": \"E0068\",\n          \"explanation\": \"Macro vulnerabilities deepened despite the policy response.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"evidence_id\": \"E0056\",\n          \"explanation\": \"Structural banking and revenue weaknesses remained unresolved.\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"source_mix\": \"Mostly IMF and World Bank surveillance, plus Reuters and domestic budget/appointment reporting; no structured local priors were collected in this experiment.\",\n      \"structured_prior_summary\": \"Structured local priors were unavailable across all lenses, so the judgment rests on the embedded dossier evidence, the lens coverage map, and source-confidence metadata only.\",\n      \"chapter_rationale\": \"Hasina receives a 6.5 because the record shows real, ruler-attributed efforts to protect livelihoods and stabilize the economy, not just rhetoric. The strongest positives are the large pandemic support package, the IMF-backed stabilization program, social safety-net spending, and the central-bank leadership change; the main negatives are still-serious inflation, reserve pressure, and unresolved banking and trade bottlenecks. The evidence supports competence and some broad social protection, but not a materially higher score because the economy remained fragile and several weaknesses were structural rather than corrected.\",\n      \"lower_anchor_rejected\": \"A score near 5 would understate the amount of active fiscal and social-protection response visible in 2022.\",\n      \"higher_anchor_rejected\": \"A score near 7.5 would overstate durability, because the dossier still shows clear inflation, reserve, and banking stress.\",\n      \"manual_review_required\": false,\n      \"manual_review_reason_type\": null,\n      \"manual_review_reason\": null,\n      \"chapter_specific\": [\n        {\n          \"field\": \"trajectory\",\n          \"value\": \"Modestly upward from the pandemic baseline, but the path was fragile and heavily constrained by inflation, reserves, and banking weakness.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"field\": \"external_conditions\",\n          \"value\": \"Pandemic carryover, global inflation, import-price pressure, and financial-sector stress materially limited what the government could achieve.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"field\": \"distribution_and_household_effects\",\n          \"value\": \"Safety nets and transfers were real positives, but household welfare remained pressured by prices and weaker execution than the announcement record suggests.\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"dossier_job_key\": \"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:BRA:19646\",\n      \"iso3\": \"BRA\",\n      \"ruler_id\": \"3413\",\n      \"ruler_year_id\": 19646,\n      \"ruler_name\": \"Jair Bolsonaro\",\n      \"period_start_year\": 2022,\n      \"period_end_year\": 2022,\n      \"chapter_id\": \"5B\",\n      \"rubric_version\": \"chapter_5b_v3\",\n      \"calibration_batch_id\": \"chapter-judge:2022-top20-hybrid-v2-judges-v1:2022:5B\",\n      \"calibrated_against\": [\n        \"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:RUS:15706\",\n        \"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:DEU:16984\",\n        \"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:VNM:19647\"\n      ],\n      \"score_1_to_10\": 4.5,\n      \"insufficient_evidence_reason\": null,\n      \"confidence_score\": 0.71,\n      \"plausible_score_range\": {\n        \"lower\": 4.0,\n        \"upper\": 5.0\n      },\n      \"decisive_positive_evidence\": [\n        {\n          \"evidence_id\": \"E0066\",\n          \"explanation\": \"The 2022 primary surplus suggests fiscal outcomes were not uniformly poor.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"evidence_id\": \"E0064\",\n          \"explanation\": \"Investment and contracted-project activity show some state-capacity and infrastructure follow-through.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"evidence_id\": \"E0048\",\n          \"explanation\": \"GDP growth remained positive in 2022 despite the difficult environment.\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"decisive_negative_evidence\": [\n        {\n          \"evidence_id\": \"E0051\",\n          \"explanation\": \"Food insecurity and food-price pressure were severe and broadly felt.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"evidence_id\": \"E0057\",\n          \"explanation\": \"Election-year spending that bypassed the cap raised fiscal and inflation concerns.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"evidence_id\": \"E0050\",\n          \"explanation\": \"Inflation stayed elevated and household purchasing power remained under strain.\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"inherited_baseline_and_constraints\": \"Brazil entered 2022 with post-pandemic recovery, inflation shocks, and labor-market weakness; global commodity and food-price swings mattered a lot, but so did election-year fiscal choices.\",\n      \"ruler_attribution\": \"Attribution is mixed: some positive growth and fiscal outcomes reflect the broader recovery and institutional settings, while the most salient negative choices were clearly linked to Bolsonaro's political strategy.\",\n      \"supported_lenses\": [\n        \"5B.3\",\n        \"5B.4\",\n        \"5B.6\",\n        \"5B.8\",\n        \"5B.9\",\n        \"5B.10\"\n      ],\n      \"missing_or_weak_lenses\": [\n        \"5B.1\",\n        \"5B.2\",\n        \"5B.5\",\n        \"5B.7\"\n      ],\n      \"contrary_evidence\": [\n        {\n          \"evidence_id\": \"E0048\",\n          \"explanation\": \"Positive GDP growth kept the score from dropping further.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"evidence_id\": \"E0066\",\n          \"explanation\": \"A primary surplus and completed projects provide some counterweight.\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"source_mix\": \"Official statistics, central-bank minutes, World Bank analysis, Reuters reporting, and government program releases; no structured local priors were collected in this experiment.\",\n      \"structured_prior_summary\": \"Structured local priors were unavailable across all lenses, so the judge relied on the embedded dossier evidence and the source-confidence framing only.\",\n      \"chapter_rationale\": \"Bolsonaro lands at 4.5 because the year mixed real macro activity with clearly harmful short-term politics and weak household outcomes. Growth, employment, investment, and even a fiscal surplus show that the economy was not collapsing, but food insecurity, inflation, and election-year spending that strained fiscal credibility kept the chapter firmly below the competence threshold. The evidence supports a mixed record with some competent outcomes, yet not enough fairness, durability, or restraint to justify a higher score.\",\n      \"lower_anchor_rejected\": \"A score near 3 would ignore the positive growth, surplus, and investment evidence.\",\n      \"higher_anchor_rejected\": \"A score near 6 would overstate the policy quality because food insecurity, inflation, and fiscal loosening were serious and ruler-linked.\",\n      \"manual_review_required\": false,\n      \"manual_review_reason_type\": null,\n      \"manual_review_reason\": null,\n      \"chapter_specific\": [\n        {\n          \"field\": \"trajectory\",\n          \"value\": \"Mixed and uneven: output and employment improved, but inflation, food insecurity, and election-year fiscal loosening eroded the prosperity story.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"field\": \"external_conditions\",\n          \"value\": \"Commodity and food-price shocks mattered, but the administration amplified them through discretionary spending and weak structural reform.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"field\": \"distribution_and_household_effects\",\n          \"value\": \"Household welfare lagged headline growth; the food-insecurity evidence is the clearest sign that gains were not broadly shared.\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"dossier_job_key\": \"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:CHN:15832\",\n      \"iso3\": \"CHN\",\n      \"ruler_id\": \"1432\",\n      \"ruler_year_id\": 15832,\n      \"ruler_name\": \"Xi Jinping\",\n      \"period_start_year\": 2022,\n      \"period_end_year\": 2022,\n      \"chapter_id\": \"5B\",\n      \"rubric_version\": \"chapter_5b_v3\",\n      \"calibration_batch_id\": \"chapter-judge:2022-top20-hybrid-v2-judges-v1:2022:5B\",\n      \"calibrated_against\": [\n        \"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:RUS:15706\",\n        \"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:DEU:16984\",\n        \"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:VNM:19647\"\n      ],\n      \"score_1_to_10\": 6.0,\n      \"insufficient_evidence_reason\": null,\n      \"confidence_score\": 0.74,\n      \"plausible_score_range\": {\n        \"lower\": 5.5,\n        \"upper\": 6.5\n      },\n      \"decisive_positive_evidence\": [\n        {\n          \"evidence_id\": \"E0072\",\n          \"explanation\": \"Fixed-asset investment still grew, with infrastructure and manufacturing relatively strong.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"evidence_id\": \"E0075\",\n          \"explanation\": \"The labor market created millions of new urban jobs in 2022.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"evidence_id\": \"E0076\",\n          \"explanation\": \"The central bank used a broad stabilization toolkit to support growth and the property sector.\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"decisive_negative_evidence\": [\n        {\n          \"evidence_id\": \"E0073\",\n          \"explanation\": \"Property development collapsed sharply, showing a major drag on prosperity.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"evidence_id\": \"E0066\",\n          \"explanation\": \"Developer investment and new construction starts fell hard, indicating deep sector stress.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"evidence_id\": \"E0075\",\n          \"explanation\": \"Youth unemployment remained very high even with aggregate job creation.\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"inherited_baseline_and_constraints\": \"China entered 2022 with strong state capacity and a large investment apparatus, but also with a property bubble, weak private investment, and rising youth-labor-market strain.\",\n      \"ruler_attribution\": \"Attribution is strong for the overall policy environment and party-state direction, but weaker for whether Xi personally optimized the growth mix rather than simply presiding over it.\",\n      \"supported_lenses\": [\n        \"5B.1\",\n        \"5B.2\",\n        \"5B.3\",\n        \"5B.4\",\n        \"5B.6\",\n        \"5B.8\",\n        \"5B.9\",\n        \"5B.10\"\n      ],\n      \"missing_or_weak_lenses\": [\n        \"5B.5\",\n        \"5B.7\"\n      ],\n      \"contrary_evidence\": [\n        {\n          \"evidence_id\": \"E0073\",\n          \"explanation\": \"The property sector contracted sharply.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"evidence_id\": \"E0066\",\n          \"explanation\": \"Private investment and new starts were too weak to call the year broadly balanced.\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"source_mix\": \"Official party-state texts and statistics, NBS and PBC data, plus Reuters-based reporting on the property crisis and personnel consolidation; no structured local priors were collected in this experiment.\",\n      \"structured_prior_summary\": \"Structured local priors were unavailable across all lenses; the judge used the dossier's own evidence and the projection's lens mapping only.\",\n      \"chapter_rationale\": \"Xi scores 6.0 because the record shows a powerful state apparatus that still delivered investment growth, job creation, and aggressive stabilization. The score is capped well below the top band because the property crash, weak private investment, and youth unemployment reveal a serious distortion in the prosperity model, while the evidence on correction and broad fairness is weaker than the evidence on top-down control. This is a competent but constrained performance, not a transformational one.\",\n      \"lower_anchor_rejected\": \"A score near 5 would underrate the scale of state-led investment, jobs, and stabilization capacity.\",\n      \"higher_anchor_rejected\": \"A score near 7 would overstate breadth and durability, because the property crisis and weak private sector remained unresolved.\",\n      \"manual_review_required\": false,\n      \"manual_review_reason_type\": null,\n      \"manual_review_reason\": null,\n      \"chapter_specific\": [\n        {\n          \"field\": \"trajectory\",\n          \"value\": \"Growth held up, but the economy became more state-led and less balanced as the property sector weakened and private investment lagged.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"field\": \"external_conditions\",\n          \"value\": \"The property downturn, pandemic after-effects, and global slowdown constrained the year; policy response mattered, but so did structural imbalances.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"field\": \"distribution_and_household_effects\",\n          \"value\": \"Aggregate investment and jobs improved, yet youth labor distress and property weakness meant household gains were uneven.\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"dossier_job_key\": \"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:COD:16113\",\n      \"iso3\": \"COD\",\n      \"ruler_id\": \"2830\",\n      \"ruler_year_id\": 16113,\n      \"ruler_name\": \"F\\u0000e9lix Tshisekedi\",\n      \"period_start_year\": 2022,\n      \"period_end_year\": 2022,\n      \"chapter_id\": \"5B\",\n      \"rubric_version\": \"chapter_5b_v3\",\n      \"calibration_batch_id\": \"chapter-judge:2022-top20-hybrid-v2-judges-v1:2022:5B\",\n      \"calibrated_against\": [\n        \"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:RUS:15706\",\n        \"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:DEU:16984\",\n        \"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:VNM:19647\"\n      ],\n      \"score_1_to_10\": 4.0,\n      \"insufficient_evidence_reason\": null,\n      \"confidence_score\": 0.68,\n      \"plausible_score_range\": {\n        \"lower\": 3.5,\n        \"upper\": 4.5\n      },\n      \"decisive_positive_evidence\": [\n        {\n          \"evidence_id\": \"E0069\",\n          \"explanation\": \"World Bank budget support and reform financing show some credible governance and connectivity agenda.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"evidence_id\": \"E0072\",\n          \"explanation\": \"Telecom liberalization and market reforms point to real policy effort.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"evidence_id\": \"E0075\",\n          \"explanation\": \"The 145-territories program shows direct presidential sponsorship of local development works.\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"decisive_negative_evidence\": [\n        {\n          \"evidence_id\": \"E0078\",\n          \"explanation\": \"The missing mining-company payments indicate serious state-capture and leakage problems.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"evidence_id\": \"E0071\",\n          \"explanation\": \"Poverty reduction remained elusive despite growth.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"evidence_id\": \"E0074\",\n          \"explanation\": \"Eastern conflict remained severe, limiting any broad prosperity claim.\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"inherited_baseline_and_constraints\": \"The DRC entered 2022 with conflict, weak state capacity, mining dependence, poverty, and major delivery gaps. Those constraints were severe, but they do not erase the need to judge what the presidency did with the room it had.\",\n      \"ruler_attribution\": \"Attribution is partial: Tshisekedi clearly sponsored reform and development programs, but the strongest positive items are often external financing or self-reported program design, while the negative leakages and conflict were only partly under his direct control.\",\n      \"supported_lenses\": [\n        \"5B.3\",\n        \"5B.4\",\n        \"5B.6\",\n        \"5B.8\",\n        \"5B.9\",\n        \"5B.10\"\n      ],\n      \"missing_or_weak_lenses\": [\n        \"5B.1\",\n        \"5B.2\",\n        \"5B.5\",\n        \"5B.7\"\n      ],\n      \"contrary_evidence\": [\n        {\n          \"evidence_id\": \"E0078\",\n          \"explanation\": \"The audit finding on missing funds is a major negative signal.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"evidence_id\": \"E0071\",\n          \"explanation\": \"Broad poverty gains were still not visible.\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"source_mix\": \"IMF and World Bank surveillance, presidential-office program announcements, and Reuters-based audit reporting; no structured local priors were collected in this experiment.\",\n      \"structured_prior_summary\": \"Structured local priors were unavailable across all lenses; the judgment relies on the dossier evidence and lens mapping only.\",\n      \"chapter_rationale\": \"Tshisekedi receives 4.0 because the dossier shows real reform activity and some development ambition, but not enough durable prosperity to move the country out of the mixed band. The strongest negatives are the missing mining payments, continued conflict, and the fact that poverty reduction remained elusive even where macro indicators improved. That combination supports some credit for policy effort, but not a high score for actual household prosperity.\",\n      \"lower_anchor_rejected\": \"A score near 3 would understate the range of active reform and development initiatives shown in the record.\",\n      \"higher_anchor_rejected\": \"A score near 5 would overstate results, because leakage, conflict, and poverty persistence still dominate the household picture.\",\n      \"manual_review_required\": false,\n      \"manual_review_reason_type\": null,\n      \"manual_review_reason\": null,\n      \"chapter_specific\": [\n        {\n          \"field\": \"trajectory\",\n          \"value\": \"There was reform motion, but the prosperity trajectory remained weak because state capacity and conflict constraints outweighed the announced programs.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"field\": \"external_conditions\",\n          \"value\": \"Conflict in the east, mining dependence, and inherited fragility constrained what could be achieved in 2022.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"field\": \"distribution_and_household_effects\",\n          \"value\": \"Household gains were thin; poverty and conflict costs were still too large to describe the year as broadly prosperous.\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"dossier_job_key\": \"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:DEU:16984\",\n      \"iso3\": \"DEU\",\n      \"ruler_id\": \"2975\",\n      \"ruler_year_id\": 16984,\n      \"ruler_name\": \"Olaf Scholz\",\n      \"period_start_year\": 2022,\n      \"period_end_year\": 2022,\n      \"chapter_id\": \"5B\",\n      \"rubric_version\": \"chapter_5b_v3\",\n      \"calibration_batch_id\": \"chapter-judge:2022-top20-hybrid-v2-judges-v1:2022:5B\",\n      \"calibrated_against\": [\n        \"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:RUS:15706\",\n        \"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:TUR:15972\",\n        \"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:VNM:19647\"\n      ],\n      \"score_1_to_10\": 7.0,\n      \"insufficient_evidence_reason\": null,\n      \"confidence_score\": 0.77,\n      \"plausible_score_range\": {\n        \"lower\": 6.5,\n        \"upper\": 7.5\n      },\n      \"decisive_positive_evidence\": [\n        {\n          \"evidence_id\": \"E0048\",\n          \"explanation\": \"The supplementary budget was an aggressive, coherent crisis response with direct household relief.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"evidence_id\": \"E0051\",\n          \"explanation\": \"The 200 billion euro shield shows large-scale stabilization and protection of firms and households.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"evidence_id\": \"E0052\",\n          \"explanation\": \"The OECD judged the government had acted swiftly and in a generally well-targeted way.\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"decisive_negative_evidence\": [\n        {\n          \"evidence_id\": \"E0059\",\n          \"explanation\": \"The Bundesrechnungshof warned the energy-shield financing design carried significant fiscal and constitutional risk.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"evidence_id\": \"E0053\",\n          \"explanation\": \"The IMF still expected weak growth and recommended tighter fiscal policy.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"evidence_id\": \"E0057\",\n          \"explanation\": \"Employment was strong, but inflation and real-income pressure were still present in the same year.\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"inherited_baseline_and_constraints\": \"Germany faced the energy shock from Russia's war, high inflation, and the need to cushion households and firms without undermining fiscal credibility.\",\n      \"ruler_attribution\": \"Attribution is strong for the crisis packages and cabinet coordination, but weaker for the independent labor-market and employment tailwinds that also supported the year.\",\n      \"supported_lenses\": [\n        \"5B.1\",\n        \"5B.3\",\n        \"5B.4\",\n        \"5B.6\",\n        \"5B.8\",\n        \"5B.9\",\n        \"5B.10\"\n      ],\n      \"missing_or_weak_lenses\": [\n        \"5B.2\",\n        \"5B.5\",\n        \"5B.7\"\n      ],\n      \"contrary_evidence\": [\n        {\n          \"evidence_id\": \"E0059\",\n          \"explanation\": \"Independent auditors questioned the financing design.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"evidence_id\": \"E0053\",\n          \"explanation\": \"The IMF still saw room for tighter policy and weaker growth.\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"source_mix\": \"Federal ministry releases, constitutional text, labor statistics, OECD/IMF surveillance, and the federal audit office; no structured local priors were collected in this experiment.\",\n      \"structured_prior_summary\": \"Structured local priors were unavailable across all lenses; the judgment relies on embedded evidence and coverage mapping only.\",\n      \"chapter_rationale\": \"Scholz scores 7.0 because the government responded to the 2022 energy shock with unusually large, concrete relief and stabilization measures that protected households and firms. The main reason the score is not higher is that the financing design drew serious fiscal and constitutional criticism and inflation still eroded purchasing power, even if the labor market stayed exceptionally strong. The dossier therefore supports effective crisis management with real but bounded weaknesses.\",\n      \"lower_anchor_rejected\": \"A score near 6 would understate the scale and coherence of the energy-crisis response.\",\n      \"higher_anchor_rejected\": \"A score near 8 would overstate durability, because fiscal-design criticism and inflation remain material.\",\n      \"manual_review_required\": false,\n      \"manual_review_reason_type\": null,\n      \"manual_review_reason\": null,\n      \"chapter_specific\": [\n        {\n          \"field\": \"trajectory\",\n          \"value\": \"The year was a defensive success: Germany preserved employment and cushioned the shock, but the upside was limited by inflation and fiscal stress.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"field\": \"external_conditions\",\n          \"value\": \"Russia's war in Ukraine and the energy-price shock were the dominant constraints; policy quality mattered because the shock was external and severe.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"field\": \"distribution_and_household_effects\",\n          \"value\": \"Relief was broad and household-focused, but the benefits were partly temporary and still offset by inflation.\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"dossier_job_key\": \"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:EGY:16232\",\n      \"iso3\": \"EGY\",\n      \"ruler_id\": \"2851\",\n      \"ruler_year_id\": 16232,\n      \"ruler_name\": \"Abdel Fattah el-Sisi\",\n      \"period_start_year\": 2022,\n      \"period_end_year\": 2022,\n      \"chapter_id\": \"5B\",\n      \"rubric_version\": \"chapter_5b_v3\",\n      \"calibration_batch_id\": \"chapter-judge:2022-top20-hybrid-v2-judges-v1:2022:5B\",\n      \"calibrated_against\": [\n        \"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:RUS:15706\",\n        \"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:DEU:16984\",\n        \"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:VNM:19647\"\n      ],\n      \"score_1_to_10\": 3.0,\n      \"insufficient_evidence_reason\": null,\n      \"confidence_score\": 0.74,\n      \"plausible_score_range\": {\n        \"lower\": 2.5,\n        \"upper\": 3.5\n      },\n      \"decisive_positive_evidence\": [\n        {\n          \"evidence_id\": \"E0053\",\n          \"explanation\": \"The IMF agreement showed an attempted stabilization and reform package.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"evidence_id\": \"E0057\",\n          \"explanation\": \"Social-protection expansion helped narrow the damage for some households.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"evidence_id\": \"E0059\",\n          \"explanation\": \"Lifting import curbs and opening more sectors to the private sector signaled some corrective movement.\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"decisive_negative_evidence\": [\n        {\n          \"evidence_id\": \"E0054\",\n          \"explanation\": \"Inflation reached 18.7 percent after devaluation and import restrictions.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"evidence_id\": \"E0055\",\n          \"explanation\": \"The IMF package itself reflected deep state-footprint and competitiveness problems.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"evidence_id\": \"E0051\",\n          \"explanation\": \"Military economic privilege and uneven competition remained unresolved.\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"inherited_baseline_and_constraints\": \"Egypt entered 2022 with a state-heavy economy, currency stress, import dependence, and chronic inflation vulnerability. Those constraints were serious, but the score turns on how the presidency handled them, not on the constraints alone.\",\n      \"ruler_attribution\": \"Attribution is moderate: Sisi clearly presided over the appointment, devaluation, and reform package, but the IMF and external financing conditions strongly shaped the policy mix.\",\n      \"supported_lenses\": [\n        \"5B.2\",\n        \"5B.3\",\n        \"5B.6\",\n        \"5B.8\",\n        \"5B.9\",\n        \"5B.10\"\n      ],\n      \"missing_or_weak_lenses\": [\n        \"5B.1\",\n        \"5B.4\",\n        \"5B.5\",\n        \"5B.7\"\n      ],\n      \"contrary_evidence\": [\n        {\n          \"evidence_id\": \"E0054\",\n          \"explanation\": \"Inflation and currency weakness were severe.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"evidence_id\": \"E0051\",\n          \"explanation\": \"Privileged military economic structures still distorted the field.\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"source_mix\": \"Constitutional text, official biography, IMF and World Bank releases, Reuters reporting, and policy analysis; no structured local priors were collected in this experiment.\",\n      \"structured_prior_summary\": \"Structured local priors were unavailable across all lenses; the judgment relies on the dossier's embedded evidence and the projection map only.\",\n      \"chapter_rationale\": \"Sisi gets 3.0 because the 2022 record is dominated by currency stress, high inflation, and a state-heavy model that still needed IMF rescue. There were real corrective steps, especially the IMF package, social protection, and a move toward a larger private sector role, but those actions were reactive and only partially credible as durable prosperity policy. The evidence supports a stressed and only partially corrected economy, not a robust stewardship story.\",\n      \"lower_anchor_rejected\": \"A score near 2 would underplay the fact that there was a real stabilization and social-protection effort.\",\n      \"higher_anchor_rejected\": \"A score near 4 would overstate the success of reforms that remained conditional and incomplete.\",\n      \"manual_review_required\": false,\n      \"manual_review_reason_type\": null,\n      \"manual_review_reason\": null,\n      \"chapter_specific\": [\n        {\n          \"field\": \"trajectory\",\n          \"value\": \"The trajectory was defensive and fragile: stabilization was attempted, but inflation and external dependence still defined the year.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"field\": \"external_conditions\",\n          \"value\": \"Foreign-currency shortages, import dependence, and IMF conditionality sharply constrained the room for maneuver.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"field\": \"distribution_and_household_effects\",\n          \"value\": \"Households were protected somewhat through social programs, but inflation still eroded purchasing power heavily.\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"dossier_job_key\": \"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:ETH:16782\",\n      \"iso3\": \"ETH\",\n      \"ruler_id\": \"2310\",\n      \"ruler_year_id\": 16782,\n      \"ruler_name\": \"Abiy Ahmed\",\n      \"period_start_year\": 2022,\n      \"period_end_year\": 2022,\n      \"chapter_id\": \"5B\",\n      \"rubric_version\": \"chapter_5b_v3\",\n      \"calibration_batch_id\": \"chapter-judge:2022-top20-hybrid-v2-judges-v1:2022:5B\",\n      \"calibrated_against\": [\n        \"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:RUS:15706\",\n        \"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:DEU:16984\",\n        \"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:VNM:19647\"\n      ],\n      \"score_1_to_10\": 3.0,\n      \"insufficient_evidence_reason\": null,\n      \"confidence_score\": 0.70,\n      \"plausible_score_range\": {\n        \"lower\": 2.5,\n        \"upper\": 3.5\n      },\n      \"decisive_positive_evidence\": [\n        {\n          \"evidence_id\": \"E0046\",\n          \"explanation\": \"The reconstruction grant targeted conflict-affected services, women, and girls.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"evidence_id\": \"E0048\",\n          \"explanation\": \"Large grants supported health access and flood resilience in late 2022.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"evidence_id\": \"E0053\",\n          \"explanation\": \"Urban safety-net support helped vulnerable households and women.\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"decisive_negative_evidence\": [\n        {\n          \"evidence_id\": \"E0050\",\n          \"explanation\": \"Inflation was still extremely high in 2022.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"evidence_id\": \"E0051\",\n          \"explanation\": \"Debt restructuring was delayed by civil war and foreign-exchange strain.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"evidence_id\": \"E0043\",\n          \"explanation\": \"The IMF explicitly described multiple shocks, fiscal strain, and persistent macro imbalances.\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"inherited_baseline_and_constraints\": \"Ethiopia in 2022 was constrained by civil war, macro instability, inflation, and disrupted services. Those conditions severely limited what any ruler could achieve, but they still leave room to judge whether the response was competent and broad-based.\",\n      \"ruler_attribution\": \"Attribution is partial: Abiy's government clearly sponsored some recovery and safety-net measures, but conflict and macro stress dominated and made direct personal credit thin.\",\n      \"supported_lenses\": [\n        \"5B.1\",\n        \"5B.3\",\n        \"5B.6\",\n        \"5B.8\",\n        \"5B.9\",\n        \"5B.10\"\n      ],\n      \"missing_or_weak_lenses\": [\n        \"5B.2\",\n        \"5B.4\",\n        \"5B.5\",\n        \"5B.7\"\n      ],\n      \"contrary_evidence\": [\n        {\n          \"evidence_id\": \"E0050\",\n          \"explanation\": \"Inflation remained extremely high.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"evidence_id\": \"E0051\",\n          \"explanation\": \"The civil war delayed debt relief and worsened the macro position.\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"source_mix\": \"IMF, World Bank, and Ethiopian government releases, plus Reuters-derived reporting; no structured local priors were collected in this experiment.\",\n      \"structured_prior_summary\": \"Structured local priors were unavailable across all lenses; the judgment relies on the dossier evidence and projection map only.\",\n      \"chapter_rationale\": \"Abiy scores 3.0 because the dossier shows some real reconstruction and safety-net effort, but the year was still dominated by war, inflation, and macro fragility. The positive items are mainly compensatory and recovery-oriented, while the negative evidence shows that civil-war disruption and inflation still overwhelmed broad prosperity. This is a crisis-management record with limited room for success, not a strong economic stewardship case.\",\n      \"lower_anchor_rejected\": \"A score near 2 would ignore the concrete grants and social-protection measures that were actually put in place.\",\n      \"higher_anchor_rejected\": \"A score near 4 would overstate the degree to which recovery was visible or durable in 2022.\",\n      \"manual_review_required\": false,\n      \"manual_review_reason_type\": null,\n      \"manual_review_reason\": null,\n      \"chapter_specific\": [\n        {\n          \"field\": \"trajectory\",\n          \"value\": \"The year was mostly defensive recovery under conflict, not a clean prosperity-upturn.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"field\": \"external_conditions\",\n          \"value\": \"Civil war, external financing constraints, and global inflation were the decisive headwinds.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"field\": \"distribution_and_household_effects\",\n          \"value\": \"Targeted support existed, but household welfare remained weak and uneven across conflict-affected areas.\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"dossier_job_key\": \"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:IDN:16199\",\n      \"iso3\": \"IDN\",\n      \"ruler_id\": \"2636\",\n      \"ruler_year_id\": 16199,\n      \"ruler_name\": \"Joko Widodo\",\n      \"period_start_year\": 2022,\n      \"period_end_year\": 2022,\n      \"chapter_id\": \"5B\",\n      \"rubric_version\": \"chapter_5b_v3\",\n      \"calibration_batch_id\": \"chapter-judge:2022-top20-hybrid-v2-judges-v1:2022:5B\",\n      \"calibrated_against\": [\n        \"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:RUS:15706\",\n        \"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:DEU:16984\",\n        \"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:VNM:19647\"\n      ],\n      \"score_1_to_10\": 7.0,\n      \"insufficient_evidence_reason\": null,\n      \"confidence_score\": 0.78,\n      \"plausible_score_range\": {\n        \"lower\": 6.5,\n        \"upper\": 7.5\n      },\n      \"decisive_positive_evidence\": [\n        {\n          \"evidence_id\": \"E0057\",\n          \"explanation\": \"Inflation ended at 5.51 percent after coordinated fuel-price and fiscal moves.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"evidence_id\": \"E0059\",\n          \"explanation\": \"Tax revenue exceeded target, supporting fiscal space.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"evidence_id\": \"E0061\",\n          \"explanation\": \"Unemployment fell and jobs recovered during 2022.\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"decisive_negative_evidence\": [\n        {\n          \"evidence_id\": \"E0064\",\n          \"explanation\": \"The CPI remained weak enough on anti-corruption performance to show governance problems.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"evidence_id\": \"E0066\",\n          \"explanation\": \"The cooking-oil crisis required a reshuffle, suggesting policy execution problems.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"evidence_id\": \"E0063\",\n          \"explanation\": \"Inequality improved only slightly, which limits the equity story.\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"inherited_baseline_and_constraints\": \"Indonesia entered 2022 with a post-pandemic rebound, commodity tailwinds, and a large but still reform-constrained economy. Policy quality mattered because the country had enough macro room to either amplify or waste that rebound.\",\n      \"ruler_attribution\": \"Attribution is fairly strong for fiscal design, inflation response, and cabinet choices, though commodity prices, reopening, and central-bank policy also mattered materially.\",\n      \"supported_lenses\": [\n        \"5B.1\",\n        \"5B.2\",\n        \"5B.3\",\n        \"5B.4\",\n        \"5B.6\",\n        \"5B.8\",\n        \"5B.9\",\n        \"5B.10\"\n      ],\n      \"missing_or_weak_lenses\": [\n        \"5B.5\",\n        \"5B.7\"\n      ],\n      \"contrary_evidence\": [\n        {\n          \"evidence_id\": \"E0064\",\n          \"explanation\": \"Corruption perceptions remained weak.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"evidence_id\": \"E0066\",\n          \"explanation\": \"The cooking-oil crisis exposed administrative fragility.\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"source_mix\": \"Official statistics, IMF and World Bank surveillance, fiscal/legal releases, and Reuters-based reporting; no structured local priors were collected in this experiment.\",\n      \"structured_prior_summary\": \"Structured local priors were unavailable across all lenses; the judge relied on the dossier evidence and source-confidence metadata only.\",\n      \"chapter_rationale\": \"Jokowi scores 7.0 because the 2022 record shows broad, competent management of a rebound year: inflation was contained, unemployment fell, tax revenue beat target, and social protection was tightened around the fuel shock. The score is not higher because corruption performance stayed weak, some redistribution gains were modest, and the cooking-oil episode showed that implementation was not seamless. Even so, the dossier supports a strong prosperity trajectory with broad household gains and credible fiscal control.\",\n      \"lower_anchor_rejected\": \"A score near 6 would understate the breadth of the macro stabilization and revenue performance.\",\n      \"higher_anchor_rejected\": \"A score near 8 would overstate institutional quality, because corruption and execution problems remained visible.\",\n      \"manual_review_required\": false,\n      \"manual_review_reason_type\": null,\n      \"manual_review_reason\": null,\n      \"chapter_specific\": [\n        {\n          \"field\": \"trajectory\",\n          \"value\": \"The trajectory was clearly upward: recovery, fiscal outperformance, and lower unemployment outweighed the inflation shock.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"field\": \"external_conditions\",\n          \"value\": \"Commodity prices and reopening helped, but the government still had to manage the fuel shock and inflation risk.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"field\": \"distribution_and_household_effects\",\n          \"value\": \"Household relief was real through transfers and social spending, though distributional improvement was only modest.\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"dossier_job_key\": \"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:IND:19645\",\n      \"iso3\": \"IND\",\n      \"ruler_id\": \"1517\",\n      \"ruler_year_id\": 19645,\n      \"ruler_name\": \"Narendra Modi\",\n      \"period_start_year\": 2022,\n      \"period_end_year\": 2022,\n      \"chapter_id\": \"5B\",\n      \"rubric_version\": \"chapter_5b_v3\",\n      \"calibration_batch_id\": \"chapter-judge:2022-top20-hybrid-v2-judges-v1:2022:5B\",\n      \"calibrated_against\": [\n        \"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:RUS:15706\",\n        \"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:DEU:16984\",\n        \"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:VNM:19647\"\n      ],\n      \"score_1_to_10\": 6.5,\n      \"insufficient_evidence_reason\": null,\n      \"confidence_score\": 0.74,\n      \"plausible_score_range\": {\n        \"lower\": 6.0,\n        \"upper\": 7.0\n      },\n      \"decisive_positive_evidence\": [\n        {\n          \"evidence_id\": \"E0056\",\n          \"explanation\": \"The IMF praised India's digital public infrastructure and rapid support delivery.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"evidence_id\": \"E0058\",\n          \"explanation\": \"The Union Budget raised capital expenditure substantially.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"evidence_id\": \"E0065\",\n          \"explanation\": \"GST compensation and fiscal support to states improved federal fiscal management.\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"decisive_negative_evidence\": [\n        {\n          \"evidence_id\": \"E0053\",\n          \"explanation\": \"The IMF still flagged labor-market weaknesses and informality.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"evidence_id\": \"E0058\",\n          \"explanation\": \"A 6.4 percent fiscal deficit is substantial even in a growth year.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"evidence_id\": \"E0067\",\n          \"explanation\": \"The budget and policy mix still left major distributional issues unresolved.\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"inherited_baseline_and_constraints\": \"India entered 2022 with recovery momentum, inflation pressure, and large structural gaps in jobs, informality, and public-service delivery. That made the year a test of whether growth could be translated into broader opportunity.\",\n      \"ruler_attribution\": \"Attribution is strong for budget priorities, macro direction, and digital-public-infrastructure leadership, but weaker for wage formation and labor outcomes that depend on many actors.\",\n      \"supported_lenses\": [\n        \"5B.1\",\n        \"5B.2\",\n        \"5B.3\",\n        \"5B.4\",\n        \"5B.6\",\n        \"5B.8\",\n        \"5B.9\",\n        \"5B.10\"\n      ],\n      \"missing_or_weak_lenses\": [\n        \"5B.5\",\n        \"5B.7\"\n      ],\n      \"contrary_evidence\": [\n        {\n          \"evidence_id\": \"E0053\",\n          \"explanation\": \"Labor-market and inclusion gaps were still material.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"evidence_id\": \"E0067\",\n          \"explanation\": \"Distributional issues and large deficits limited the case for a higher score.\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"source_mix\": \"IMF and World Bank surveillance, PRS budget analysis, and official ministry releases; no structured local priors were collected in this experiment.\",\n      \"structured_prior_summary\": \"Structured local priors were unavailable across all lenses; the judgment rests on the dossier evidence and source metadata only.\",\n      \"chapter_rationale\": \"Modi scores 6.5 because the dossier shows real, ruler-backed economic architecture: digital public infrastructure, capital spending, tax and investment reforms, and fiscal support to states all point to active stewardship. The score is held below the top band because labor-market quality, informality, and distributional weaknesses remained stubborn, and the fiscal stance was still loose enough to raise concern. This is competent, broad, and mostly forward-looking policy, but not a full prosperity breakthrough.\",\n      \"lower_anchor_rejected\": \"A score near 6 would understate the scale of the digital and fiscal policy architecture the government put in place.\",\n      \"higher_anchor_rejected\": \"A score near 7.5 would overstate household-level convergence, because jobs and distribution remained weak.\",\n      \"manual_review_required\": false,\n      \"manual_review_reason_type\": null,\n      \"manual_review_reason\": null,\n      \"chapter_specific\": [\n        {\n          \"field\": \"trajectory\",\n          \"value\": \"The trajectory was positive in macro and infrastructure terms, but the labor market and distribution remained the main drag.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"field\": \"external_conditions\",\n          \"value\": \"Post-pandemic recovery and inflation shocks shaped the year, but the policy response was still broadly active and coherent.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"field\": \"distribution_and_household_effects\",\n          \"value\": \"Digital support and budget allocations helped, yet the dossier still shows unresolved informality, unemployment, and inequality.\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"dossier_job_key\": \"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:IRN:19648\",\n      \"iso3\": \"IRN\",\n      \"ruler_id\": \"3412\",\n      \"ruler_year_id\": 19648,\n      \"ruler_name\": \"Ali Khamenei\",\n      \"period_start_year\": 2022,\n      \"period_end_year\": 2022,\n      \"chapter_id\": \"5B\",\n      \"rubric_version\": \"chapter_5b_v3\",\n      \"calibration_batch_id\": \"chapter-judge:2022-top20-hybrid-v2-judges-v1:2022:5B\",\n      \"calibrated_against\": [\n        \"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:RUS:15706\",\n        \"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:DEU:16984\",\n        \"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:TUR:15972\"\n      ],\n      \"score_1_to_10\": 2.5,\n      \"insufficient_evidence_reason\": null,\n      \"confidence_score\": 0.72,\n      \"plausible_score_range\": {\n        \"lower\": 2.0,\n        \"upper\": 3.0\n      },\n      \"decisive_positive_evidence\": [\n        {\n          \"evidence_id\": \"E0060\",\n          \"explanation\": \"The development-plan guidelines still articulated a growth-and-stability framework.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"evidence_id\": \"E0050\",\n          \"explanation\": \"There was some gradual macro recovery despite sanctions.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"evidence_id\": \"E0051\",\n          \"explanation\": \"Higher oil and tax revenues helped the fiscal picture somewhat.\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"decisive_negative_evidence\": [\n        {\n          \"evidence_id\": \"E0054\",\n          \"explanation\": \"Ordinary households faced a severe cost-of-living squeeze.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"evidence_id\": \"E0057\",\n          \"explanation\": \"The rial's record lows show regime-level economic instability.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"evidence_id\": \"E0053\",\n          \"explanation\": \"The IMF identified fiscal deficits, currency depreciation, and sanctions as major inflation drivers.\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"inherited_baseline_and_constraints\": \"Iran's 2022 economy was heavily constrained by sanctions, inflation, currency weakness, and low household purchasing power. Those constraints are real, but the chapter still asks whether the supreme-leader-centered system responded with competent, broadly beneficial policy.\",\n      \"ruler_attribution\": \"Attribution is partial and mostly system-level: Khamenei set the strategic frame and retained supreme command, but the dossier is thin on direct 2022 execution choices tied personally to him.\",\n      \"supported_lenses\": [\n        \"5B.2\",\n        \"5B.3\",\n        \"5B.6\",\n        \"5B.9\",\n        \"5B.10\"\n      ],\n      \"missing_or_weak_lenses\": [\n        \"5B.1\",\n        \"5B.4\",\n        \"5B.5\",\n        \"5B.7\",\n        \"5B.8\"\n      ],\n      \"contrary_evidence\": [\n        {\n          \"evidence_id\": \"E0054\",\n          \"explanation\": \"The cost-of-living squeeze was severe.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"evidence_id\": \"E0057\",\n          \"explanation\": \"The currency collapse was a major prosperity hit.\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"source_mix\": \"Constitutional text, IMF and World Bank surveillance, Reuters-based reporting, and a secondary reproduction of leadership guidelines; no structured local priors were collected in this experiment.\",\n      \"structured_prior_summary\": \"Structured local priors were unavailable across all lenses; the judgment relies on the dossier evidence and coverage map only.\",\n      \"chapter_rationale\": \"Khamenei scores 2.5 because the record shows a system stuck in sanctions-driven inflation, currency collapse, and falling living standards, with only limited signs of effective correction. The positive evidence is mostly about strategic framing and partial macro recovery, while the negative evidence is direct and concrete on household distress and currency instability. This is a weak prosperity record with little defensible basis for a higher score.\",\n      \"lower_anchor_rejected\": \"A score of 1 would overstate the case because the dossier still shows some recovery, oil revenue improvement, and policy planning.\",\n      \"higher_anchor_rejected\": \"A score near 3.5 would overstate the limited and mostly indirect evidence of durable correction.\",\n      \"manual_review_required\": false,\n      \"manual_review_reason_type\": null,\n      \"manual_review_reason\": null,\n      \"chapter_specific\": [\n        {\n          \"field\": \"trajectory\",\n          \"value\": \"The economy remained stuck in a low-prosperity, high-instability pattern with only partial stabilization.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"field\": \"external_conditions\",\n          \"value\": \"Sanctions and currency pressure were central constraints, but they do not fully explain the absence of stronger corrective policy.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"field\": \"distribution_and_household_effects\",\n          \"value\": \"Household welfare was badly eroded, and the dossier gives little reason to think gains were shared broadly.\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"dossier_job_key\": \"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:JPN:16638\",\n      \"iso3\": \"JPN\",\n      \"ruler_id\": \"2895\",\n      \"ruler_year_id\": 16638,\n      \"ruler_name\": \"Fumio Kishida\",\n      \"period_start_year\": 2022,\n      \"period_end_year\": 2022,\n      \"chapter_id\": \"5B\",\n      \"rubric_version\": \"chapter_5b_v3\",\n      \"calibration_batch_id\": \"chapter-judge:2022-top20-hybrid-v2-judges-v1:2022:5B\",\n      \"calibrated_against\": [\n        \"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:RUS:15706\",\n        \"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:DEU:16984\",\n        \"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:VNM:19647\"\n      ],\n      \"score_1_to_10\": 5.5,\n      \"insufficient_evidence_reason\": null,\n      \"confidence_score\": 0.75,\n      \"plausible_score_range\": {\n        \"lower\": 5.0,\n        \"upper\": 6.0\n      },\n      \"decisive_positive_evidence\": [\n        {\n          \"evidence_id\": \"E0061\",\n          \"explanation\": \"The large 2022 package was a real, ruler-led stabilization and household-relief intervention.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"evidence_id\": \"E0062\",\n          \"explanation\": \"Year-end household assistance and child-support measures were concrete and broad.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"evidence_id\": \"E0056\",\n          \"explanation\": \"The new capitalism agenda and wage orientation gave the year a clear distributional direction.\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"decisive_negative_evidence\": [\n        {\n          \"evidence_id\": \"E0067\",\n          \"explanation\": \"Real wages fell in 2022 despite the policy push.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"evidence_id\": \"E0059\",\n          \"explanation\": \"Wage gains were too small to offset inflation meaningfully.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"evidence_id\": \"E0064\",\n          \"explanation\": \"Imported-cost inflation and currency weakness still defined the year.\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"inherited_baseline_and_constraints\": \"Japan entered 2022 with pandemic after-effects, imported inflation, and a weak yen, while still enjoying strong institutions and policy capacity. The question is whether Kishida turned that capacity into real household gains fast enough.\",\n      \"ruler_attribution\": \"Attribution is moderate to strong for the policy package and wage agenda, but weaker for actual wage outcomes, which depended on firms, the BOJ, and global prices.\",\n      \"supported_lenses\": [\n        \"5B.1\",\n        \"5B.3\",\n        \"5B.4\",\n        \"5B.6\",\n        \"5B.8\",\n        \"5B.9\",\n        \"5B.10\"\n      ],\n      \"missing_or_weak_lenses\": [\n        \"5B.2\",\n        \"5B.5\",\n        \"5B.7\"\n      ],\n      \"contrary_evidence\": [\n        {\n          \"evidence_id\": \"E0067\",\n          \"explanation\": \"Real wages fell, which is a direct drag on household prosperity.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"evidence_id\": \"E0059\",\n          \"explanation\": \"The wage response lagged the price shock.\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"source_mix\": \"Prime Minister's Office releases, IMF and Reuters reporting, and labor-statistics releases; no structured local priors were collected in this experiment.\",\n      \"structured_prior_summary\": \"Structured local priors were unavailable across all lenses; the judgment depends on the dossier evidence and the chapter projection only.\",\n      \"chapter_rationale\": \"Kishida scores 5.5 because the 2022 record contains a serious effort to redistribute income and support households, but the outcome remained limited by falling real wages and imported inflation. The government clearly acted, and it did so with coherent budgets and relief packages, yet the strongest household metric in the dossier is still negative. That makes this a mixed but not weak performance: better than mere crisis drift, short of a clear prosperity success.\",\n      \"lower_anchor_rejected\": \"A score near 4.5 would underrate the scale and coherence of the relief and wage-oriented policy package.\",\n      \"higher_anchor_rejected\": \"A score near 6.5 would overstate realized wage and household gains, which the dossier does not show.\",\n      \"manual_review_required\": false,\n      \"manual_review_reason_type\": null,\n      \"manual_review_reason\": null,\n      \"chapter_specific\": [\n        {\n          \"field\": \"trajectory\",\n          \"value\": \"Policy intent pointed upward, but the realized trajectory was held back by inflation and weak wage pass-through.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"field\": \"external_conditions\",\n          \"value\": \"Imported inflation, the weak yen, and global commodity shocks were major constraints.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"field\": \"distribution_and_household_effects\",\n          \"value\": \"Relief and child support helped, but real household purchasing power still fell over the year.\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"dossier_job_key\": \"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:MEX:15801\",\n      \"iso3\": \"MEX\",\n      \"ruler_id\": \"2779\",\n      \"ruler_year_id\": 15801,\n      \"ruler_name\": \"Andr\\u0000e9s Manuel L\\u0000f3pez Obrador\",\n      \"period_start_year\": 2022,\n      \"period_end_year\": 2022,\n      \"chapter_id\": \"5B\",\n      \"rubric_version\": \"chapter_5b_v3\",\n      \"calibration_batch_id\": \"chapter-judge:2022-top20-hybrid-v2-judges-v1:2022:5B\",\n      \"calibrated_against\": [\n        \"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:RUS:15706\",\n        \"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:DEU:16984\",\n        \"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:VNM:19647\"\n      ],\n      \"score_1_to_10\": 5.5,\n      \"insufficient_evidence_reason\": null,\n      \"confidence_score\": 0.72,\n      \"plausible_score_range\": {\n        \"lower\": 5.0,\n        \"upper\": 6.0\n      },\n      \"decisive_positive_evidence\": [\n        {\n          \"evidence_id\": \"E0057\",\n          \"explanation\": \"Official poverty data show a substantial decline by 2022.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"evidence_id\": \"E0050\",\n          \"explanation\": \"Anti-inflation subsidies cushioned households against price pressure.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"evidence_id\": \"E0048\",\n          \"explanation\": \"The World Bank supported inclusive-growth reforms and social protection priorities.\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"decisive_negative_evidence\": [\n        {\n          \"evidence_id\": \"E0051\",\n          \"explanation\": \"The electricity-overhaul defeat exposed investor uncertainty around AMLO's energy agenda.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"evidence_id\": \"E0052\",\n          \"explanation\": \"Energy politics risked missing the semiconductor investment wave.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"evidence_id\": \"E0054\",\n          \"explanation\": \"Foreign-bribery enforcement remained weak and underdeveloped.\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"inherited_baseline_and_constraints\": \"Mexico in 2022 had a resilient macro framework, but weak long-run investment, energy-policy uncertainty, and ongoing poverty and health challenges. The main question is whether AMLO's policies translated into broad household improvement without damaging investment conditions.\",\n      \"ruler_attribution\": \"Attribution is mixed: the poverty decline and labor outcomes support AMLO-era relevance, but the investment and energy weaknesses are also partly inherited and institutional.\",\n      \"supported_lenses\": [\n        \"5B.1\",\n        \"5B.3\",\n        \"5B.4\",\n        \"5B.6\",\n        \"5B.8\",\n        \"5B.9\",\n        \"5B.10\"\n      ],\n      \"missing_or_weak_lenses\": [\n        \"5B.2\",\n        \"5B.5\",\n        \"5B.7\"\n      ],\n      \"contrary_evidence\": [\n        {\n          \"evidence_id\": \"E0051\",\n          \"explanation\": \"Policy uncertainty around electricity reform hurt investor confidence.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"evidence_id\": \"E0052\",\n          \"explanation\": \"Energy policy risked leaving Mexico behind in new investment opportunities.\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"source_mix\": \"OECD, World Bank, Reuters, official budget releases, and independent poverty analysis; no structured local priors were collected in this experiment.\",\n      \"structured_prior_summary\": \"Structured local priors were unavailable across all lenses; the judgment depends on the dossier evidence and source-confidence metadata only.\",\n      \"chapter_rationale\": \"AMLO scores 5.5 because Mexico showed real household progress in 2022, especially on poverty, while the government also used subsidies and fiscal management to cushion inflation. The ceiling is lower than a 7 because the energy and investment story is still troubling: policy uncertainty, weak enforcement, and concern about missing new industrial opportunities all remained visible. This is a mixed prosperity record with real social gains but persistent structural and investor-confidence weaknesses.\",\n      \"lower_anchor_rejected\": \"A score near 4.5 would understate the poverty reduction and household cushioning documented in the dossier.\",\n      \"higher_anchor_rejected\": \"A score near 6.5 would overstate the quality of the investment climate and the durability of the gains.\",\n      \"manual_review_required\": false,\n      \"manual_review_reason_type\": null,\n      \"manual_review_reason\": null,\n      \"chapter_specific\": [\n        {\n          \"field\": \"trajectory\",\n          \"value\": \"Household welfare improved on poverty metrics, but the investment trajectory remained too uncertain for a high score.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"field\": \"external_conditions\",\n          \"value\": \"Inflation and post-pandemic conditions mattered, but the energy-policy environment was also a meaningful self-inflicted constraint.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"field\": \"distribution_and_household_effects\",\n          \"value\": \"The poverty decline is the main positive; health access and long-run opportunity still lagged behind headline improvement.\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"dossier_job_key\": \"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:NGA:15787\",\n      \"iso3\": \"NGA\",\n      \"ruler_id\": \"2776\",\n      \"ruler_year_id\": 15787,\n      \"ruler_name\": \"Muhammadu Buhari\",\n      \"period_start_year\": 2022,\n      \"period_end_year\": 2022,\n      \"chapter_id\": \"5B\",\n      \"rubric_version\": \"chapter_5b_v3\",\n      \"calibration_batch_id\": \"chapter-judge:2022-top20-hybrid-v2-judges-v1:2022:5B\",\n      \"calibrated_against\": [\n        \"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:RUS:15706\",\n        \"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:DEU:16984\",\n        \"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:TUR:15972\"\n      ],\n      \"score_1_to_10\": 2.5,\n      \"insufficient_evidence_reason\": null,\n      \"confidence_score\": 0.76,\n      \"plausible_score_range\": {\n        \"lower\": 2.0,\n        \"upper\": 3.0\n      },\n      \"decisive_positive_evidence\": [\n        {\n          \"evidence_id\": \"E0058\",\n          \"explanation\": \"The health-insurance law was a concrete pro-poor policy move.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"evidence_id\": \"E0057\",\n          \"explanation\": \"Anti-money-laundering and proceeds-of-crime laws strengthened the legal framework.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"evidence_id\": \"E0060\",\n          \"explanation\": \"A technocratic statistics appointment modestly improved state capacity.\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"decisive_negative_evidence\": [\n        {\n          \"evidence_id\": \"E0050\",\n          \"explanation\": \"Inflation, poverty, and subsidy burdens remained severe.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"evidence_id\": \"E0048\",\n          \"explanation\": \"Regressive fuel and FX subsidies crowded out pro-poor spending.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"evidence_id\": \"E0051\",\n          \"explanation\": \"The IMF said the oil-price opportunity was not harnessed and governance fixes were still needed.\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"inherited_baseline_and_constraints\": \"Nigeria entered 2022 with subsidy distortions, low revenue, inflation pressure, and a weak external position. Those inherited problems were severe, but the score reflects whether the presidency managed them competently and fairly.\",\n      \"ruler_attribution\": \"Attribution is moderate: Buhari clearly set fiscal, legal, and appointment choices, but much of the crisis was inherited and some key levers were constrained by oil theft, subsidies, and exchange-rate rigidity.\",\n      \"supported_lenses\": [\n        \"5B.2\",\n        \"5B.3\",\n        \"5B.4\",\n        \"5B.6\",\n        \"5B.7\",\n        \"5B.9\",\n        \"5B.10\"\n      ],\n      \"missing_or_weak_lenses\": [\n        \"5B.1\",\n        \"5B.5\",\n        \"5B.8\"\n      ],\n      \"contrary_evidence\": [\n        {\n          \"evidence_id\": \"E0050\",\n          \"explanation\": \"The macro and welfare situation was plainly deteriorating.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"evidence_id\": \"E0048\",\n          \"explanation\": \"Subsidies and low revenue were a structural drag on development.\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"source_mix\": \"World Bank and IMF surveillance, official government acts, central-bank policy records, and Reuters-based reporting; no structured local priors were collected in this experiment.\",\n      \"structured_prior_summary\": \"Structured local priors were unavailable across all lenses; the judgment relies on the dossier evidence and the source-confidence metadata only.\",\n      \"chapter_rationale\": \"Buhari scores 2.5 because the year was still dominated by subsidy distortions, high inflation, poverty pressure, and poor use of fiscal room. There were some genuine reforms, including better legal tools and a modest technocratic appointment, but they were too small to offset the broad economic drag or to show durable correction. The evidence points to a weak, crisis-ridden prosperity record with only limited institutional positives.\",\n      \"lower_anchor_rejected\": \"A score near 1 would ignore the real though limited legal and institutional reforms in the dossier.\",\n      \"higher_anchor_rejected\": \"A score near 3.5 would overstate the strength of the pro-poor and macro-stabilization record relative to the scale of the crisis.\",\n      \"manual_review_required\": false,\n      \"manual_review_reason_type\": null,\n      \"manual_review_reason\": null,\n      \"chapter_specific\": [\n        {\n          \"field\": \"trajectory\",\n          \"value\": \"The trajectory was downward or stagnant overall, with reforms too small to reverse the macro drag.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"field\": \"external_conditions\",\n          \"value\": \"Oil-price and exchange-rate pressures mattered, but the subsidy structure and policy mix were also self-inflicted constraints.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"field\": \"distribution_and_household_effects\",\n          \"value\": \"Household welfare was squeezed by inflation and subsidy distortion; the pro-poor legal moves did not materially change that picture in 2022.\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"dossier_job_key\": \"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:PAK:16682\",\n      \"iso3\": \"PAK\",\n      \"ruler_id\": \"2911\",\n      \"ruler_year_id\": 16682,\n      \"ruler_name\": \"Shehbaz Sharif\",\n      \"period_start_year\": 2022,\n      \"period_end_year\": 2022,\n      \"chapter_id\": \"5B\",\n      \"rubric_version\": \"chapter_5b_v3\",\n      \"calibration_batch_id\": \"chapter-judge:2022-top20-hybrid-v2-judges-v1:2022:5B\",\n      \"calibrated_against\": [\n        \"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:RUS:15706\",\n        \"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:DEU:16984\",\n        \"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:TUR:15972\"\n      ],\n      \"score_1_to_10\": 3.5,\n      \"insufficient_evidence_reason\": null,\n      \"confidence_score\": 0.70,\n      \"plausible_score_range\": {\n        \"lower\": 3.0,\n        \"upper\": 4.0\n      },\n      \"decisive_positive_evidence\": [\n        {\n          \"evidence_id\": \"E0053\",\n          \"explanation\": \"Targeted subsidy relief was directed at lower-income households.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"evidence_id\": \"E0058\",\n          \"explanation\": \"The IMF program aimed at a primary surplus and a more sustainable fiscal path.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"evidence_id\": \"E0060\",\n          \"explanation\": \"A career central banker was appointed to the State Bank, which supported stabilization.\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"decisive_negative_evidence\": [\n        {\n          \"evidence_id\": \"E0062\",\n          \"explanation\": \"The economy was in a balance-of-payments crisis with severe inflation and reserve pressure.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"evidence_id\": \"E0067\",\n          \"explanation\": \"Inflation was still near crisis levels at year end.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"evidence_id\": \"E0050\",\n          \"explanation\": \"Sharif inherited an economic spiral that his first months did not yet reverse.\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"inherited_baseline_and_constraints\": \"Pakistan in 2022 was already in a serious balance-of-payments and inflation crisis when Sharif took office. The chapter therefore rewards stabilization work only if it is visible and credible against that inherited emergency.\",\n      \"ruler_attribution\": \"Attribution is moderate: Sharif clearly made personnel, fiscal, and subsidy choices, but the crisis itself was inherited and IMF conditionality constrained his room for maneuver.\",\n      \"supported_lenses\": [\n        \"5B.1\",\n        \"5B.2\",\n        \"5B.3\",\n        \"5B.4\",\n        \"5B.6\",\n        \"5B.9\",\n        \"5B.10\"\n      ],\n      \"missing_or_weak_lenses\": [\n        \"5B.5\",\n        \"5B.7\",\n        \"5B.8\"\n      ],\n      \"contrary_evidence\": [\n        {\n          \"evidence_id\": \"E0062\",\n          \"explanation\": \"The macro crisis remained severe despite the policy pivot.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"evidence_id\": \"E0067\",\n          \"explanation\": \"Inflation stayed extremely high by year end.\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"source_mix\": \"Official finance-ministry releases, IMF program documents, Reuters reporting, and local newspaper coverage; no structured local priors were collected in this experiment.\",\n      \"structured_prior_summary\": \"Structured local priors were unavailable across all lenses; the judgment is based on the dossier evidence and source-confidence metadata only.\",\n      \"chapter_rationale\": \"Sharif scores 3.5 because the dossier shows genuine stabilization intent and some competent administrative moves, but the crisis was still overwhelming by year end. Targeted relief, IMF progress, and a technocratic central-bank appointment are real positives; however, high inflation, reserve stress, and a balance-of-payments crisis kept the prosperity picture weak. This is a constrained crisis-management record with limited success, not a broad economic turnaround.\",\n      \"lower_anchor_rejected\": \"A score near 2.5 would understate the seriousness of the stabilization effort and the policy adjustments actually made.\",\n      \"higher_anchor_rejected\": \"A score near 4.5 would overstate the degree to which the crisis had been brought under control by 2022.\",\n      \"manual_review_required\": false,\n      \"manual_review_reason_type\": null,\n      \"manual_review_reason\": null,\n      \"chapter_specific\": [\n        {\n          \"field\": \"trajectory\",\n          \"value\": \"The trajectory was one of partial stabilization from a very weak starting point, not a clean recovery.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"field\": \"external_conditions\",\n          \"value\": \"Inherited macro collapse, IMF conditionality, and external price shocks severely limited the government's room to improve outcomes quickly.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"field\": \"distribution_and_household_effects\",\n          \"value\": \"Relief was targeted, but household purchasing power remained badly strained and broad welfare gains were not yet visible.\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"dossier_job_key\": \"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:PHL:16194\",\n      \"iso3\": \"PHL\",\n      \"ruler_id\": \"2844\",\n      \"ruler_year_id\": 16194,\n      \"ruler_name\": \"Bongbong Marcos\",\n      \"period_start_year\": 2022,\n      \"period_end_year\": 2022,\n      \"chapter_id\": \"5B\",\n      \"rubric_version\": \"chapter_5b_v3\",\n      \"calibration_batch_id\": \"chapter-judge:2022-top20-hybrid-v2-judges-v1:2022:5B\",\n      \"calibrated_against\": [\n        \"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:RUS:15706\",\n        \"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:DEU:16984\",\n        \"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:VNM:19647\"\n      ],\n      \"score_1_to_10\": 5.0,\n      \"insufficient_evidence_reason\": null,\n      \"confidence_score\": 0.72,\n      \"plausible_score_range\": {\n        \"lower\": 4.5,\n        \"upper\": 5.5\n      },\n      \"decisive_positive_evidence\": [\n        {\n          \"evidence_id\": \"E0049\",\n          \"explanation\": \"Marcos set a fiscal-management and tax-reform agenda early in office.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"evidence_id\": \"E0057\",\n          \"explanation\": \"The debt-to-GDP ratio fell below target, helping fiscal credibility.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"evidence_id\": \"E0060\",\n          \"explanation\": \"Kadiwa stores reached many households with lower-priced food.\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"decisive_negative_evidence\": [\n        {\n          \"evidence_id\": \"E0055\",\n          \"explanation\": \"Inflation was still high and household prices were under pressure.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"evidence_id\": \"E0068\",\n          \"explanation\": \"Real median income and poverty measures deteriorated for important groups.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"evidence_id\": \"E0056\",\n          \"explanation\": \"Unemployment remained meaningful and uneven across regions.\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"inherited_baseline_and_constraints\": \"The Philippines entered 2022 with post-pandemic recovery, inflation pressure, and uneven labor-market healing. The key issue is whether the new administration translated the rebound into household gains fast enough to count as a prosperity success.\",\n      \"ruler_attribution\": \"Attribution is moderate: Marcos clearly set budget and food-policy direction, but the macro outcome also reflected reopening, exchange-rate conditions, and post-pandemic normalization.\",\n      \"supported_lenses\": [\n        \"5B.1\",\n        \"5B.2\",\n        \"5B.3\",\n        \"5B.4\",\n        \"5B.6\",\n        \"5B.8\",\n        \"5B.9\",\n        \"5B.10\"\n      ],\n      \"missing_or_weak_lenses\": [\n        \"5B.5\",\n        \"5B.7\"\n      ],\n      \"contrary_evidence\": [\n        {\n          \"evidence_id\": \"E0055\",\n          \"explanation\": \"Inflation and real-wage pressure were still substantial.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"evidence_id\": \"E0068\",\n          \"explanation\": \"Household income and poverty outcomes were mixed to negative in the retrospective data.\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"source_mix\": \"Official presidential speeches, finance and statistics releases, IMF and other multilateral analysis, and official program reporting; no structured local priors were collected in this experiment.\",\n      \"structured_prior_summary\": \"Structured local priors were unavailable across all lenses; the judgment relies on the dossier evidence and source-confidence metadata only.\",\n      \"chapter_rationale\": \"Marcos scores 5.0 because the dossier shows a new administration that quickly set up a fiscal, food, and infrastructure agenda and kept macro indicators from worsening further. The score is capped by inflation, falling real incomes, and mixed poverty outcomes, which show that the year was still about stabilization rather than broad prosperity. This is a middling record with some credible policy design, but not enough lived improvement to push into the next band.\",\n      \"lower_anchor_rejected\": \"A score near 4 would underrate the fiscal and food-access measures the administration actually implemented.\",\n      \"higher_anchor_rejected\": \"A score near 6 would overstate household gains, which the income and poverty data do not support.\",\n      \"manual_review_required\": false,\n      \"manual_review_reason_type\": null,\n      \"manual_review_reason\": null,\n      \"chapter_specific\": [\n        {\n          \"field\": \"trajectory\",\n          \"value\": \"The trajectory was stabilization-first: macro management improved, but household welfare had not fully caught up by year end.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"field\": \"external_conditions\",\n          \"value\": \"Inflation, reopening dynamics, and post-pandemic normalization all shaped the year, so attribution must stay modest.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"field\": \"distribution_and_household_effects\",\n          \"value\": \"Food-access efforts helped, but the retrospective data still show uneven and sometimes negative household outcomes.\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"dossier_job_key\": \"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:RUS:15706\",\n      \"iso3\": \"RUS\",\n      \"ruler_id\": \"2759\",\n      \"ruler_year_id\": 15706,\n      \"ruler_name\": \"Vladimir Putin\",\n      \"period_start_year\": 2022,\n      \"period_end_year\": 2022,\n      \"chapter_id\": \"5B\",\n      \"rubric_version\": \"chapter_5b_v3\",\n      \"calibration_batch_id\": \"chapter-judge:2022-top20-hybrid-v2-judges-v1:2022:5B\",\n      \"calibrated_against\": [\n        \"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:DEU:16984\",\n        \"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:TUR:15972\",\n        \"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:VNM:19647\"\n      ],\n      \"score_1_to_10\": 1.5,\n      \"insufficient_evidence_reason\": null,\n      \"confidence_score\": 0.80,\n      \"plausible_score_range\": {\n        \"lower\": 1.0,\n        \"upper\": 2.0\n      },\n      \"decisive_positive_evidence\": [\n        {\n          \"evidence_id\": \"E0058\",\n          \"explanation\": \"The central bank still showed some capacity to stabilize markets under stress.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"evidence_id\": \"E0061\",\n          \"explanation\": \"Rate cuts later in 2022 reflected partial stabilization after the shock.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"evidence_id\": \"E0062\",\n          \"explanation\": \"The central bank claimed its emergency measures prevented a worse spiral.\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"decisive_negative_evidence\": [\n        {\n          \"evidence_id\": \"E0065\",\n          \"explanation\": \"The gas rouble-payment decree intensified coercive economic pressure and sanctions conflict.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"evidence_id\": \"E0066\",\n          \"explanation\": \"Defense spending surged and the budget shifted sharply into deficit.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"evidence_id\": \"E0072\",\n          \"explanation\": \"The economy contracted in 2022 because of the invasion and sanctions shock.\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"inherited_baseline_and_constraints\": \"Russia entered 2022 with a relatively strong pre-war macro position, but Putin's invasion created the central constraint: sanctions, war spending, and coercive economic policy rapidly replaced ordinary prosperity management.\",\n      \"ruler_attribution\": \"Attribution is extremely strong for the main negatives because they follow directly from Putin's war and coercive choices; the positives are mostly crisis containment by technocratic institutions he retained.\",\n      \"supported_lenses\": [\n        \"5B.2\",\n        \"5B.3\",\n        \"5B.6\",\n        \"5B.9\",\n        \"5B.10\"\n      ],\n      \"missing_or_weak_lenses\": [\n        \"5B.1\",\n        \"5B.4\",\n        \"5B.5\",\n        \"5B.7\",\n        \"5B.8\"\n      ],\n      \"contrary_evidence\": [\n        {\n          \"evidence_id\": \"E0065\",\n          \"explanation\": \"There was some macro stabilization and institutional resilience, so the score is not a flat zero.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"evidence_id\": \"E0062\",\n          \"explanation\": \"The central bank says emergency measures prevented an even worse financial collapse.\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"source_mix\": \"Reuters-based reporting, Bank of Russia releases, and official fiscal data; no structured local priors were collected in this experiment.\",\n      \"structured_prior_summary\": \"Structured local priors were unavailable across all lenses; the judgment relies on the dossier evidence and source-confidence metadata only.\",\n      \"chapter_rationale\": \"Putin scores 1.5 because the 2022 record is defined by a war of choice that destroyed broad prosperity, cut household demand and incomes, and forced the economy into coercive, militarized adjustment. The only meaningful positives are technocratic crisis containment and partial stabilization, but those do not outweigh the direct negative effects of invasion, sanctions, inflation, and war spending. This is far below a normal mixed record: it is a severe prosperity destruction case, just short of the realized-catastrophe floor reserved for the most extreme outcomes.\",\n      \"lower_anchor_rejected\": \"A score of 1 would reserve the absolute floor for a realized nuclear or equivalent catastrophe; this file, while devastating, is an economic-war destruction case rather than that floor.\",\n      \"higher_anchor_rejected\": \"A score near 3 would ignore the direct contraction, inflation, household-income loss, and militarized fiscal shift documented here.\",\n      \"manual_review_required\": false,\n      \"manual_review_reason_type\": null,\n      \"manual_review_reason\": null,\n      \"chapter_specific\": [\n        {\n          \"field\": \"trajectory\",\n          \"value\": \"The trajectory collapsed from pre-war stability into war economy, contraction, and coercive adaptation.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"field\": \"external_conditions\",\n          \"value\": \"Sanctions mattered, but the central external condition was Putin's own invasion decision, which triggered the collapse.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"field\": \"distribution_and_household_effects\",\n          \"value\": \"Household demand and real incomes fell, and the prosperity burden was broad rather than confined to elites.\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"dossier_job_key\": \"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:THA:19649\",\n      \"iso3\": \"THA\",\n      \"ruler_id\": \"3414\",\n      \"ruler_year_id\": 19649,\n      \"ruler_name\": \"Prayut Chan-o-cha\",\n      \"period_start_year\": 2022,\n      \"period_end_year\": 2022,\n      \"chapter_id\": \"5B\",\n      \"rubric_version\": \"chapter_5b_v3\",\n      \"calibration_batch_id\": \"chapter-judge:2022-top20-hybrid-v2-judges-v1:2022:5B\",\n      \"calibrated_against\": [\n        \"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:RUS:15706\",\n        \"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:DEU:16984\",\n        \"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:VNM:19647\"\n      ],\n      \"score_1_to_10\": 5.5,\n      \"insufficient_evidence_reason\": null,\n      \"confidence_score\": 0.70,\n      \"plausible_score_range\": {\n        \"lower\": 5.0,\n        \"upper\": 6.0\n      },\n      \"decisive_positive_evidence\": [\n        {\n          \"evidence_id\": \"E0055\",\n          \"explanation\": \"The economy recovered to pre-pandemic levels and government fiscal policy remained supportive.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"evidence_id\": \"E0064\",\n          \"explanation\": \"Tourism support and reopening helped the recovery and directly targeted household activity.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"evidence_id\": \"E0066\",\n          \"explanation\": \"Fiscal policy was deliberately refocused toward vulnerable groups as conditions normalized.\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"decisive_negative_evidence\": [\n        {\n          \"evidence_id\": \"E0056\",\n          \"explanation\": \"Poverty was projected to rise again as emergency relief faded.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"evidence_id\": \"E0057\",\n          \"explanation\": \"Rural poverty and lower incomes remained structurally severe.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"evidence_id\": \"E0068\",\n          \"explanation\": \"Investment pledges fell sharply, which weakens the longer-run prosperity case.\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"inherited_baseline_and_constraints\": \"Thailand entered 2022 with a reopening recovery, household debt, rural poverty, and tourism dependence. The year rewarded policymakers who could preserve the rebound without letting the social and investment side crack.\",\n      \"ruler_attribution\": \"Attribution is moderate: Prayut clearly presided over budget, tourism, and relief choices, but reopening and tourism normalization did much of the economic work.\",\n      \"supported_lenses\": [\n        \"5B.1\",\n        \"5B.3\",\n        \"5B.4\",\n        \"5B.6\",\n        \"5B.8\",\n        \"5B.9\",\n        \"5B.10\"\n      ],\n      \"missing_or_weak_lenses\": [\n        \"5B.2\",\n        \"5B.5\",\n        \"5B.7\"\n      ],\n      \"contrary_evidence\": [\n        {\n          \"evidence_id\": \"E0056\",\n          \"explanation\": \"Poverty was projected to rise again.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"evidence_id\": \"E0057\",\n          \"explanation\": \"Rural deprivation remained a major drag on broad-based prosperity.\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"source_mix\": \"World Bank and IMF surveillance, BOT releases, Reuters reporting, and official budget/tourism announcements; no structured local priors were collected in this experiment.\",\n      \"structured_prior_summary\": \"Structured local priors were unavailable across all lenses; the judgment rests on the dossier evidence and source-confidence metadata only.\",\n      \"chapter_rationale\": \"Prayut scores 5.5 because Thailand clearly recovered in macro terms and the government continued to use fiscal tools and targeted support to cushion households. The ceiling is limited because poverty was still projected to rise, rural deprivation remained strong, and investment interest weakened. This is a decent rebound-management record, but not yet a broad prosperity success story.\",\n      \"lower_anchor_rejected\": \"A score near 4.5 would ignore the recovery to pre-pandemic output and the active fiscal support to households.\",\n      \"higher_anchor_rejected\": \"A score near 6.5 would overstate the breadth of prosperity gains when poverty and investment signals were still weak.\",\n      \"manual_review_required\": false,\n      \"manual_review_reason_type\": null,\n      \"manual_review_reason\": null,\n      \"chapter_specific\": [\n        {\n          \"field\": \"trajectory\",\n          \"value\": \"The year was a partial recovery with better macro numbers, but the distributional and investment picture remained uneven.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"field\": \"external_conditions\",\n          \"value\": \"Tourism reopening and global conditions helped; those tailwinds reduce but do not erase the government's responsibility for the end-state.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"field\": \"distribution_and_household_effects\",\n          \"value\": \"Targeted support helped vulnerable groups, but rural poverty and household debt still limited broad gains.\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"dossier_job_key\": \"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:TUR:15972\",\n      \"iso3\": \"TUR\",\n      \"ruler_id\": \"2813\",\n      \"ruler_year_id\": 15972,\n      \"ruler_name\": \"Recep Tayyip Erdo\\u00011fan\",\n      \"period_start_year\": 2022,\n      \"period_end_year\": 2022,\n      \"chapter_id\": \"5B\",\n      \"rubric_version\": \"chapter_5b_v3\",\n      \"calibration_batch_id\": \"chapter-judge:2022-top20-hybrid-v2-judges-v1:2022:5B\",\n      \"calibrated_against\": [\n        \"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:RUS:15706\",\n        \"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:DEU:16984\",\n        \"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:VNM:19647\"\n      ],\n      \"score_1_to_10\": 2.0,\n      \"insufficient_evidence_reason\": null,\n      \"confidence_score\": 0.80,\n      \"plausible_score_range\": {\n        \"lower\": 1.5,\n        \"upper\": 2.5\n      },\n      \"decisive_positive_evidence\": [\n        {\n          \"evidence_id\": \"E0052\",\n          \"explanation\": \"The government tried to shield vulnerable groups from energy and food prices.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"evidence_id\": \"E0049\",\n          \"explanation\": \"Employment and tourism recovered in parts of the year.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"evidence_id\": \"E0050\",\n          \"explanation\": \"Real GDP still grew in the first half of 2022.\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"decisive_negative_evidence\": [\n        {\n          \"evidence_id\": \"E0054\",\n          \"explanation\": \"Inflation reached extreme levels under the low-rate policy model.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"evidence_id\": \"E0053\",\n          \"explanation\": \"The IMF said the policy-rate cuts worsened vulnerabilities and required early tightening.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"evidence_id\": \"E0057\",\n          \"explanation\": \"The low-rate bet exposed Turkey to war-driven and energy-price shocks.\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"inherited_baseline_and_constraints\": \"Turkey entered 2022 with a fragile currency, inflation pressure, and a policy model already at odds with orthodox stabilization. The main question is whether Erdogan's chosen path protected prosperity or damaged it further.\",\n      \"ruler_attribution\": \"Attribution is very strong for the low-rate policy, the appointment of the economic team, and the macro model that produced the inflation spiral.\",\n      \"supported_lenses\": [\n        \"5B.3\",\n        \"5B.6\",\n        \"5B.9\",\n        \"5B.10\"\n      ],\n      \"missing_or_weak_lenses\": [\n        \"5B.1\",\n        \"5B.2\",\n        \"5B.4\",\n        \"5B.5\",\n        \"5B.7\",\n        \"5B.8\"\n      ],\n      \"contrary_evidence\": [\n        {\n          \"evidence_id\": \"E0050\",\n          \"explanation\": \"There was still some growth and tourism recovery.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"evidence_id\": \"E0052\",\n          \"explanation\": \"Household relief existed, even if it was not enough to offset the macro damage.\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"source_mix\": \"World Bank, OECD, IMF, and Reuters-based reporting; no structured local priors were collected in this experiment.\",\n      \"structured_prior_summary\": \"Structured local priors were unavailable across all lenses; the judge relied on the embedded evidence and coverage map only.\",\n      \"chapter_rationale\": \"Erdogan scores 2.0 because the low-rate experiment produced extreme inflation, a collapsing currency, and clear macro instability that hurt household prosperity. The evidence for positives is mostly partial cushioning and growth that did not solve the core problem; the evidence for negatives is direct, repeated, and ruler-linked. This is a harmful economic record with some limited mitigation, but little sign of competent prosperity stewardship.\",\n      \"lower_anchor_rejected\": \"A score of 1 would be too low because the dossier still shows some growth, tourism recovery, and targeted relief.\",\n      \"higher_anchor_rejected\": \"A score near 3 would overstate the value of the mitigation measures relative to the scale of inflation and instability.\",\n      \"manual_review_required\": false,\n      \"manual_review_reason_type\": null,\n      \"manual_review_reason\": null,\n      \"chapter_specific\": [\n        {\n          \"field\": \"trajectory\",\n          \"value\": \"The trajectory deteriorated into high inflation and exchange-rate instability even as some activity recovered.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"field\": \"external_conditions\",\n          \"value\": \"War spillovers and commodity prices mattered, but the low-rate regime was the key self-inflicted amplifier.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"field\": \"distribution_and_household_effects\",\n          \"value\": \"Vulnerable households were partially shielded, but real incomes and purchasing power were still badly damaged.\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"dossier_job_key\": \"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:USA:15810\",\n      \"iso3\": \"USA\",\n      \"ruler_id\": \"2782\",\n      \"ruler_year_id\": 15810,\n      \"ruler_name\": \"Joe Biden\",\n      \"period_start_year\": 2022,\n      \"period_end_year\": 2022,\n      \"chapter_id\": \"5B\",\n      \"rubric_version\": \"chapter_5b_v3\",\n      \"calibration_batch_id\": \"chapter-judge:2022-top20-hybrid-v2-judges-v1:2022:5B\",\n      \"calibrated_against\": [\n        \"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:RUS:15706\",\n        \"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:DEU:16984\",\n        \"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:VNM:19647\"\n      ],\n      \"score_1_to_10\": 6.5,\n      \"insufficient_evidence_reason\": null,\n      \"confidence_score\": 0.75,\n      \"plausible_score_range\": {\n        \"lower\": 6.0,\n        \"upper\": 7.0\n      },\n      \"decisive_positive_evidence\": [\n        {\n          \"evidence_id\": \"E0057\",\n          \"explanation\": \"The fiscal-year deficit improved sharply and jobs were strong.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"evidence_id\": \"E0064\",\n          \"explanation\": \"The Inflation Reduction Act was a major enacted policy with explicit economic and health aims.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"evidence_id\": \"E0065\",\n          \"explanation\": \"CHIPS implementation was concrete industrial policy, not just rhetoric.\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"decisive_negative_evidence\": [\n        {\n          \"evidence_id\": \"E0059\",\n          \"explanation\": \"Inflation remained high at year end.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"evidence_id\": \"E0060\",\n          \"explanation\": \"Real earnings fell, reducing household purchasing power.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"evidence_id\": \"E0068\",\n          \"explanation\": \"Household income and poverty measures worsened for important groups.\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"inherited_baseline_and_constraints\": \"The U.S. entered 2022 with a strong labor rebound but also with inflation, supply-chain stress, and the fiscal hangover of pandemic support. The chapter needs to weigh policy design against those inherited macro conditions.\",\n      \"ruler_attribution\": \"Attribution is moderate: Biden clearly led the fiscal and industrial agenda, but inflation and real wages were also shaped by the Fed, global shocks, and the post-pandemic normalization.\",\n      \"supported_lenses\": [\n        \"5B.1\",\n        \"5B.3\",\n        \"5B.4\",\n        \"5B.6\",\n        \"5B.8\",\n        \"5B.9\",\n        \"5B.10\"\n      ],\n      \"missing_or_weak_lenses\": [\n        \"5B.2\",\n        \"5B.5\",\n        \"5B.7\"\n      ],\n      \"contrary_evidence\": [\n        {\n          \"evidence_id\": \"E0059\",\n          \"explanation\": \"Inflation still hurt households.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"evidence_id\": \"E0068\",\n          \"explanation\": \"Distributional outcomes were mixed and some groups lost ground.\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"source_mix\": \"Treasury, BLS, BEA, CBO, IMF, and executive-branch implementation releases; no structured local priors were collected in this experiment.\",\n      \"structured_prior_summary\": \"Structured local priors were unavailable across all lenses; the judgment uses the dossier evidence and source-confidence metadata only.\",\n      \"chapter_rationale\": \"Biden scores 6.5 because 2022 combined strong labor markets, a lower deficit, and real industrial-policy enactment with the clear drag of inflation and falling real earnings. The positive side is not just macro recovery but actual policy implementation: IRA, CHIPS, infrastructure, and fiscal results are all visible in the dossier. The score is held below the top band because household purchasing power still eroded and distribution was uneven, so the prosperity gains were real but incomplete.\",\n      \"lower_anchor_rejected\": \"A score near 6 would underrate the scale of enacted industrial policy and fiscal improvement.\",\n      \"higher_anchor_rejected\": \"A score near 7.5 would overstate household welfare because inflation and real earnings were still negative in 2022.\",\n      \"manual_review_required\": false,\n      \"manual_review_reason_type\": null,\n      \"manual_review_reason\": null,\n      \"chapter_specific\": [\n        {\n          \"field\": \"trajectory\",\n          \"value\": \"The U.S. trajectory was upward in jobs and policy capacity, but inflation kept the lived-prosperity story from being fully positive.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"field\": \"external_conditions\",\n          \"value\": \"The Fed, global supply shocks, and post-pandemic normalization mattered a lot; attribution to the White House should stay partial.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"field\": \"distribution_and_household_effects\",\n          \"value\": \"Household real earnings and some income measures fell, so the gains were broad in labor-market terms but not yet fully shared.\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"dossier_job_key\": \"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:VNM:19647\",\n      \"iso3\": \"VNM\",\n      \"ruler_id\": \"3411\",\n      \"ruler_year_id\": 19647,\n      \"ruler_name\": \"Nguy\\u001ec5n Ph\\u0000fa Tr\\u001ecdng\",\n      \"period_start_year\": 2022,\n      \"period_end_year\": 2022,\n      \"chapter_id\": \"5B\",\n      \"rubric_version\": \"chapter_5b_v3\",\n      \"calibration_batch_id\": \"chapter-judge:2022-top20-hybrid-v2-judges-v1:2022:5B\",\n      \"calibrated_against\": [\n        \"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:RUS:15706\",\n        \"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:DEU:16984\",\n        \"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:TUR:15972\"\n      ],\n      \"score_1_to_10\": 7.0,\n      \"insufficient_evidence_reason\": null,\n      \"confidence_score\": 0.77,\n      \"plausible_score_range\": {\n        \"lower\": 6.5,\n        \"upper\": 7.5\n      },\n      \"decisive_positive_evidence\": [\n        {\n          \"evidence_id\": \"E0048\",\n          \"explanation\": \"State investment and FDI inflows were strong in 2022.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"evidence_id\": \"E0047\",\n          \"explanation\": \"Inflation met the target and stayed relatively low.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"evidence_id\": \"E0052\",\n          \"explanation\": \"The year-end review claimed most development targets were met or surpassed.\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"decisive_negative_evidence\": [\n        {\n          \"evidence_id\": \"E0054\",\n          \"explanation\": \"The anti-corruption drive chilled transactions and investment.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"evidence_id\": \"E0046\",\n          \"explanation\": \"Skills shortages and weak tertiary education limited the productivity story.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"evidence_id\": \"E0045\",\n          \"explanation\": \"Poverty reduction and inequality remained a structural challenge.\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"inherited_baseline_and_constraints\": \"Vietnam entered 2022 with strong macro fundamentals, a successful export and FDI base, and a one-party system capable of rapid coordination. The limitation is that this same system can also create opaque controls and anti-graft side effects.\",\n      \"ruler_attribution\": \"Attribution is strong at the party-state level for growth, planning, and anti-corruption direction, but the dossier is less direct on Tr\\u001ecdng's personal execution than on the system he headed.\",\n      \"supported_lenses\": [\n        \"5B.1\",\n        \"5B.2\",\n        \"5B.3\",\n        \"5B.4\",\n        \"5B.6\",\n        \"5B.8\",\n        \"5B.9\",\n        \"5B.10\"\n      ],\n      \"missing_or_weak_lenses\": [\n        \"5B.5\",\n        \"5B.7\"\n      ],\n      \"contrary_evidence\": [\n        {\n          \"evidence_id\": \"E0054\",\n          \"explanation\": \"The anti-graft crackdown had real economic side effects.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"evidence_id\": \"E0045\",\n          \"explanation\": \"Poverty and inequality did not disappear.\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"source_mix\": \"Party-state texts, statistics releases, World Bank and IMF surveillance, and Reuters-based reporting; no structured local priors were collected in this experiment.\",\n      \"structured_prior_summary\": \"Structured local priors were unavailable across all lenses; the judgment rests on the dossier evidence and source metadata only.\",\n      \"chapter_rationale\": \"Tr\\u001ecdng scores 7.0 because Vietnam's 2022 record is one of the strongest in the batch on macro stability, investment, and delivery. The main negative is that the anti-corruption drive clearly had side effects on procurement and investment, and skills and poverty gaps remained, so the score is not higher. Still, the evidence supports a broad, resilient prosperity outcome with credible policy coordination and strong growth.\",\n      \"lower_anchor_rejected\": \"A score near 6 would understate the strength of the 2022 growth, inflation, and investment record.\",\n      \"higher_anchor_rejected\": \"A score near 8 would overstate equity and implementation quality, since the anti-graft campaign and skills gaps still hurt the broader picture.\",\n      \"manual_review_required\": false,\n      \"manual_review_reason_type\": null,\n      \"manual_review_reason\": null,\n      \"chapter_specific\": [\n        {\n          \"field\": \"trajectory\",\n          \"value\": \"The trajectory was strongly upward on macro growth and investment, but with some governance-induced friction.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"field\": \"external_conditions\",\n          \"value\": \"Global recovery helped, but Vietnam still had to manage structural skills shortages and anti-corruption side effects.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"field\": \"distribution_and_household_effects\",\n          \"value\": \"Broad macro gains were visible, but poverty and inequality constraints kept the distribution story from reaching the top band.\"\n        }\n      ]\n    }\n  ],\n  \"unavailable_dossiers\": [],\n  \"batch_notes\": [\n    \"Anchors used for calibration spanned a low case (Russia/Turkey), a middle case (Germany/Philippines/Japan), and a high case (Vietnam/Indonesia) so the scores were not anchored to any one regime type or income level.\",\n    \"I weighted ruler-attributed policy, implementation, and household effects above GDP headlines alone; strong macro outcomes without fair distribution were not scored as high as broad prosperity.\",\n    \"Where evidence was mostly plans, speeches, or self-reporting, I kept scores conservative and used the plausible ranges to reflect remaining uncertainty.\"\n  ],\n  \"run_profile\": {\n    \"provider_profile\": \"openai:gpt-5.4-mini\",\n    \"provider\": \"openai\",\n    \"model\": \"gpt-5.4-mini\",\n    \"dossier_count\": 20,\n    \"unavailable_dossier_count\": 0,\n    \"usage\": {\n      \"input_tokens\": \"unknown_not_exposed_by_tool\",\n      \"output_tokens\": \"unknown_not_exposed_by_tool\",\n      \"total_tokens\": \"unknown_not_exposed_by_tool\",\n      \"estimated_cost_usd\": \"unknown_not_exposed_by_tool\"\n    }\n  }\n}"}}
