{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_0","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"schema_version\":\"ruler_chapter_judgment_v1\",\"job_key\":\"chapter-judge:2022-top20-hybrid-v2-judges-v1:2022:6B\",\"run_key\":\"2022-top20-hybrid-v2-judges-v1\",\"chapter_id\":\"6B\",\"target_year\":2022,\"rubric_version\":\"chapter_6b_v3\",\"calibration_batch_id\":\"chapter-judge:2022-top20-hybrid-v2-judges-v1:2022:6B\",\"evaluations\":[{\"dossier_job_key\":\"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:BGD:17068\",\"iso3\":\"BGD\",\"ruler_id\":\"2992\",\"ruler_year_id\":17068,\"ruler_name\":\"Sheikh Hasina\",\"period_start_year\":2022,\"period_end_year\":2022,\"chapter_id\":\"6B\",\"rubric_version\":\"chapter_6b_v3\",\"calibration_batch_id\":\"chapter-judge:2022-top20-hybrid-v2-judges-v1:2022:6B\",\"calibrated_against\":[\"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:ETH:16782\",\"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:BRA:19646\",\"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:USA:15810\"],\"score_1_to_10\":7.0,\"insufficient_evidence_reason\":null,\"confidence_score\":0.81,\"plausible_score_range\":{\"lower\":6.0,\"upper\":8.0},\"decisive_positive_evidence\":[{\"evidence_id\":\"E0078\",\"explanation\":\"Flagship mother-and-child benefits reached 1.25 million beneficiaries with direct cash support, showing real social-protection delivery.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0089\",\"explanation\":\"FY22 social-protection spending and cash transfers reached millions through digital delivery channels, showing governance-backed welfare action.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0086\",\"explanation\":\"Flood response mitigated severe child and WASH damage in 2022, showing crisis relief rather than mere rhetoric.\"}],\"decisive_negative_evidence\":[{\"evidence_id\":\"E0083\",\"explanation\":\"Large shares of schools still lacked safe water, sanitation, and hygiene services, showing major service gaps.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0079\",\"explanation\":\"UNICEF flagged stagnant child-budget share and low utilization, which weakens claims of highly effective execution.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0085\",\"explanation\":\"Bangladesh still had incomplete sanitation and handwashing coverage, limiting the breadth of welfare gains.\"}],\"inherited_baseline_and_constraints\":\"Bangladesh entered 2022 with a comparatively active welfare state but still faced severe climate exposure, incomplete WASH access, and uneven service quality. That baseline allows real credit for social spending and disaster response, but it also caps the score because many results remain partial and uneven.\",\"ruler_attribution\":\"Mostly attributable to Hasina's government and policy apparatus, with several gains shared across ministries, donors, and local delivery systems rather than personally directed by one officeholder.\",\"supported_lenses\":[\"6B.2 basic services\",\"6B.3 vulnerable groups\",\"6B.5 evidence and correction\",\"6B.6 crisis response\",\"6B.8 dignity and equity\",\"6B.9 durable institutions\",\"6B.10 life chances\"],\"missing_or_weak_lenses\":[\"6B.1 welfare as core purpose\",\"6B.4 professional administration\",\"6B.7 politicized welfare\"],\"contrary_evidence\":[{\"evidence_id\":\"E0083\",\"explanation\":\"School WASH deficits and incomplete sanitation coverage cut against a near-universal service story.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0079\",\"explanation\":\"Implementation weakness and low utilization show that budgeted welfare did not always translate into effective delivery.\"}],\"source_mix\":\"Mostly official and IGO sources, especially IMF, World Bank, UNICEF, WFP, and UNICEF DATA, with no external search beyond the embedded dossier and no reliance on client-matrix material.\",\"structured_prior_summary\":\"Structured local priors were not collected in this experiment, so the judgment relies on the embedded dossier evidence, the reviewer exclusions already present there, and cross-case calibration within the batch.\",\"chapter_rationale\":\"Sheikh Hasina earns a clear positive score because the record shows a real welfare-state portfolio rather than rhetoric alone: expanded cash benefits, social-protection budgeting, education delivery, and disaster mitigation all appear in the 2022 evidence. The main limits are equally clear. Water, sanitation, and school-facility gaps remain substantial, implementation efficiency is uneven, and several gains are donor-supported or system-level rather than personally driven. That is enough for a solid above-average score, but not enough for an 8 because broad, durable, and independently audited improvements are still incomplete.\",\"lower_anchor_rejected\":\"A lower score would ignore the breadth of concrete social-protection, education, and crisis-response action that the dossier documents in 2022.\",\"higher_anchor_rejected\":\"An 8 would require stronger evidence of broad, durable, and equitable improvement with better outcome verification across the service portfolio; the dossier remains too mixed for that.\",\"manual_review_required\":false,\"manual_review_reason_type\":null,\"manual_review_reason\":null,\"chapter_specific\":[{\"field\":\"evidenced_service_domains\",\"value\":\"social protection, education, WASH, child welfare, disaster response\"},{\"field\":\"distribution_and_dignity\",\"value\":\"women, children, and poor households are clearly targeted, but coverage and service quality remain uneven\"},{\"field\":\"crisis_context\",\"value\":\"flood damage and climate risk make the 2022 response especially relevant\"},{\"field\":\"trajectory\",\"value\":\"clear baseline-adjusted improvement with persistent access and quality gaps\"}]},{\"dossier_job_key\":\"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:BRA:19646\",\"iso3\":\"BRA\",\"ruler_id\":\"3413\",\"ruler_year_id\":19646,\"ruler_name\":\"Jair Bolsonaro\",\"period_start_year\":2022,\"period_end_year\":2022,\"chapter_id\":\"6B\",\"rubric_version\":\"chapter_6b_v3\",\"calibration_batch_id\":\"chapter-judge:2022-top20-hybrid-v2-judges-v1:2022:6B\",\"calibrated_against\":[\"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:ETH:16782\",\"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:DEU:16984\",\"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:USA:15810\"],\"score_1_to_10\":4.5,\"insufficient_evidence_reason\":null,\"confidence_score\":0.76,\"plausible_score_range\":{\"lower\":3.5,\"upper\":5.5},\"decisive_positive_evidence\":[{\"evidence_id\":\"E0071\",\"explanation\":\"Auxílio Brasil conditionalities were tied to health and education tracking, showing concrete welfare administration.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0073\",\"explanation\":\"Targeting updates for social assistance show some capacity to improve program administration.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0074\",\"explanation\":\"Internet Brasil and related connectivity policy added real education access support.\"}],\"decisive_negative_evidence\":[{\"evidence_id\":\"E0068\",\"explanation\":\"Millions of children and adolescents were out of school, which signals a serious human-development problem.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0069\",\"explanation\":\"Food insecurity and poverty remained very high in 2022 despite some cushioning from transfers.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0072\",\"explanation\":\"Program monitoring problems led to sanctions being annulled, showing weak execution quality.\"}],\"inherited_baseline_and_constraints\":\"Brazil in 2022 had pandemic aftershocks, inflation, and deep structural inequality. Bolsonaro can claim some targeted welfare action, but the baseline was poor and the year still ended with large child poverty, food insecurity, and school exclusion.\",\"ruler_attribution\":\"The strongest evidence is government-level and programmatic rather than personal; Bolsonaro is tied to the policy environment and executive choices, but many outcomes reflect pandemic, Congress, and subnational conditions.\",\"supported_lenses\":[\"6B.2 basic services\",\"6B.3 vulnerable groups\",\"6B.4 administration\",\"6B.5 correction\",\"6B.6 crisis response\",\"6B.8 dignity and equity\",\"6B.10 life chances\"],\"missing_or_weak_lenses\":[\"6B.1 welfare as core purpose\",\"6B.7 non-politicized welfare\",\"6B.9 durable institutions\"],\"contrary_evidence\":[{\"evidence_id\":\"E0068\",\"explanation\":\"School non-attendance and child labor remain major welfare failures.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0069\",\"explanation\":\"Food insecurity and poverty show the welfare picture was still badly compromised.\"}],\"source_mix\":\"Official Brazilian sources and Reuters/UNICEF/World Bank corroboration, with an overall evidence picture that mixes program design, implementation fixes, and negative household indicators.\",\"structured_prior_summary\":\"Structured local priors were not collected in this experiment, so the judgment relies on the embedded dossier evidence, the reviewer exclusions already present there, and cross-case calibration within the batch.\",\"chapter_rationale\":\"Bolsonaro receives a mixed score because the dossier contains real social-policy machinery, especially around conditional transfers, connectivity, and administrative targeting. But the year still shows deep welfare weakness: child poverty, school exclusion, food insecurity, and monitoring failures remain severe, and the most positive evidence is often about process rather than durable outcomes. The score sits below the middle only modestly because the government did do more than posture; it simply did not convert that into broad, reliable human-development gains.\",\"lower_anchor_rejected\":\"A lower score would miss the fact that the administration did deploy real welfare programs and administrative corrections in 2022.\",\"higher_anchor_rejected\":\"A higher score would require stronger evidence of broad, durable reductions in poverty and exclusion, which the dossier does not provide.\",\"manual_review_required\":false,\"manual_review_reason_type\":null,\"manual_review_reason\":null,\"chapter_specific\":[{\"field\":\"evidenced_service_domains\",\"value\":\"education, social protection, connectivity, housing, child welfare\"},{\"field\":\"distribution_and_dignity\",\"value\":\"some vulnerable groups were explicitly targeted, but exclusion and school non-attendance remained large\"},{\"field\":\"crisis_context\",\"value\":\"inflation and pandemic aftershocks shaped the welfare record\"},{\"field\":\"trajectory\",\"value\":\"mixed: real policy action, but weak and uneven human-development outcomes\"}]},{\"dossier_job_key\":\"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:CHN:15832\",\"iso3\":\"CHN\",\"ruler_id\":\"1432\",\"ruler_year_id\":15832,\"ruler_name\":\"Xi Jinping\",\"period_start_year\":2022,\"period_end_year\":2022,\"chapter_id\":\"6B\",\"rubric_version\":\"chapter_6b_v3\",\"calibration_batch_id\":\"chapter-judge:2022-top20-hybrid-v2-judges-v1:2022:6B\",\"calibrated_against\":[\"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:ETH:16782\",\"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:DEU:16984\",\"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:USA:15810\"],\"score_1_to_10\":7.0,\"insufficient_evidence_reason\":null,\"confidence_score\":0.72,\"plausible_score_range\":{\"lower\":6.0,\"upper\":8.0},\"decisive_positive_evidence\":[{\"evidence_id\":\"E0078\",\"explanation\":\"The 2022 public-health package covered broad health and vulnerable-group services with local implementation instructions.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0081\",\"explanation\":\"The housing program set large subsidized-rental and renovation targets, showing major welfare investment.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0084\",\"explanation\":\"Anti-relapse poverty mechanisms and follow-up support indicate durable social-policy architecture.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0088\",\"explanation\":\"New urban jobs were created at scale in 2022 despite weak youth conditions.\"}],\"decisive_negative_evidence\":[{\"evidence_id\":\"E0087\",\"explanation\":\"Housing investment and sales fell sharply, which undercuts a clean welfare-gains narrative.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0085\",\"explanation\":\"Consumption fell and disposable income growth was modest, limiting the positive story.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0088\",\"explanation\":\"Youth unemployment remained high, showing that gains were not evenly shared.\"}],\"inherited_baseline_and_constraints\":\"China entered 2022 with a large, centrally managed welfare and poverty-consolidation system. That makes major gains plausible, but it also means the score should not be inflated by macro averages alone: 2022 still showed property stress, weak consumption, and uneven labor-market outcomes, especially for young people.\",\"ruler_attribution\":\"Much of the evidence is system-level and collective under Xi rather than personally ordered one by one, but the policy line, institutional design, and national targets are clearly associated with his leadership.\",\"supported_lenses\":[\"6B.2 basic services\",\"6B.3 vulnerable groups\",\"6B.4 professional administration\",\"6B.5 measurement and correction\",\"6B.6 crisis response\",\"6B.8 dignity and opportunity\",\"6B.9 durable institutions\",\"6B.10 life chances\"],\"missing_or_weak_lenses\":[\"6B.1 welfare as core purpose\",\"6B.7 non-politicized welfare\"],\"contrary_evidence\":[{\"evidence_id\":\"E0087\",\"explanation\":\"Property-sector contraction and falling investment show a serious offset to the welfare story.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0085\",\"explanation\":\"Weak consumption and only modest income growth limit the interpretation of 2022 as a broad welfare leap.\"}],\"source_mix\":\"Official Chinese sources dominate, with national statistics and ministry briefings supplemented by UNICEF and World Bank context; the record is strong on policy architecture and outcomes but weaker on independent ruler-specific attribution.\",\"structured_prior_summary\":\"Structured local priors were not collected in this experiment, so the judgment relies on the embedded dossier evidence, the reviewer exclusions already present there, and cross-case calibration within the batch.\",\"chapter_rationale\":\"Xi Jinping earns a high score because the dossier shows broad, state-backed human-development activity: health services, poverty-relapse prevention, housing targets, and job creation all appear at scale. The score is capped below the top band because the record is not uniformly positive: housing and investment fell, consumption weakened, youth labor stress persisted, and much of the evidence is system-level rather than personally attributable to Xi. That is strong performance in ordinary life-chance terms, but not an exceptional, near-universal welfare transformation.\",\"lower_anchor_rejected\":\"A lower score would ignore the breadth of formal welfare architecture and the substantial 2022 outcomes documented in the dossier.\",\"higher_anchor_rejected\":\"An 8 would require stronger evidence of equitable, durable gains with less macro drag and clearer ruler-level causation than the dossier provides.\",\"manual_review_required\":false,\"manual_review_reason_type\":null,\"manual_review_reason\":null,\"chapter_specific\":[{\"field\":\"evidenced_service_domains\",\"value\":\"health, housing, poverty consolidation, labor, social services\"},{\"field\":\"distribution_and_dignity\",\"value\":\"rural poor children, vulnerable groups, and relocated households are explicitly prioritized, but youth and housing stresses remain\"},{\"field\":\"crisis_context\",\"value\":\"property downturn and post-COVID adjustment frame the 2022 record\"},{\"field\":\"trajectory\",\"value\":\"broad improvement with significant macro and distributional headwinds\"}]},{\"dossier_job_key\":\"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:COD:16113\",\"iso3\":\"COD\",\"ruler_id\":\"2830\",\"ruler_year_id\":16113,\"ruler_name\":\"Félix Tshisekedi\",\"period_start_year\":2022,\"period_end_year\":2022,\"chapter_id\":\"6B\",\"rubric_version\":\"chapter_6b_v3\",\"calibration_batch_id\":\"chapter-judge:2022-top20-hybrid-v2-judges-v1:2022:6B\",\"calibrated_against\":[\"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:ETH:16782\",\"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:BRA:19646\",\"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:USA:15810\"],\"score_1_to_10\":3.5,\"insufficient_evidence_reason\":null,\"confidence_score\":0.77,\"plausible_score_range\":{\"lower\":2.5,\"upper\":4.5},\"decisive_positive_evidence\":[{\"evidence_id\":\"E0075\",\"explanation\":\"The 145-territories program and its project list show concrete development intent and presidential sponsorship.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0080\",\"explanation\":\"The 2022-2026 CPF prioritized human capital and inclusive development, including education and social protection.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0084\",\"explanation\":\"World Bank finance supported governance, transport, and connectivity reforms.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0090\",\"explanation\":\"WHO and local health teams improved vaccine-data triangulation and planning.\"}],\"decisive_negative_evidence\":[{\"evidence_id\":\"E0086\",\"explanation\":\"Poverty reduction remained elusive and growth benefits were not broadly shared.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0094\",\"explanation\":\"Mass displacement and clean-water shortages left children in acute risk and dependence on emergency aid.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0095\",\"explanation\":\"School closures and minimal education funding pledge show severe service disruption.\"}],\"inherited_baseline_and_constraints\":\"The DRC in 2022 was conflict-affected, regionally fragmented, and heavily dependent on external finance and emergency relief. That baseline sharply limits credit for any government plan and makes severe deprivation the dominant reality of the year.\",\"ruler_attribution\":\"Tshisekedi is clearly associated with the development agenda and presidential sponsorship, but actual delivery was heavily shared with the World Bank, WHO, UNICEF, and provincial authorities; direct ruler causation remains thin.\",\"supported_lenses\":[\"6B.2 basic services\",\"6B.3 vulnerable groups\",\"6B.4 professional administration\",\"6B.5 evidence and correction\",\"6B.6 crisis response\",\"6B.8 dignity and opportunity\",\"6B.10 life chances\"],\"missing_or_weak_lenses\":[\"6B.1 welfare as core purpose\",\"6B.7 non-politicized welfare\",\"6B.9 durable institutions\"],\"contrary_evidence\":[{\"evidence_id\":\"E0094\",\"explanation\":\"Emergency conditions and mass displacement show that avoidable suffering remained severe.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0086\",\"explanation\":\"Even the positive macro narrative says poverty reduction had not yet been achieved in a broad household sense.\"}],\"source_mix\":\"Mostly official presidential, World Bank, WHO, UNICEF, and humanitarian sources. The dossier is rich on programs and crisis conditions but weaker on completed outputs and direct presidential control.\",\"structured_prior_summary\":\"Structured local priors were not collected in this experiment, so the judgment relies on the embedded dossier evidence, the reviewer exclusions already present there, and cross-case calibration within the batch.\",\"chapter_rationale\":\"Tshisekedi gets a low score because the dossier shows serious development intent and some external financing, but the human-development environment remains dominated by conflict, displacement, school closure, weak poverty reduction, and emergency dependence. The record is better than pure neglect: there are projects, service reforms, and crisis-response systems. But the evidence does not show that those plans materially changed life chances at scale in 2022, so the score stays well below the middle.\",\"lower_anchor_rejected\":\"A lower score would ignore the real development-program architecture and emergency response measures documented in the dossier.\",\"higher_anchor_rejected\":\"A higher score would require stronger evidence of completed, ruler-attributable improvements in household welfare and service delivery, which is absent here.\",\"manual_review_required\":false,\"manual_review_reason_type\":null,\"manual_review_reason\":null,\"chapter_specific\":[{\"field\":\"evidenced_service_domains\",\"value\":\"health, education, water, social protection, connectivity\"},{\"field\":\"distribution_and_dignity\",\"value\":\"girls, women, displaced people, and conflict-affected communities are named, but access remains fragile\"},{\"field\":\"crisis_context\",\"value\":\"conflict, displacement, disease outbreaks, and school closures dominate the 2022 baseline\"},{\"field\":\"trajectory\",\"value\":\"development agenda present, but outcomes remain largely aspirational\"}]},{\"dossier_job_key\":\"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:DEU:16984\",\"iso3\":\"DEU\",\"ruler_id\":\"2975\",\"ruler_year_id\":16984,\"ruler_name\":\"Olaf Scholz\",\"period_start_year\":2022,\"period_end_year\":2022,\"chapter_id\":\"6B\",\"rubric_version\":\"chapter_6b_v3\",\"calibration_batch_id\":\"chapter-judge:2022-top20-hybrid-v2-judges-v1:2022:6B\",\"calibrated_against\":[\"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:ETH:16782\",\"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:BRA:19646\",\"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:USA:15810\"],\"score_1_to_10\":7.0,\"insufficient_evidence_reason\":null,\"confidence_score\":0.82,\"plausible_score_range\":{\"lower\":6.0,\"upper\":8.0},\"decisive_positive_evidence\":[{\"evidence_id\":\"E0064\",\"explanation\":\"The minimum-wage increase gave a large, concrete income gain to more than six million workers.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0065\",\"explanation\":\"Wohngeld Plus and the heating subsidy materially expanded housing assistance for millions of people.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0066\",\"explanation\":\"Ukrainian refugees received access to basic security, health care, language courses, and labor-market support.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0101\",\"explanation\":\"The 200 billion euro economic shield and gas/heat price brake show serious crisis mitigation capacity.\"}],\"decisive_negative_evidence\":[{\"evidence_id\":\"E0070\",\"explanation\":\"OECD noted the relief packages were not always well targeted to the most vulnerable households.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0072\",\"explanation\":\"High employment did not eliminate inflation and real-wage pressure, which limited net welfare gains.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0102\",\"explanation\":\"Bürgergeld was enacted at year-end but entered into force only in 2023, reducing within-2022 realized impact.\"}],\"inherited_baseline_and_constraints\":\"Germany entered 2022 with high baseline welfare, strong institutions, and major external shocks from the war in Ukraine and energy prices. That means the score should reward protection against crisis loss and targeted relief, but not confuse crisis management with a full welfare transformation.\",\"ruler_attribution\":\"Mostly cabinet-level and coalition-level under Scholz rather than personally executed each day, but the major relief packages, wage hike, refugee protection, and energy shield are clearly tied to his government and public leadership.\",\"supported_lenses\":[\"6B.2 basic services\",\"6B.3 vulnerable groups\",\"6B.4 professional administration\",\"6B.5 correction and monitoring\",\"6B.6 crisis response\",\"6B.8 dignity and equal opportunity\",\"6B.9 durable institutions\",\"6B.10 life chances\"],\"missing_or_weak_lenses\":[\"6B.1 welfare as core purpose\",\"6B.7 politicized welfare\"],\"contrary_evidence\":[{\"evidence_id\":\"E0070\",\"explanation\":\"The OECD says some relief was not well targeted, which weakens the claim of highly efficient distribution.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0102\",\"explanation\":\"A major social reform was enacted late and only partly realized within 2022.\"}],\"source_mix\":\"Official German government sources, BMAS/BMWSB/BMF material, and OECD/IMF/statistical corroboration, with strong coverage of crisis response and social transfers.\",\"structured_prior_summary\":\"Structured local priors were not collected in this experiment, so the judgment relies on the embedded dossier evidence, the reviewer exclusions already present there, and cross-case calibration within the batch.\",\"chapter_rationale\":\"Scholz receives a clearly positive score because 2022 shows real and broad crisis protection: a minimum-wage jump, housing benefits, refugee security, and a large energy shield all directly improved ordinary life chances. The score does not rise into the top band because Germany started from a high baseline, some measures were imperfectly targeted, and several reforms were still only partly realized by year-end. This is strong crisis-state performance, not a once-in-a-generation welfare transformation.\",\"lower_anchor_rejected\":\"A lower score would understate the scale and concreteness of the relief delivered to workers, tenants, and refugees.\",\"higher_anchor_rejected\":\"An 8 would require broader, more durable, and more equitable gains with stronger within-year outcome verification than the dossier provides.\",\"manual_review_required\":false,\"manual_review_reason_type\":null,\"manual_review_reason\":null,\"chapter_specific\":[{\"field\":\"evidenced_service_domains\",\"value\":\"wages, housing, refugee support, energy relief, social security\"},{\"field\":\"distribution_and_dignity\",\"value\":\"low-paid workers, tenants, and Ukrainian refugees are explicitly protected\"},{\"field\":\"crisis_context\",\"value\":\"energy shock and war-driven displacement define the welfare challenge\"},{\"field\":\"trajectory\",\"value\":\"clear protective gains, but mostly as crisis mitigation in a high-baseline system\"}]},{\"dossier_job_key\":\"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:EGY:16232\",\"iso3\":\"EGY\",\"ruler_id\":\"2851\",\"ruler_year_id\":16232,\"ruler_name\":\"Abdel Fattah el-Sisi\",\"period_start_year\":2022,\"period_end_year\":2022,\"chapter_id\":\"6B\",\"rubric_version\":\"chapter_6b_v3\",\"calibration_batch_id\":\"chapter-judge:2022-top20-hybrid-v2-judges-v1:2022:6B\",\"calibrated_against\":[\"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:ETH:16782\",\"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:BRA:19646\",\"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:USA:15810\"],\"score_1_to_10\":5.0,\"insufficient_evidence_reason\":null,\"confidence_score\":0.7,\"plausible_score_range\":{\"lower\":4.0,\"upper\":6.0},\"decisive_positive_evidence\":[{\"evidence_id\":\"E0057\",\"explanation\":\"Takaful and Karama coverage and targeting for women and Upper Egypt show a substantial cash-transfer safety net.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0060\",\"explanation\":\"Bread-security financing directly cushioned households from price shocks and protected basic consumption.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0063\",\"explanation\":\"Education remediation for marginalized children shows some targeted correction of pandemic learning loss.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0068\",\"explanation\":\"Hospital-sector planning and universal health-insurance implementation show institutional welfare ambition.\"}],\"decisive_negative_evidence\":[{\"evidence_id\":\"E0063\",\"explanation\":\"Learning loss and unequal access were still the story, not a completed recovery.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0068\",\"explanation\":\"Health-system reform was still work in progress rather than a finished outcome.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0071\",\"explanation\":\"Rural sanitation goals remained project-level and not yet outcome-verified.\"}],\"inherited_baseline_and_constraints\":\"Egypt's 2022 baseline combined sizable social-program architecture with inflation pressure, weak labor-market conditions, and incomplete service quality. That supports some credit for cushioning poor households, but it also means the year looks more like managed fragility than deep human-development progress.\",\"ruler_attribution\":\"Most evidence is state- and ministry-level under Sisi, often co-produced with the World Bank and WHO. The ruler is responsible for the policy environment, but the dossier does not show a personal, end-to-end welfare-management style.\",\"supported_lenses\":[\"6B.2 basic services\",\"6B.3 vulnerable groups\",\"6B.4 professional administration\",\"6B.5 evidence and correction\",\"6B.6 crisis response\",\"6B.8 dignity and equity\",\"6B.10 life chances\"],\"missing_or_weak_lenses\":[\"6B.1 welfare as core purpose\",\"6B.7 politicized welfare\",\"6B.9 durable institutions\"],\"contrary_evidence\":[{\"evidence_id\":\"E0063\",\"explanation\":\"Learning-loss remediation shows the state was responding to a real deficit, not delivering an already solved system.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0071\",\"explanation\":\"Sanitation and service access were still mostlete policy conversion into benefits.\"}],\"decisive_negative_evidence\":[{\"evidence_id\":\"E0097\",\"explanation\":\"Labor-market strength is real but not purely attributable to Biden.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0098\",\"explanation\":\"Food insecurity rose in 2022, showing social stress and incomplete welfare gains.\"}],\"inherited_baseline_and_constraints\":\"Biden inherited a pandemic-disrupted economy and had to govern through inflation, supply-chain stress, and partisan constraints. The central question is whether the administration turned legislation into implementation machinery, not whether every outcome was fully under presidential control.\",\"ruler_attribution\":\"Strong presidential ownership of agenda-setting and executive implementation, with many details handled by agencies and Congress. The record shows a functioning policy state and credible conversion of legislation into action, while some outcomes remain shared or pending.\",\"supported_lenses\":[\"8B.1\",\"8B.2\",\"8B.3\",\"8B.4\",\"8B.5\",\"8B.6\",\"8B.8\",\"8B.9\",\"8B.10\"],\"missing_or_weak_lenses\":[\"8B.7\"],\"contrary_evidence\":[{\"evidence_id\":\"E0097\",\"explanation\":\"Labor-market outcomes were strong, but not a clean measure of presidential skill alone.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0098\",\"explanation\":\"Food insecurity worsened, limiting the welfare success story.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0096\",\"explanation\":\"Many IRA benefits were scheduled for later years, so 2022 is mostly implementation design.\"}],\"source_mix\":\"Mostly official White House, agency, and departmental records, supplemented by IMF and Reuters. Strong on legislation-to-implementation conversion; weaker on fully isolated outcome attribution and year-end welfare gains.\",\"structured_prior_summary\":\"No structured local priors were collected in this experiment.\",\"chapter_rationale\":\"Biden's 2022 chapter is fairly strong: the administration translated a large legislative agenda into active implementation machinery across infrastructure, industrial policy, health costs, and cabinet coordination, while the labor market remained resilient. The constraints are that many benefits were still pending and some social stress, like food insecurity, remained elevated. This is a high score because the file shows both policy design and credible implementation.\",\"lower_anchor_rejected\":\"A 6 would understate the amount of actual implementation architecture and concrete action in the file.\",\"higher_anchor_rejected\":\"An 8 would require more durable realized outcomes within 2022 and clearer separation from external macro and Fed effects.\",\"manual_review_required\":false,\"manual_review_reason_type\":null,\"manual_review_reason\":null,\"chapter_specific\":[{\"field\":\"program_basis\",\"value\":\"explicit: bottom-up, middle-out, industrial-policy and social-cost-reduction agenda\"},{\"field\":\"program_type\",\"value\":\"policy, state_building\"},{\"field\":\"strategic_clarity\",\"value\":\"clear\"},{\"field\":\"operationalization\",\"value\":\"strong\"},{\"field\":\"mobilization_and_coordination\",\"value\":\"strong\"},{\"field\":\"adaptation\",\"value\":\"effective\"},{\"field\":\"goal_progress\",\"value\":\"substantial\"},{\"field\":\"durability\",\"value\":\"durable\"},{\"field\":\"trajectory\",\"value\":\"The administration converted major legislation into implementation systems and visible policy action, though some benefits were still pending.\"},{\"field\":\"morality_separation_check\",\"value\":\"Approval or disapproval of the objectives did not affect the score.\"},{\"field\":\"lens_strengths\",\"value\":\"8B.2, 8B.3, 8B.4, 8B.5, 8B.6, 8B.9\"},{\"field\":\"lens_gaps\",\"value\":\"8B.7\"},{\"field\":\"defensible_score_range\",\"value\":\"6.5-7.5\"}]},{\"dossier_job_key\":\"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:VNM:19647\",\"iso3\":\"VNM\",\"ruler_id\":\"3411\",\"ruler_year_id\":19647,\"ruler_name\":\"Nguyễn Phú Trọng\",\"period_start_year\":2022,\"period_end_year\":2022,\"chapter_id\":\"8B\",\"rubric_version\":\"chapter_8b_v3\",\"calibration_batch_id\":\"chapter-judge:2022-saturation-v3-stage1-controlled:2022:8B\",\"calibrated_against\":[\"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:DEU:16984\",\"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:USA:15810\",\"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:RUS:15706\"],\"score_1_to_10\":6.5,\"insufficient_evidence_reason\":null,\"confidence_score\":77,\"plausible_score_range\":{\"lower\":6,\"upper\":7},\"decisive_positive_evidence\":[{\"evidence_id\":\"E0039\",\"explanation\":\"Trọng clearly set economic direction and coordinated the 2022 agenda.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0073\",\"explanation\":\"The anti-corruption system produced large discipline and prosecution numbers.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0088\",\"explanation\":\"Vietnam's strong 2022 macro outcome provides a positive end-of-period indicator.\"}],\"decisive_negative_evidence\":[{\"evidence_id\":\"E0084\",\"explanation\":\"The crackdown chilled supply chains and investment, showing real governance costs.\"},{\"evidence"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_1","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"schema_version\":\"ruler_chapter_judgment_v1\",\"job_key\":\"chapter-judge:2022-saturation-v3-stage1-controlled:2022:8B\",\"run_key\":\"2022-saturation-v3-stage1-controlled\",\"chapter_id\":\"8B\",\"target_year\":2022,\"rubric_version\":\"chapter_8b_v3\",\"calibration_batch_id\":\"chapter-judge:2022-saturation-v3-stage1-controlled:2022:8B\",\"evaluations\":[{\"dossier_job_key\":\"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:BGD:17068\",\"iso3\":\"BGD\",\"ruler_id\":\"2992\",\"ruler_year_id\":17068,\"ruler_name\":\"Sheikh Hasina\",\"period_start_year\":2022,\"period_end_year\":2022,\"chapter_id\":\"8B\",\"rubric_version\":\"chapter_8b_v3\",\"calibration_batch_id\":\"chapter-judge:2022-saturation-v3-stage1-controlled:2022:8B\",\"calibrated_against\":[\"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:DEU:16984\",\"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:USA:15810\",\"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:RUS:15706\"],\"score_1_to_10\":6,\"insufficient_evidence_reason\":null,\"confidence_score\":72,\"plausible_score_range\":{\"lower\":5.5,\"upper\":6.5},\"decisive_positive_evidence\":[{\"evidence_id\":\"E0059\",\"explanation\":\"Concrete 2022 stabilization package with policy changes.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0081\",\"explanation\":\"Large FY22 safety-net budget and G2P expansion.\"}],\"decisive_negative_evidence\":[{\"evidence_id\":\"E0064\",\"explanation\":\"Fuel-price shock and reserve stress show reactive crisis management.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0054\",\"explanation\":\"IMF still flagged inflation and banking vulnerabilities.\"}],\"inherited_baseline_and_constraints\":\"Growth-oriented but stress-prone macro baseline; inflation, reserves, and banking risks mattered.\",\"ruler_attribution\":\"Strong government ownership of fiscal and social policy, but implementation ran through ministries and the central bank; attribution is real but not exclusive.\",\"supported_lenses\":[\"8B.1\",\"8B.2\",\"8B.3\",\"8B.6\",\"8B.7\",\"8B.9\",\"8B.10\"],\"missing_or_weak_lenses\":[\"8B.4\",\"8B.5\",\"8B.8\"],\"contrary_evidence\":[{\"evidence_id\":\"E0064\",\"explanation\":\"Reactive fuel-price management under stress.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0075\",\"explanation\":\"Climate-resilience gains are partly inherited/system-level.\"}],\"source_mix\":\"Official IMF/World Bank/government plus Reuters-style reporting; strongest on policy and rollout, weaker on independent delivery audits.\",\"structured_prior_summary\":\"No structured local priors were collected in this experiment.\",\"chapter_rationale\":\"Bangladesh in 2022 shows real fiscal and social-policy execution: the government stabilized the macro response, expanded transfers, and pushed financed reforms. The main limit is that delivery-quality evidence is thinner than announcement evidence, so this is solid competence rather than top-tier mastery.\",\"lower_anchor_rejected\":\"A 5 would miss the scale of actual policy action and transfer rollout.\",\"higher_anchor_rejected\":\"A 7 would overstate durable, independently verified delivery.\",\"manual_review_required\":false,\"manual_review_reason_type\":null,\"manual_review_reason\":null,\"chapter_specific\":[{\"field\":\"program_basis\",\"value\":\"mostly_explicit\"},{\"field\":\"program_type\",\"value\":\"policy, state_building\"},{\"field\":\"strategic_clarity\",\"value\":\"clear\"},{\"field\":\"operationalization\",\"value\":\"strong\"},{\"field\":\"goal_progress\",\"value\":\"substantial\"},{\"field\":\"durability\",\"value\":\"mixed\"}]},{\"dossier_job_key\":\"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:BRA:19646\",\"iso3\":\"BRA\",\"ruler_id\":\"3413\",\"ruler_year_id\":19646,\"ruler_name\":\"Jair Bolsonaro\",\"period_start_year\":2022,\"period_end_year\":2022,\"chapter_id\":\"8B\",\"rubric_version\":\"chapter_8b_v3\",\"calibration_batch_id\":\"chapter-judge:2022-saturation-v3-stage1-controlled:2022:8B\",\"calibrated_against\":[\"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:DEU:16984\",\"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:USA:15810\",\"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:RUS:15706\"],\"score_1_to_10\":5,\"insufficient_evidence_reason\":null,\"confidence_score\":68,\"plausible_score_range\":{\"lower\":4.5,\"upper\":5.5},\"decisive_positive_evidence\":[{\"evidence_id\":\"E0070\",\"explanation\":\"Auxílio Brasil expansion was a real transfer rollout.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0061\",\"explanation\":\"Presidential budget-delegation decree shows concrete executive action.\"}],\"decisive_negative_evidence\":[{\"evidence_id\":\"E0103\",\"explanation\":\"Spending package bypassed the cap and signaled fiscal strain.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0097\",\"explanation\":\"Independent critique questioned sustainability of broad relief.\"}],\"inherited_baseline_and_constraints\":\"Inflationary, election-year, coalition-constrained environment with inherited macro stress.\",\"ruler_attribution\":\"Real government ownership, but many outcomes were mediated by Congress, markets, and inherited conditions.\",\"supported_lenses\":[\"8B.1\",\"8B.2\",\"8B.3\",\"8B.4\",\"8B.6\",\"8B.7\",\"8B.8\",\"8B.10\"],\"missing_or_weak_lenses\":[\"8B.5\",\"8B.9\"],\"contrary_evidence\":[{\"evidence_id\":\"E0103\",\"explanation\":\"Politically driven fiscal strain.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0097\",\"explanation\":\"External sustainability concerns.\"}],\"source_mix\":\"Official releases plus Reuters-style reporting and one independent statistics retrospective; good on rollout, weaker on durability.\",\"structured_prior_summary\":\"No structured local priors were collected in this experiment.\",\"chapter_rationale\":\"Bolsonaro’s 2022 record is mixed: some real transfers and program actions, but also election-year fiscal strain and fragile execution. This is competent enough to clear the bottom-middle, but not enough for a higher score.\",\"lower_anchor_rejected\":\"A 4 would undercount the actual policy conversion and transfer rollout.\",\"higher_anchor_rejected\":\"A 6 would overstate durability and quality of execution.\",\"manual_review_required\":false,\"manual_review_reason_type\":null,\"manual_review_reason\":null,\"chapter_specific\":[{\"field\":\"program_basis\",\"value\":\"mostly_explicit\"},{\"field\":\"program_type\",\"value\":\"policy, survival\"},{\"field\":\"strategic_clarity\",\"value\":\"clear\"},{\"field\":\"operationalization\",\"value\":\"mixed\"},{\"field\":\"goal_progress\",\"value\":\"mixed\"},{\"field\":\"durability\",\"value\":\"fragile\"}]},{\"dossier_job_key\":\"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:CHN:15832\",\"iso3\":\"CHN\",\"ruler_id\":\"1432\",\"ruler_year_id\":15832,\"ruler_name\":\"Xi Jinping\",\"period_start_year\":2022,\"period_end_year\":2022,\"chapter_id\":\"8B\",\"rubric_version\":\"chapter_8b_v3\",\"calibration_batch_id\":\"chapter-judge:2022-saturation-v3-stage1-controlled:2022:8B\",\"calibrated_against\":[\"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:DEU:16984\",\"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:USA:15810\",\"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:RUS:15706\"],\"score_1_to_10\":7,\"insufficient_evidence_reason\":null,\"confidence_score\":77,\"plausible_score_range\":{\"lower\":6.5,\"upper\":7.5},\"decisive_positive_evidence\":[{\"evidence_id\":\"E0103\",\"explanation\":\"20th Congress report set a broad program under Xi's leadership.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0105\",\"explanation\":\"33-measure stabilization package shows real machinery, not just slogans.\"}],\"decisive_negative_evidence\":[{\"evidence_id\":\"E0040\",\"explanation\":\"Shanghai lockdown damage shows severe costs and limits.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0112\",\"explanation\":\"Zero-COVID downgrade was reactive and only partial.\"}],\"inherited_baseline_and_constraints\":\"Centralized party-state with strong capacity but severe zero-COVID and property-sector stress.\",\"ruler_attribution\":\"Strong direct ownership of strategy and elite selection; implementation is party-state wide and official-heavy, but real mobilization and some adaptation are visible.\",\"supported_lenses\":[\"8B.1\",\"8B.2\",\"8B.3\",\"8B.4\",\"8B.5\",\"8B.6\",\"8B.8\",\"8B.9\",\"8B.10\"],\"missing_or_weak_lenses\":[\"8B.7\"],\"contrary_evidence\":[{\"evidence_id\":\"E0040\",\"explanation\":\"Coercive lockdown harm.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0108\",\"explanation\":\"Anti-corruption enforcement quality remains unclear.\"}],\"source_mix\":\"Mostly official party-state material, supplemented by Reuters; strong on direction and architecture, weaker on independent outcome audits.\",\"structured_prior_summary\":\"No structured local priors were collected in this experiment.\",\"chapter_rationale\":\"Xi’s 2022 record is strong on program ownership, mobilization, and some adaptation, including a major stabilization package and the later COVID policy shift. The main drag is that the year also featured major coercive costs and the file remains official-heavy. That is a high but not exceptional competence score.\",\"lower_anchor_rejected\":\"A 6 would understate the breadth of mobilization and adaptation.\",\"higher_anchor_rejected\":\"An 8 would require clearer independent evidence of durable gains and less reliance on official self-report.\",\"manual_review_required\":false,\"manual_review_reason_type\":null,\"manual_review_reason\":null,\"chapter_specific\":[{\"field\":\"program_basis\",\"value\":\"explicit\"},{\"field\":\"program_type\",\"value\":\"policy, state_building, regime_control\"},{\"field\":\"strategic_clarity\",\"value\":\"exceptional\"},{\"field\":\"operationalization\",\"value\":\"strong\"},{\"field\":\"goal_progress\",\"value\":\"substantial\"},{\"field\":\"durability\",\"value\":\"mixed\"}]},{\"dossier_job_key\":\"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:COD:16113\",\"iso3\":\"COD\",\"ruler_id\":\"2830\",\"ruler_year_id\":16113,\"ruler_name\":\"Félix Tshisekedi\",\"period_start_year\":2022,\"period_end_year\":2022,\"chapter_id\":\"8B\",\"rubric_version\":\"chapter_8b_v3\",\"calibration_batch_id\":\"chapter-judge:2022-saturation-v3-stage1-controlled:2022:8B\",\"calibrated_against\":[\"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:DEU:16984\",\"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:USA:15810\",\"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:RUS:15706\"],\"score_1_to_10\":4.5,\"insufficient_evidence_reason\":null,\"confidence_score\":63,\"plausible_score_range\":{\"lower\":4,\"upper\":5},\"decisive_positive_evidence\":[{\"evidence_id\":\"E0108\",\"explanation\":\"145-territories program shows presidential oversight and mobilization.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0118\",\"explanation\":\"IMF macro prudence, especially halting central-bank financing.\"}],\"decisive_negative_evidence\":[{\"evidence_id\":\"E0119\",\"explanation\":\"Vaccination campaign still catching up from a low base.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0121\",\"explanation\":\"Eastern-provinces grant was approved, not completed.\"}],\"inherited_baseline_and_constraints\":\"Weak state, conflict, and limited administrative reach make completed delivery hard to prove.\",\"ruler_attribution\":\"Some direct oversight and state mobilization, but heavy donor/provincial dependence and thin completion evidence keep credit partial.\",\"supported_lenses\":[\"8B.2\",\"8B.3\",\"8B.4\",\"8B.5\",\"8B.6\",\"8B.8\",\"8B.9\",\"8B.10\"],\"missing_or_weak_lenses\":[\"8B.1\",\"8B.7\"],\"contrary_evidence\":[{\"evidence_id\":\"E0100\",\"explanation\":\"Offshore-structure allegations weaken the integrity picture.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0115\",\"explanation\":\"Several projects are future-oriented, not finished 2022 outputs.\"}],\"source_mix\":\"Official presidential, IMF, World Bank, WHO, and local reporting; strong on launch and design, weak on independent completion audits.\",\"structured_prior_summary\":\"No structured local priors were collected in this experiment.\",\"chapter_rationale\":\"Tshisekedi’s 2022 record shows partial mobilization and some macro prudence, but most of the file is still about program launch rather than completed delivery. The state moved, but durable outcome proof is thin. That keeps the score just below the middle.\",\"lower_anchor_rejected\":\"A 4 would ignore the visible state mobilization and macro-policy shift.\",\"higher_anchor_rejected\":\"A 5.5 would overstate completion and durability.\",\"manual_review_required\":false,\"manual_review_reason_type\":null,\"manual_review_reason\":null,\"chapter_specific\":[{\"field\":\"program_basis\",\"value\":\"mixed\"},{\"field\":\"program_type\",\"value\":\"policy, state_building\"},{\"field\":\"strategic_clarity\",\"value\":\"partial\"},{\"field\":\"operationalization\",\"value\":\"mixed\"},{\"field\":\"goal_progress\",\"value\":\"mixed\"},{\"field\":\"durability\",\"value\":\"fragile\"}]},{\"dossier_job_key\":\"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:DEU:16984\",\"iso3\":\"DEU\",\"ruler_id\":\"2975\",\"ruler_year_id\":16984,\"ruler_name\":\"Olaf Scholz\",\"period_start_year\":2022,\"period_end_year\":2022,\"chapter_id\":\"8B\",\"rubric_version\":\"chapter_8b_v3\",\"calibration_batch_id\":\"chapter-judge:2022-saturation-v3-stage1-controlled:2022:8B\",\"calibrated_against\":[\"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:DEU:16984\",\"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:USA:15810\",\"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:RUS:15706\"],\"score_1_to_10\":7,\"insufficient_evidence_reason\":null,\"confidence_score\":80,\"plausible_score_range\":{\"lower\":6.5,\"upper\":7.5},\"decisive_positive_evidence\":[{\"evidence_id\":\"E0087\",\"explanation\":\"Bundeswehr special fund is a major strategic conversion of the Ukraine shock.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0092\",\"explanation\":\"Uniper package is decisive crisis management for energy security.\"}],\"decisive_negative_evidence\":[{\"evidence_id\":\"E0095\",\"explanation\":\"OECD says relief targeting could be better.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0097\",\"explanation\":\"Ifu warns about fiscal sustainability costs.\"}],\"inherited_baseline_and_constraints\":\"Strong administrative state under severe Ukraine-energy-refugee shocks.\",\"ruler_attribution\":\"Good central ownership with many measures implemented through ministries; the record is stronger on execution than on perfect chancellor-only attribution.\",\"supported_lenses\":[\"8B.2\",\"8B.3\",\"8B.4\",\"8B.5\",\"8B.6\",\"8B.8\",\"8B.9\",\"8B.10\"],\"missing_or_weak_lenses\":[\"8B.7\"],\"contrary_evidence\":[{\"evidence_id\":\"E0095\",\"explanation\":\"Targeting weaknesses.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0097\",\"explanation\":\"Fiscal-cost critique.\"}],\"source_mix\":\"Mostly federal, ministry, IMF, OECD, and ifo material; strong on implementation and crisis response.\",\"structured_prior_summary\":\"No structured local priors were collected in this experiment.\",\"chapter_rationale\":\"Scholz’s 2022 record is strong because Germany turned war and energy shock into a large, coordinated state response. There are still design critiques, but implementation was real and visible. This is a high score, not a perfect one.\",\"lower_anchor_rejected\":\"A 6 would understate the breadth of coordinated execution.\",\"higher_anchor_rejected\":\"An 8 would require clearer evidence of durable long-run gains and less concern about targeting costs.\",\"manual_review_required\":false,\"manual_review_reason_type\":null,\"manual_review_reason\":null,\"chapter_specific\":[{\"field\":\"program_basis\",\"value\":\"explicit\"},{\"field\":\"program_type\",\"value\":\"policy, state_building\"},{\"field\":\"strategic_clarity\",\"value\":\"clear\"},{\"field\":\"operationalization\",\"value\":\"strong\"},{\"field\":\"goal_progress\",\"value\":\"substantial\"},{\"field\":\"durability\",\"value\":\"durable\"}]},{\"dossier_job_key\":\"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:EGY:16232\",\"iso3\":\"EGY\",\"ruler_id\":\"2851\",\"ruler_year_id\":16232,\"ruler_name\":\"Abdel Fattah el-Sisi\",\"period_start_year\":2022,\"period_end_year\":2022,\"chapter_id\":\"8B\",\"rubric_version\":\"chapter_8b_v3\",\"calibration_batch_id\":\"chapter-judge:2022-saturation-v3-stage1-controlled:2022:8B\",\"calibrated_against\":[\"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:DEU:16984\",\"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:U