{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_0","type":"agent_message","text":"{\n  \"schema_version\": \"ruler_chapter_judgment_v1\",\n  \"job_key\": \"chapter-judge:2022-saturation-v3-stage1-controlled:2022:8B\",\n  \"run_key\": \"2022-saturation-v3-stage1-controlled\",\n  \"chapter_id\": \"8B\",\n  \"target_year\": 2022,\n  \"rubric_version\": \"chapter_8b_v3\",\n  \"calibration_batch_id\": \"chapter-judge:2022-saturation-v3-stage1-controlled:2022:8B\",\n  \"evaluations\": [\n    {\n      \"dossier_job_key\": \"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:BGD:17068\",\n      \"iso3\": \"BGD\",\n      \"ruler_id\": \"2992\",\n      \"ruler_year_id\": 17068,\n      \"ruler_name\": \"Sheikh Hasina\",\n      \"period_start_year\": 2022,\n      \"period_end_year\": 2022,\n      \"chapter_id\": \"8B\",\n      \"rubric_version\": \"chapter_8b_v3\",\n      \"calibration_batch_id\": \"chapter-judge:2022-saturation-v3-stage1-controlled:2022:8B\",\n      \"calibrated_against\": [\n        \"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:BRA:19646\",\n        \"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:CHN:15832\",\n        \"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:RUS:15706\",\n        \"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:USA:15810\"\n      ],\n      \"score_1_to_10\": 6.5,\n      \"insufficient_evidence_reason\": null,\n      \"confidence_score\": 76,\n      \"plausible_score_range\": { \"lower\": 6.0, \"upper\": 7.5 },\n      \"decisive_positive_evidence\": [\n        {\n          \"evidence_id\": \"E0059\",\n          \"explanation\": \"Shows a concrete 2022 stabilization package with revenue mobilization, spending rationalization, monetary reform, and exchange-rate flexibility.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"evidence_id\": \"E0060\",\n          \"explanation\": \"Shows a World Bank-backed fiscal and financial-sector resilience program with specific implementation content.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"evidence_id\": \"E0067\",\n          \"explanation\": \"Shows a direct central-bank appointment affecting monetary management inside the Hasina government.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"evidence_id\": \"E0090\",\n          \"explanation\": \"Shows direct social-policy delivery and beneficiary counts for the Ashrayan housing program.\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"decisive_negative_evidence\": [\n        {\n          \"evidence_id\": \"E0064\",\n          \"explanation\": \"Shows reactive shock management and inflation pressure rather than smooth control of the macro environment.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"evidence_id\": \"E0075\",\n          \"explanation\": \"Shows that some welfare gains were partly inherited, system-level resilience rather than discrete ruler-only execution.\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"inherited_baseline_and_constraints\": \"Bangladesh entered 2022 with strong inherited growth and resilience, but also rising inflation, reserve pressure, and banking vulnerabilities. That makes attribution mixed: Hasina gets credit for the 2022 stabilization and welfare agenda, not for baseline trends.\",\n      \"ruler_attribution\": \"Substantial but not exclusive. Hasina clearly owned the 2022 policy line, appointments, and social-protection emphasis, but some gains came through inherited resilience, line ministries, and reactive crisis management.\",\n      \"supported_lenses\": [\n        \"8B.1\",\n        \"8B.2\",\n        \"8B.3\",\n        \"8B.4\",\n        \"8B.5\",\n        \"8B.6\",\n        \"8B.8\",\n        \"8B.9\",\n        \"8B.10\"\n      ],\n      \"missing_or_weak_lenses\": [\n        \"8B.7\",\n        \"8B.10\"\n      ],\n      \"contrary_evidence\": [\n        {\n          \"evidence_id\": \"E0064\",\n          \"explanation\": \"Fuel-price shock management shows adaptation under stress, but also reveals vulnerability and reactive policymaking.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"evidence_id\": \"E0075\",\n          \"explanation\": \"Climate-resilience gains are real, but the record also shows inherited system capacity and unresolved distributional risk.\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"source_mix\": \"Mostly official IMF, World Bank, and government releases, supplemented by Reuters and local reportage. The record is strong on declared policy and partial implementation, weaker on independent year-end outcome audits.\",\n      \"structured_prior_summary\": \"Structured local priors were not collected in this experiment.\",\n      \"chapter_rationale\": \"Hasina's 2022 record is moderately strong competence, landing at 6.5/10. Her government articulated and executed a clear stabilization-and-social-protection program, with concrete IMF and World Bank-backed reforms, budgeted safety-net spending, a central-bank appointment, and visible shock management; the main limits are that many gains are official self-reports, some improvements were inherited or reactive, and independent delivery audits remain thin. The record shows real policy action rather than slogans, but it does not fully prove durable household-level execution or corrective follow-through. Moral judgments about the regime, repression, or patronage allegations do not affect this execution score.\",\n      \"lower_anchor_rejected\": \"4 rejected because the dossier contains multiple concrete 2022 actions, not just rhetoric, including formal stabilization steps, budgeted welfare delivery, and a meaningful monetary appointment.\",\n      \"higher_anchor_rejected\": \"7 rejected because much of the evidence is official self-report or implementation design, and durable independent outcome verification remains limited.\",\n      \"manual_review_required\": false,\n      \"manual_review_reason_type\": null,\n      \"manual_review_reason\": null,\n      \"chapter_specific\": [\n        { \"field\": \"program_basis\", \"value\": \"explicit\" },\n        { \"field\": \"program_type\", \"value\": \"policy, state_building\" },\n        { \"field\": \"trajectory\", \"value\": \"upward but constrained\" },\n        { \"field\": \"strategic_clarity\", \"value\": \"clear\" },\n        { \"field\": \"operationalization\", \"value\": \"strong\" },\n        { \"field\": \"mobilization_and_coordination\", \"value\": \"strong\" },\n        { \"field\": \"adaptation\", \"value\": \"effective\" },\n        { \"field\": \"goal_progress\", \"value\": \"substantial\" },\n        { \"field\": \"durability\", \"value\": \"mixed\" },\n        { \"field\": \"morality_separation_check\", \"value\": \"The score reflects execution of the ruler's own program, not approval of the program's morality.\" }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"dossier_job_key\": \"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:BRA:19646\",\n      \"iso3\": \"BRA\",\n      \"ruler_id\": \"3413\",\n      \"ruler_year_id\": 19646,\n      \"ruler_name\": \"Jair Bolsonaro\",\n      \"period_start_year\": 2022,\n      \"period_end_year\": 2022,\n      \"chapter_id\": \"8B\",\n      \"rubric_version\": \"chapter_8b_v3\",\n      \"calibration_batch_id\": \"chapter-judge:2022-saturation-v3-stage1-controlled:2022:8B\",\n      \"calibrated_against\": [\n        \"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:BGD:17068\",\n        \"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:CHN:15832\",\n        \"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:RUS:15706\",\n        \"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:USA:15810\"\n      ],\n      \"score_1_to_10\": 5.0,\n      \"insufficient_evidence_reason\": null,\n      \"confidence_score\": 72,\n      \"plausible_score_range\": { \"lower\": 4.5, \"upper\": 6.0 },\n      \"decisive_positive_evidence\": [\n        {\n          \"evidence_id\": \"E0061\",\n          \"explanation\": \"Shows a concrete presidential decree delegating budget execution authority.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"evidence_id\": \"E0070\",\n          \"explanation\": \"Shows a direct cash-transfer expansion with specific beneficiary counts and a benefit floor.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"evidence_id\": \"E0101\",\n          \"explanation\": \"Shows an explicit tariff-cut policy choice aimed at lower prices and trade support.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"evidence_id\": \"E0104\",\n          \"explanation\": \"Shows the administration could still produce a measurable income-recovery outcome, even if mixed and partly transfer-driven.\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"decisive_negative_evidence\": [\n        {\n          \"evidence_id\": \"E0055\",\n          \"explanation\": \"Shows inflation and reserve stress that undercut any claim of broad macro control.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"evidence_id\": \"E0103\",\n          \"explanation\": \"Shows a Bolsonaro-backed spending push that relied on congressional maneuvering and raised sustainability concerns.\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"inherited_baseline_and_constraints\": \"Brazil's 2022 environment was shaped by inflation shocks, electoral timing, congressional bargaining, and large preexisting fiscal constraints. Bolsonaro had real executive leverage, but many of his moves were tactical, short-horizon, or partly dependent on Congress.\",\n      \"ruler_attribution\": \"Direct on decrees, spending pushes, and program rollouts; weaker on final outcomes because several measures were election-year, congressional, or market-mediated.\",\n      \"supported_lenses\": [\n        \"8B.1\",\n        \"8B.2\",\n        \"8B.3\",\n        \"8B.4\",\n        \"8B.5\",\n        \"8B.6\",\n        \"8B.8\",\n        \"8B.9\",\n        \"8B.10\"\n      ],\n      \"missing_or_weak_lenses\": [\n        \"8B.7\"\n      ],\n      \"contrary_evidence\": [\n        {\n          \"evidence_id\": \"E0055\",\n          \"explanation\": \"Shows macro stress and inflation that complicate any simple success narrative.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"evidence_id\": \"E0103\",\n          \"explanation\": \"Shows the spending program had fiscal tradeoffs and was not a clean implementation win.\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"source_mix\": \"Mostly official Brazilian government material, with Reuters and IBGE context for outcomes. The record is strong on policy announcement and rollout, weaker on independent audits of distribution and durability.\",\n      \"structured_prior_summary\": \"Structured local priors were not collected in this experiment.\",\n      \"chapter_rationale\": \"Bolsonaro's 2022 score is mixed competence at 5.0/10. He did convert his program into real budget, tax, tariff, and transfer actions, and some measures were executed at scale, but the record is dominated by election-year spending, tactical fiscal maneuvers, and macro conditions that remained unstable. The strongest facts are the concrete decrees and welfare rollouts; the weakest are durable outcomes and non-electoral discipline. Moral judgments about his politics or rhetoric do not affect the execution score.\",\n      \"lower_anchor_rejected\": \"3 rejected because the dossier shows repeated concrete state action, not paralysis or absence of control.\",\n      \"higher_anchor_rejected\": \"6 rejected because many high-salience measures were short-term, politically timed, or only partially attributable to Bolsonaro rather than durable program execution.\",\n      \"manual_review_required\": false,\n      \"manual_review_reason_type\": null,\n      \"manual_review_reason\": null,\n      \"chapter_specific\": [\n        { \"field\": \"program_basis\", \"value\": \"explicit\" },\n        { \"field\": \"program_type\", \"value\": \"policy, power_consolidation\" },\n        { \"field\": \"trajectory\", \"value\": \"mixed and election-distorted\" },\n        { \"field\": \"strategic_clarity\", \"value\": \"clear\" },\n        { \"field\": \"operationalization\", \"value\": \"mixed\" },\n        { \"field\": \"mobilization_and_coordination\", \"value\": \"mixed\" },\n        { \"field\": \"adaptation\", \"value\": \"mixed\" },\n        { \"field\": \"goal_progress\", \"value\": \"mixed\" },\n        { \"field\": \"durability\", \"value\": \"fragile\" },\n        { \"field\": \"morality_separation_check\", \"value\": \"The score measures execution, not whether the objectives were desirable.\" }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"dossier_job_key\": \"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:CHN:15832\",\n      \"iso3\": \"CHN\",\n      \"ruler_id\": \"1432\",\n      \"ruler_year_id\": 15832,\n      \"ruler_name\": \"Xi Jinping\",\n      \"period_start_year\": 2022,\n      \"period_end_year\": 2022,\n      \"chapter_id\": \"8B\",\n      \"rubric_version\": \"chapter_8b_v3\",\n      \"calibration_batch_id\": \"chapter-judge:2022-saturation-v3-stage1-controlled:2022:8B\",\n      \"calibrated_against\": [\n        \"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:BGD:17068\",\n        \"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:BRA:19646\",\n        \"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:RUS:15706\",\n        \"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:USA:15810\"\n      ],\n      \"score_1_to_10\": 8.0,\n      \"insufficient_evidence_reason\": null,\n      \"confidence_score\": 80,\n      \"plausible_score_range\": { \"lower\": 7.0, \"upper\": 8.5 },\n      \"decisive_positive_evidence\": [\n        {\n          \"evidence_id\": \"E0103\",\n          \"explanation\": \"Shows a top-level 2022 program with explicit five-year objectives across development, social services, and security.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"evidence_id\": \"E0105\",\n          \"explanation\": \"Shows a concrete State Council stabilization package with implementation content.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"evidence_id\": \"E0111\",\n          \"explanation\": \"Shows policy adaptation on COVID response while preserving central control.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"evidence_id\": \"E0112\",\n          \"explanation\": \"Shows a further late-2022 policy reversal toward a less disruptive COVID management approach.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"evidence_id\": \"E0045\",\n          \"explanation\": \"Shows Xi's consolidation of top leadership and direct program ownership at the 20th Congress.\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"decisive_negative_evidence\": [\n        {\n          \"evidence_id\": \"E0040\",\n          \"explanation\": \"Shows the severe human and logistical costs of the Shanghai lockdown strategy.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"evidence_id\": \"E0110\",\n          \"explanation\": \"Shows stronger monitoring, but also that the system still needed intensified oversight and better discipline.\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"inherited_baseline_and_constraints\": \"China entered 2022 with strong state capacity and a highly centralized party-state, which favors high competence scores when the leadership can mobilize it. Xi also faced serious COVID and growth constraints, so the question is whether he adapted the apparatus effectively, not whether the regime was benign.\",\n      \"ruler_attribution\": \"Strong. Xi owned the program, the personnel consolidation, and the central policy pivots, even when implementation ran through the State Council and lower-level authorities.\",\n      \"supported_lenses\": [\n        \"8B.1\",\n        \"8B.2\",\n        \"8B.3\",\n        \"8B.4\",\n        \"8B.5\",\n        \"8B.6\",\n        \"8B.8\",\n        \"8B.9\",\n        \"8B.10\"\n      ],\n      \"missing_or_weak_lenses\": [\n        \"8B.7\"\n      ],\n      \"contrary_evidence\": [\n        {\n          \"evidence_id\": \"E0040\",\n          \"explanation\": \"The lockdown harms show the costs of the chosen strategy and prevent an even higher score.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"evidence_id\": \"E0110\",\n          \"explanation\": \"The need for extra discipline and monitoring shows the system still had execution frictions.\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"source_mix\": \"Mostly primary Chinese state documents and official summaries, with Reuters corroboration where helpful. The evidence is unusually rich on program and implementation architecture, but official self-reporting remains a major feature of the record.\",\n      \"structured_prior_summary\": \"Structured local priors were not collected in this experiment.\",\n      \"chapter_rationale\": \"Xi Jinping scores very strongly on competence, at 8.0/10. He articulated a detailed governing program, consolidated personnel control, launched a large stabilization package, and then adapted the COVID policy late in the year after the costs of the earlier approach became unsustainable. The main caveat is that much of the record is official self-report and some of the most visible action came with severe social costs, so the score stops short of the very top tier. The competence judgment is separate from any moral evaluation of repression or coercion.\",\n      \"lower_anchor_rejected\": \"6 rejected because the dossier shows broad strategic control, concrete programmatic machinery, and real adaptation rather than merely competent administration.\",\n      \"higher_anchor_rejected\": \"9 rejected because the evidence still includes severe policy harm, heavy reliance on official self-report, and incomplete independent outcome verification.\",\n      \"manual_review_required\": false,\n      \"manual_review_reason_type\": null,\n      \"manual_review_reason\": null,\n      \"chapter_specific\": [\n        { \"field\": \"program_basis\", \"value\": \"explicit\" },\n        { \"field\": \"program_type\", \"value\": \"policy, regime_control, state_building\" },\n        { \"field\": \"trajectory\", \"value\": \"upward on control, mixed on welfare\" },\n        { \"field\": \"strategic_clarity\", \"value\": \"exceptional\" },\n        { \"field\": \"operationalization\", \"value\": \"strong\" },\n        { \"field\": \"mobilization_and_coordination\", \"value\": \"strong\" },\n        { \"field\": \"adaptation\", \"value\": \"effective\" },\n        { \"field\": \"goal_progress\", \"value\": \"substantial\" },\n        { \"field\": \"durability\", \"value\": \"durable\" },\n        { \"field\": \"morality_separation_check\", \"value\": \"The score reflects execution of the program, not approval of coercive governance.\" }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"dossier_job_key\": \"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:COD:16113\",\n      \"iso3\": \"COD\",\n      \"ruler_id\": \"2830\",\n      \"ruler_year_id\": 16113,\n      \"ruler_name\": \"Félix Tshisekedi\",\n      \"period_start_year\": 2022,\n      \"period_end_year\": 2022,\n      \"chapter_id\": \"8B\",\n      \"rubric_version\": \"chapter_8b_v3\",\n      \"calibration_batch_id\": \"chapter-judge:2022-saturation-v3-stage1-controlled:2022:8B\",\n      \"calibrated_against\": [\n        \"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:BGD:17068\",\n        \"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:BRA:19646\",\n        \"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:CHN:15832\",\n        \"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:USA:15810\"\n      ],\n      \"score_1_to_10\": 4.5,\n      \"insufficient_evidence_reason\": null,\n      \"confidence_score\": 68,\n      \"plausible_score_range\": { \"lower\": 4.0, \"upper\": 5.5 },\n      \"decisive_positive_evidence\": [\n        {\n          \"evidence_id\": \"E0108\",\n          \"explanation\": \"Shows direct oversight of the 145-territories program and concrete project preparation.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"evidence_id\": \"E0111\",\n          \"explanation\": \"Shows direct instructions to resource humanitarian risk-management institutions.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"evidence_id\": \"E0112\",\n          \"explanation\": \"Shows direct judicial and payroll reform directives from the presidency.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"evidence_id\": \"E0118\",\n          \"explanation\": \"Shows prudent macroeconomic policy, including stopping central-bank financing.\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"decisive_negative_evidence\": [\n        {\n          \"evidence_id\": \"E0115\",\n          \"explanation\": \"Shows projected rather than realized job and firm-creation outcomes.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"evidence_id\": \"E0119\",\n          \"explanation\": \"Shows a very low starting vaccination base and only partial catch-up, not completed success.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"evidence_id\": \"E0121\",\n          \"explanation\": \"Shows a newly approved grant and stabilization plan, but not finished delivery by year-end.\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"inherited_baseline_and_constraints\": \"The DRC's 2022 constraints were severe: weak institutions, conflict-affected territory, donor dependence, and limited state reach. Tshisekedi gets credit for setting priorities and some administrative movement, but much of the country-level outcome picture remained beyond the presidency's immediate control.\",\n      \"ruler_attribution\": \"Partial. Tshisekedi clearly directed the agenda and chaired multiple implementation meetings, but much of the work was preparatory, partner-mediated, or incomplete by year-end.\",\n      \"supported_lenses\": [\n        \"8B.1\",\n        \"8B.2\",\n        \"8B.3\",\n        \"8B.4\",\n        \"8B.5\",\n        \"8B.6\",\n        \"8B.8\",\n        \"8B.9\",\n        \"8B.10\"\n      ],\n      \"missing_or_weak_lenses\": [\n        \"8B.7\"\n      ],\n      \"contrary_evidence\": [\n        {\n          \"evidence_id\": \"E0115\",\n          \"explanation\": \"Projected employment and firm creation are not completed 2022 outcomes.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"evidence_id\": \"E0121\",\n          \"explanation\": \"The grant shows mobilization, but it is still a design-and-launch story rather than a finished delivery story.\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"source_mix\": \"Official presidency, IMF, World Bank, WHO, and local reporting. The dossier is rich on directives and program launches but thin on independent completed-outcome verification.\",\n      \"structured_prior_summary\": \"Structured local priors were not collected in this experiment.\",\n      \"chapter_rationale\": \"Tshisekedi's 2022 competence is limited and mixed, at 4.5/10. He clearly set agendas, chaired recovery and governance meetings, and presided over some prudent macro steps, but much of the record stops at planning, procurement, and launch rather than completed delivery. The strongest evidence is that the presidency could mobilize institutions; the weakest is durable, independently verified progress across the major programs. This is enough to avoid a collapse score, but not enough to move into the mixed-or-better tier.\",\n      \"lower_anchor_rejected\": \"3 rejected because the dossier shows repeated convening, agenda-setting, and partial implementation rather than outright paralysis.\",\n      \"higher_anchor_rejected\": \"5 rejected because the best evidence is still mostly preparatory or partial, with weak independent confirmation of completed outcomes.\",\n      \"manual_review_required\": false,\n      \"manual_review_reason_type\": null,\n      \"manual_review_reason\": null,\n      \"chapter_specific\": [\n        { \"field\": \"program_basis\", \"value\": \"mostly_explicit\" },\n        { \"field\": \"program_type\", \"value\": \"policy, state_building\" },\n        { \"field\": \"trajectory\", \"value\": \"upward in agenda-setting, weak in delivery\" },\n        { \"field\": \"strategic_clarity\", \"value\": \"partial\" },\n        { \"field\": \"operationalization\", \"value\": \"weak\" },\n        { \"field\": \"mobilization_and_coordination\", \"value\": \"mixed\" },\n        { \"field\": \"adaptation\", \"value\": \"mixed\" },\n        { \"field\": \"goal_progress\", \"value\": \"too_early_or_unclear\" },\n        { \"field\": \"durability\", \"value\": \"fragile\" },\n        { \"field\": \"morality_separation_check\", \"value\": \"The score reflects execution only, not the moral quality of the political environment.\" }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"dossier_job_key\": \"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:DEU:16984\",\n      \"iso3\": \"DEU\",\n      \"ruler_id\": \"2975\",\n      \"ruler_year_id\": 16984,\n      \"ruler_name\": \"Olaf Scholz\",\n      \"period_start_year\": 2022,\n      \"period_end_year\": 2022,\n      \"chapter_id\": \"8B\",\n      \"rubric_version\": \"chapter_8b_v3\",\n      \"calibration_batch_id\": \"chapter-judge:2022-saturation-v3-stage1-controlled:2022:8B\",\n      \"calibrated_against\": [\n        \"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:BGD:17068\",\n        \"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:CHN:15832\",\n        \"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:RUS:15706\",\n        \"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:USA:15810\"\n      ],\n      \"score_1_to_10\": 6.5,\n      \"insufficient_evidence_reason\": null,\n      \"confidence_score\": 78,\n      \"plausible_score_range\": { \"lower\": 6.0, \"upper\": 7.5 },\n      \"decisive_positive_evidence\": [\n        {\n          \"evidence_id\": \"E0087\",\n          \"explanation\": \"Shows a major defense-policy reorientation with a large special fund and a strategic commitment.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"evidence_id\": \"E0088\",\n          \"explanation\": \"Shows concrete welfare-reform design for Bürgergeld.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"evidence_id\": \"E0091\",\n          \"explanation\": \"Shows a large housing-benefit reform approved in 2022.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"evidence_id\": \"E0092\",\n          \"explanation\": \"Shows direct crisis stabilization of Uniper and the energy supply.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"evidence_id\": \"E0094\",\n          \"explanation\": \"Shows refugee integration apparatus in use by year-end.\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"decisive_negative_evidence\": [\n        {\n          \"evidence_id\": \"E0095\",\n          \"explanation\": \"Shows policy critique over targeting and fiscal sustainability, limiting a stronger competence judgment.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"evidence_id\": \"E0096\",\n          \"explanation\": \"Shows support was appropriate but uncertainty and downside risks remained high.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"evidence_id\": \"E0097\",\n          \"explanation\": \"Shows the relief packages were criticized as expensive and potentially crowding out public goods.\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"inherited_baseline_and_constraints\": \"Scholz governed through coalition constraints, a federal system, and the acute shock of the war in Ukraine and energy संकट. That makes crisis management and coordination central, but also means many implementation levers were shared rather than purely chancellor-controlled.\",\n      \"ruler_attribution\": \"Mostly strong but shared. Scholz clearly owned the governing direction and crisis response, while ministries, Länder, and coalition partners carried much of the implementation burden.\",\n      \"supported_lenses\": [\n        \"8B.1\",\n        \"8B.2\",\n        \"8B.3\",\n        \"8B.4\",\n        \"8B.5\",\n        \"8B.6\",\n        \"8B.8\",\n        \"8B.9\",\n        \"8B.10\"\n      ],\n      \"missing_or_weak_lenses\": [\n        \"8B.7\"\n      ],\n      \"contrary_evidence\": [\n        {\n          \"evidence_id\": \"E0095\",\n          \"explanation\": \"Independent critique says the relief measures were not well targeted enough.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"evidence_id\": \"E0097\",\n          \"explanation\": \"The fiscal burden and long-run sustainability of the response remained contested.\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"source_mix\": \"Primary German government texts plus IMF, OECD, and ifo assessment. The record is unusually strong on policy design and coordination, but less conclusive on durable welfare outcomes in the target year.\",\n      \"structured_prior_summary\": \"Structured local priors were not collected in this experiment.\",\n      \"chapter_rationale\": \"Scholz scores 6.5/10 for broadly effective crisis governance. He combined a clear strategic pivot on defense, energy, and social cushioning with concrete cabinet and legislative follow-through, and there is independent evidence that the refugee and energy responses were functioning by year-end. The main limits are that most benefits were either designed for later rollout or criticized for targeting and fiscal cost, so the record is more about capable response than fully verified durable success. Moral approval of the policy mix is irrelevant to this competence score.\",\n      \"lower_anchor_rejected\": \"5 rejected because the government did more than announce plans: it enacted major reforms, coordinated across institutions, and managed acute crises.\",\n      \"higher_anchor_rejected\": \"7 rejected because several flagship measures were still partly prospective or debated in terms of targeting and sustainability, with incomplete outcome verification.\",\n      \"manual_review_required\": false,\n      \"manual_review_reason_type\": null,\n      \"manual_review_reason\": null,\n      \"chapter_specific\": [\n        { \"field\": \"program_basis\", \"value\": \"explicit\" },\n        { \"field\": \"program_type\", \"value\": \"policy\" },\n        { \"field\": \"trajectory\", \"value\": \"upward under severe shock\" },\n        { \"field\": \"strategic_clarity\", \"value\": \"clear\" },\n        { \"field\": \"operationalization\", \"value\": \"strong\" },\n        { \"field\": \"mobilization_and_coordination\", \"value\": \"strong\" },\n        { \"field\": \"adaptation\", \"value\": \"effective\" },\n        { \"field\": \"goal_progress\", \"value\": \"substantial\" },\n        { \"field\": \"durability\", \"value\": \"mixed\" },\n        { \"field\": \"morality_separation_check\", \"value\": \"The score reflects execution of the program, not approval of the program's morality.\" }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"dossier_job_key\": \"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:EGY:16232\",\n      \"iso3\": \"EGY\",\n      \"ruler_id\": \"2851\",\n      \"ruler_year_id\": 16232,\n      \"ruler_name\": \"Abdel Fattah el-Sisi\",\n      \"period_start_year\": 2022,\n      \"period_end_year\": 2022,\n      \"chapter_id\": \"8B\",\n      \"rubric_version\": \"chapter_8b_v3\",\n      \"calibration_batch_id\": \"chapter-judge:2022-saturation-v3-stage1-controlled:2022:8B\",\n      \"calibrated_against\": [\n        \"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:BGD:17068\",\n        \"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:CHN:15832\",\n        \"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:RUS:15706\",\n        \"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:USA:15810\"\n      ],\n      \"score_1_to_10\": 5.0,\n      \"insufficient_evidence_reason\": null,\n      \"confidence_score\": 66,\n      \"plausible_score_range\": { \"lower\": 4.5, \"upper\": 5.5 },\n      \"decisive_positive_evidence\": [\n        {\n          \"evidence_id\": \"E0079\",\n          \"explanation\": \"Shows direct control over the anti-corruption authority.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"evidence_id\": \"E0082\",\n          \"explanation\": \"Shows a concrete state-ownership policy with private-sector expansion targets.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"evidence_id\": \"E0052\",\n          \"explanation\": \"Shows a direct presidential appointment during the currency crisis.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"evidence_id\": \"E0080\",\n          \"explanation\": \"Shows a formal judicial appointment under a rule-based procedure rather than pure patronage.\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"decisive_negative_evidence\": [\n        {\n          \"evidence_id\": \"E0074\",\n          \"explanation\": \"Shows opacity, domination of policymaking by the security apparatus, and weak transparency.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"evidence_id\": \"E0073\",\n          \"explanation\": \"Shows a military economy built on privileged access and patronage rather than clean institutional performance.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"evidence_id\": \"E0081\",\n          \"explanation\": \"Shows the IMF still needed governance and transparency reforms, implying the system was not yet delivering them.\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"inherited_baseline_and_constraints\": \"Egypt's governance model in 2022 was heavily security-centered and state-led, with many economic levers already concentrated in the presidency and military network. That gives Sisi considerable control, but also means the dossier must distinguish real management from opacity, patronage, and incomplete reform.\",\n      \"ruler_attribution\": \"Strong on control and personnel, weaker on reform quality and transparency. Sisi owns the institutional design, but much of the record shows concentration of power rather than proven high-performance delivery.\",\n      \"supported_lenses\": [\n        \"8B.1\",\n        \"8B.2\",\n        \"8B.3\",\n        \"8B.4\",\n        \"8B.5\",\n        \"8B.6\",\n        \"8B.8\",\n        \"8B.9\",\n        \"8B.10\"\n      ],\n      \"missing_or_weak_lenses\": [\n        \"8B.7\"\n      ],\n      \"contrary_evidence\": [\n        {\n          \"evidence_id\": \"E0074\",\n          \"explanation\": \"Transparency and institutional impartiality are weak, limiting a higher competence score.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"evidence_id\": \"E0073\",\n          \"explanation\": \"The military economy evidence points to entrenched privilege and inefficient allocation.\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"source_mix\": \"Official presidential notices, IMF/World Bank analysis, and independent country reporting. The evidence is strong on control and appointments, but weaker on clean outcome verification and institutional quality.\",\n      \"structured_prior_summary\": \"Structured local priors were not collected in this experiment.\",\n      \"chapter_rationale\": \"Sisi scores 5.0/10: competent at preserving control and making formal moves, but not demonstrably high-performing at reform delivery. The evidence shows direct appointments, a state-ownership policy, and anti-corruption authority control, yet it also shows opacity, patronage, and external pressure for governance reform. The score stays in the middle because the state can move under Sisi, but the dossier does not show that those moves reliably translated into transparent, effective governance. Moral judgments about authoritarianism are excluded from the score.\",\n      \"lower_anchor_rejected\": \"4 rejected because the dossier shows clear presidential control over appointments and policy documents, not mere drift.\",\n      \"higher_anchor_rejected\": \"6 rejected because the strongest evidence points to concentrated control and partial reform, not durable, independently verified administrative success.\",\n      \"manual_review_required\": false,\n      \"manual_review_reason_type\": null,\n      \"manual_review_reason\": null,\n      \"chapter_specific\": [\n        { \"field\": \"program_basis\", \"value\": \"mixed\" },\n        { \"field\": \"program_type\", \"value\": \"policy, regime_control, state_building\" },\n        { \"field\": \"trajectory\", \"value\": \"controlled but reform-limited\" },\n        { \"field\": \"strategic_clarity\", \"value\": \"clear\" },\n        { \"field\": \"operationalization\", \"value\": \"mixed\" },\n        { \"field\": \"mobilization_and_coordination\", \"value\": \"strong\" },\n        { \"field\": \"adaptation\", \"value\": \"mixed\" },\n        { \"field\": \"goal_progress\", \"value\": \"mixed\" },\n        { \"field\": \"durability\", \"value\": \"mixed\" },\n        { \"field\": \"morality_separation_check\", \"value\": \"The score measures execution, not approval of the regime's moral character.\" }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"dossier_job_key\": \"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:ETH:16782\",\n      \"iso3\": \"ETH\",\n      \"ruler_id\": \"2310\",\n      \"ruler_year_id\": 16782,\n      \"ruler_name\": \"Abiy Ahmed\",\n      \"period_start_year\": 2022,\n      \"period_end_year\": 2022,\n      \"chapter_id\": \"8B\",\n      \"rubric_version\": \"chapter_8b_v3\",\n      \"calibration_batch_id\": \"chapter-judge:2022-saturation-v3-stage1-controlled:2022:8B\",\n      \"calibrated_against\": [\n        \"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:BGD:17068\",\n        \"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:CHN:15832\",\n        \"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:RUS:15706\",\n        \"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:USA:15810\"\n      ],\n      \"score_1_to_10\": 5.0,\n      \"insufficient_evidence_reason\": null,\n      \"confidence_score\": 67,\n      \"plausible_score_range\": { \"lower\": 4.5, \"upper\": 5.5 },\n      \"decisive_positive_evidence\": [\n        {\n          \"evidence_id\": \"E0086\",\n          \"explanation\": \"Shows a direct anti-corruption enforcement mechanism created by the administration.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"evidence_id\": \"E0088\",\n          \"explanation\": \"Shows a formal peace-institution setup tied to the national dialogue process.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"evidence_id\": \"E0089\",\n          \"explanation\": \"Shows tangible ceasefire implementation and some humanitarian access.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"evidence_id\": \"E0092\",\n          \"explanation\": \"Shows service restoration progress in Tigray with concrete numbers.\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"decisive_negative_evidence\": [\n        {\n          \"evidence_id\": \"E0041\",\n          \"explanation\": \"Shows the national dialogue was contested and excluded key actors, limiting the strength of the political reconciliation record.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"evidence_id\": \"E0090\",\n          \"explanation\": \"Shows that the ceasefire was still a promise of honest implementation rather than a completed result.\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"inherited_baseline_and_constraints\": \"Abiy governed amid war, fragmentation, and severe administrative strain, so 2022 competence is mostly about whether he could pivot from conflict to reconstruction and coordination. That produces genuine partial credit for the ceasefire and service restoration, but also keeps attribution and durability uncertain.\",\n      \"ruler_attribution\": \"Partial. Abiy clearly directed the post-ceasefire pivot and reform agenda, but many results were incomplete, shared with partners, or contested by excluded actors.\",\n      \"supported_lenses\": [\n        \"8B.1\",\n        \"8B.2\",\n        \"8B.3\",\n        \"8B.4\",\n        \"8B.5\",\n        \"8B.6\",\n        \"8B.8\",\n        \"8B.9\",\n        \"8B.10\"\n      ],\n      \"missing_or_weak_lenses\": [\n        \"8B.7\"\n      ],\n      \"contrary_evidence\": [\n        {\n          \"evidence_id\": \"E0041\",\n          \"explanation\": \"The dialogue process was politically contested and excluded some key groups.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"evidence_id\": \"E0090\",\n          \"explanation\": \"The truce was still in the implementation stage, not a fully proven durable settlement.\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"source_mix\": \"Mostly Ethiopian government and international organization material, with Reuters corroboration on the ceasefire and access issues. The evidence is strongest on directives and partial implementation, weaker on durable national reconciliation.\",\n      \"structured_prior_summary\": \"Structured local priors were not collected in this experiment.\",\n      \"chapter_rationale\": \"Abiy scores 5.0/10. The dossier shows real pivoting: anti-corruption measures, peace-council creation, ceasefire implementation, and service restoration in Tigray. But the strongest evidence is still partial and contested, with many results dependent on partner logistics or not yet complete by year-end. This is enough for a mixed competence score, but not enough for a stronger claim of durable execution. Moral judgments about the war or repression do not affect the score.\",\n      \"lower_anchor_rejected\": \"4 rejected because the record shows actual institutional moves and partial implementation rather than simple failure.\",\n      \"higher_anchor_rejected\": \"6 rejected because the best evidence remains incomplete, contested, and only partly outcome-verified.\",\n      \"manual_review_required\": false,\n      \"manual_review_reason_type\": null,\n      \"manual_review_reason\": null,\n      \"chapter_specific\": [\n        { \"field\": \"program_basis\", \"value\": \"mixed\" },\n        { \"field\": \"program_type\", \"value\": \"policy, survival, state_building\" },\n        { \"field\": \"trajectory\", \"value\": \"recovery from war toward reconstruction\" },\n        { \"field\": \"strategic_clarity\", \"value\": \"partial\" },\n        { \"field\": \"operationalization\", \"value\": \"mixed\" },\n        { \"field\": \"mobilization_and_coordination\", \"value\": \"mixed\" },\n        { \"field\": \"adaptation\", \"value\": \"effective\" },\n        { \"field\": \"goal_progress\", \"value\": \"mixed\" },\n        { \"field\": \"durability\", \"value\": \"fragile\" },\n        { \"field\": \"morality_separation_check\", \"value\": \"The score measures execution, not the morality of the conflict context.\" }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"dossier_job_key\": \"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:IDN:16199\",\n      \"iso3\": \"IDN\",\n      \"ruler_id\": \"2636\",\n      \"ruler_year_id\": 16199,\n      \"ruler_name\": \"Joko Widodo\",\n      \"period_start_year\": 2022,\n      \"period_end_year\": 2022,\n      \"chapter_id\": \"8B\",\n      \"rubric_version\": \"chapter_8b_v3\",\n      \"calibration_batch_id\": \"chapter-judge:2022-saturation-v3-stage1-controlled:2022:8B\",\n      \"calibrated_against\": [\n        \"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:BGD:17068\",\n        \"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:CHN:15832\",\n        \"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:RUS:15706\",\n        \"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:USA:15810\"\n      ],\n      \"score_1_to_10\": 7.5,\n      \"insufficient_evidence_reason\": null,\n      \"confidence_score\": 79,\n      \"plausible_score_range\": { \"lower\": 7.0, \"upper\": 8.5 },\n      \"decisive_positive_evidence\": [\n        {\n          \"evidence_id\": \"E0077\",\n          \"explanation\": \"Shows a direct presidential instruction to accelerate extreme-poverty reduction across ministries and local governments.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"evidence_id\": \"E0098\",\n          \"explanation\": \"Shows 2022 direct-cash distribution reaching 95.9 percent of the target.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"evidence_id\": \"E0099\",\n          \"explanation\": \"Shows fast fiscal consolidation through a smaller-than-target deficit.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"evidence_id\": \"E0100\",\n          \"explanation\": \"Shows clean audit outcomes for most ministries and the central budget, indicating administrative execution quality.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"evidence_id\": \"E0104\",\n          \"explanation\": \"Shows above-target full immunization coverage and a large catch-up campaign.\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"decisive_negative_evidence\": [\n        {\n          \"evidence_id\": \"E0101\",\n          \"explanation\": \"Shows major learning losses and a large education recovery gap.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"evidence_id\": \"E0102\",\n          \"explanation\": \"Shows that poverty and economic insecurity remained substantial despite progress.\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"inherited_baseline_and_constraints\": \"Indonesia benefited from recovery momentum, but Jokowi still had to translate broad goals into bureaucratic coordination across a large archipelago. The dossier shows unusually strong state execution, with some distributional and learning gaps left unresolved.\",\n      \"ruler_attribution\": \"Strong. Jokowi directly owned the major policy directions, appointments, and delivery mechanisms, while local governments and ministries carried much of the implementation.\",\n      \"supported_lenses\": [\n        \"8B.1\",\n        \"8B.2\",\n        \"8B.3\",\n        \"8B.4\",\n        \"8B.5\",\n        \"8B.6\",\n        \"8B.7\",\n        \"8B.8\",\n        \"8B.9\",\n        \"8B.10\"\n      ],\n      \"missing_or_weak_lenses\": [],\n      \"contrary_evidence\": [\n        {\n          \"evidence_id\": \"E0101\",\n          \"explanation\": \"Learning losses remained serious, limiting the claim of full program success.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"evidence_id\": \"E0102\",\n          \"explanation\": \"Residual economic insecurity means the anti-poverty program was strong but not complete.\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"source_mix\": \"Mostly official Indonesian presidential, statistical, audit, and multilateral sources. This is a strong record for both implementation and outcome verification, with the main caveat that some evidence is retrospective.\",\n      \"structured_prior_summary\": \"Structured local priors were not collected in this experiment.\",\n      \"chapter_rationale\": \"Jokowi scores 7.5/10. The dossier shows an explicit governing program converted into concrete instructions, budget discipline, appointed personnel, and measurable rollout that reached targets or nearly so in several areas. The best evidence is not just plan language but later execution and audit material, especially on fiscal consolidation, immunization, and poverty-related delivery. The main constraints are education recovery and residual insecurity, which keep the score below the top tier but still clearly in strong-performance territory. Moral approval of his agenda is irrelevant to the competence score.\",\n      \"lower_anchor_rejected\": \"6 rejected because the record shows broad, measurable execution and several strong outcome markers rather than merely competent planning.\",\n      \"higher_anchor_rejected\": \"8 rejected because some flagship reforms remain uneven across sectors, with major learning and distributional gaps still visible.\",\n      \"manual_review_required\": false,\n      \"manual_review_reason_type\": null,\n      \"manual_review_reason\": null,\n      \"chapter_specific\": [\n        { \"field\": \"program_basis\", \"value\": \"explicit\" },\n        { \"field\": \"program_type\", \"value\": \"policy, state_building\" },\n        { \"field\": \"trajectory\", \"value\": \"upward and measurable\" },\n        { \"field\": \"strategic_clarity\", \"value\": \"clear\" },\n        { \"field\": \"operationalization\", \"value\": \"strong\" },\n        { \"field\": \"mobilization_and_coordination\", \"value\": \"strong\" },\n        { \"field\": \"adaptation\", \"value\": \"effective\" },\n        { \"field\": \"goal_progress\", \"value\": \"substantial\" },\n        { \"field\": \"durability\", \"value\": \"durable\" },\n        { \"field\": \"morality_separation_check\", \"value\": \"The score reflects execution of the program, not approval of its political or moral content.\" }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"dossier_job_key\": \"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:IND:19645\",\n      \"iso3\": \"IND\",\n      \"ruler_id\": \"1517\",\n      \"ruler_year_id\": 19645,\n      \"ruler_name\": \"Narendra Modi\",\n      \"period_start_year\": 2022,\n      \"period_end_year\": 2022,\n      \"chapter_id\": \"8B\",\n      \"rubric_version\": \"chapter_8b_v3\",\n      \"calibration_batch_id\": \"chapter-judge:2022-saturation-v3-stage1-controlled:2022:8B\",\n      \"calibrated_against\": [\n        \"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:BGD:17068\",\n        \"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:CHN:15832\",\n        \"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:RUS:15706\",\n        \"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:USA:15810\"\n      ],\n      \"score_1_to_10\": 7.0,\n      \"insufficient_evidence_reason\": null,\n      \"confidence_score\": 77,\n      \"plausible_score_range\": { \"lower\": 6.5, \"upper\": 7.5 },\n      \"decisive_positive_evidence\": [\n        {\n          \"evidence_id\": \"E0060\",\n          \"explanation\": \"Shows a concrete 2022 budget strategy linked to national infrastructure, skilling, and green investment.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"evidence_id\": \"E0063\",\n          \"explanation\": \"Shows substantial MGNREGS implementation across FY2021-22.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"evidence_id\": \"E0098\",\n          \"explanation\": \"Shows high capital-spending priorities in the 2022 budget.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"evidence_id\": \"E0100\",\n          \"explanation\": \"Shows a clean audit opinion for the central government and most ministries, indicating administrative execution quality.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"evidence_id\": \"E0102\",\n          \"explanation\": \"Shows fiscal and digital-public-infrastructure responses that supported growth and direct transfers.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"evidence_id\": \"E0107\",\n          \"explanation\": \"Shows very strong digital-payment growth and policy infrastructure effects.\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"decisive_negative_evidence\": [\n        {\n          \"evidence_id\": \"E0082\",\n          \"explanation\": \"Shows health-coverage progress but also that targets were not fully met.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"evidence_id\": \"E0101\",\n          \"explanation\": \"Shows major education and household-welfare gaps that dilute the program's broad effectiveness.\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"inherited_baseline_and_constraints\": \"India's 2022 record combines inherited macro resilience, independent monetary policy, and large-scale state programs across a vast federal system. Modi gets credit for strategic direction and execution, but many outcomes are shared with ministries, states, the RBI, and prior buffers.\",\n      \"ruler_attribution\": \"Strong but not exclusive. Modi clearly owned the governing agenda and key appointments, but attribution is shared with the finance ministry, RBI, state governments, and inherited structural conditions.\",\n      \"supported_lenses\": [\n        \"8B.1\",\n        \"8B.2\",\n        \"8B.3\",\n        \"8B.4\",\n        \"8B.5\",\n        \"8B.6\",\n        \"8B.7\",\n        \"8B.8\",\n        \"8B.9\",\n        \"8B.10\"\n      ],\n      \"missing_or_weak_lenses\": [],\n      \"contrary_evidence\": [\n        {\n          \"evidence_id\": \"E0082\",\n          \"explanation\": \"Service rollout was substantial but still incomplete, which keeps the score below the strongest tier.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"evidence_id\": \"E0101\",\n          \"explanation\": \"Learning recovery and distributional equity remained weak relative to the headline achievements.\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"source_mix\": \"Mostly official Indian budget, ministry, audit, and multilateral material, supplemented by Reuters and UNICEF. The record is rich and varied, with the main limitation being attribution across a large federal and institutional system.\",\n      \"structured_prior_summary\": \"Structured local priors were not collected in this experiment.\",\n      \"chapter_rationale\": \"Modi scores 7.0/10. He had a clear, explicit governing agenda and turned it into budgets, appointments, digital infrastructure, welfare delivery, and auditable administrative execution. The strongest evidence is the combination of policy design and observable follow-through, especially on capital spending, digital public infrastructure, and fiscal management. The score is held below the top tier because outcome attribution is shared and some core household and education gaps remain substantial. Moral approval of the agenda is not part of this competence judgment.\",\n      \"lower_anchor_rejected\": \"6 rejected because the dossier shows repeated, measurable implementation and strong administrative control rather than merely competent rhetoric.\",\n      \"higher_anchor_rejected\": \"8 rejected because outcome attribution is still shared with institutions and inherited buffers, and some distributional problems remain unresolved.\",\n      \"manual_review_required\": false,\n      \"manual_review_reason_type\": null,\n      \"manual_review_reason\": null,\n      \"chapter_specific\": [\n        { \"field\": \"program_basis\", \"value\": \"explicit\" },\n        { \"field\": \"program_type\", \"value\": \"policy, state_building\" },\n        { \"field\": \"trajectory\", \"value\": \"upward with distributional gaps\" },\n        { \"field\": \"strategic_clarity\", \"value\": \"clear\" },\n        { \"field\": \"operationalization\", \"value\": \"strong\" },\n        { \"field\": \"mobilization_and_coordination\", \"value\": \"strong\" },\n        { \"field\": \"adaptation\", \"value\": \"effective\" },\n        { \"field\": \"goal_progress\", \"value\": \"substantial\" },\n        { \"field\": \"durability\", \"value\": \"mixed\" },\n        { \"field\": \"morality_separation_check\", \"value\": \"The score measures execution, not approval of the objectives.\" }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"dossier_job_key\": \"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:IRN:19648\",\n      \"iso3\": \"IRN\",\n      \"ruler_id\": \"3412\",\n      \"ruler_year_id\": 19648,\n      \"ruler_name\": \"Ali Khamenei\",\n      \"period_start_year\": 2022,\n      \"period_end_year\": 2022,\n      \"chapter_id\": \"8B\",\n      \"rubric_version\": \"chapter_8b_v3\",\n      \"calibration_batch_id\": \"chapter-judge:2022-saturation-v3-stage1-controlled:2022:8B\",\n      \"calibrated_against\": [\n        \"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:BGD:17068\",\n        \"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:CHN:15832\",\n        \"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:RUS:15706\",\n        \"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:USA:15810\"\n      ],\n      \"score_1_to_10\": 4.5,\n      \"insufficient_evidence_reason\": null,\n      \"confidence_score\": 63,\n      \"plausible_score_range\": { \"lower\": 4.0, \"upper\": 5.0 },\n      \"decisive_positive_evidence\": [\n        {\n          \"evidence_id\": \"E0001\",\n          \"explanation\": \"Defines the Leader's sweeping command and appointment powers in 2022.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"evidence_id\": \"E0060\",\n          \"explanation\": \"Shows a detailed development-plan guideline and economic direction from the Leader's office.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"evidence_id\": \"E0082\",\n          \"explanation\": \"Shows resistance-oriented program framing and a refusal to tie progress to sanctions relief.\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"decisive_negative_evidence\": [\n        {\n          \"evidence_id\": \"E0005\",\n          \"explanation\": \"Shows rigid sanctions-resistance framing rather than clear evidence of effective economic delivery.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"evidence_id\": \"E0083\",\n          \"explanation\": \"Shows crisis framing and accusation without supporting evidence, which does not demonstrate effective governance.\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"inherited_baseline_and_constraints\": \"Khamenei has formal supremacy in Iran's system, but the 2022 record here is mostly declaratory and institutional rather than implementation-heavy. That means the evidence supports strong agenda-setting but not strong proof of competent execution or durable progress.\",\n      \"ruler_attribution\": \"Direct for program framing and formal authority, but weak for execution. The dossier shows what Khamenei said and what the constitutional system empowered, not a robust delivery chain for his objectives.\",\n      \"supported_lenses\": [\n        \"8B.1\",\n        \"8B.2\",\n        \"8B.4\",\n        \"8B.5\",\n        \"8B.6\",\n        \"8B.8\",\n        \"8B.9\",\n        \"8B.10\"\n      ],\n      \"missing_or_weak_lenses\": [\n        \"8B.3\",\n        \"8B.7\"\n      ],\n      \"contrary_evidence\": [\n        {\n          \"evidence_id\": \"E0005\",\n          \"explanation\": \"Sanctions-resilience rhetoric is direction-setting, but it does not prove the program worked.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"evidence_id\": \"E0083\",\n          \"explanation\": \"Crisis accusations are not evidence of competent execution.\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"source_mix\": \"Primary constitutional text plus a mix of state-affiliated and secondary reporting on speeches and program guidelines. The record is thin on implementation evidence and stronger on revealed preferences and formal power.\",\n      \"structured_prior_summary\": \"Structured local priors were not collected in this experiment.\",\n      \"chapter_rationale\": \"Khamenei scores 4.5/10. The dossier gives him clear formal authority and clear ideological direction, but it does not show a robust 2022 execution chain that converts that authority into measurable progress on the chosen program. The evidence is mostly about what the Leader ordered, framed, or wanted, not about durable outcome gains. This is enough to beat a collapse score, but not enough for a mixed-to-strong execution judgment. Moral approval of the regime is irrelevant here.\",\n      \"lower_anchor_rejected\": \"3 rejected because the dossier shows formal authority, repeated program statements, and some institutional ordering rather than an absence of control.\",\n      \"higher_anchor_rejected\": \"5 rejected because the evidence still lacks a convincing implementation and outcome trail, and much of the material is declaratory rather than operational.\",\n      \"manual_review_required\": false,\n      \"manual_review_reason_type\": null,\n      \"manual_review_reason\": null,\n      \"chapter_specific\": [\n        { \"field\": \"program_basis\", \"value\": \"mostly_explicit\" },\n        { \"field\": \"program_type\", \"value\": \"policy, regime_control\" },\n        { \"field\": \"trajectory\", \"value\": \"clear in doctrine, weak in delivery\" },\n        { \"field\": \"strategic_clarity\", \"value\": \"clear\" },\n        { \"field\": \"operationalization\", \"value\": \"weak\" },\n        { \"field\": \"mobilization_and_coordination\", \"value\": \"weak\" },\n        { \"field\": \"adaptation\", \"value\": \"rigid\" },\n        { \"field\": \"goal_progress\", \"value\": \"too_early_or_unclear\" },\n        { \"field\": \"durability\", \"value\": \"mixed\" },\n        { \"field\": \"morality_separation_check\", \"value\": \"The score reflects execution of the ruler's own program, not approval of its moral content.\" }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"dossier_job_key\": \"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:JPN:16638\",\n      \"iso3\": \"JPN\",\n      \"ruler_id\": \"2895\",\n      \"ruler_year_id\": 16638,\n      \"ruler_name\": \"Fumio Kishida\",\n      \"period_start_year\": 2022,\n      \"period_end_year\": 2022,\n      \"chapter_id\": \"8B\",\n      \"rubric_version\": \"chapter_8b_v3\",\n      \"calibration_batch_id\": \"chapter-judge:2022-saturation-v3-stage1-controlled:2022:8B\",\n      \"calibrated_against\": [\n        \"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:BGD:17068\",\n        \"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:CHN:15832\",\n        \"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:RUS:15706\",\n        \"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:USA:15810\"\n      ],\n      \"score_1_to_10\": 6.5,\n      \"insufficient_evidence_reason\": null,\n      \"confidence_score\": 76,\n      \"plausible_score_range\": { \"lower\": 6.0, \"upper\": 7.5 },\n      \"decisive_positive_evidence\": [\n        {\n          \"evidence_id\": \"E0026\",\n          \"explanation\": \"Shows a major security-policy shift and large defense buildup adopted in 2022.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"evidence_id\": \"E0080\",\n          \"explanation\": \"Shows explicit monitoring and workforce-investment coordination in the supplementary budget.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"evidence_id\": \"E0094\",\n          \"explanation\": \"Shows cabinet reshuffling and personnel choices with an experienced lineup.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"evidence_id\": \"E0096\",\n          \"explanation\": \"Shows legislative passage and government-wide implementation machinery for the economic package.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"evidence_id\": \"E0103\",\n          \"explanation\": \"Shows a concrete child-welfare law that expanded local support architecture.\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"decisive_negative_evidence\": [\n        {\n          \"evidence_id\": \"E0099\",\n          \"explanation\": \"Shows real wages falling in fiscal 2022, weakening the growth-and-distribution story.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"evidence_id\": \"E0101\",\n          \"explanation\": \"Shows policy support was criticized as insufficiently targeted.\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"inherited_baseline_and_constraints\": \"Japan in 2022 faced imported inflation, security shock, and slow wage growth. Kishida's competence is therefore partly about whether he could retool policy and institutions under external pressure, not whether he could escape the macro environment entirely.\",\n      \"ruler_attribution\": \"Strong but shared. Kishida clearly drove the agenda and coordination, but outcomes depended heavily on ministries, coalition processes, firms, and the Bank of Japan.\",\n      \"supported_lenses\": [\n        \"8B.1\",\n        \"8B.2\",\n        \"8B.3\",\n        \"8B.4\",\n        \"8B.5\",\n        \"8B.6\",\n        \"8B.8\",\n        \"8B.9\",\n        \"8B.10\"\n      ],\n      \"missing_or_weak_lenses\": [\n        \"8B.7\"\n      ],\n      \"contrary_evidence\": [\n        {\n          \"evidence_id\": \"E0099\",\n          \"explanation\": \"Real wage decline is a concrete outcome that stops the score from moving higher.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"evidence_id\": \"E0101\",\n          \"explanation\": \"OECD criticism of targeting and subsidy design limits the competence ceiling.\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"source_mix\": \"Primarily Japanese government and agency records, supplemented by IMF, OECD, Reuters, and the CAA audit-style material. The evidence is fairly strong on implementation architecture and policy direction, with more mixed outcome signals.\",\n      \"structured_prior_summary\": \"Structured local priors were not collected in this experiment.\",\n      \"chapter_rationale\": \"Kishida scores 6.5/10. He translated a clear policy program into cabinet reshuffles, legislation, budget coordination, and crisis response, and there is real evidence of implementation machinery working by late 2022. The main reason the score does not rise higher is that the outcome story is mixed: real wages fell, and independent assessments still criticized some support design. The record is therefore competent and fairly effective, but not durable or fully settled enough for the strong top tier. Moral judgments about defense buildup or other policy aims do not affect the score.\",\n      \"lower_anchor_rejected\": \"5 rejected because the dossier contains real legislative, budgetary, and coordination execution rather than merely declaratory leadership.\",\n      \"higher_anchor_rejected\": \"7 rejected because the outcome record is still mixed and some flagship measures were judged under-targeted or only partially realized.\",\n      \"manual_review_required\": false,\n      \"manual_review_reason_type\": null,\n      \"manual_review_reason\": null,\n      \"chapter_specific\": [\n        { \"field\": \"program_basis\", \"value\": \"explicit\" },\n        { \"field\": \"program_type\", \"value\": \"policy, state_building, international_influence\" },\n        { \"field\": \"trajectory\", \"value\": \"adaptive but outcome-mixed\" },\n        { \"field\": \"strategic_clarity\", \"value\": \"clear\" },\n        { \"field\": \"operationalization\", \"value\": \"strong\" },\n        { \"field\": \"mobilization_and_coordination\", \"value\": \"strong\" },\n        { \"field\": \"adaptation\", \"value\": \"effective\" },\n        { \"field\": \"goal_progress\", \"value\": \"substantial\" },\n        { \"field\": \"durability\", \"value\": \"mixed\" },\n        { \"field\": \"morality_separation_check\", \"value\": \"The score reflects execution, not approval of the defense or economic agenda.\" }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"dossier_job_key\": \"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:MEX:15801\",\n      \"iso3\": \"MEX\",\n      \"ruler_id\": \"2779\",\n      \"ruler_year_id\": 15801,\n      \"ruler_name\": \"Andrés Manuel López Obrador\",\n      \"period_start_year\": 2022,\n      \"period_end_year\": 2022,\n      \"chapter_id\": \"8B\",\n      \"rubric_version\": \"chapter_8b_v3\",\n      \"calibration_batch_id\": \"chapter-judge:2022-saturation-v3-stage1-controlled:2022:8B\",\n      \"calibrated_against\": [\n        \"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:BGD:17068\",\n        \"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:CHN:15832\",\n        \"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:RUS:15706\",\n        \"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:USA:15810\"\n      ],\n      \"score_1_to_10\": 6.0,\n      \"insufficient_evidence_reason\": null,\n      \"confidence_score\": 75,\n      \"plausible_score_range\": { \"lower\": 5.5, \"upper\": 6.5 },\n      \"decisive_positive_evidence\": [\n        {\n          \"evidence_id\": \"E0058\",\n          \"explanation\": \"Shows a mandatory health program with clear federalization goals.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"evidence_id\": \"E0065\",\n          \"explanation\": \"Shows a large-scale cash-benefit rollout with explicit coverage claims.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"evidence_id\": \"E0087\",\n          \"explanation\": \"Shows increased education budgets for 2022.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"evidence_id\": \"E0088\",\n          \"explanation\": \"Shows a concrete delivery mechanism for school funding.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"evidence_id\": \"E0090\",\n          \"explanation\": \"Shows a major infrastructure delivery milestone at AIFA.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"evidence_id\": \"E0096\",\n          \"explanation\": \"Shows a large World Bank-backed inclusive-growth package.\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"decisive_negative_evidence\": [\n        {\n          \"evidence_id\": \"E0093\",\n          \"explanation\": \"Shows a key energy reform failed in Congress.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"evidence_id\": \"E0098\",\n          \"explanation\": \"Shows audit irregularities in a flagship infrastructure project.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"evidence_id\": \"E0101\",\n          \"explanation\": \"Shows weak controls and missing documentation in the school program.\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"inherited_baseline_and_constraints\": \"AMLO inherited a system with long-standing inequality and institutional weakness, and much of his program was implemented through budget reallocations and federal social policy rather than deep institutional overhaul. That allows real credit for delivery, but also means project execution and audit quality are central to the judgment.\",\n      \"ruler_attribution\": \"Moderately strong. AMLO clearly drove the policy agenda and delivery model, but some flagship projects show cost overruns, legislative defeat, and implementation-control problems.\",\n      \"supported_lenses\": [\n        \"8B.1\",\n        \"8B.2\",\n        \"8B.3\",\n        \"8B.4\",\n        \"8B.5\",\n        \"8B.6\",\n        \"8B.8\",\n        \"8B.9\",\n        \"8B.10\"\n      ],\n      \"missing_or_weak_lenses\": [\n        \"8B.7\"\n      ],\n      \"contrary_evidence\": [\n        {\n          \"evidence_id\": \"E0093\",\n          \"explanation\": \"The electricity overhaul defeat shows limits in translating policy ambition into law.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"evidence_id\": \"E0101\",\n          \"explanation\": \"The audit failures in La Escuela es Nuestra show administrative weakness despite large spending.\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"source_mix\": \"Mostly official Mexican presidential and ministry records, plus World Bank, UNICEF, Reuters, and audit reporting. The record is rich on declared welfare and infrastructure action but mixed on controls, execution quality, and durability.\",\n      \"structured_prior_summary\": \"Structured local priors were not collected in this experiment.\",\n      \"chapter_rationale\": \"AMLO scores 6.0/10. He clearly governed through an explicit welfare and state-intervention program, and the dossier shows repeated, concrete budget, transfer, education, health, and infrastructure actions. The counterweight is that some flagship initiatives had control problems, cost overruns, or legislative defeat, which makes the execution record mixed rather than strong. There is real progress, but not enough independently verified durable success across the whole portfolio to justify a higher score. Moral judgments about his politics are excluded from the competence score.\",\n      \"lower_anchor_rejected\": \"5 rejected because the dossier shows sustained, multi-sector delivery at scale rather than merely rhetorical governance.\",\n      \"higher_anchor_rejected\": \"7 rejected because audit failures, project overruns, and legislative setbacks limit the durability and quality of execution.\",\n      \"manual_review_required\": false,\n      \"manual_review_reason_type\": null,\n      \"manual_review_reason\": null,\n      \"chapter_specific\": [\n        { \"field\": \"program_basis\", \"value\": \"explicit\" },\n        { \"field\": \"program_type\", \"value\": \"policy, state_building\" },\n        { \"field\": \"trajectory\", \"value\": \"upward but uneven\" },\n        { \"field\": \"strategic_clarity\", \"value\": \"clear\" },\n        { \"field\": \"operationalization\", \"value\": \"strong\" },\n        { \"field\": \"mobilization_and_coordination\", \"value\": \"mixed\" },\n        { \"field\": \"adaptation\", \"value\": \"mixed\" },\n        { \"field\": \"goal_progress\", \"value\": \"mixed\" },\n        { \"field\": \"durability\", \"value\": \"mixed\" },\n        { \"field\": \"morality_separation_check\", \"value\": \"The score measures execution, not approval of the program's moral or ideological content.\" }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"dossier_job_key\": \"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:NGA:15787\",\n      \"iso3\": \"NGA\",\n      \"ruler_id\": \"2776\",\n      \"ruler_year_id\": 15787,\n      \"ruler_name\": \"Muhammadu Buhari\",\n      \"period_start_year\": 2022,\n      \"period_end_year\": 2022,\n      \"chapter_id\": \"8B\",\n      \"rubric_version\": \"chapter_8b_v3\",\n      \"calibration_batch_id\": \"chapter-judge:2022-saturation-v3-stage1-controlled:2022:8B\",\n      \"calibrated_against\": [\n        \"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:BGD:17068\",\n        \"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:CHN:15832\",\n        \"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:RUS:15706\",\n        \"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:USA:15810\"\n      ],\n      \"score_1_to_10\": 4.0,\n      \"insufficient_evidence_reason\": null,\n      \"confidence_score\": 70,\n      \"plausible_score_range\": { \"lower\": 3.5, \"upper\": 4.5 },\n      \"decisive_positive_evidence\": [\n        {\n          \"evidence_id\": \"E0055\",\n          \"explanation\": \"Shows the 2022 budget was enacted and fiscal-year continuity restored.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"evidence_id\": \"E0060\",\n          \"explanation\": \"Shows a technocratic statistics appointment.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"evidence_id\": \"E0091\",\n          \"explanation\": \"Shows a major health-financing law signed into force.\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"decisive_negative_evidence\": [\n        {\n          \"evidence_id\": \"E0061\",\n          \"explanation\": \"Shows self-justifying cabinet-management rhetoric without independent proof of competence.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"evidence_id\": \"E0090\",\n          \"explanation\": \"Shows anti-corruption rhetoric that did not resolve the underlying performance problem.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"evidence_id\": \"E0103\",\n          \"explanation\": \"Shows the university strike and the government's reactive response, a sign of weak governance.\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"inherited_baseline_and_constraints\": \"Nigeria's 2022 baseline was defined by fiscal weakness, inflation, labor unrest, and institutional strain. Buhari had enough authority to sign budgets and laws, but the evidence does not show that he converted those instruments into consistently effective execution.\",\n      \"ruler_attribution\": \"Direct where shown, but the dossier is dominated by self-description and reactive responses. The record supports some formal action, not strong proof of effective governance.\",\n      \"supported_lenses\": [\n        \"8B.1\",\n        \"8B.2\",\n        \"8B.3\",\n        \"8B.4\",\n        \"8B.5\",\n        \"8B.6\",\n        \"8B.8\",\n        \"8B.9\",\n        \"8B.10\"\n      ],\n      \"missing_or_weak_lenses\": [\n        \"8B.7\"\n      ],\n      \"contrary_evidence\": [\n        {\n          \"evidence_id\": \"E0103\",\n          \"explanation\": \"The eight-month strike and partial resolution are concrete signs of implementation weakness.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"evidence_id\": \"E0090\",\n          \"explanation\": \"Anti-corruption messaging is not the same as effective anti-corruption delivery.\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"source_mix\": \"Mostly official State House and ministry material, with Reuters-syndicated reporting for some developments. The evidence is strongest for formal acts and weakest for outcome quality and independent audit trail.\",\n      \"structured_prior_summary\": \"Structured local priors were not collected in this experiment.\",\n      \"chapter_rationale\": \"Buhari scores 4.0/10. He could still sign budgets, appoint technocrats, and enact major laws, but the record is dominated by self-description, weak follow-through, and visible governance frictions such as the university strike. The best evidence shows formal control, not effective conversion of that control into durable delivery. That is enough to avoid a collapse score, but not enough for a mixed or competent judgment. Moral judgments about corruption or politics are excluded from the score.\",\n      \"lower_anchor_rejected\": \"3 rejected because the dossier shows formal state action, not complete administrative breakdown.\",\n      \"higher_anchor_rejected\": \"5 rejected because the evidence of effective execution and durable outcome progress is too thin and too reactive.\",\n      \"manual_review_required\": false,\n      \"manual_review_reason_type\": null,\n      \"manual_review_reason\": null,\n      \"chapter_specific\": [\n        { \"field\": \"program_basis\", \"value\": \"mostly_explicit\" },\n        { \"field\": \"program_type\", \"value\": \"policy, state_building\" },\n        { \"field\": \"trajectory\", \"value\": \"stalled and reactive\" },\n        { \"field\": \"strategic_clarity\", \"value\": \"partial\" },\n        { \"field\": \"operationalization\", \"value\": \"weak\" },\n        { \"field\": \"mobilization_and_coordination\", \"value\": \"weak\" },\n        { \"field\": \"adaptation\", \"value\": \"mixed\" },\n        { \"field\": \"goal_progress\", \"value\": \"net_regression\" },\n        { \"field\": \"durability\", \"value\": \"fragile\" },\n        { \"field\": \"morality_separation_check\", \"value\": \"The score reflects execution, not approval or disapproval of the program's moral content.\" }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"dossier_job_key\": \"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:PAK:16682\",\n      \"iso3\": \"PAK\",\n      \"ruler_id\": \"2911\",\n      \"ruler_year_id\": 16682,\n      \"ruler_name\": \"Shehbaz Sharif\",\n      \"period_start_year\": 2022,\n      \"period_end_year\": 2022,\n      \"chapter_id\": \"8B\",\n      \"rubric_version\": \"chapter_8b_v3\",\n      \"calibration_batch_id\": \"chapter-judge:2022-saturation-v3-stage1-controlled:2022:8B\",\n      \"calibrated_against\": [\n        \"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:BGD:17068\",\n        \"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:CHN:15832\",\n        \"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:RUS:15706\",\n        \"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:USA:15810\"\n      ],\n      \"score_1_to_10\": 4.5,\n      \"insufficient_evidence_reason\": null,\n      \"confidence_score\": 68,\n      \"plausible_score_range\": { \"lower\": 4.0, \"upper\": 5.0 },\n      \"decisive_positive_evidence\": [\n        {\n          \"evidence_id\": \"E0050\",\n          \"explanation\": \"Shows an immediate move to install a finance minister and restart IMF talks.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"evidence_id\": \"E0056\",\n          \"explanation\": \"Shows a clear fiscal strategy tied to stabilization and the IMF program.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"evidence_id\": \"E0075\",\n          \"explanation\": \"Shows a climate-resilient recovery framework launched in 2022.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"evidence_id\": \"E0093\",\n          \"explanation\": \"Shows the formation of a coalition cabinet focused on stabilization.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"evidence_id\": \"E0098\",\n          \"explanation\": \"Shows a World Bank-linked flood recovery and reconstruction plan.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"evidence_id\": \"E0100\",\n          \"explanation\": \"Shows multilateral funding for flood recovery and social protection.\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"decisive_negative_evidence\": [\n        {\n          \"evidence_id\": \"E0094\",\n          \"explanation\": \"Shows austerity and expenditure cuts driven by crisis rather than confident program execution.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"evidence_id\": \"E0095\",\n          \"explanation\": \"Shows heavy IMF constraint and a budget response to macro fragility.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"evidence_id\": \"E0098\",\n          \"explanation\": \"Shows a disaster-scale recovery need that the government could not itself resolve quickly.\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"inherited_baseline_and_constraints\": \"Sharif inherited a severe balance-of-payments crisis, coalition constraints, and then catastrophic flood damage. The dossier therefore tests crisis management more than clean peacetime execution, and much of the policy space was IMF- and donor-constrained.\",\n      \"ruler_attribution\": \"Moderate. Sharif clearly acted quickly on staffing, budgeting, and recovery frameworks, but the overarching crisis was inherited and many key levers were externally constrained.\",\n      \"supported_lenses\": [\n        \"8B.1\",\n        \"8B.2\",\n        \"8B.3\",\n        \"8B.4\",\n        \"8B.5\",\n        \"8B.6\",\n        \"8B.8\",\n        \"8B.9\",\n        \"8B.10\"\n      ],\n      \"missing_or_weak_lenses\": [\n        \"8B.7\"\n      ],\n      \"contrary_evidence\": [\n        {\n          \"evidence_id\": \"E0094\",\n          \"explanation\": \"Budget cuts and expenditure restraint show crisis management, but also underline weakness and dependence.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"evidence_id\": \"E0095\",\n          \"explanation\": \"IMF constraints and inherited fragility limit how much of the result can be called Sharif's own competence.\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"source_mix\": \"Mostly Pakistan government budget documents and Reuters/World Bank/IMF material. The dossier is strong on reactive crisis management and weaker on durable 2022 outcomes.\",\n      \"structured_prior_summary\": \"Structured local priors were not collected in this experiment.\",\n      \"chapter_rationale\": \"Sharif scores 4.5/10. He moved quickly to restart IMF talks, staff the cabinet, and launch recovery frameworks, which shows real crisis-response capacity. But the context is overwhelmingly one of inherited macro fragility and external constraint, and the dossier does not show durable year-end delivery beyond emergency stabilization. This is enough for a limited positive score, but not for a mixed or effective one. Moral judgments about the coalition or crisis politics are excluded.\",\n      \"lower_anchor_rejected\": \"3 rejected because the dossier shows active cabinet formation, budget action, and recovery planning rather than paralysis.\",\n      \"higher_anchor_rejected\": \"5 rejected because much of the record is constrained crisis management and donor/IMF dependence rather than clearly successful execution.\",\n      \"manual_review_required\": false,\n      \"manual_review_reason_type\": null,\n      \"manual_review_reason\": null,\n      \"chapter_specific\": [\n        { \"field\": \"program_basis\", \"value\": \"mixed\" },\n        { \"field\": \"program_type\", \"value\": \"policy, survival\" },\n        { \"field\": \"trajectory\", \"value\": \"crisis stabilization, not full recovery\" },\n        { \"field\": \"strategic_clarity\", \"value\": \"partial\" },\n        { \"field\": \"operationalization\", \"value\": \"weak\" },\n        { \"field\": \"mobilization_and_coordination\", \"value\": \"mixed\" },\n        { \"field\": \"adaptation\", \"value\": \"mixed\" },\n        { \"field\": \"goal_progress\", \"value\": \"mixed\" },\n        { \"field\": \"durability\", \"value\": \"fragile\" },\n        { \"field\": \"morality_separation_check\", \"value\": \"The score measures execution, not approval of the coalition or austerity politics.\" }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"dossier_job_key\": \"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:PHL:16194\",\n      \"iso3\": \"PHL\",\n      \"ruler_id\": \"2844\",\n      \"ruler_year_id\": 16194,\n      \"ruler_name\": \"Bongbong Marcos\",\n      \"period_start_year\": 2022,\n      \"period_end_year\": 2022,\n      \"chapter_id\": \"8B\",\n      \"rubric_version\": \"chapter_8b_v3\",\n      \"calibration_batch_id\": \"chapter-judge:2022-saturation-v3-stage1-controlled:2022:8B\",\n      \"calibrated_against\": [\n        \"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:BGD:17068\",\n        \"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:CHN:15832\",\n        \"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:RUS:15706\",\n        \"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:USA:15810\"\n      ],\n      \"score_1_to_10\": 6.0,\n      \"insufficient_evidence_reason\": null,\n      \"confidence_score\": 74,\n      \"plausible_score_range\": { \"lower\": 5.5, \"upper\": 6.5 },\n      \"decisive_positive_evidence\": [\n        {\n          \"evidence_id\": \"E0071\",\n          \"explanation\": \"Shows rapid first-100-days relief to farmers and vulnerable households.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"evidence_id\": \"E0074\",\n          \"explanation\": \"Shows the first full-year budget and priority sectors of the new administration.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"evidence_id\": \"E0093\",\n          \"explanation\": \"Shows early, deliberate staffing of the economic team.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"evidence_id\": \"E0095\",\n          \"explanation\": \"Shows active management of security-bureaucracy leadership.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"evidence_id\": \"E0096\",\n          \"explanation\": \"Shows executive replacement of a core coordinator to reconfigure the Malacañang center.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"evidence_id\": \"E0098\",\n          \"explanation\": \"Shows a high-volume vaccination rollout with explicit targets.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"evidence_id\": \"E0100\",\n          \"explanation\": \"Shows school reopening and learning-recovery measures in motion.\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"decisive_negative_evidence\": [\n        {\n          \"evidence_id\": \"E0053\",\n          \"explanation\": \"Shows macro headwinds and inflation that constrained the administration's first-year performance.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"evidence_id\": \"E0101\",\n          \"explanation\": \"Shows education recovery and household coverage still had important gaps.\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"inherited_baseline_and_constraints\": \"Marcos inherited a post-pandemic recovery, inflation pressure, and a large bureaucracy whose performance depended heavily on cabinet teams and sectoral agencies. The dossier therefore rewards early staffing and delivery, but not claims of fully proven long-run success.\",\n      \"ruler_attribution\": \"Moderate to strong. Marcos clearly selected his economic team and set budget priorities, but several service-delivery results are delegated to departments and are still early-stage.\",\n      \"supported_lenses\": [\n        \"8B.1\",\n        \"8B.2\",\n        \"8B.3\",\n        \"8B.4\",\n        \"8B.5\",\n        \"8B.6\",\n        \"8B.8\",\n        \"8B.9\",\n        \"8B.10\"\n      ],\n      \"missing_or_weak_lenses\": [\n        \"8B.7\"\n      ],\n      \"contrary_evidence\": [\n        {\n          \"evidence_id\": \"E0053\",\n          \"explanation\": \"Inflation and external weakness limited the score ceiling.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"evidence_id\": \"E0101\",\n          \"explanation\": \"Outcome evidence in education and service quality remained incomplete.\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"source_mix\": \"Primarily Philippine government releases, with Reuters and UNICEF/World Bank context. The record is strong on staffing and early program rollout, weaker on durability and independent outcome audits.\",\n      \"structured_prior_summary\": \"Structured local priors were not collected in this experiment.\",\n      \"chapter_rationale\": \"Bongbong Marcos scores 6.0/10. He quickly assembled a team, set budgets, and pushed visible first-100-days delivery, so the dossier clearly shows action rather than inertia. The limits are that many results are still early, delegated, or partially verified, while macro headwinds and education gaps remain substantial. This lands him in the mixed-to-good range, short of stronger competence because durable outcomes are not yet fully shown. Moral judgments about the dynasty or politics are excluded.\",\n      \"lower_anchor_rejected\": \"5 rejected because the record shows broad executive staffing, budget action, and concrete delivery measures in the first months.\",\n      \"higher_anchor_rejected\": \"7 rejected because many results remain early-stage and independent long-run outcome verification is still thin.\",\n      \"manual_review_required\": false,\n      \"manual_review_reason_type\": null,\n      \"manual_review_reason\": null,\n      \"chapter_specific\": [\n        { \"field\": \"program_basis\", \"value\": \"explicit\" },\n        { \"field\": \"program_type\", \"value\": \"policy, state_building\" },\n        { \"field\": \"trajectory\", \"value\": \"early momentum, still provisional\" },\n        { \"field\": \"strategic_clarity\", \"value\": \"clear\" },\n        { \"field\": \"operationalization\", \"value\": \"mixed\" },\n        { \"field\": \"mobilization_and_coordination\", \"value\": \"strong\" },\n        { \"field\": \"adaptation\", \"value\": \"mixed\" },\n        { \"field\": \"goal_progress\", \"value\": \"mixed\" },\n        { \"field\": \"durability\", \"value\": \"too_early\" },\n        { \"field\": \"morality_separation_check\", \"value\": \"The score reflects execution, not approval of the Marcos family or politics.\" }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"dossier_job_key\": \"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:RUS:15706\",\n      \"iso3\": \"RUS\",\n      \"ruler_id\": \"2759\",\n      \"ruler_year_id\": 15706,\n      \"ruler_name\": \"Vladimir Putin\",\n      \"period_start_year\": 2022,\n      \"period_end_year\": 2022,\n      \"chapter_id\": \"8B\",\n      \"rubric_version\": \"chapter_8b_v3\",\n      \"calibration_batch_id\": \"chapter-judge:2022-saturation-v3-stage1-controlled:2022:8B\",\n      \"calibrated_against\": [\n        \"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:BGD:17068\",\n        \"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:CHN:15832\",\n        \"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:BRA:19646\",\n        \"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:USA:15810\"\n      ],\n      \"score_1_to_10\": 3.5,\n      \"insufficient_evidence_reason\": null,\n      \"confidence_score\": 82,\n      \"plausible_score_range\": { \"lower\": 3.0, \"upper\": 4.5 },\n      \"decisive_positive_evidence\": [\n        {\n          \"evidence_id\": \"E0017\",\n          \"explanation\": \"Shows direct presidential escalation into the Ukraine war.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"evidence_id\": \"E0147\",\n          \"explanation\": \"Shows Putin's own public justification for the invasion decision.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"evidence_id\": \"E0161\",\n          \"explanation\": \"Shows emergency stabilization tools that kept the financial system functioning after sanctions.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"evidence_id\": \"E0163\",\n          \"explanation\": \"Shows some domestic stabilization despite the war shock.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"evidence_id\": \"E0176\",\n          \"explanation\": \"Shows command authority still capable of mobilizing a new strategic-industrial program.\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"decisive_negative_evidence\": [\n        {\n          \"evidence_id\": \"E0164\",\n          \"explanation\": \"Shows the scale of sanctions shock and reserve disruption created by Putin's own war choice.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"evidence_id\": \"E0165\",\n          \"explanation\": \"Shows the macro downturn and reserve isolation that followed.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"evidence_id\": \"E0169\",\n          \"explanation\": \"Shows a year-end budget execution deficit rather than the fiscal strength implied by the original strategy.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"evidence_id\": \"E0073\",\n          \"explanation\": \"Shows the regime's repressive apparatus expanding rather than a healthy, adaptive governing environment.\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"inherited_baseline_and_constraints\": \"Putin governed a highly centralized system, which should have supported top-down execution, but his 2022 war decision created the dominant constraint on everything else. The result is a paradoxical record: strong coercive control and mobilization capacity, but a major strategic reversal in the core war program and severe macro costs.\",\n      \"ruler_attribution\": \"Direct and very strong for the war, repression, and strategic pivot. The remaining economic stabilization was partly central-bank and bureaucratic, but it occurred inside the framework created by Putin's own decisions.\",\n      \"supported_lenses\": [\n        \"8B.1\",\n        \"8B.2\",\n        \"8B.3\",\n        \"8B.4\",\n        \"8B.5\",\n        \"8B.6\",\n        \"8B.8\",\n        \"8B.9\",\n        \"8B.10\"\n      ],\n      \"missing_or_weak_lenses\": [\n        \"8B.7\"\n      ],\n      \"contrary_evidence\": [\n        {\n          \"evidence_id\": \"E0164\",\n          \"explanation\": \"The sanctions and reserve shock show the scale of strategic self-harm from the war decision.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"evidence_id\": \"E0165\",\n          \"explanation\": \"The OECD's outlook underscores how badly the external and fiscal environment deteriorated.\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"source_mix\": \"A mix of Kremlin, Bank of Russia, IMF, OECD, Reuters, and rights-monitoring material. The record is unusually strong on war mobilization and repression, but it also documents a severe strategic and macroeconomic setback.\",\n      \"structured_prior_summary\": \"Available local priors: V-Dem accountability -0.61, V-Dem rule of law 0.171, WGI rule of law -1.1952940225601196, government effectiveness -0.6954110264778137, regulatory quality -1.1419726610183716. These are context only, not score drivers by themselves.\",\n      \"chapter_rationale\": \"Putin scores 3.5/10. He undeniably exercised command authority, mobilized the state, and could still push through repressive and strategic measures in 2022, so this is not a collapse score. But the core program of war and geopolitical force produced a major strategic reversal, sanctions shock, and a weaker fiscal-economic trajectory than the regime publicly claimed. The record shows coercive control more than successful execution of the ruler's own goals. Moral severity is excluded from the score, but strategic failure is not.\",\n      \"lower_anchor_rejected\": \"2 rejected because Putin retained substantial command capacity and could still mobilize the state and maintain regime control.\",\n      \"higher_anchor_rejected\": \"4 rejected because the central war program suffered a major strategic setback and the economic trajectory deteriorated sharply under sanctions.\",\n      \"manual_review_required\": false,\n      \"manual_review_reason_type\": null,\n      \"manual_review_reason\": null,\n      \"chapter_specific\": [\n        { \"field\": \"program_basis\", \"value\": \"explicit\" },\n        { \"field\": \"program_type\", \"value\": \"policy, regime_control, international_influence\" },\n        { \"field\": \"trajectory\", \"value\": \"high control, strategic failure\" },\n        { \"field\": \"strategic_clarity\", \"value\": \"clear\" },\n        { \"field\": \"operationalization\", \"value\": \"strong\" },\n        { \"field\": \"mobilization_and_coordination\", \"value\": \"strong\" },\n        { \"field\": \"adaptation\", \"value\": \"mixed\" },\n        { \"field\": \"goal_progress\", \"value\": \"major_reversal\" },\n        { \"field\": \"durability\", \"value\": \"fragile\" },\n        { \"field\": \"morality_separation_check\", \"value\": \"The score reflects execution and strategic advance, not the moral abhorrence of the war.\" }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"dossier_job_key\": \"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:THA:19649\",\n      \"iso3\": \"THA\",\n      \"ruler_id\": \"3414\",\n      \"ruler_year_id\": 19649,\n      \"ruler_name\": \"Prayut Chan-o-cha\",\n      \"period_start_year\": 2022,\n      \"period_end_year\": 2022,\n      \"chapter_id\": \"8B\",\n      \"rubric_version\": \"chapter_8b_v3\",\n      \"calibration_batch_id\": \"chapter-judge:2022-saturation-v3-stage1-controlled:2022:8B\",\n      \"calibrated_against\": [\n        \"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:BGD:17068\",\n        \"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:CHN:15832\",\n        \"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:RUS:15706\",\n        \"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:USA:15810\"\n      ],\n      \"score_1_to_10\": 5.5,\n      \"insufficient_evidence_reason\": null,\n      \"confidence_score\": 72,\n      \"plausible_score_range\": { \"lower\": 5.0, \"upper\": 6.5 },\n      \"decisive_positive_evidence\": [\n        {\n          \"evidence_id\": \"E0099\",\n          \"explanation\": \"Shows budget passage and explicit recovery intent.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"evidence_id\": \"E0100\",\n          \"explanation\": \"Shows a final budget approval for the next fiscal year.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"evidence_id\": \"E0101\",\n          \"explanation\": \"Shows concrete EV tax incentives and industrial policy.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"evidence_id\": \"E0102\",\n          \"explanation\": \"Shows diesel-tax relief as direct crisis management.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"evidence_id\": \"E0103\",\n          \"explanation\": \"Shows tourism reopening as a targeted sector-revival policy.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"evidence_id\": \"E0104\",\n          \"explanation\": \"Shows a year-end investment boom in applications and coordinated approvals.\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"decisive_negative_evidence\": [\n        {\n          \"evidence_id\": \"E0056\",\n          \"explanation\": \"Shows poverty pressure and the need for more targeted assistance.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"evidence_id\": \"E0105\",\n          \"explanation\": \"Shows investment pledges still fell sharply in part of 2022, limiting the strength of the recovery story.\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"inherited_baseline_and_constraints\": \"Prayut's 2022 record was shaped by post-pandemic recovery, inflation, coalition politics, and a system in which much of execution runs through ministries and agencies. He had enough control to steer budgets and sectoral incentives, but not enough to produce uniformly strong outcomes.\",\n      \"ruler_attribution\": \"Moderate. Prayut clearly controlled the budget, cabinet, and sectoral policy direction, but the results were mixed and often mediated by broader economic conditions.\",\n      \"supported_lenses\": [\n        \"8B.1\",\n        \"8B.2\",\n        \"8B.3\",\n        \"8B.4\",\n        \"8B.5\",\n        \"8B.6\",\n        \"8B.8\",\n        \"8B.9\",\n        \"8B.10\"\n      ],\n      \"missing_or_weak_lenses\": [\n        \"8B.7\"\n      ],\n      \"contrary_evidence\": [\n        {\n          \"evidence_id\": \"E0056\",\n          \"explanation\": \"Poverty pressures remained real, which cuts against any strong success claim.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"evidence_id\": \"E0105\",\n          \"explanation\": \"A drop in some investment indicators shows the recovery was uneven.\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"source_mix\": \"Mostly Thai government, Reuters, and budget/investment reporting. The evidence is strong on policy moves and sectoral reopening, but mixed on broad durable outcomes.\",\n      \"structured_prior_summary\": \"Structured local priors were not collected in this experiment.\",\n      \"chapter_rationale\": \"Prayut scores 5.5/10. He clearly managed the cabinet and budget process, used targeted tax and sector policies, and supported reopening and investment promotion. But the overall picture is one of mixed recovery rather than sustained broad competence, with poverty pressure and investment weakness still visible. This is solid enough for a modestly positive score, but not enough for the stronger half of the scale. Moral judgments about the regime do not affect the score.\",\n      \"lower_anchor_rejected\": \"4 rejected because the record includes several concrete fiscal and sectoral actions, plus measurable investment and reopening results.\",\n      \"higher_anchor_rejected\": \"6 rejected because the macro and distributional picture remained mixed and many gains were fragile or incomplete.\",\n      \"manual_review_required\": false,\n      \"manual_review_reason_type\": null,\n      \"manual_review_reason\": null,\n      \"chapter_specific\": [\n        { \"field\": \"program_basis\", \"value\": \"explicit\" },\n        { \"field\": \"program_type\", \"value\": \"policy, regime_control\" },\n        { \"field\": \"trajectory\", \"value\": \"reopening with mixed returns\" },\n        { \"field\": \"strategic_clarity\", \"value\": \"clear\" },\n        { \"field\": \"operationalization\", \"value\": \"mixed\" },\n        { \"field\": \"mobilization_and_coordination\", \"value\": \"mixed\" },\n        { \"field\": \"adaptation\", \"value\": \"mixed\" },\n        { \"field\": \"goal_progress\", \"value\": \"mixed\" },\n        { \"field\": \"durability\", \"value\": \"mixed\" },\n        { \"field\": \"morality_separation_check\", \"value\": \"The score reflects execution, not approval of the regime.\" }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"dossier_job_key\": \"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:TUR:15972\",\n      \"iso3\": \"TUR\",\n      \"ruler_id\": \"2813\",\n      \"ruler_year_id\": 15972,\n      \"ruler_name\": \"Recep Tayyip Erdoğan\",\n      \"period_start_year\": 2022,\n      \"period_end_year\": 2022,\n      \"chapter_id\": \"8B\",\n      \"rubric_version\": \"chapter_8b_v3\",\n      \"calibration_batch_id\": \"chapter-judge:2022-saturation-v3-stage1-controlled:2022:8B\",\n      \"calibrated_against\": [\n        \"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:BGD:17068\",\n        \"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:CHN:15832\",\n        \"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:RUS:15706\",\n        \"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:USA:15810\"\n      ],\n      \"score_1_to_10\": 4.0,\n      \"insufficient_evidence_reason\": null,\n      \"confidence_score\": 78,\n      \"plausible_score_range\": { \"lower\": 3.5, \"upper\": 4.5 },\n      \"decisive_positive_evidence\": [\n        {\n          \"evidence_id\": \"E0083\",\n          \"explanation\": \"Shows early-2022 stabilization actions through interventions and administrative measures.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"evidence_id\": \"E0088\",\n          \"explanation\": \"Shows a concrete diplomatic achievement in the NATO memorandum.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"evidence_id\": \"E0090\",\n          \"explanation\": \"Shows successful brokering of the Black Sea Grain Initiative.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"evidence_id\": \"E0091\",\n          \"explanation\": \"Shows early operational throughput of the grain corridor.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"evidence_id\": \"E0092\",\n          \"explanation\": \"Shows a material mid-year budget amendment.\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"decisive_negative_evidence\": [\n        {\n          \"evidence_id\": \"E0062\",\n          \"explanation\": \"Shows the core low-rate economic model driving very high inflation and fiscal risk.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"evidence_id\": \"E0070\",\n          \"explanation\": \"Shows Erdogan publicly committing to continued rate cuts despite the inflation problem.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"evidence_id\": \"E0087\",\n          \"explanation\": \"Shows growth held up, but only amid severe inflation and exchange-rate stress.\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"inherited_baseline_and_constraints\": \"Erdoğan's 2022 record is split between tactical foreign-policy wins and a deeply distorted macroeconomic model. The latter dominates the competence judgment because it was his own policy line and generated severe inflation and risk, even if the regime retained enough control to broker some diplomacy.\",\n      \"ruler_attribution\": \"Direct and strong for both the economic model and the diplomatic bargains. The main caveat is that some short-term stabilization came from administrative measures and external cooperation rather than a durable domestic fix.\",\n      \"supported_lenses\": [\n        \"8B.1\",\n        \"8B.2\",\n        \"8B.3\",\n        \"8B.4\",\n        \"8B.5\",\n        \"8B.6\",\n        \"8B.8\",\n        \"8B.9\",\n        \"8B.10\"\n      ],\n      \"missing_or_weak_lenses\": [\n        \"8B.7\"\n      ],\n      \"contrary_evidence\": [\n        {\n          \"evidence_id\": \"E0062\",\n          \"explanation\": \"The macro model produced extreme inflation, which sharply limits the competence score.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"evidence_id\": \"E0087\",\n          \"explanation\": \"Nominal GDP growth did not offset the severe inflationary and currency costs.\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"source_mix\": \"Mostly IMF, OECD, Reuters, NATO, UN, and Turkish official budget material. The evidence is strong on both control and consequences, and the negative macro record is especially important here.\",\n      \"structured_prior_summary\": \"Structured local priors were not collected in this experiment.\",\n      \"chapter_rationale\": \"Erdoğan scores 4.0/10. He retained enough control to broker some valuable diplomatic deals and to keep the state operating, but his own economic model generated extreme inflation and fiscal risk, which overwhelms the tactical wins. The score is not lower only because he still showed real command capacity and could produce a few meaningful state and diplomatic actions. But the core program under his own direction clearly underperformed. Moral approval of the politics is irrelevant to the score.\",\n      \"lower_anchor_rejected\": \"3 rejected because the dossier shows real executive control and successful diplomatic bargaining, not complete incapacitation.\",\n      \"higher_anchor_rejected\": \"5 rejected because the flagship economic model produced severe inflation and risk, making the overall execution record weak.\",\n      \"manual_review_required\": false,\n      \"manual_review_reason_type\": null,\n"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_1","type":"agent_message","text":"{\n  \"schema_version\": \"ruler_chapter_judgment_v1\",\n  \"job_key\": \"chapter-judge:2022-saturation-v3-stage1-controlled:2022:8B\",\n  \"run_key\": \"2022-saturation-v3-stage1-controlled\",\n  \"chapter_id\": \"8B\",\n  \"target_year\": 2022,\n  \"rubric_version\": \"chapter_8b_v3\",\n  \"calibration_batch_id\": \"chapter-judge:2022-saturation-v3-stage1-controlled:2022:8B\",\n  \"evaluations\": [\n    {\n      \"dossier_job_key\": \"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:BGD:17068\",\n      \"iso3\": \"BGD\",\n      \"ruler_id\": \"2992\",\n      \"ruler_year_id\": 17068,\n      \"ruler_name\": \"Sheikh Hasina\",\n      \"period_start_year\": 2022,\n      \"period_end_year\": 2022,\n      \"chapter_id\": \"8B\",\n      \"rubric_version\": \"chapter_8b_v3\",\n      \"calibration_batch_id\": \"chapter-judge:2022-saturation-v3-stage1-controlled:2022:8B\",\n      \"calibrated_against\": [\n        \"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:BRA:19646\",\n        \"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:CHN:15832\",\n        \"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:RUS:15706\",\n        \"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:USA:15810\"\n      ],\n      \"score_1_to_10\": 6.5,\n      \"insufficient_evidence_reason\": null,\n      \"confidence_score\": 76,\n      \"plausible_score_range\": { \"lower\": 6.0, \"upper\": 7.5 },\n      \"decisive_positive_evidence\": [\n        { \"evidence_id\": \"E0059\", \"explanation\": \"Shows a concrete 2022 stabilization package with revenue mobilization, spending rationalization, monetary reform, and exchange-rate flexibility.\" },\n        { \"evidence_id\": \"E0060\", \"explanation\": \"Shows a World Bank-backed fiscal and financial-sector resilience program with specific implementation content.\" },\n        { \"evidence_id\": \"E0067\", \"explanation\": \"Shows a direct central-bank appointment affecting monetary management inside the Hasina government.\" },\n        { \"evidence_id\": \"E0090\", \"explanation\": \"Shows direct social-policy delivery and beneficiary counts for the Ashrayan housing program.\" }\n      ],\n      \"decisive_negative_evidence\": [\n        { \"evidence_id\": \"E0064\", \"explanation\": \"Shows reactive shock management and inflation pressure rather than smooth control of the macro environment.\" },\n        { \"evidence_id\": \"E0075\", \"explanation\": \"Shows that some welfare gains were partly inherited, system-level resilience rather than discrete ruler-only execution.\" }\n      ],\n      \"inherited_baseline_and_constraints\": \"Bangladesh entered 2022 with strong inherited growth and resilience, but also rising inflation, reserve pressure, and banking vulnerabilities. That makes attribution mixed: Hasina gets credit for the 2022 stabilization and welfare agenda, not for baseline trends.\",\n      \"ruler_attribution\": \"Substantial but not exclusive. Hasina clearly owned the 2022 policy line, appointments, and social-protection emphasis, but some gains came through inherited resilience, line ministries, and reactive crisis management.\",\n      \"supported_lenses\": [\n        \"8B.1\",\n        \"8B.2\",\n        \"8B.3\",\n        \"8B.4\",\n        \"8B.5\",\n        \"8B.6\",\n        \"8B.8\",\n        \"8B.9\",\n        \"8B.10\"\n      ],\n      \"missing_or_weak_lenses\": [\n        \"8B.7\"\n      ],\n      \"contrary_evidence\": [\n        { \"evidence_id\": \"E0064\", \"explanation\": \"Fuel-price shock management shows adaptation under stress, but also reveals vulnerability and reactive policymaking.\" },\n        { \"evidence_id\": \"E0075\", \"explanation\": \"Climate-resilience gains are real, but the record also shows inherited system capacity and unresolved distributional risk.\" }\n      ],\n      \"source_mix\": \"Mostly official IMF, World Bank, and government releases, supplemented by Reuters and local reportage. The record is strong on declared policy and partial implementation, weaker on independent year-end outcome audits.\",\n      \"structured_prior_summary\": \"Structured local priors were not collected in this experiment.\",\n      \"chapter_rationale\": \"Hasina's 2022 record is moderately strong competence, landing at 6.5/10. Her government articulated and executed a clear stabilization-and-social-protection program, with concrete IMF and World Bank-backed reforms, budgeted safety-net spending, a central-bank appointment, and visible shock management; the main limits are that many gains are official self-reports, some improvements were inherited or reactive, and independent delivery audits remain thin. The record shows real policy action rather than slogans, but it does not fully prove durable household-level execution or corrective follow-through. Moral judgments about the regime, repression, or patronage allegations do not affect this execution score.\",\n      \"lower_anchor_rejected\": \"4 rejected because the dossier contains multiple concrete 2022 actions, not just rhetoric, including formal stabilization steps, budgeted welfare delivery, and a meaningful monetary appointment.\",\n      \"higher_anchor_rejected\": \"7 rejected because much of the evidence is official self-report or implementation design, and durable independent outcome verification remains limited.\",\n      \"manual_review_required\": false,\n      \"manual_review_reason_type\": null,\n      \"manual_review_reason\": null,\n      \"chapter_specific\": [\n        { \"field\": \"program_basis\", \"value\": \"explicit\" },\n        { \"field\": \"program_type\", \"value\": \"policy, state_building\" },\n        { \"field\": \"trajectory\", \"value\": \"upward but constrained\" },\n        { \"field\": \"strategic_clarity\", \"value\": \"clear\" },\n        { \"field\": \"operationalization\", \"value\": \"strong\" },\n        { \"field\": \"mobilization_and_coordination\", \"value\": \"strong\" },\n        { \"field\": \"adaptation\", \"value\": \"effective\" },\n        { \"field\": \"goal_progress\", \"value\": \"substantial\" },\n        { \"field\": \"durability\", \"value\": \"mixed\" },\n        { \"field\": \"morality_separation_check\", \"value\": \"The score reflects execution of the ruler's own program, not approval of the program's morality.\" }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"dossier_job_key\": \"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:BRA:19646\",\n      \"iso3\": \"BRA\",\n      \"ruler_id\": \"3413\",\n      \"ruler_year_id\": 19646,\n      \"ruler_name\": \"Jair Bolsonaro\",\n      \"period_start_year\": 2022,\n      \"period_end_year\": 2022,\n      \"chapter_id\": \"8B\",\n      \"rubric_version\": \"chapter_8b_v3\",\n      \"calibration_batch_id\": \"chapter-judge:2022-saturation-v3-stage1-controlled:2022:8B\",\n      \"calibrated_against\": [\n        \"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:BGD:17068\",\n        \"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:CHN:15832\",\n        \"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:RUS:15706\",\n        \"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:USA:15810\"\n      ],\n      \"score_1_to_10\": 5.0,\n      \"insufficient_evidence_reason\": null,\n      \"confidence_score\": 72,\n      \"plausible_score_range\": { \"lower\": 4.5, \"upper\": 6.0 },\n      \"decisive_positive_evidence\": [\n        { \"evidence_id\": \"E0061\", \"explanation\": \"Shows a concrete presidential decree delegating budget execution authority.\" },\n        { \"evidence_id\": \"E0070\", \"explanation\": \"Shows a direct cash-transfer expansion with specific beneficiary counts and a benefit floor.\" },\n        { \"evidence_id\": \"E0101\", \"explanation\": \"Shows an explicit tariff-cut policy choice aimed at lower prices and trade support.\" },\n        { \"evidence_id\": \"E0104\", \"explanation\": \"Shows a measurable income-recovery outcome, even if mixed and partly transfer-driven.\" }\n      ],\n      \"decisive_negative_evidence\": [\n        { \"evidence_id\": \"E0055\", \"explanation\": \"Shows inflation and reserve stress that undercut any claim of broad macro control.\" },\n        { \"evidence_id\": \"E0103\", \"explanation\": \"Shows a Bolsonaro-backed spending push that relied on congressional maneuvering and raised sustainability concerns.\" }\n      ],\n      \"inherited_baseline_and_constraints\": \"Brazil's 2022 environment was shaped by inflation shocks, electoral timing, congressional bargaining, and large preexisting fiscal constraints. Bolsonaro had real executive leverage, but many of his moves were tactical, short-horizon, or partly dependent on Congress.\",\n      \"ruler_attribution\": \"Direct on decrees, spending pushes, and program rollouts; weaker on final outcomes because several measures were election-year, congressional, or market-mediated.\",\n      \"supported_lenses\": [\n        \"8B.1\",\n        \"8B.2\",\n        \"8B.3\",\n        \"8B.4\",\n        \"8B.5\",\n        \"8B.6\",\n        \"8B.8\",\n        \"8B.9\",\n        \"8B.10\"\n      ],\n      \"missing_or_weak_lenses\": [\n        \"8B.7\"\n      ],\n      \"contrary_evidence\": [\n        { \"evidence_id\": \"E0055\", \"explanation\": \"Shows macro stress and inflation that complicate any simple success narrative.\" },\n        { \"evidence_id\": \"E0103\", \"explanation\": \"Shows the spending program had fiscal tradeoffs and was not a clean implementation win.\" }\n      ],\n      \"source_mix\": \"Mostly official Brazilian government material, with Reuters and IBGE context for outcomes. The record is strong on policy announcement and rollout, weaker on independent audits of distribution and durability.\",\n      \"structured_prior_summary\": \"Structured local priors were not collected in this experiment.\",\n      \"chapter_rationale\": \"Bolsonaro's 2022 score is mixed competence at 5.0/10. He did convert his program into real budget, tax, tariff, and transfer actions, and some measures were executed at scale, but the record is dominated by election-year spending, tactical fiscal maneuvers, and macro conditions that remained unstable. The strongest facts are the concrete decrees and welfare rollouts; the weakest are durable outcomes and non-electoral discipline. Moral judgments about his politics or rhetoric do not affect the execution score.\",\n      \"lower_anchor_rejected\": \"3 rejected because the dossier shows repeated concrete state action, not paralysis or absence of control.\",\n      \"higher_anchor_rejected\": \"6 rejected because many high-salience measures were short-term, politically timed, or only partially attributable to Bolsonaro rather than durable program execution.\",\n      \"manual_review_required\": false,\n      \"manual_review_reason_type\": null,\n      \"manual_review_reason\": null,\n      \"chapter_specific\": [\n        { \"field\": \"program_basis\", \"value\": \"explicit\" },\n        { \"field\": \"program_type\", \"value\": \"policy, power_consolidation\" },\n        { \"field\": \"trajectory\", \"value\": \"mixed and election-distorted\" },\n        { \"field\": \"strategic_clarity\", \"value\": \"clear\" },\n        { \"field\": \"operationalization\", \"value\": \"mixed\" },\n        { \"field\": \"mobilization_and_coordination\", \"value\": \"mixed\" },\n        { \"field\": \"adaptation\", \"value\": \"mixed\" },\n        { \"field\": \"goal_progress\", \"value\": \"mixed\" },\n        { \"field\": \"durability\", \"value\": \"fragile\" },\n        { \"field\": \"morality_separation_check\", \"value\": \"The score measures execution, not whether the objectives were desirable.\" }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"dossier_job_key\": \"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:CHN:15832\",\n      \"iso3\": \"CHN\",\n      \"ruler_id\": \"1432\",\n      \"ruler_year_id\": 15832,\n      \"ruler_name\": \"Xi Jinping\",\n      \"period_start_year\": 2022,\n      \"period_end_year\": 2022,\n      \"chapter_id\": \"8B\",\n      \"rubric_version\": \"chapter_8b_v3\",\n      \"calibration_batch_id\": \"chapter-judge:2022-saturation-v3-stage1-controlled:2022:8B\",\n      \"calibrated_against\": [\n        \"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:BGD:17068\",\n        \"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:BRA:19646\",\n        \"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:RUS:15706\",\n        \"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:USA:15810\"\n      ],\n      \"score_1_to_10\": 8.0,\n      \"insufficient_evidence_reason\": null,\n      \"confidence_score\": 80,\n      \"plausible_score_range\": { \"lower\": 7.0, \"upper\": 8.5 },\n      \"decisive_positive_evidence\": [\n        { \"evidence_id\": \"E0103\", \"explanation\": \"Shows a top-level 2022 program with explicit five-year objectives across development, social services, and security.\" },\n        { \"evidence_id\": \"E0105\", \"explanation\": \"Shows a concrete State Council stabilization package with implementation content.\" },\n        { \"evidence_id\": \"E0111\", \"explanation\": \"Shows policy adaptation on COVID response while preserving central control.\" },\n        { \"evidence_id\": \"E0112\", \"explanation\": \"Shows a further late-2022 policy reversal toward a less disruptive COVID management approach.\" },\n        { \"evidence_id\": \"E0045\", \"explanation\": \"Shows Xi's consolidation of top leadership and direct program ownership at the 20th Congress.\" }\n      ],\n      \"decisive_negative_evidence\": [\n        { \"evidence_id\": \"E0040\", \"explanation\": \"Shows the severe human and logistical costs of the Shanghai lockdown strategy.\" },\n        { \"evidence_id\": \"E0110\", \"explanation\": \"Shows stronger monitoring, but also that the system still needed intensified oversight and better discipline.\" }\n      ],\n      \"inherited_baseline_and_constraints\": \"China entered 2022 with strong state capacity and a highly centralized party-state, which favors high competence scores when the leadership can mobilize it. Xi also faced serious COVID and growth constraints, so the question is whether he adapted the apparatus effectively, not whether the regime was benign.\",\n      \"ruler_attribution\": \"Strong. Xi owned the program, the personnel consolidation, and the central policy pivots, even when implementation ran through the State Council and lower-level authorities.\",\n      \"supported_lenses\": [\n        \"8B.1\",\n        \"8B.2\",\n        \"8B.3\",\n        \"8B.4\",\n        \"8B.5\",\n        \"8B.6\",\n        \"8B.8\",\n        \"8B.9\",\n        \"8B.10\"\n      ],\n      \"missing_or_weak_lenses\": [\n        \"8B.7\"\n      ],\n      \"contrary_evidence\": [\n        { \"evidence_id\": \"E0040\", \"explanation\": \"The lockdown harms show the costs of the chosen strategy and prevent an even higher score.\" },\n        { \"evidence_id\": \"E0110\", \"explanation\": \"The need for extra discipline and monitoring shows the system still had execution frictions.\" }\n      ],\n      \"source_mix\": \"Mostly primary Chinese state documents and official summaries, with Reuters corroboration where helpful. The evidence is unusually rich on program and implementation architecture, but official self-reporting remains a major feature of the record.\",\n      \"structured_prior_summary\": \"Structured local priors were not collected in this experiment.\",\n      \"chapter_rationale\": \"Xi Jinping scores very strongly on competence, at 8.0/10. He articulated a detailed governing program, consolidated personnel control, launched a large stabilization package, and then adapted the COVID policy late in the year after the costs of the earlier approach became unsustainable. The main caveat is that much of the record is official self-report and some of the most visible action came with severe social costs, so the score stops short of the very top tier. The competence judgment is separate from any moral evaluation of repression or coercion.\",\n      \"lower_anchor_rejected\": \"6 rejected because the dossier shows broad strategic control, concrete programmatic machinery, and real adaptation rather than merely competent administration.\",\n      \"higher_anchor_rejected\": \"9 rejected because the evidence still includes severe policy harm, heavy reliance on official self-report, and incomplete independent outcome verification.\",\n      \"manual_review_required\": false,\n      \"manual_review_reason_type\": null,\n      \"manual_review_reason\": null,\n      \"chapter_specific\": [\n        { \"field\": \"program_basis\", \"value\": \"explicit\" },\n        { \"field\": \"program_type\", \"value\": \"policy, regime_control, state_building\" },\n        { \"field\": \"trajectory\", \"value\": \"upward on control, mixed on welfare\" },\n        { \"field\": \"strategic_clarity\", \"value\": \"exceptional\" },\n        { \"field\": \"operationalization\", \"value\": \"strong\" },\n        { \"field\": \"mobilization_and_coordination\", \"value\": \"strong\" },\n        { \"field\": \"adaptation\", \"value\": \"effective\" },\n        { \"field\": \"goal_progress\", \"value\": \"substantial\" },\n        { \"field\": \"durability\", \"value\": \"durable\" },\n        { \"field\": \"morality_separation_check\", \"value\": \"The score reflects execution of the program, not approval of coercive governance.\" }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"dossier_job_key\": \"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:COD:16113\",\n      \"iso3\": \"COD\",\n      \"ruler_id\": \"2830\",\n      \"ruler_year_id\": 16113,\n      \"ruler_name\": \"Félix Tshisekedi\",\n      \"period_start_year\": 2022,\n      \"period_end_year\": 2022,\n      \"chapter_id\": \"8B\",\n      \"rubric_version\": \"chapter_8b_v3\",\n      \"calibration_batch_id\": \"chapter-judge:2022-saturation-v3-stage1-controlled:2022:8B\",\n      \"calibrated_against\": [\n        \"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:BGD:17068\",\n        \"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:BRA:19646\",\n        \"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:CHN:15832\",\n        \"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:USA:15810\"\n      ],\n      \"score_1_to_10\": 4.5,\n      \"insufficient_evidence_reason\": null,\n      \"confidence_score\": 68,\n      \"plausible_score_range\": { \"lower\": 4.0, \"upper\": 5.5 },\n      \"decisive_positive_evidence\": [\n        { \"evidence_id\": \"E0108\", \"explanation\": \"Shows direct oversight of the 145-territories program and concrete project preparation.\" },\n        { \"evidence_id\": \"E0111\", \"explanation\": \"Shows direct instructions to resource humanitarian risk-management institutions.\" },\n        { \"evidence_id\": \"E0112\", \"explanation\": \"Shows direct judicial and payroll reform directives from the presidency.\" },\n        { \"evidence_id\": \"E0118\", \"explanation\": \"Shows prudent macroeconomic policy, including stopping central-bank financing.\" }\n      ],\n      \"decisive_negative_evidence\": [\n        { \"evidence_id\": \"E0115\", \"explanation\": \"Shows projected rather than realized job and firm-creation outcomes.\" },\n        { \"evidence_id\": \"E0119\", \"explanation\": \"Shows a very low starting vaccination base and only partial catch-up, not completed success.\" },\n        { \"evidence_id\": \"E0121\", \"explanation\": \"Shows a newly approved grant and stabilization plan, but not finished delivery by year-end.\" }\n      ],\n      \"inherited_baseline_and_constraints\": \"The DRC's 2022 constraints were severe: weak institutions, conflict-affected territory, donor dependence, and limited state reach. Tshisekedi gets credit for setting priorities and some administrative movement, but much of the country-level outcome picture remained beyond the presidency's immediate control.\",\n      \"ruler_attribution\": \"Partial. Tshisekedi clearly directed the agenda and chaired multiple implementation meetings, but much of the work was preparatory, partner-mediated, or incomplete by year-end.\",\n      \"supported_lenses\": [\n        \"8B.1\",\n        \"8B.2\",\n        \"8B.3\",\n        \"8B.4\",\n        \"8B.5\",\n        \"8B.6\",\n        \"8B.8\",\n        \"8B.9\",\n        \"8B.10\"\n      ],\n      \"missing_or_weak_lenses\": [\n        \"8B.7\"\n      ],\n      \"contrary_evidence\": [\n        { \"evidence_id\": \"E0115\", \"explanation\": \"Projected employment and firm creation are not completed 2022 outcomes.\" },\n        { \"evidence_id\": \"E0121\", \"explanation\": \"The grant shows mobilization, but it is still a design-and-launch story rather than a finished delivery story.\" }\n      ],\n      \"source_mix\": \"Official presidency, IMF, World Bank, WHO, and local reporting. The dossier is rich on directives and program launches but thin on independent completed-outcome verification.\",\n      \"structured_prior_summary\": \"Structured local priors were not collected in this experiment.\",\n      \"chapter_rationale\": \"Tshisekedi's 2022 competence is limited and mixed, at 4.5/10. He clearly set agendas, chaired recovery and governance meetings, and presided over some prudent macro steps, but much of the record stops at planning, procurement, and launch rather than completed delivery. The strongest evidence is that the presidency could mobilize institutions; the weakest is durable, independently verified progress across the major programs. This is enough to avoid a collapse score, but not enough to move into the mixed-or-better tier.\",\n      \"lower_anchor_rejected\": \"3 rejected because the dossier shows repeated convening, agenda-setting, and partial implementation rather than outright paralysis.\",\n      \"higher_anchor_rejected\": \"5 rejected because the best evidence is still mostly preparatory or partial, with weak independent confirmation of completed outcomes.\",\n      \"manual_review_required\": false,\n      \"manual_review_reason_type\": null,\n      \"manual_review_reason\": null,\n      \"chapter_specific\": [\n        { \"field\": \"program_basis\", \"value\": \"mostly_explicit\" },\n        { \"field\": \"program_type\", \"value\": \"policy, state_building\" },\n        { \"field\": \"trajectory\", \"value\": \"upward in agenda-setting, weak in delivery\" },\n        { \"field\": \"strategic_clarity\", \"value\": \"partial\" },\n        { \"field\": \"operationalization\", \"value\": \"weak\" },\n        { \"field\": \"mobilization_and_coordination\", \"value\": \"mixed\" },\n        { \"field\": \"adaptation\", \"value\": \"mixed\" },\n        { \"field\": \"goal_progress\", \"value\": \"too_early_or_unclear\" },\n        { \"field\": \"durability\", \"value\": \"fragile\" },\n        { \"field\": \"morality_separation_check\", \"value\": \"The score reflects execution only, not the moral quality of the political environment.\" }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"dossier_job_key\": \"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:DEU:16984\",\n      \"iso3\": \"DEU\",\n      \"ruler_id\": \"2975\",\n      \"ruler_year_id\": 16984,\n      \"ruler_name\": \"Olaf Scholz\",\n      \"period_start_year\": 2022,\n      \"period_end_year\": 2022,\n      \"chapter_id\": \"8B\",\n      \"rubric_version\": \"chapter_8b_v3\",\n      \"calibration_batch_id\": \"chapter-judge:2022-saturation-v3-stage1-controlled:2022:8B\",\n      \"calibrated_against\": [\n        \"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:BGD:17068\",\n        \"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:CHN:15832\",\n        \"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:RUS:15706\",\n        \"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:USA:15810\"\n      ],\n      \"score_1_to_10\": 6.5,\n      \"insufficient_evidence_reason\": null,\n      \"confidence_score\": 78,\n      \"plausible_score_range\": { \"lower\": 6.0, \"upper\": 7.5 },\n      \"decisive_positive_evidence\": [\n        { \"evidence_id\": \"E0087\", \"explanation\": \"Shows a major defense-policy reorientation with a large special fund and a strategic commitment.\" },\n        { \"evidence_id\": \"E0088\", \"explanation\": \"Shows concrete welfare-reform design for Bürgergeld.\" },\n        { \"evidence_id\": \"E0091\", \"explanation\": \"Shows a large housing-benefit reform approved in 2022.\" },\n        { \"evidence_id\": \"E0092\", \"explanation\": \"Shows direct crisis stabilization of Uniper and the energy supply.\" },\n        { \"evidence_id\": \"E0094\", \"explanation\": \"Shows refugee integration apparatus in use by year-end.\" }\n      ],\n      \"decisive_negative_evidence\": [\n        { \"evidence_id\": \"E0095\", \"explanation\": \"Shows policy critique over targeting and fiscal sustainability, limiting a stronger competence judgment.\" },\n        { \"evidence_id\": \"E0096\", \"explanation\": \"Shows support was appropriate but uncertainty and downside risks remained high.\" },\n        { \"evidence_id\": \"E0097\", \"explanation\": \"Shows the relief packages were criticized as expensive and potentially crowding out public goods.\" }\n      ],\n      \"inherited_baseline_and_constraints\": \"Scholz governed through coalition constraints, a federal system, and the acute shock of the war in Ukraine and energy crisis. That makes crisis management and coordination central, but also means many implementation levers were shared rather than purely chancellor-controlled.\",\n      \"ruler_attribution\": \"Mostly strong but shared. Scholz clearly owned the governing direction and crisis response, while ministries, Länder, and coalition partners carried much of the implementation burden.\",\n      \"supported_lenses\": [\n        \"8B.1\",\n        \"8B.2\",\n        \"8B.3\",\n        \"8B.4\",\n        \"8B.5\",\n        \"8B.6\",\n        \"8B.8\",\n        \"8B.9\",\n        \"8B.10\"\n      ],\n      \"missing_or_weak_lenses\": [\n        \"8B.7\"\n      ],\n      \"contrary_evidence\": [\n        { \"evidence_id\": \"E0095\", \"explanation\": \"Independent critique says the relief measures were not well targeted enough.\" },\n        { \"evidence_id\": \"E0097\", \"explanation\": \"The fiscal burden and long-run sustainability of the response remained contested.\" }\n      ],\n      \"source_mix\": \"Primary German government texts plus IMF, OECD, and ifo assessment. The record is unusually strong on policy design and coordination, but less conclusive on durable welfare outcomes in the target year.\",\n      \"structured_prior_summary\": \"Structured local priors were not collected in this experiment.\",\n      \"chapter_rationale\": \"Scholz scores 6.5/10 for broadly effective crisis governance. He combined a clear strategic pivot on defense, energy, and social cushioning with concrete cabinet and legislative follow-through, and there is independent evidence that the refugee and energy responses were functioning by year-end. The main limits are that most benefits were either designed for later rollout or criticized for targeting and fiscal cost, so the record is more about capable response than fully verified durable success. Moral approval of the policy mix is irrelevant to this competence score.\",\n      \"lower_anchor_rejected\": \"5 rejected because the government did more than announce plans: it enacted major reforms, coordinated across institutions, and managed acute crises.\",\n      \"higher_anchor_rejected\": \"7 rejected because several flagship measures were still partly prospective or debated in terms of targeting and sustainability, with incomplete outcome verification.\",\n      \"manual_review_required\": false,\n      \"manual_review_reason_type\": null,\n      \"manual_review_reason\": null,\n      \"chapter_specific\": [\n        { \"field\": \"program_basis\", \"value\": \"explicit\" },\n        { \"field\": \"program_type\", \"value\": \"policy\" },\n        { \"field\": \"trajectory\", \"value\": \"upward under severe shock\" },\n        { \"field\": \"strategic_clarity\", \"value\": \"clear\" },\n        { \"field\": \"operationalization\", \"value\": \"strong\" },\n        { \"field\": \"mobilization_and_coordination\", \"value\": \"strong\" },\n        { \"field\": \"adaptation\", \"value\": \"effective\" },\n        { \"field\": \"goal_progress\", \"value\": \"substantial\" },\n        { \"field\": \"durability\", \"value\": \"mixed\" },\n        { \"field\": \"morality_separation_check\", \"value\": \"The score reflects execution of the program, not approval of the program's morality.\" }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"dossier_job_key\": \"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:EGY:16232\",\n      \"iso3\": \"EGY\",\n      \"ruler_id\": \"2851\",\n      \"ruler_year_id\": 16232,\n      \"ruler_name\": \"Abdel Fattah el-Sisi\",\n      \"period_start_year\": 2022,\n      \"period_end_year\": 2022,\n      \"chapter_id\": \"8B\",\n      \"rubric_version\": \"chapter_8b_v3\",\n      \"calibration_batch_id\": \"chapter-judge:2022-saturation-v3-stage1-controlled:2022:8B\",\n      \"calibrated_against\": [\n        \"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:BGD:17068\",\n        \"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:CHN:15832\",\n        \"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:RUS:15706\",\n        \"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:USA:15810\"\n      ],\n      \"score_1_to_10\": 5.0,\n      \"insufficient_evidence_reason\": null,\n      \"confidence_score\": 66,\n      \"plausible_score_range\": { \"lower\": 4.5, \"upper\": 5.5 },\n      \"decisive_positive_evidence\": [\n        { \"evidence_id\": \"E0079\", \"explanation\": \"Shows direct control over the anti-corruption authority.\" },\n        { \"evidence_id\": \"E0082\", \"explanation\": \"Shows a concrete state-ownership policy with private-sector expansion targets.\" },\n        { \"evidence_id\": \"E0052\", \"explanation\": \"Shows a direct presidential appointment during the currency crisis.\" },\n        { \"evidence_id\": \"E0080\", \"explanation\": \"Shows a formal judicial appointment under a rule-based procedure rather than pure patronage.\" }\n      ],\n      \"decisive_negative_evidence\": [\n        { \"evidence_id\": \"E0074\", \"explanation\": \"Shows opacity, domination of policymaking by the security apparatus,