scores 5.0/10: competent at preserving control and making formal moves, but not demonstrably high-performing at reform delivery. The evidence shows direct appointments, a state-ownership policy, and anti-corruption authority control, yet it also shows opacity, patronage, and external pressure for governance reform. The score stays in the middle because the state can move under Sisi, but the dossier does not show that those moves reliably translated into transparent, effective governance. Moral judgments about authoritarianism are excluded from the score.\",\n      \"lower_anchor_rejected\": \"4 rejected because the dossier shows clear presidential control over appointments and policy documents, not mere drift.\",\n      \"higher_anchor_rejected\": \"6 rejected because the strongest evidence points to concentrated control and partial reform, not durable, independently verified administrative success.\",\n      \"manual_review_required\": false,\n      \"manual_review_reason_type\": null,\n      \"manual_review_reason\": null,\n      \"chapter_specific\": [\n        { \"field\": \"program_basis\", \"value\": \"mixed\" },\n        { \"field\": \"program_type\", \"value\": \"policy, regime_control, state_building\" },\n        { \"field\": \"trajectory\", \"value\": \"controlled but reform-limited\" },\n        { \"field\": \"strategic_clarity\", \"value\": \"clear\" },\n        { \"field\": \"operationalization\", \"value\": \"mixed\" },\n        { \"field\": \"mobilization_and_coordination\", \"value\": \"strong\" },\n        { \"field\": \"adaptation\", \"value\": \"mixed\" },\n        { \"field\": \"goal_progress\", \"value\": \"mixed\" },\n        { \"field\": \"durability\", \"value\": \"mixed\" },\n        { \"field\": \"morality_separation_check\", \"value\": \"The score measures execution, not approval of the regime's moral character.\" }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"dossier_job_key\": \"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:ETH:16782\",\n      \"iso3\": \"ETH\",\n      \"ruler_id\": \"2310\",\n      \"ruler_year_id\": 16782,\n      \"ruler_name\": \"Abiy Ahmed\",\n      \"period_start_year\": 2022,\n      \"period_end_year\": 2022,\n      \"chapter_id\": \"8B\",\n      \"rubric_version\": \"chapter_8b_v3\",\n      \"calibration_batch_id\": \"chapter-judge:2022-saturation-v3-stage1-controlled:2022:8B\",\n      \"calibrated_against\": [\n        \"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:BGD:17068\",\n        \"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:CHN:15832\",\n        \"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:RUS:15706\",\n        \"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:USA:15810\"\n      ],\n      \"score_1_to_10\": 5.0,\n      \"insufficient_evidence_reason\": null,\n      \"confidence_score\": 67,\n      \"plausible_score_range\": { \"lower\": 4.5, \"upper\": 5.5 },\n      \"decisive_positive_evidence\": [\n        { \"evidence_id\": \"E0086\", \"explanation\": \"Shows a direct anti-corruption enforcement mechanism created by the administration.\" },\n        { \"evidence_id\": \"E0088\", \"explanation\": \"Shows a formal peace-institution setup tied to the national dialogue process.\" },\n        { \"evidence_id\": \"E0089\", \"explanation\": \"Shows tangible ceasefire implementation and some humanitarian access.\" },\n        { \"evidence_id\": \"E0092\", \"explanation\": \"Shows service restoration progress in Tigray with concrete numbers.\" }\n      ],\n      \"decisive_negative_evidence\": [\n        { \"evidence_id\": \"E0041\", \"explanation\": \"Shows the national dialogue was contested and excluded key actors, limiting the strength of the political reconciliation record.\" },\n        { \"evidence_id\": \"E0090\", \"explanation\": \"Shows that the ceasefire was still a promise of honest implementation rather than a completed result.\" }\n      ],\n      \"inherited_baseline_and_constraints\": \"Abiy governed amid war, fragmentation, and severe administrative strain, so 2022 competence is mostly about whether he could pivot from conflict to reconstruction and coordination. That produces genuine partial credit for the ceasefire and service restoration, but also keeps attribution and durability uncertain.\",\n      \"ruler_attribution\": \"Partial. Abiy clearly directed the post-ceasefire pivot and reform agenda, but many results were incomplete, shared with partners, or contested by excluded actors.\",\n      \"supported_lenses\": [\n        \"8B.1\",\n        \"8B.2\",\n        \"8B.3\",\n        \"8B.4\",\n        \"8B.5\",\n        \"8B.6\",\n        \"8B.8\",\n        \"8B.9\",\n        \"8B.10\"\n      ],\n      \"missing_or_weak_lenses\": [\n        \"8B.7\"\n      ],\n      \"contrary_evidence\": [\n        { \"evidence_id\": \"E0041\", \"explanation\": \"The dialogue process was politically contested and excluded some key groups.\" },\n        { \"evidence_id\": \"E0090\", \"explanation\": \"The truce was still in the implementation stage, not a fully proven durable settlement.\" }\n      ],\n      \"source_mix\": \"Mostly Ethiopian government and international organization material, with Reuters corroboration on the ceasefire and access issues. The evidence is strongest on directives and partial implementation, weaker on durable national reconciliation.\",\n      \"structured_prior_summary\": \"Structured local priors were not collected in this experiment.\",\n      \"chapter_rationale\": \"Abiy scores 5.0/10. The dossier shows real pivoting: anti-corruption measures, peace-council creation, ceasefire implementation, and service restoration in Tigray. But the strongest evidence is still partial and contested, with many results dependent on partner logistics or not yet complete by year-end. This is enough for a mixed competence score, but not enough for a stronger claim of durable execution. Moral judgments about the war or repression do not affect the score.\",\n      \"lower_anchor_rejected\": \"4 rejected because the record shows actual institutional moves and partial implementation rather than simple failure.\",\n      \"higher_anchor_rejected\": \"6 rejected because the best evidence remains incomplete, contested, and only partly outcome-verified.\",\n      \"manual_review_required\": false,\n      \"manual_review_reason_type\": null,\n      \"manual_review_reason\": null,\n      \"chapter_specific\": [\n        { \"field\": \"program_basis\", \"value\": \"mixed\" },\n        { \"field\": \"program_type\", \"value\": \"policy, survival, state_building\" },\n        { \"field\": \"trajectory\", \"value\": \"recovery from war toward reconstruction\" },\n        { \"field\": \"strategic_clarity\", \"value\": \"partial\" },\n        { \"field\": \"operationalization\", \"value\": \"mixed\" },\n        { \"field\": \"mobilization_and_coordination\", \"value\": \"mixed\" },\n        { \"field\": \"adaptation\", \"value\": \"effective\" },\n        { \"field\": \"goal_progress\", \"value\": \"mixed\" },\n        { \"field\": \"durability\", \"value\": \"fragile\" },\n        { \"field\": \"morality_separation_check\", \"value\": \"The score measures execution, not the morality of the conflict context.\" }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"dossier_job_key\": \"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:IDN:16199\",\n      \"iso3\": \"IDN\",\n      \"ruler_id\": \"2636\",\n      \"ruler_year_id\": 16199,\n      \"ruler_name\": \"Joko Widodo\",\n      \"period_start_year\": 2022,\n      \"period_end_year\": 2022,\n      \"chapter_id\": \"8B\",\n      \"rubric_version\": \"chapter_8b_v3\",\n      \"calibration_batch_id\": \"chapter-judge:2022-saturation-v3-stage1-controlled:2022:8B\",\n      \"calibrated_against\": [\n        \"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:BGD:17068\",\n        \"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:CHN:15832\",\n        \"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:RUS:15706\",\n        \"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:USA:15810\"\n      ],\n      \"score_1_to_10\": 7.5,\n      \"insufficient_evidence_reason\": null,\n      \"confidence_score\": 79,\n      \"plausible_score_range\": { \"lower\": 7.0, \"upper\": 8.5 },\n      \"decisive_positive_evidence\": [\n        { \"evidence_id\": \"E0077\", \"explanation\": \"Shows a direct presidential instruction to accelerate extreme-poverty reduction across ministries and local governments.\" },\n        { \"evidence_id\": \"E0098\", \"explanation\": \"Shows 2022 direct-cash distribution reaching 95.9 percent of the target.\" },\n        { \"evidence_id\": \"E0099\", \"explanation\": \"Shows fast fiscal consolidation through a smaller-than-target deficit.\" },\n        { \"evidence_id\": \"E0100\", \"explanation\": \"Shows clean audit outcomes for most ministries and the central budget, indicating administrative execution quality.\" },\n        { \"evidence_id\": \"E0104\", \"explanation\": \"Shows above-target full immunization coverage and a large catch-up campaign.\" }\n      ],\n      \"decisive_negative_evidence\": [\n        { \"evidence_id\": \"E0101\", \"explanation\": \"Shows major learning losses and a large education recovery gap.\" },\n        { \"evidence_id\": \"E0102\", \"explanation\": \"Shows that poverty and economic insecurity remained substantial despite progress.\" }\n      ],\n      \"inherited_baseline_and_constraints\": \"Indonesia benefited from recovery momentum, but Jokowi still had to translate broad goals into bureaucratic coordination across a large archipelago. The dossier shows unusually strong state execution, with some distributional and learning gaps left unresolved.\",\n      \"ruler_attribution\": \"Strong. Jokowi directly owned the major policy directions, appointments, and delivery mechanisms, while local governments and ministries carried much of the implementation.\",\n      \"supported_lenses\": [\n        \"8B.1\",\n        \"8B.2\",\n        \"8B.3\",\n        \"8B.4\",\n        \"8B.5\",\n        \"8B.6\",\n        \"8B.7\",\n        \"8B.8\",\n        \"8B.9\",\n        \"8B.10\"\n      ],\n      \"missing_or_weak_lenses\": [],\n      \"contrary_evidence\": [\n        { \"evidence_id\": \"E0101\", \"explanation\": \"Learning losses remained serious, limiting the claim of full program success.\" },\n        { \"evidence_id\": \"E0102\", \"explanation\": \"Residual economic insecurity means the anti-poverty program was strong but not complete.\" }\n      ],\n      \"source_mix\": \"Mostly official Indonesian presidential, statistical, audit, and multilateral sources. This is a strong record for both implementation and outcome verification, with the main caveat that some evidence is retrospective.\",\n      \"structured_prior_summary\": \"Structured local priors were not collected in this experiment.\",\n      \"chapter_rationale\": \"Jokowi scores 7.5/10. The dossier shows an explicit governing program converted into concrete instructions, budget discipline, appointed personnel, and measurable rollout that reached targets or nearly so in several areas. The best evidence is not just plan language but later execution and audit material, especially on fiscal consolidation, immunization, and poverty-related delivery. The main constraints are education recovery and residual economic insecurity, which keep the score below the top tier but still clearly in strong-performance territory. Moral approval of his agenda is irrelevant to the competence score.\",\n      \"lower_anchor_rejected\": \"6 rejected because the record shows broad, measurable execution and several strong outcome markers rather than merely competent planning.\",\n      \"higher_anchor_rejected\": \"8 rejected because some flagship reforms remain uneven across sectors, with major learning and distributional gaps still visible.\",\n      \"manual_review_required\": false,\n      \"manual_review_reason_type\": null,\n      \"manual_review_reason\": null,\n      \"chapter_specific\": [\n        { \"field\": \"program_basis\", \"value\": \"explicit\" },\n        { \"field\": \"program_type\", \"value\": \"policy, state_building\