ng recovery and distributional equity remained weak relative to the headline achievements.\" }\n      ],\n      \"source_mix\": \"Mostly official Indian budget, ministry, audit, and multilateral material, supplemented by Reuters and UNICEF. The record is rich and varied, with the main limitation being attribution across a large federal and institutional system.\",\n      \"structured_prior_summary\": \"Structured local priors were not collected in this experiment.\",\n      \"chapter_rationale\": \"Modi scores 7.0/10. He had a clear, explicit governing agenda and turned it into budgets, appointments, digital infrastructure, welfare delivery, and auditable administrative execution. The strongest evidence is the combination of policy design and observable follow-through, especially on capital spending, digital public infrastructure, and fiscal management. The score is held below the top tier because outcome attribution is shared and some core household and education gaps remain substantial. Moral approval of the agenda is not part of this competence judgment.\",\n      \"lower_anchor_rejected\": \"6 rejected because the dossier shows repeated, measurable implementation and strong administrative control rather than merely competent rhetoric.\",\n      \"higher_anchor_rejected\": \"8 rejected because outcome attribution is still shared with institutions and inherited buffers, and some distributional problems remain unresolved.\",\n      \"manual_review_required\": false,\n      \"manual_review_reason_type\": null,\n      \"manual_review_reason\": null,\n      \"chapter_specific\": [\n        { \"field\": \"program_basis\", \"value\": \"explicit\" },\n        { \"field\": \"program_type\", \"value\": \"policy, state_building\" },\n        { \"field\": \"trajectory\", \"value\": \"upward with distributional gaps\" },\n        { \"field\": \"strategic_clarity\", \"value\": \"clear\" },\n        { \"field\": \"operationalization\", \"value\": \"strong\" },\n        { \"field\": \"mobilization_and_coordination\", \"value\": \"strong\" },\n        { \"field\": \"adaptation\", \"value\": \"effective\" },\n        { \"field\": \"goal_progress\", \"value\": \"substantial\" },\n        { \"field\": \"durability\", \"value\": \"mixed\" },\n        { \"field\": \"morality_separation_check\", \"value\": \"The score measures execution, not approval of the objectives.\" }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"dossier_job_key\": \"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:IRN:19648\",\n      \"iso3\": \"IRN\",\n      \"ruler_id\": \"3412\",\n      \"ruler_year_id\": 19648,\n      \"ruler_name\": \"Ali Khamenei\",\n      \"period_start_year\": 2022,\n      \"period_end_year\": 2022,\n      \"chapter_id\": \"8B\",\n      \"rubric_version\": \"chapter_8b_v3\",\n      \"calibration_batch_id\": \"chapter-judge:2022-saturation-v3-stage1-controlled:2022:8B\",\n      \"calibrated_against\": [\n        \"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:BGD:17068\",\n        \"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:CHN:15832\",\n        \"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:RUS:15706\",\n        \"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:USA:15810\"\n      ],\n      \"score_1_to_10\": 4.5,\n      \"insufficient_evidence_reason\": null,\n      \"confidence_score\": 63,\n      \"plausible_score_range\": { \"lower\": 4.0, \"upper\": 5.0 },\n      \"decisive_positive_evidence\": [\n        { \"evidence_id\": \"E0001\", \"explanation\": \"Defines the Leader's sweeping command and appointment powers in 2022.\" },\n        { \"evidence_id\": \"E0060\", \"explanation\": \"Shows a detailed development-plan guideline and economic direction from the Leader's office.\" },\n        { \"evidence_id\": \"E0082\", \"explanation\": \"Shows resistance-oriented program framing and a refusal to tie progress to sanctions relief.\" }\n      ],\n      \"decisive_negative_evidence\": [\n        { \"evidence_id\": \"E0005\", \"explanation\": \"Shows rigid sanctions-resistance framing rather than clear evidence of effective economic delivery.\" },\n        { \"evidence_id\": \"E0083\", \"explanation\": \"Shows crisis framing and accusation without supporting evidence, which does not demonstrate effective governance.\" }\n      ],\n      \"inherited_baseline_and_constraints\": \"Khamenei has formal supremacy in Iran's system, but the 2022 record here is mostly declaratory and institutional rather than implementation-heavy. That means the evidence supports strong agenda-setting but not strong proof of competent execution or durable progress.\",\n      \"ruler_attribution\": \"Direct for program framing and formal authority, but weak for execution. The dossier shows what Khamenei said and what the constitutional system empowered, not a robust delivery chain for his objectives.\",\n      \"supported_lenses\": [\n        \"8B.1\",\n        \"8B.2\",\n        \"8B.4\",\n        \"8B.5\",\n        \"8B.6\",\n        \"8B.8\",\n        \"8B.9\",\n        \"8B.10\"\n      ],\n      \"missing_or_weak_lenses\": [\n        \"8B.3\",\n        \"8B.7\"\n      ],\n      \"contrary_evidence\": [\n        { \"evidence_id\": \"E0005\", \"explanation\": \"Sanctions-resilience rhetoric is direction-setting, but it does not prove the program worked.\" },\n        { \"evidence_id\": \"E0083\", \"explanation\": \"Crisis accusations are not evidence of competent execution.\" }\n      ],\n      \"source_mix\": \"Primary constitutional text plus a mix of state-affiliated and secondary reporting on speeches and program guidelines. The record is thin on implementation evidence and stronger on revealed preferences and formal power.\",\n      \"structured_prior_summary\": \"Structured local priors were not collected in this experiment.\",\n      \"chapter_rationale\": \"Khamenei scores 4.5/10. The dossier gives him clear formal authority and clear ideological direction, but it does not show a robust 2022 execution chain that converts that authority into measurable progress on the chosen program. The evidence is mostly about what the Leader ordered, framed, or wanted, not about durable outcome gains. This is enough to beat a collapse score, but not enough for a mixed-to-strong execution judgment. Moral approval of the regime is irrelevant here.\",\n      \"lower_anchor_rejected\": \"3 rejected because the dossier shows formal authority, repeated program statements, and some institutional ordering rather than an absence of control.\",\n      \"higher_anchor_rejected\": \"5 rejected because the evidence still lacks a convincing implementation and outcome trail, and much of the material is declaratory rather than operational.\",\n      \"manual_review_required\": false,\n      \"manual_review_reason_type\": null,\n      \"manual_review_reason\": null,\n      \"chapter_specific\": [\n        { \"field\": \"program_basis\", \"value\": \"mostly_explicit\" },\n        { \"field\": \"program_type\", \"value\": \"policy, regime_control\" },\n        { \"field\": \"trajectory\", \"value\": \"clear in doctrine, weak in delivery\" },\n        { \"field\": \"strategic_clarity\", \"value\": \"clear\" },\n        { \"field\": \"operationalization\", \"value\": \"weak\" },\n        { \"field\": \"mobilization_and_coordination\", \"value\": \"weak\" },\n        { \"field\": \"adaptation\", \"value\": \"rigid\" },\n        { \"field\": \"goal_progress\", \"value\": \"too_early_or_unclear\" },\n        { \"field\": \"durability\", \"value\": \"mixed\" },\n        { \"field\": \"morality_separation_check\", \"value\": \"The score reflects execution of the ruler's own program, not approval of its moral content.\" }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"dossier_job_key\": \"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:JPN:16638\",\n      \"iso3\": \"JPN\",\n      \"ruler_id\": \"2895\",\n      \"ruler_year_id\": 16638,\n      \"ruler_name\": \"Fumio Kishida\",\n      \"period_start_year\": 2022,\n      \"period_end_year\": 2022,\n      \"chapter_id\": \"8B\",\n      \"rubric_version\": \"chapter_8b_v3\",\n      \"calibration_batch_id\": \"chapter-judge:2022-saturation-v3-stage1-controlled:2022:8B\",\n      \"calibrated_against\": [\n        \"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:BGD:17068\",\n        \"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:CHN:15832\",\n        \"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:RUS:15706\",\n        \"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:USA:15810\"\n      ],\n      \"score_1_to_10\": 6.5,\n      \"insufficient_evidence_reason\": null,\n      \"confidence_score\": 76,\n      \"plausible_score_range\": { \"lower\": 6.0, \"upper\": 7.5 },\n      \"decisive_positive_evidence\": [\n        { \"evidence_id\": \"E0026\", \"explanation\": \"Shows a major security-policy shift and large defense buildup adopted in 2022.\" },\n        { \"evidence_id\": \"E0080\", \"explanation\": \"Shows explicit monitoring and workforce-investment coordination in the supplementary budget.\" },\n       "}}
