{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_0","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"schema_version\":\"ruler_chapter_judgment_v1\",\"job_key\":\"chapter-judge:2022-saturation-v3-stage1-controlled:2022:8B\",\"run_key\":\"2022-saturation-v3-stage1-controlled\",\"chapter_id\":\"8B\",\"target_year\":2022,\"rubric_version\":\"chapter_8b_v3\",\"calibration_batch_id\":\"chapter-judge:2022-saturation-v3-stage1-controlled:2022:8B\",\"evaluations\":[{\"dossier_job_key\":\"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:BGD:17068\",\"iso3\":\"BGD\",\"ruler_id\":\"2992\",\"ruler_year_id\":17068,\"ruler_name\":\"Sheikh Hasina\",\"period_start_year\":2022,\"period_end_year\":2022,\"chapter_id\":\"8B\",\"rubric_version\":\"chapter_8b_v3\",\"calibration_batch_id\":\"chapter-judge:2022-saturation-v3-stage1-controlled:2022:8B\",\"calibrated_against\":[\"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:DEU:16984\",\"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:IND:19645\",\"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:RUS:15706\"],\"score_1_to_10\":6.5,\"insufficient_evidence_reason\":null,\"confidence_score\":76,\"plausible_score_range\":{\"lower\":6.0,\"upper\":7.5},\"decisive_positive_evidence\":[{\"evidence_id\":\"E0059\",\"explanation\":\"The 2022 stabilization package set concrete policy priorities such as revenue mobilization, monetary modernization, and exchange-rate flexibility, showing a clear governing program translated into action.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0060\",\"explanation\":\"The World Bank credit for economic resilience shows formal implementation through fiscal and financial-sector reform, not just rhetoric.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0081\",\"explanation\":\"The FY22 budgeted social safety-net expansion shows allocative commitment and a state delivery channel aimed at broad welfare objectives.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0067\",\"explanation\":\"The appointment of a central bank governor with macro-finance experience is direct evidence of personnel choices aligned to the program.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0090\",\"explanation\":\"The homelessness and housing program shows direct executive agenda-setting and a concrete delivery claim within the year.\"}],\"decisive_negative_evidence\":[{\"evidence_id\":\"E0064\",\"explanation\":\"The fuel-price shock and reserve pressure show real macro stress and constrain any claim of clean competence.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0075\",\"explanation\":\"Climate-resilience gains were largely inherited/system-level rather than uniquely Hasina-directed, limiting ruler-specific credit.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0057\",\"explanation\":\"The same IMF material notes health and education spending remained low, showing that social-protection gains did not solve broader delivery gaps.\"}],\"inherited_baseline_and_constraints\":\"Bangladesh entered 2022 with growth, poverty-reduction, and climate-resilience gains already built into the system, but also with inflation, reserve pressure, and banking vulnerabilities that limited what any ruler could accomplish in one year.\",\"ruler_attribution\":\"Hasina has substantial ownership of the budget, welfare, and macro-stabilization agenda, but many implementations ran through ministries and inherited institutional capacity rather than personal hands-on control.\",\"supported_lenses\":[\"8B.1\",\"8B.2\",\"8B.3\",\"8B.4\",\"8B.5\",\"8B.6\",\"8B.7\",\"8B.8\",\"8B.9\",\"8B.10\"],\"missing_or_weak_lenses\":[\"8B.7\",\"8B.8\"],\"contrary_evidence\":[{\"evidence_id\":\"E0064\",\"explanation\":\"Inflation, reserve decline, and fuel-price hikes complicate any strong reading of 2022 economic competence.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0057\",\"explanation\":\"Health and education financing gaps show that social-policy gains were partial, not comprehensive.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0075\",\"explanation\":\"Some welfare and resilience advantages reflect long-run inherited systems rather than 2022 ruler execution alone.\"}],\"source_mix\":\"Primary IMF and World Bank material, official budget and government notices, plus a Reuters wire and local reporting. The dossier is mostly official or multilateral, with enough external corroboration to support a moderate-high confidence judgment, but household-level outcome audits remain thinner than program design.\",\"structured_prior_summary\":\"No structured local priors were collected in this experiment; the score rests on the embedded dossier evidence and cross-lens comparison only.\",\"chapter_rationale\":\"Sheikh Hasina scores as moderately strong on competence because the record shows a clear governing program for economic stabilization, social protection, and welfare delivery, and it also shows that parts of that program were translated into budgets, appointments, and visible policy actions during 2022. The strongest evidence is not abstract rhetoric but concrete state action: a stabilization package, expanded social safety-net spending, a central-bank appointment, and housing and cash-transfer programs. The limiting factor is that the dossier still lacks independent, household-level proof that these initiatives broadly solved delivery problems, and the same year also featured inflation, reserve stress, and other macro constraints. This places her above a merely symbolic or stalled administrator, but below a ruler whose 2022 record demonstrates durable, independently verified outcome gains across most of the agenda.\",\"lower_anchor_rejected\":\"A 5.5 score is too low because this dossier contains real budgetary conversion, appointments, and program rollout, not just a declared plan.\",\"higher_anchor_rejected\":\"A materially higher score is not defensible because independent execution audits and household-level outcome evidence are limited, and several gains remain partly inherited or only partially implemented.\",\"manual_review_required\":false,\"manual_review_reason_type\":null,\"manual_review_reason\":null,\"chapter_specific\":[{\"field\":\"program_basis\",\"value\":\"explicit: growth, stabilization, social protection, housing, and climate-resilience governance.\"},{\"field\":\"program_type\",\"value\":\"policy; state_building.\"},{\"field\":\"strategic_clarity\",\"value\":\"clear.\"},{\"field\":\"operationalization_and_coordination\",\"value\":\"strong: budgets, appointments, and program channels are visible.\"},{\"field\":\"adaptation_and_correction\",\"value\":\"mixed: there is active stabilization, but the record also shows stress and incomplete follow-through.\"},{\"field\":\"goal_progress_and_durability\",\"value\":\"mixed to substantial: some goals advanced, but durability and independence of outcome evidence are incomplete.\"},{\"field\":\"trajectory\",\"value\":\"upward but incomplete.\"},{\"field\":\"morality_separation_check\",\"value\":\"The score reflects execution only; welfare value and alleged integrity problems are evaluated elsewhere.\"},{\"field\":\"defensible_score_range\",\"value\":\"6.0-7.5.\"}]},{\"dossier_job_key\":\"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:BRA:19646\",\"iso3\":\"BRA\",\"ruler_id\":\"3413\",\"ruler_year_id\":19646,\"ruler_name\":\"Jair Bolsonaro\",\"period_start_year\":2022,\"period_end_year\":2022,\"chapter_id\":\"8B\",\"rubric_version\":\"chapter_8b_v3\",\"calibration_batch_id\":\"chapter-judge:2022-saturation-v3-stage1-controlled:2022:8B\",\"calibrated_against\":[\"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:DEU:16984\",\"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:IND:19645\",\"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:RUS:15706\"],\"score_1_to_10\":5.5,\"insufficient_evidence_reason\":null,\"confidence_score\":69,\"plausible_score_range\":{\"lower\":5.0,\"upper\":6.0},\"decisive_positive_evidence\":[{\"evidence_id\":\"E0061\",\"explanation\":\"The presidential decree delegating budget-credit authority is direct evidence of executive action and administrative control.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0065\",\"explanation\":\"Plano Safra 2022/23 shows concrete rural-credit allocation and implementation of a major sector policy.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0070\",\"explanation\":\"The Auxílio Brasil expansion shows real-scale social transfer rollout under the administration.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0074\",\"explanation\":\"Internet Brasil creation demonstrates new policy formation and presidential assent.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0101\",\"explanation\":\"The tariff cut is a concrete macro-policy choice aimed at prices and trade support.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0102\",\"explanation\":\"The state-state agreement on fuel and electricity taxes shows crisis management through intergovernmental negotiation.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0064\",\"explanation\":\"PPI's year-end implementation summary provides evidence of completed projects and contracted investment.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0104\",\"explanation\":\"IBGE's retrospective income recovery data show that some 2022 outcomes did improve, even if partly transfer-driven.\"}],\"decisive_negative_evidence\":[{\"evidence_id\":\"E0055\",\"explanation\":\"The central bank minutes show high inflation and mixed economic conditions, limiting any strong competence claim.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0103\",\"explanation\":\"The Bolsonaro-backed spending package bypassing the cap shows political tacticalism and fiscal strain rather than clean governance.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0097\",\"explanation\":\"The campaign program is largely intent and election rhetoric, so it does not substantially strengthen the implementation record.\"}],\"inherited_baseline_and_constraints\":\"Brazil entered 2022 with commodity, inflation, and coalition constraints, so some outcomes reflect the external environment and Congress as much as Bolsonaro's choices.\",\"ruler_attribution\":\"Bolsonaro clearly owned the executive agenda and election-year policy mix, but many outcomes were mediated by Congress, regulators, and the broader macro cycle, which caps personal credit.\",\"supported_lenses\":[\"8B.1\",\"8B.2\",\"8B.3\",\"8B.4\",\"8B.5\",\"8B.6\",\"8B.7\",\"8B.8\",\"8B.9\",\"8B.10\"],\"missing_or_weak_lenses\":[\"8B.7\",\"8B.8\"],\"contrary_evidence\":[{\"evidence_id\":\"E0055\",\"explanation\":\"Inflation and commodity shocks complicate performance attribution.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0103\",\"explanation\":\"Fiscal loosening and election-year spending undercut a clean competence reading.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0104\",\"explanation\":\"Income recovery was partly transfer-driven and not a pure measure of durable policy skill.\"}],\"source_mix\":\"Mostly official Brazilian decrees, ministry releases, and program pages, supplemented by Reuters and IBGE retrospective data. The mix is good for tracing policy action, but several of the strongest items are self-described government achievements rather than independent audits.\",\"structured_prior_summary\":\"No structured local priors were collected in this experiment; the judgment relies on the dossier's mixed evidence of rollout, fiscal politics, and macro outcomes only.\",\"chapter_rationale\":\"Jair Bolsonaro lands in the middle of the scale because his 2022 record shows real state action, but not a clean or durable governing success. The dossier contains concrete policies and implementations: delegated budget authority, rural credit, cash transfers, tariff cuts, school connectivity, and other visible administrative moves. At the same time, the year was heavily election-shaped, the fiscal stance was politically stressed, and the evidence on outcomes is mixed rather than clearly durable. That is enough to beat a merely symbolic or stalled record, but not enough to justify a stronger score because the clearest gains are tangled with fiscal strain, external conditions, and short-term politics.\",\"lower_anchor_rejected\":\"A 4.5 score is too low because the dossier shows multiple enacted programs and budgetary actions, not just slogans or surviving by inertia.\",\"higher_anchor_rejected\":\"A materially higher score is not defensible because the most important outcomes are mixed, several measures are election-driven, and independent durability evidence is limited.\",\"manual_review_required\":false,\"manual_review_reason_type\":null,\"manual_review_reason\":null,\"chapter_specific\":[{\"field\":\"program_basis\",\"value\":\"mixed: social transfers, price relief, rural credit, tariff cuts, infrastructure, and campaign-era economic liberalism.\"},{\"field\":\"program_type\",\"value\":\"policy; state_building; power_consolidation.\"},{\"field\":\"strategic_clarity\",\"value\":\"clear but politically opportunistic.\"},{\"field\":\"operationalization_and_coordination\",\"value\":\"mixed: real rollouts exist, but Congress and inflation constrained execution.\"},{\"field\":\"adaptation_and_correction\",\"value\":\"mixed: some corrective policy action, but much of it was reactive and election-timed.\"},{\"field\":\"goal_progress_and_durability\",\"value\":\"mixed: tangible delivery is visible, but durable outcome evidence is uneven.\"},{\"field\":\"trajectory\",\"value\":\"mixed, with short-term delivery and weak long-run coherence.\"},{\"field\":\"morality_separation_check\",\"value\":\"The score is about execution of the revealed program, not the program's moral character or electoral ethics.\"},{\"field\":\"defensible_score_range\",\"value\":\"5.0-6.0.\"}]},{\"dossier_job_key\":\"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:CHN:15832\",\"iso3\":\"CHN\",\"ruler_id\":\"1432\",\"ruler_year_id\":15832,\"ruler_name\":\"Xi Jinping\",\"period_start_year\":2022,\"period_end_year\":2022,\"chapter_id\":\"8B\",\"rubric_version\":\"chapter_8b_v3\",\"calibration_batch_id\":\"chapter-judge:2022-saturation-v3-stage1-controlled:2022:8B\",\"calibrated_against\":[\"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:DEU:16984\",\"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:IND:19645\",\"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:RUS:15706\"],\"score_1_to_10\":8.0,\"insufficient_evidence_reason\":null,\"confidence_score\":87,\"plausible_score_range\":{\"lower\":7.5,\"upper\":8.5},\"decisive_positive_evidence\":[{\"evidence_id\":\"E0077\",\"explanation\":\"The Party Constitution changes show explicit programmatic direction and centralized political ownership of a long-run strategy.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0103\",\"explanation\":\"The Congress report lays out a detailed five-year program, which is strong evidence of strategic clarity and agenda-setting.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0105\",\"explanation\":\"The 33-measure stabilization package shows rapid translation of the program into concrete economic instruments.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0107\",\"explanation\":\"Targeted credit and urban-service adjustments show state apparatus mobilization beyond mere rhetoric.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0108\",\"explanation\":\"The anti-corruption campaign is not just declaratory; it is backed by procedures and personnel control.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0111\",\"explanation\":\"The 20 COVID measures show adaptation and recalibration rather than rigid insistence on a failed policy line.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0112\",\"explanation\":\"The year-end shift in COVID management shows the leadership could reverse course after severe disruption.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0045\",\"explanation\":\"The third-term consolidation confirms the political program was implemented at the top of the system.\"}],\"decisive_negative_evidence\":[{\"evidence_id\":\"E0040\",\"explanation\":\"The Shanghai lockdown episode shows severe coercive costs and disruption, which cap any claim of clean administrative success.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0052\",\"explanation\":\"The easing of curbs after protest pressure shows the system was reactive, not perfectly anticipatory.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0108\",\"explanation\":\"Anti-corruption rhetoric alone does not prove impartial enforcement, so some of the best evidence remains programmatic rather than fully outcome-verified.\"}],\"inherited_baseline_and_constraints\":\"China entered 2022 with unusually high state capacity and a one-party apparatus already capable of mobilization, so the main question is not raw power but whether Xi used it coherently toward his own goals under zero-COVID and slowing-growth constraints.\",\"ruler_attribution\":\"Xi's ownership of the program is very strong: the dossier shows top-level party control, direct agenda-setting, and coordinated state action. The main caveat is that some outcomes reflect collective party-state machinery and some gains are easier to see in policy outputs than in independently audited welfare results.\",\"supported_lenses\":[\"8B.1\",\"8B.2\",\"8B.3\",\"8B.4\",\"8B.5\",\"8B.6\",\"8B.7\",\"8B.8\",\"8B.9\",\"8B.10\"],\"missing_or_weak_lenses\":[\"8B.7\",\"8B.9\"],\"contrary_evidence\":[{\"evidence_id\":\"E0040\",\"explanation\":\"The Shanghai lockdown shows harsh cost and disruption, limiting the competence ceiling.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0052\",\"explanation\":\"Some policy changes were reactive to protest pressure, not purely planned correction.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0108\",\"explanation\":\"Stated anti-corruption resolve is not the same as independently verified impartial enforcement.\"}],\"source_mix\":\"Heavy use of official party-state texts and speeches, with Reuters and other external reporting for corroboration and consequence checks. The mix is strong for policy line, appointments, and implementation architecture, but less strong for independent evaluation of welfare and rights outcomes.\",\"structured_prior_summary\":\"No structured local priors were collected in this experiment; the judgment is driven by the embedded dossier's strong programmatic and implementation evidence.\",\"chapter_rationale\":\"Xi Jinping scores in the strong range because the dossier shows unusually clear strategic direction and unusually strong conversion of that direction into state action. The 2022 record includes a detailed five-year program, a large stabilization package, targeted credit and urban-policy measures, a top-level leadership consolidation, and a late-year COVID policy reversal that shows adaptation when the earlier line became untenable. The main things holding the score below the very top are that some of the sharpest outcomes are still official self-reports, the repression and lockdown costs are severe, and independent outcome verification is thinner than the policy architecture. Even so, this is clearly stronger than a merely competent or mixed record: the leadership consistently mobilized the party-state toward its chosen program and adjusted course when needed.\",\"lower_anchor_rejected\":\"A 7.0 score is too low because the dossier shows sustained top-down mobilization, concrete policy packages, and real adaptation across major priorities.\",\"higher_anchor_rejected\":\"A 9.0 score is too high because the evidence does not yet show fully durable, independently audited success across the whole portfolio, and some of the most visible achievements are paired with severe coercive costs.\",\"manual_review_required\":false,\"manual_review_reason_type\":null,\"manual_review_reason\":null,\"chapter_specific\":[{\"field\":\"program_basis\",\"value\":\"explicit: party control, common prosperity, growth, security, and zero-COVID management.\"},{\"field\":\"program_type\",\"value\":\"policy; regime_control; power_consolidation; state_building.\"},{\"field\":\"strategic_clarity\",\"value\":\"exceptional.\"},{\"field\":\"operationalization_and_coordination\",\"value\":\"strong to exceptional.\"},{\"field\":\"adaptation_and_correction\",\"value\":\"effective: the late-2022 COVID rollback is a real course correction.\"},{\"field\":\"goal_progress_and_durability\",\"value\":\"substantial, with durable political consolidation but mixed policy durability.\"},{\"field\":\"trajectory\",\"value\":\"upward on control and agenda-setting, mixed on social-cost outcomes.\"},{\"field\":\"morality_separation_check\",\"value\":\"The score reflects execution of Xi's program, not approval of the program's political or moral content.\"},{\"field\":\"defensible_score_range\",\"value\":\"7.5-8.5.\"}]},{\"dossier_job_key\":\"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:COD:16113\",\"iso3\":\"COD\",\"ruler_id\":\"2830\",\"ruler_year_id\":16113,\"ruler_name\":\"Félix Tshisekedi\",\"period_start_year\":2022,\"period_end_year\":2022,\"chapter_id\":\"8B\",\"rubric_version\":\"chapter_8b_v3\",\"calibration_batch_id\":\"chapter-judge:2022-saturation-v3-stage1-controlled:2022:8B\",\"calibrated_against\":[\"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:DEU:16984\",\"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:IND:19645\",\"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:RUS:15706\"],\"score_1_to_10\":4.5,\"insufficient_evidence_reason\":null,\"confidence_score\":67,\"plausible_score_range\":{\"lower\":4.0,\"upper\":5.0},\"decisive_positive_evidence\":[{\"evidence_id\":\"E0108\",\"explanation\":\"Tshisekedi personally chaired an evaluation meeting on the 145-territories program, showing direct oversight of a major development initiative.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0111\",\"explanation\":\"The solidarity and disaster-management fund and the monitoring mechanism show real institutional setup under his direction.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0112\",\"explanation\":\"The swearing-in and directives to magistrates show some institutional reform activity and presidential attention to governance.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0118\",\"explanation\":\"The IMF's prudential macro assessment shows some real policy discipline, especially ending central-bank financing of the government.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0121\",\"explanation\":\"The eastern provinces grant shows mobilization of major donor-backed stabilization resources in line with the government's agenda.\"}],\"decisive_negative_evidence\":[{\"evidence_id\":\"E0117\",\"explanation\":\"The telecom reform still needed secondary legislation, showing that key reforms were incomplete in 2022.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0119\",\"explanation\":\"The vaccination campaign's low baseline and catch-up character show effort under strain rather than completed success.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0107\",\"explanation\":\"The World Bank framework supports priorities but also highlights weak governance and the gap between agenda and delivery.\"}],\"inherited_baseline_and_constraints\":\"The DRC's baseline in 2022 was heavily constrained by weak institutions, donor dependence, conflict exposure, and thin administrative reach, so even real programs were hard to convert into durable statewide results.\",\"ruler_attribution\":\"Tshisekedi owns the reform agenda and some visible oversight actions, but many implementation steps are donor-mediated, ministry-led, or merely preparatory, which keeps attribution and effectiveness modest rather than strong.\",\"supported_lenses\":[\"8B.1\",\"8B.2\",\"8B.3\",\"8B.4\",\"8B.5\",\"8B.6\",\"8B.7\",\"8B.8\",\"8B.9\",\"8B.10\"],\"missing_or_weak_lenses\":[\"8B.7\",\"8B.8\",\"8B.10\"],\"contrary_evidence\":[{\"evidence_id\":\"E0117\",\"explanation\":\"Key reforms were still incomplete and required follow-on legislation.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0119\",\"explanation\":\"Campaign targets were ambitious relative to the weak baseline, limiting evidence of success.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0107\",\"explanation\":\"The supporting framework points to priorities and financing, not yet to broad independent outcome success.\"}],\"source_mix\":\"Official presidential pages, IMF and World Bank documents, WHO and local reporting. The mix is adequate for tracing agenda and partial implementation, but strong independent outcome audits are still thin.\",\"structured_prior_summary\":\"No structured local priors were collected in this experiment; the dossier itself provides only thin evidence on institutional quality and delivery.\",\"chapter_rationale\":\"Félix Tshisekedi is a mixed case: the record shows real agenda-setting, some direct oversight, and some policy discipline, but not enough durable state capacity to score as broadly effective. The strongest favorable evidence is that he personally chaired development and governance meetings and the government did move on macro stabilization, telecom reform, humanitarian funding, and eastern-province assistance. The limiting evidence is that many of these actions were still at the level of setup, financing, or incomplete legal change, and the dossier repeatedly shows weak implementation follow-through. That makes him better than a purely ceremonial or collapsed ruler, but still well short of the kind of sustained, outcome-backed competence needed for a higher score.\",\"lower_anchor_rejected\":\"A 3.5 score is too low because the dossier contains real presidential oversight, macro discipline, and program mobilization rather than only stasis or failure.\",\"higher_anchor_rejected\":\"A score above 5 is not defensible because most major programs remain incomplete, donor-mediated, or weakly verified at the outcome level.\",\"manual_review_required\":false,\"manual_review_reason_type\":null,\"manual_review_reason\":null,\"chapter_specific\":[{\"field\":\"program_basis\",\"value\":\"mixed: development, anti-corruption, social protection, and territorial stabilization.\"},{\"field\":\"program_type\",\"value\":\"policy; state_building; international_influence.\"},{\"field\":\"strategic_clarity\",\"value\":\"partial.\"},{\"field\":\"operationalization_and_coordination\",\"value\":\"mixed: some concrete institutions and funds, but much remains preparatory.\"},{\"field\":\"adaptation_and_correction\",\"value\":\"mixed: there are real corrections, but the evidence is not durable or fully verified.\"},{\"field\":\"goal_progress_and_durability\",\"value\":\"mixed, with some mobilization but weak durable proof of broad state reach.\"},{\"field\":\"trajectory\",\"value\":\"slight upward movement, but still fragile.\"},{\"field\":\"morality_separation_check\",\"value\":\"The score is an execution judgment only; conflict environment and governance weakness are not moral deductions here.\"},{\"field\":\"defensible_score_range\",\"value\":\"4.0-5.0.\"}]},{\"dossier_job_key\":\"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:DEU:16984\",\"iso3\":\"DEU\",\"ruler_id\":\"2975\",\"ruler_year_id\":16984,\"ruler_name\":\"Olaf Scholz\",\"period_start_year\":2022,\"period_end_year\":2022,\"chapter_id\":\"8B\",\"rubric_version\":\"chapter_8b_v3\",\"calibration_batch_id\":\"chapter-judge:2022-saturation-v3-stage1-controlled:2022:8B\",\"calibrated_against\":[\"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:IND:19645\",\"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:RUS:15706\",\"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:USA:15810\"],\"score_1_to_10\":6.5,\"insufficient_evidence_reason\":null,\"confidence_score\":79,\"plausible_score_range\":{\"lower\":6.0,\"upper\":7.0},\"decisive_positive_evidence\":[{\"evidence_id\":\"E0087\",\"explanation\":\"The 100 billion euro Bundeswehr fund is a major strategic shift and a concrete policy commitment.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0092\",\"explanation\":\"The Uniper stabilization package shows crisis management and willingness to act decisively on energy security.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0093\",\"explanation\":\"The refugee coordination framework shows real federal mobilization with local implementation partners.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0088\",\"explanation\":\"The Bürgergeld reform shows a substantive social-policy redesign backed by the cabinet and ministry.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0091\",\"explanation\":\"Wohngeld Plus shows large-scale social-benefit reform that was actually approved in 2022.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0094\",\"explanation\":\"The representative survey gives evidence that integration systems were being used in practice by year-end.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0096\",\"explanation\":\"The IMF judged the government response to energy shocks appropriate, which is strong independent corroboration.\"}],\"decisive_negative_evidence\":[{\"evidence_id\":\"E0095\",\"explanation\":\"The OECD said some support was too broad and could have been better targeted, limiting the score ceiling.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0097\",\"explanation\":\"ifo criticism about the cost of relief packages shows sustainability and targeting concerns.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0096\",\"explanation\":\"The same IMF material also notes that uncertainty and downside risks remained high, so the shock was not solved.\"}],\"inherited_baseline_and_constraints\":\"Germany started from a high-capacity administrative baseline, but 2022 was dominated by the Ukraine war and energy shock, so the benchmark is crisis response and implementation quality rather than radical transformation.\",\"ruler_attribution\":\"Scholz clearly owned the governing program and crisis response, though much of the implementation was coalition-based and ministry-driven; that lowers personal exclusivity but not the competence signal.\",\"supported_lenses\":[\"8B.1\",\"8B.2\",\"8B.3\",\"8B.4\",\"8B.5\",\"8B.6\",\"8B.7\",\"8B.8\",\"8B.9\",\"8B.10\"],\"missing_or_weak_lenses\":[\"8B.7\",\"8B.8\"],\"contrary_evidence\":[{\"evidence_id\":\"E0095\",\"explanation\":\"Policy support was criticised as broad and inefficient.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0097\",\"explanation\":\"Relief packages raised sustainability concerns.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0096\",\"explanation\":\"External risk remained high despite the response.\"}],\"source_mix\":\"Mostly official German federal sources and ministry releases, plus IMF, OECD, and ifo assessments. This is a strong mix for tracing state action and checking it against independent macro commentary.\",\"structured_prior_summary\":\"No structured local priors were collected in this experiment; the dossier is already well-supported by official documents and independent surveillance.\",\"chapter_rationale\":\"Olaf Scholz scores as fairly effective because the dossier shows a government that did not merely announce priorities but actually mobilized budgets, legislation, and crisis interventions in a difficult year. The energy package, refugee coordination, social-benefit reforms, and defense reorientation are all concrete and contemporaneous, and several are independently recognized by the IMF and OECD as real policy responses. The score is not higher because the relief architecture was imperfectly targeted, the shock environment remained severe, and some benefits were not yet fully visible by year-end. That combination is clearly above a mixed or hesitant record, but not strong enough for the highly durable, broadly transformative tier.\",\"lower_anchor_rejected\":\"A 5.5 score is too low because the dossier contains multiple enacted, coordinated, and crisis-relevant interventions with independent confirmation.\",\"higher_anchor_rejected\":\"A score above 7 is too high because the evidence still shows major targeting and sustainability concerns, and several benefits were not yet fully realized in 2022.\",\"manual_review_required\":false,\"manual_review_reason_type\":null,\"manual_review_reason\":null,\"chapter_specific\":[{\"field\":\"program_basis\",\"value\":\"explicit: modern state, social security, energy security, defense reinforcement, and refugee support.\"},{\"field\":\"program_type\",\"value\":\"policy; state_building.\"},{\"field\":\"strategic_clarity\",\"value\":\"clear.\"},{\"field\":\"operationalization_and_coordination\",\"value\":\"strong: cabinet, ministries, and Bundestag all moved in concert.\"},{\"field\":\"adaptation_and_correction\",\"value\":\"effective: the energy and refugee responses are real crisis adaptations.\"},{\"field\":\"goal_progress_and_durability\",\"value\":\"substantial but not durable enough for a higher tier.\"},{\"field\":\"trajectory\",\"value\":\"upward in crisis response, with durable reforms still pending.\"},{\"field\":\"morality_separation_check\",\"value\":\"The score reflects execution, not endorsement of any policy goals.\"},{\"field\":\"defensible_score_range\",\"value\":\"6.0-7.0.\"}]},{\"dossier_job_key\":\"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:EGY:16232\",\"iso3\":\"EGY\",\"ruler_id\":\"2851\",\"ruler_year_id\":16232,\"ruler_name\":\"Abdel Fattah el-Sisi\",\"period_start_year\":2022,\"period_end_year\":2022,\"chapter_id\":\"8B\",\"rubric_version\":\"chapter_8b_v3\",\"calibration_batch_id\":\"chapter-judge:2022-saturation-v3-stage1-controlled:2022:8B\",\"calibrated_against\":[\"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:DEU:16984\",\"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:IND:19645\",\"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:RUS:15706\"],\"score_1_to_10\":5.5,\"insufficient_evidence_reason\":null,\"confidence_score\":72,\"plausible_score_range\":{\"lower\":5.0,\"upper\":6.0},\"decisive_positive_evidence\":[{\"evidence_id\":\"E0052\",\"explanation\":\"The caretaker central-bank appointment is direct executive action in the middle of a currency crisis.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0079\",\"explanation\":\"The appointment of a military general to lead the anti-corruption authority shows direct personnel control over oversight institutions.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0082\",\"explanation\":\"The state ownership policy is a concrete presidential policy decision with measurable sectoral targets.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0081\",\"explanation\":\"The IMF-supported governance and transparency package shows policy direction toward reform, even if not yet fully executed.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0078\",\"explanation\":\"The first-time military appointment to a top court shows real institutional penetration and personnel management.\"}],\"decisive_negative_evidence\":[{\"evidence_id\":\"E0074\",\"explanation\":\"Freedom House's assessment of security-dominated policymaking and low transparency sharply caps claims of clean administrative competence.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0073\",\"explanation\":\"The military-economy opacity and patronage structure show that the system remained opaque and unevenly disciplined.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0080\",\"explanation\":\"The professional judicial appointment is a counterexample that shows the dossier is mixed rather than uniformly patronage-driven.\"}],\"inherited_baseline_and_constraints\":\"Egypt's baseline is a deeply military-shaped, opaque, and centralized state with substantial inherited control but persistent fiscal and institutional distortions, so the relevant question is how much Sisi turned that control into effective policy rather than whether he had control at all.\",\"ruler_attribution\":\"Sisi's ownership of appointments and high-level policy is very strong, but many outcomes remain opaque and institutionally mediated, so the score reflects control plus partial policy conversion, not proven broad effectiveness.\",\"supported_lenses\":[\"8B.1\",\"8B.2\",\"8B.3\",\"8B.4\",\"8B.5\",\"8B.6\",\"8B.7\",\"8B.8\",\"8B.9\",\"8B.10\"],\"missing_or_weak_lenses\":[\"8B.7\",\"8B.8\",\"8B.10\"],\"contrary_evidence\":[{\"evidence_id\":\"E0074\",\"explanation\":\"The system remains opaque and security-dominated.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0073\",\"explanation\":\"Military financial opacity and patronage remain significant.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0080\",\"explanation\":\"Not every appointment is political capture; the record is mixed, not one-dimensional.\"}],\"source_mix\":\"A strong mix of presidential notices, IMF and Freedom House analysis, and independent Egyptian reporting. The source pattern is enough to judge state control and some policy conversion, but outcome verification is still limited by opacity.\",\"structured_prior_summary\":\"No structured local priors were collected in this experiment; the dossier's own evidence is already heavy on control and light on audited outcomes.\",\"chapter_rationale\":\"Abdel Fattah el-Sisi scores in the middle because the dossier shows a leader with strong control over appointments and policy direction, but not one whose 2022 record demonstrates consistently verified delivery. There are real actions here: a central-bank appointment during crisis, an anti-corruption chief selected by the presidency, a state-ownership policy, and IMF-linked governance reforms. Yet much of the evidence is about control architecture and stated reform intent, while independent proof of broad implementation or improved outcomes is thin. That supports a score above a weak or stalled regime, but below the stronger, outcome-verified tier.\",\"lower_anchor_rejected\":\"A 4.5 score is too low because the record contains concrete presidential actions, not just rhetoric or drift.\",\"higher_anchor_rejected\":\"A score above 6 is too high because the dossier remains opaque and lacks enough independent outcome verification to show durable effectiveness.\",\"manual_review_required\":false,\"manual_review_reason_type\":null,\"manual_review_reason\":null,\"chapter_specific\":[{\"field\":\"program_basis\",\"value\":\"mixed: macro stabilization, state ownership, oversight control, and governance reform.\"},{\"field\":\"program_type\",\"value\":\"policy; regime_control; state_building.\"},{\"field\":\"strategic_clarity\",\"value\":\"clear at the level of control and state direction, weaker on public-benefit execution.\"},{\"field\":\"operationalization_and_coordination\",\"value\":\"mixed: appointments and policy documents exist, but output verification is thin.\"},{\"field\":\"adaptation_and_correction\",\"value\":\"mixed: crisis appointments and policy redesign are visible, but not enough to show decisive correction.\"},{\"field\":\"goal_progress_and_durability\",\"value\":\"mixed: some state control is durable, but broad effectiveness is not independently shown.\"},{\"field\":\"trajectory\",\"value\":\"stable control with partial reform movement.\"},{\"field\":\"morality_separation_check\",\"value\":\"The score is an execution assessment only and does not reward or punish the regime's moral character.\"},{\"field\":\"defensible_score_range\",\"value\":\"5.0-6.0.\"}]},{\"dossier_job_key\":\"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:ETH:16782\",\"iso3\":\"ETH\",\"ruler_id\":\"2310\",\"ruler_year_id\":16782,\"ruler_name\":\"Abiy Ahmed\",\"period_start_year\":2022,\"period_end_year\":2022,\"chapter_id\":\"8B\",\"rubric_version\":\"chapter_8b_v3\",\"calibration_batch_id\":\"chapter-judge:2022-saturation-v3-stage1-controlled:2022:8B\",\"calibrated_against\":[\"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:DEU:16984\",\"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:IND:19645\",\"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:RUS:15706\"],\"score_1_to_10\":5.0,\"insufficient_evidence_reason\":null,\"confidence_score\":66,\"plausible_score_range\":{\"lower\":4.5,\"upper\":5.5},\"decisive_positive_evidence\":[{\"evidence_id\":\"E0082\",\"explanation\":\"The IMF-backed reform agenda shows a clear policy direction toward macro correction, FX reform, and private-sector-led growth.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0086\",\"explanation\":\"The anti-corruption committee is a concrete institutional response to a governance problem.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0088\",\"explanation\":\"The National Peace Council shows an attempt to build coordination around the peace process.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0089\",\"explanation\":\"Aid access opening after the ceasefire shows real implementation movement, even if incomplete.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0091\",\"explanation\":\"The nationwide measles campaign is a concrete government-led health action with partner support.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0092\",\"explanation\":\"Service-restoration figures in Tigray indicate partial post-ceasefire state re-entry.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0093\",\"explanation\":\"UN/OCHA-quoted trucking and corridor data show the relief corridor was actually functioning by year-end.\"}],\"decisive_negative_evidence\":[{\"evidence_id\":\"E0041\",\"explanation\":\"The national dialogue record is contested and shows exclusion and orchestration accusations, weakening the score ceiling.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0090\",\"explanation\":\"The ceasefire-implementation promise is not outcome proof; it remains declaratory.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0083\",\"explanation\":\"The monitoring report exposes inequities and implementation challenges, showing the underlying recovery was incomplete.\"}],\"inherited_baseline_and_constraints\":\"Ethiopia in 2022 was still shaped by war, severe humanitarian stress, and weak institutions, so even real policy moves are partly recovery from collapse rather than clean routine governance.\",\"ruler_attribution\":\"Abiy's government clearly owns the 2022 reform, ceasefire, and recovery agenda, but much of the visible evidence is partial implementation or partner-mediated delivery rather than fully independently verified success.\",\"supported_lenses\":[\"8B.1\",\"8B.2\",\"8B.3\",\"8B.4\",\"8B.5\",\"8B.6\",\"8B.7\",\"8B.8\",\"8B.9\",\"8B.10\"],\"missing_or_weak_lenses\":[\"8B.7\",\"8B.8\",\"8B.10\"],\"contrary_evidence\":[{\"evidence_id\":\"E0041\",\"explanation\":\"Dialogue inclusivity is disputed and some critics saw orchestration rather than genuine opening.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0083\",\"explanation\":\"Monitoring data show uneven recovery and existing vulnerabilities.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0090\",\"explanation\":\"Ceasefire promises alone do not establish durable implementation.\"}],\"source_mix\":\"A mix of official Ethiopian releases, the IMF, World Bank, WHO, Reuters, and independent reporting. The evidence is enough to see both policy activity and persistent execution gaps, but the dossier remains thin on fully audited outcomes.\",\"structured_prior_summary\":\"No structured local priors were collected in this experiment; the dossier's evidence already captures a constrained post-conflict state with partial recovery.\",\"chapter_rationale\":\"Abiy Ahmed earns a mid-range score because 2022 shows genuine mobilization after crisis, but not enough sustained implementation to call the year strongly effective. The government launched anti-corruption, peace, health, and service-restoration initiatives, and it also moved on ceasefire-linked humanitarian access. Those are not trivial; they show state re-entry and a real attempt to shift from conflict management to recovery. But the same dossier repeatedly shows partial access, incomplete reforms, contested dialogue politics, and weak independent outcome verification, so the record stops short of a high competence score.\",\"lower_anchor_rejected\":\"A 4.0 score is too low because the dossier shows real post-ceasefire mobilization and concrete institutional action, not just symbolic gestures.\",\"higher_anchor_rejected\":\"A score above 5.5 is too high because implementation is still partial, contested, and thinly audited across the main priorities.\",\"manual_review_required\":false,\"manual_review_reason_type\":null,\"manual_review_reason\":null,\"chapter_specific\":[{\"field\":\"program_basis\",\"value\":\"mixed: recovery, peace, anti-corruption, and macro correction after conflict.\"},{\"field\":\"program_type\",\"value\":\"policy; state_building; survival.\"},{\"field\":\"strategic_clarity\",\"value\":\"partial: the direction is clear, but the state is still in recovery mode.\"},{\"field\":\"operationalization_and_coordination\",\"value\":\"mixed: several concrete actions exist, but delivery is uneven and partner-mediated.\"},{\"field\":\"adaptation_and_correction\",\"value\":\"mixed: ceasefire and reform responses show adaptation, but only partial success.\"},{\"field\":\"goal_progress_and_durability\",\"value\":\"mixed: some progress, but no durable broad recovery yet.\"},{\"field\":\"trajectory\",\"value\":\"upward from conflict toward partial recovery.\"},{\"field\":\"morality_separation_check\",\"value\":\"The score is about governing effectiveness, not approval of the conflict or repression context.\"},{\"field\":\"defensible_score_range\",\"value\":\"4.5-5.5.\"}]},{\"dossier_job_key\":\"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:IDN:16199\",\"iso3\":\"IDN\",\"ruler_id\":\"2636\",\"ruler_year_id\":16199,\"ruler_name\":\"Joko Widodo\",\"period_start_year\":2022,\"period_end_year\":2022,\"chapter_id\":\"8B\",\"rubric_version\":\"chapter_8b_v3\",\"calibration_batch_id\":\"chapter-judge:2022-saturation-v3-stage1-controlled:2022:8B\",\"calibrated_against\":[\"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:DEU:16984\",\"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:IND:19645\",\"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:RUS:15706\"],\"score_1_to_10\":7.0,\"insufficient_evidence_reason\":null,\"confidence_score\":82,\"plausible_score_range\":{\"lower\":6.5,\"upper\":7.5},\"decisive_positive_evidence\":[{\"evidence_id\":\"E0077\",\"explanation\":\"The poverty-elimination instruction is a direct presidential act with clear cross-ministry implementation mandates.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0088\",\"explanation\":\"The cabinet appointment rationale shows active selection of experienced personnel for implementation tasks.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0098\",\"explanation\":\"The fuel-subsidy reallocation assistance rollout shows rapid conversion of policy change into large-scale relief delivery.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0099\",\"explanation\":\"The 2022 fiscal deficit came in below target, indicating strong fiscal management relative to plan.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0100\",\"explanation\":\"The unqualified audit opinion on the 2022 financial statements is strong evidence of administrative and fiscal implementation quality.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0103\",\"explanation\":\"The Nusantara capital work start shows a flagship program moving into the execution phase.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0104\",\"explanation\":\"WHO-reported immunization coverage above target is an independent outcome signal that the health campaign worked.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0102\",\"explanation\":\"The poverty assessment confirms real long-run gains in security, even though vulnerability remains.\"}],\"decisive_negative_evidence\":[{\"evidence_id\":\"E0101\",\"explanation\":\"The learning-crisis evidence shows that some core human-capital outcomes remained badly challenged.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0097\",\"explanation\":\"The World Bank still said a large share of Indonesians remained economically insecure, so the progress was incomplete.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0081\",\"explanation\":\"Regsosek is strong design evidence, but it remains a system-build rather than a proven outcome by itself.\"}],\"inherited_baseline_and_constraints\":\"Indonesia entered 2022 with preexisting macro resilience and a large bureaucracy, but also with pandemic learning losses and broad economic insecurity that limited the speed at which gains could become universal.\",\"ruler_attribution\":\"Jokowi has strong ownership of the program because the dossier shows direct executive instructions, budget choices, appointments, and rollout management. Much execution is delegated, but the top-line alignment between program, personnel, and implementation is unusually clear.\",\"supported_lenses\":[\"8B.1\",\"8B.2\",\"8B.3\",\"8B.4\",\"8B.5\",\"8B.6\",\"8B.7\",\"8B.8\",\"8B.9\",\"8B.10\"],\"missing_or_weak_lenses\":[\"8B.7\",\"8B.8\"],\"contrary_evidence\":[{\"evidence_id\":\"E0101\",\"explanation\":\"Learning losses remained severe.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0097\",\"explanation\":\"Large parts of the population remained vulnerable to shocks.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0081\",\"explanation\":\"The new registration system is still infrastructure for future targeting, not a completed welfare outcome.\"}],\"source_mix\":\"A strong mix of official presidential, statistical, audit, World Bank, WHO, and UNICEF evidence. This is one of the better-documented dossiers for both implementation and outcome checks, though some results still reflect inherited post-pandemic recovery.\",\"structured_prior_summary\":\"No structured local priors were collected in this experiment; the dossier itself already contains both rollout evidence and independent outcome checks.\",\"chapter_rationale\":\"Joko Widodo scores in the strong range because the dossier shows a president who repeatedly translated programmatic goals into state action and then produced at least some independently visible outcomes. The clearest strengths are poverty and relief policy, budget management, health-system expansion, immunization performance, and the start of the capital relocation project, all coupled with a clean FY2022 audit picture. The limitations are real: learning losses remained severe and a large share of the population was still economically insecure. Even so, the record is materially better than a merely competent mixed case because the program is broad, the mobilization is visible, and several major outcomes moved in the intended direction.\",\"lower_anchor_rejected\":\"A 6.0 score is too low because the dossier contains multiple independently checked outcomes plus strong evidence of direct executive mobilization and fiscal discipline.\",\"higher_anchor_rejected\":\"A score above 7.5 is too high because important human-capital problems persist and some flagship programs are still early in execution rather than fully durable.\",\"manual_review_required\":false,\"manual_review_reason_type\":null,\"manual_review_reason\":null,\"chapter_specific\":[{\"field\":\"program_basis\",\"value\":\"explicit: poverty reduction, fiscal discipline, health coverage, capital relocation, and human-capital rebuilding.\"},{\"field\":\"program_type\",\"value\":\"policy; state_building.\"},{\"field\":\"strategic_clarity\",\"value\":\"clear.\"},{\"field\":\"operationalization_and_coordination\",\"value\":\"strong: directives, appointments, budgets, and implementation channels line up.\"},{\"field\":\"adaptation_and_correction\",\"value\":\"effective: subsidy reallocation, audit discipline, and health rollout adjustments are visible.\"},{\"field\":\"goal_progress_and_durability\",\"value\":\"substantial, with some gains independently verified and some still emerging.\"},{\"field\":\"trajectory\",\"value\":\"upward and fairly durable, though not complete.\"},{\"field\":\"morality_separation_check\",\"value\":\"The score is an execution judgment only; it does not reward or punish ideology or personal character.\"},{\"field\":\"defensible_score_range\",\"value\":\"6.5-7.5.\"}]},{\"dossier_job_key\":\"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:IND:19645\",\"iso3\":\"IND\",\"ruler_id\":\"1517\",\"ruler_year_id\":19645,\"ruler_name\":\"Narendra Modi\",\"period_start_year\":2022,\"period_end_year\":2022,\"chapter_id\":\"8B\",\"rubric_version\":\"chapter_8b_v3\",\"calibration_batch_id\":\"chapter-judge:2022-saturation-v3-stage1-controlled:2022:8B\",\"calibrated_against\":[\"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:DEU:16984\",\"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:RUS:15706\",\"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:USA:15810\"],\"score_1_to_10\":7.0,\"insufficient_evidence_reason\":null,\"confidence_score\":81,\"plausible_score_range\":{\"lower\":6.5,\"upper\":7.5},\"decisive_positive_evidence\":[{\"evidence_id\":\"E0060\",\"explanation\":\"The budget-linked infrastructure and skilling agenda shows clear strategic design translated into policy instruments.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0063\",\"explanation\":\"MGNREGS implementation statistics provide concrete execution evidence on a large labor program.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0081\",\"explanation\":\"The World Bank health-sector loans show central policy mobilization and a serious expansion of public-health capacity.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0082\",\"explanation\":\"The CAG audit gives an independent snapshot of functional health centers and beneficiary registration by late 2022.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0098\",\"explanation\":\"The GatiShakti reporting shows a large implementation platform with clear coordination and project review activity.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0099\",\"explanation\":\"The deficit coming in below target suggests solid fiscal management relative to the year-end plan.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0100\",\"explanation\":\"The unqualified audit opinion on the 2022 accounts is strong evidence of administrative/fiscal implementation quality.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0102\",\"explanation\":\"IMF surveillance shows the government responding to shocks with fiscal support, monetary tightening, and digital public infrastructure.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0103\",\"explanation\":\"World Bank macro assessment gives additional corroboration that reforms improved resilience.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0107\",\"explanation\":\"The digital-payments expansion shows a major policy system working at scale.\"}],\"decisive_negative_evidence\":[{\"evidence_id\":\"E0101\",\"explanation\":\"The learning-crisis evidence indicates major human-capital weakness remained unresolved.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0097\",\"explanation\":\"Human insecurity remained high, which limits any claim of comprehensive welfare success.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0094\",\"explanation\":\"Some of the strongest management evidence is still background/appointment quality rather than completed outcome improvement.\"}],\"inherited_baseline_and_constraints\":\"India entered 2022 with strong macro buffers and a large administrative state, but also with pandemic damage, learning loss, and uneven social development, so the evaluation has to separate inherited resilience from fresh policy execution.\",\"ruler_attribution\":\"Modi's ownership of the program is strong at the level of budget, appointments, and national initiatives, though several key levers were shared with the RBI, states, and autonomous implementing bodies.\",\"supported_lenses\":[\"8B.1\",\"8B.2\",\"8B.3\",\"8B.4\",\"8B.5\",\"8B.6\",\"8B.7\",\"8B.8\",\"8B.9\",\"8B.10\"],\"missing_or_weak_lenses\":[\"8B.7\",\"8B.8\"],\"contrary_evidence\":[{\"evidence_id\":\"E0101\",\"explanation\":\"Human-capital and learning outcomes remained weak in important areas.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0097\",\"explanation\":\"Broad economic insecurity persisted despite growth and reform.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0107\",\"explanation\":\"Some of the best macro outcomes are shared with the RBI and external conditions, not purely Modi-owned.\"}],\"source_mix\":\"A strong mix of PRS, CAG, World Bank, IMF, RBI-adjacent official material, and government releases. The evidence is unusually rich on program architecture and public-finance execution, but some of the strongest outcomes are still partially indirect or shared with other institutions.\",\"structured_prior_summary\":\"No structured local priors were collected in this experiment; the judgment relies on the dossier's mix of official, audit, and multilateral evidence.\",\"chapter_rationale\":\"Narendra Modi scores in the strong range because the dossier shows a government that not only articulated a national economic and social agenda but also pushed it through budgets, appointments, digital infrastructure, health expansion, and fiscal management. The best evidence is that large systems were actually operating: MGNREGS, Ayushman Bharat, GatiShakti, digital payments, and the 2022 budget/audit machinery all show real implementation. The score does not rise further because important human-capital gaps remain, some of the strongest outcomes are shared with other institutions or external conditions, and several programs are still design-heavy rather than fully outcome-verified. That combination is strong enough for a 7, but not for the 8-plus tier.\",\"lower_anchor_rejected\":\"A 6.0 score is too low because the dossier contains multiple large-scale, independently corroborated implementation results and fiscal/audit evidence.\",\"higher_anchor_rejected\":\"A score above 7.5 is too high because several major outcome areas remain mixed, shared-attribution issues are substantial, and human-capital results are not yet broadly durable.\",\"manual_review_required\":false,\"manual_review_reason_type\":null,\"manual_review_reason\":null,\"chapter_specific\":[{\"field\":\"program_basis\",\"value\":\"explicit: growth, digital public infrastructure, fiscal management, health, and social welfare.\"},{\"field\":\"program_type\",\"value\":\"policy; state_building.\"},{\"field\":\"strategic_clarity\",\"value\":\"clear.\"},{\"field\":\"operationalization_and_coordination\",\"value\":\"strong: ministries, auditors, and digital systems are all visible.\"},{\"field\":\"adaptation_and_correction\",\"value\":\"effective: fiscal and digital tools were used to absorb shocks and preserve rollout.\"},{\"field\":\"goal_progress_and_durability\",\"value\":\"substantial, though several gains are still shared or lagged.\"},{\"field\":\"trajectory\",\"value\":\"upward with broad but uneven durability.\"},{\"field\":\"morality_separation_check\",\"value\":\"The score reflects execution of the governing program, not its moral or ideological content.\"},{\"field\":\"defensible_score_range\",\"value\":\"6.5-7.5.\"}]},{\"dossier_job_key\":\"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:IRN:19648\",\"iso3\":\"IRN\",\"ruler_id\":\"3412\",\"ruler_year_id\":19648,\"ruler_name\":\"Ali Khamenei\",\"period_start_year\":2022,\"period_end_year\":2022,\"chapter_id\":\"8B\",\"rubric_version\":\"chapter_8b_v3\",\"calibration_batch_id\":\"chapter-judge:2022-saturation-v3-stage1-controlled:2022:8B\",\"calibrated_against\":[\"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:DEU:16984\",\"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:IND:19645\",\"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:RUS:15706\"],\"score_1_to_10\":4.5,\"insufficient_evidence_reason\":null,\"confidence_score\":70,\"plausible_score_range\":{\"lower\":4.0,\"upper\":5.0},\"decisive_positive_evidence\":[{\"evidence_id\":\"E0001\",\"explanation\":\"The constitution gives the Supreme Leader sweeping command authority, so Khamenei clearly owns the governing program's high-level direction.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0060\",\"explanation\":\"The development-plan guidelines show clear ideological and economic direction from the top office.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0082\",\"explanation\":\"Khamenei's resistance-oriented framing of the economy is direct program articulation and reveals an explicit governing preference.\"}],\"decisive_negative_evidence\":[{\"evidence_id\":\"E0005\",\"explanation\":\"The sanction-impervious growth rhetoric is strategic but not evidence of successful delivery.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0083\",\"explanation\":\"Blaming unrest on outside schemes shows crisis framing, not effective management or correction.\"}],\"inherited_baseline_and_constraints\":\"Iran in 2022 faced sanctions, inflation, protest pressure, and a tightly centralized but opaque regime, so the relevant question is not raw command but whether Khamenei's choices produced observable progress toward his own program.\",\"ruler_attribution\":\"Khamenei's ownership of strategic direction is very strong, but the evidence for effective implementation or corrective performance is much thinner than the evidence for declaratory control and hardline framing.\",\"supported_lenses\":[\"8B.1\",\"8B.2\",\"8B.3\",\"8B.4\",\"8B.5\",\"8B.6\",\"8B.7\",\"8B.8\",\"8B.9\",\"8B.10\"],\"missing_or_weak_lenses\":[\"8B.3\",\"8B.7\",\"8B.8\",\"8B.10\"],\"contrary_evidence\":[{\"evidence_id\":\"E0005\",\"explanation\":\"Economic resilience rhetoric under sanctions is not itself a performance outcome.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0083\",\"explanation\":\"Crisis-blaming rhetoric does not show correction or problem-solving.\"}],\"source_mix\":\"Mostly constitutional text, state-affiliated speeches, and a reputable secondary summary. This is enough to establish high-level command and ideological direction, but it is weak on independent outcome verification and personal attribution of day-to-day execution.\",\"structured_prior_summary\":\"No structured local priors were collected in this experiment; the dossier is highly centralized and opaque, so the main issue is not baseline capacity but the absence of independent outcome traces.\",\"chapter_rationale\":\"Ali Khamenei receives a low-mid score because the dossier clearly shows enormous authority and a well-defined ideological program, but it does not show that the program was translated into effective, outcome-producing governance in 2022. The evidence is strong on top-down direction: constitutional power, development-plan guidelines, and resistance-oriented economic framing all show ownership of the program. The evidence is weak on execution: the record is mostly declaratory, crisis-framing, or institutionally indirect, with little independent proof of durable success. That is enough to beat a purely symbolic or directionless ruler, but not enough to approach the stronger competence tiers.\",\"lower_anchor_rejected\":\"A 3.5 score is too low because the dossier clearly shows top-level command authority and repeated programmatic direction rather than mere drift.\",\"higher_anchor_rejected\":\"A score above 5 is too high because the evidence is overwhelmingly declaratory and weak on independently verified execution or durable progress.\",\"manual_review_required\":false,\"manual_review_reason_type\":null,\"manual_review_reason\":null,\"chapter_specific\":[{\"field\":\"program_basis\",\"value\":\"explicit: resistance, sanctions-impervious development, and ideological control.\"},{\"field\":\"program_type\",\"value\":\"policy; regime_control; power_consolidation.\"},{\"field\":\"strategic_clarity\",\"value\":\"clear.\"},{\"field\":\"operationalization_and_coordination\",\"value\":\"weak to mixed: the system is highly centralized, but execution evidence is thin.\"},{\"field\":\"adaptation_and_correction\",\"value\":\"rigid to mixed: the dossier shows framing and blame more than correction.\"},{\"field\":\"goal_progress_and_durability\",\"value\":\"mixed to net-regression: control persists, but the 2022 program does not visibly advance far.\"},{\"field\":\"trajectory\",\"value\":\"stable control, weak substantive progress.\"},{\"field\":\"morality_separation_check\",\"value\":\"The score does not reward or condemn the regime's moral character; it only assesses execution of the revealed program.\"},{\"field\":\"defensible_score_range\",\"value\":\"4.0-5.0.\"}]},{\"dossier_job_key\":\"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:JPN:16638\",\"iso3\":\"JPN\",\"ruler_id\":\"2895\",\"ruler_year_id\":16638,\"ruler_name\":\"Fumio Kishida\",\"period_start_year\":2022,\"period_end_year\":2022,\"chapter_id\":\"8B\",\"rubric_version\":\"chapter_8b_v3\",\"calibration_batch_id\":\"chapter-judge:2022-saturation-v3-stage1-controlled:2022:8B\",\"calibrated_against\":[\"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:DEU:16984\",\"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:IND:19645\",\"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:RUS:15706\"],\"score_1_to_10\":6.5,\"insufficient_evidence_reason\":null,\"confidence_score\":78,\"plausible_score_range\":{\"lower\":6.0,\"upper\":7.0},\"decisive_positive_evidence\":[{\"evidence_id\":\"E0052\",\"explanation\":\"Kishida's wage-growth and distribution agenda is a clear program statement with concrete policy levers.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0080\",\"explanation\":\"The reskilling and monitoring budget shows direct operationalization of the economic program.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0094\",\"explanation\":\"The cabinet reshuffle demonstrates active personnel management and prioritization.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0095\",\"explanation\":\"The startup subcommittee meeting shows agenda-setting and follow-through on innovation policy.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0096\",\"explanation\":\"The passing of almost all bills and the creation of a government-wide implementation team show real internal coordination.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0100\",\"explanation\":\"The IMF's description of the growth-and-distribution agenda corroborates the clarity and seriousness of the program.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0103\",\"explanation\":\"The Child Welfare Act revision is a concrete legislative achievement tied to the administration's agenda.\"}],\"decisive_negative_evidence\":[{\"evidence_id\":\"E0099\",\"explanation\":\"Real wages fell sharply in fiscal 2022, showing a major outcome gap relative to the wage-centered agenda.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0101\",\"explanation\":\"The OECD said support could have been better targeted, limiting the score ceiling.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0098\",\"explanation\":\"The huge stimulus package was mostly reactive to inflationary pressure rather than proof of durable success.\"}],\"inherited_baseline_and_constraints\":\"Japan's administrative baseline is high, but 2022 was constrained by imported inflation, a weak yen, and post-pandemic adjustment, so the evaluation should not confuse inherited state quality with Kishida's own execution.\",\"ruler_attribution\":\"Kishida clearly owned the program and made a series of direct cabinet and legislative moves, but several outcomes depended on external price shocks, the BOJ, and later implementation lags.\",\"supported_lenses\":[\"8B.1\",\"8B.2\",\"8B.3\",\"8B.4\",\"8B.5\",\"8B.6\",\"8B.7\",\"8B.8\",\"8B.9\",\"8B.10\"],\"missing_or_weak_lenses\":[\"8B.7\",\"8B.8\"],\"contrary_evidence\":[{\"evidence_id\":\"E0099\",\"explanation\":\"Real wages moved in the wrong direction.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0101\",\"explanation\":\"Targeting and sustainability concerns limit the strength of the response.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0098\",\"explanation\":\"The spending package was a crisis response, not durable proof of structural success.\"}],\"source_mix\":\"Mostly official PMO, ministry, and agency statements, with IMF, OECD, and Reuters corroboration. This is a solid mix for program-to-implementation tracing, though outcome evidence is partially lagged and macro shocks remain important.\",\"structured_prior_summary\":\"No structured local priors were collected in this experiment; the dossier is already rich in official and independent policy evidence.\",\"chapter_rationale\":\"Fumio Kishida scores as fairly effective because the dossier shows a coherent, repeated attempt to build a growth-and-distribution agenda and then back it with budgets, legislation, cabinet management, and implementation councils. There is genuine policy conversion here: wage-growth rhetoric, reskilling money, startup planning, social-policy revision, and major crisis response all show a working governing machine. The ceiling is held down by the fact that the key outcome indicator, real wages, moved sharply the wrong way in 2022 and some of the relief architecture was openly criticized as insufficiently targeted. So this is a competent and substantively active year, but not one with unmistakable durable success.\",\"lower_anchor_rejected\":\"A 5.5 score is too low because the dossier contains repeated concrete legislative, budgetary, and organizational actions with strong institutional follow-through.\",\"higher_anchor_rejected\":\"A score above 7 is too high because the key wage outcome deteriorated and several major measures were still reactive, partial, or not yet durable by year-end.\",\"manual_review_required\":false,\"manual_review_reason_type\":null,\"manual_review_reason\":null,\"chapter_specific\":[{\"field\":\"program_basis\",\"value\":\"explicit: growth plus distribution, wages, human capital, startup policy, and child welfare.\"},{\"field\":\"program_type\",\"value\":\"policy; state_building.\"},{\"field\":\"strategic_clarity\",\"value\":\"clear.\"},{\"field\":\"operationalization_and_coordination\",\"value\":\"strong: budgets, legislation, task forces, and council meetings line up.\"},{\"field\":\"adaptation_and_correction\",\"value\":\"effective but incomplete: crisis packages and monitoring exist, but wage erosion persists.\"},{\"field\":\"goal_progress_and_durability\",\"value\":\"mixed to substantial: some concrete gains, but the headline wage objective is not yet realized.\"},{\"field\":\"trajectory\",\"value\":\"upward on institutional conversion, mixed on output outcomes.\"},{\"field\":\"morality_separation_check\",\"value\":\"The score reflects governing effectiveness, not the desirability of the policy agenda.\"},{\"field\":\"defensible_score_range\",\"value\":\"6.0-7.0.\"}]},{\"dossier_job_key\":\"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:MEX:15801\",\"iso3\":\"MEX\",\"ruler_id\":\"2779\",\"ruler_year_id\":15801,\"ruler_name\":\"Andrés Manuel López Obrador\",\"period_start_year\":2022,\"period_end_year\":2022,\"chapter_id\":\"8B\",\"rubric_version\":\"chapter_8b_v3\",\"calibration_batch_id\":\"chapter-judge:2022-saturation-v3-stage1-controlled:2022:8B\",\"calibrated_against\":[\"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:DEU:16984\",\"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:IND:19645\",\"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:RUS:15706\"],\"score_1_to_10\":6.0,\"insufficient_evidence_reason\":null,\"confidence_score\":78,\"plausible_score_range\":{\"lower\":5.5,\"upper\":6.5},\"decisive_positive_evidence\":[{\"evidence_id\":\"E0058\",\"explanation\":\"The health-program order is a concrete policy instrument with clear federalization and coverage goals.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0065\",\"explanation\":\"The Bienpesca rollout shows direct transfer delivery at scale to a defined group.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0069\",\"explanation\":\"The 2022 social-benefits distribution shows program execution rather than mere intent.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0081\",\"explanation\":\"The 4T welfare framing is direct agenda-setting for the administration's delivery model.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0087\",\"explanation\":\"Education budget increases show that social-policy priorities were backed with resources.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0088\",\"explanation\":\"Direct control of school funds through parent committees is a concrete implementation design.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0090\",\"explanation\":\"The AIFA opening claim is a flagship infrastructure delivery event within the year.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0096\",\"explanation\":\"The World Bank operation shows policy support for inclusive growth and financial inclusion.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0102\",\"explanation\":\"Learning-camp intervention shows targeted educational recovery with measurable gains.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0103\",\"explanation\":\"The IMF's macro assessment confirms a real recovery and policy support, though with external constraints.\"}],\"decisive_negative_evidence\":[{\"evidence_id\":\"E0093\",\"explanation\":\"The electricity reform defeat shows a major policy failure to convert executive preference into law.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0098\",\"explanation\":\"The AIFA audit irregularities reveal execution and documentation problems.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0100\",\"explanation\":\"Dos Bocas cost escalation indicates serious planning and implementation strain.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0101\",\"explanation\":\"The school-program audit irregularities show weak controls and monitoring.\"}],\"inherited_baseline_and_constraints\":\"Mexico in 2022 benefited from some macro resilience and recovery momentum, but also from long-running investment weakness, inflation pressure, and the difficulty of converting a broad welfare state agenda into clean project execution.\",\"ruler_attribution\":\"AMLO clearly owns the program and much of the execution, but some major outputs are budgetary, institutional, or partner-mediated rather than personally executable, and a few flagship projects show real implementation strain.\",\"supported_lenses\":[\"8B.1\",\"8B.2\",\"8B.3\",\"8B.4\",\"8B.5\",\"8B.6\",\"8B.7\",\"8B.8\",\"8B.9\",\"8B.10\"],\"missing_or_weak_lenses\":[\"8B.7\",\"8B.8\"],\"contrary_evidence\":[{\"evidence_id\":\"E0093\",\"explanation\":\"A major signature reform was blocked in parliament.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0098\",\"explanation\":\"Audit findings show real execution problems in the flagship airport project.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0100\",\"explanation\":\"Cost escalation on Dos Bocas indicates planning and management strain.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0101\",\"explanation\":\"The school program audit shows monitoring weaknesses.\"}],\"source_mix\":\"Official welfare, budget, and program documents are mixed with audit findings, IMF and World Bank assessments, and Reuters-style reporting. The dossier is fairly rich, but several of the most important wins are still self-described or project-specific rather than national independent audits.\",\"structured_prior_summary\":\"No structured local priors were collected in this experiment; the judgment relies on the embedded evidence and the mix of official and independent checks.\",\"chapter_rationale\":\"Andrés Manuel López Obrador scores as moderately effective because the dossier shows a president who pushed a large welfare-centered agenda into budgets, direct transfers, education funding, health policy, and flagship infrastructure. There is enough concrete delivery here to distinguish him from a merely rhetorical leader: transfers went out, budget priorities were set, and several policy systems were visibly operating. The score is not higher because some of the most ambitious projects ran into real implementation and audit problems, and a major structural reform was blocked outright. In short, the year shows substantial governing activity with real delivery, but also enough execution failure and strain to keep it below the stronger tier.\",\"lower_anchor_rejected\":\"A 5.0 score is too low because the dossier contains multiple concrete transfer, budget, and infrastructure actions plus some external validation of macro recovery.\",\"higher_anchor_rejected\":\"A score above 6.5 is too high because the record also shows major implementation gaps, audit irregularities, and at least one high-salience legislative defeat.\",\"manual_review_required\":false,\"manual_review_reason_type\":null,\"manual_review_reason\":null,\"chapter_specific\":[{\"field\":\"program_basis\",\"value\":\"explicit: welfare, social protection, public infrastructure, and state-led development.\"},{\"field\":\"program_type\",\"value\":\"policy; state_building.\"},{\"field\":\"strategic_clarity\",\"value\":\"clear.\"},{\"field\":\"operationalization_and_coordination\",\"value\":\"mixed to strong: many programs are real, but some flagship projects are strained.\"},{\"field\":\"adaptation_and_correction\",\"value\":\"mixed: the administration can deliver and redirect, but not always cleanly.\"},{\"field\":\"goal_progress_and_durability\",\"value\":\"mixed to substantial: welfare delivery is visible, but durability and governance quality vary.\"},{\"field\":\"trajectory\",\"value\":\"upward on social delivery, mixed on institutional quality.\"},{\"field\":\"morality_separation_check\",\"value\":\"The score assesses execution of the governing program only.\"},{\"field\":\"defensible_score_range\",\"value\":\"5.5-6.5.\"}]},{\"dossier_job_key\":\"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:NGA:15787\",\"iso3\":\"NGA\",\"ruler_id\":\"2776\",\"ruler_year_id\":15787,\"ruler_name\":\"Muhammadu Buhari\",\"period_start_year\":2022,\"period_end_year\":2022,\"chapter_id\":\"8B\",\"rubric_version\":\"chapter_8b_v3\",\"calibration_batch_id\":\"chapter-judge:2022-saturation-v3-stage1-controlled:2022:8B\",\"calibrated_against\":[\"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:DEU:16984\",\"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:IND:19645\",\"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:RUS:15706\"],\"score_1_to_10\":4.0,\"insufficient_evidence_reason\":null,\"confidence_score\":65,\"plausible_score_range\":{\"lower\":3.5,\"upper\":4.5},\"decisive_positive_evidence\":[{\"evidence_id\":\"E0055\",\"explanation\":\"The 2022 budget was signed on time and restored the January-to-December fiscal cycle, which is basic governing competence.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0060\",\"explanation\":\"The technocratic statistics appointment is a concrete personnel choice aligned with evidence-based administration.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0091\",\"explanation\":\"The National Health Insurance Authority bill shows a real institutional reform effort.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0103\",\"explanation\":\"The ASUU suspension followed presidential appeals and fiscal action, showing some crisis intervention capability.\"}],\"decisive_negative_evidence\":[{\"evidence_id\":\"E0061\",\"explanation\":\"The cabinet-competence speech is self-justifying rather than independent proof of effective staffing.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0090\",\"explanation\":\"Anti-corruption rhetoric is not equivalent to verified results.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0092\",\"explanation\":\"The humanitarian framework is broad but heavily long-term and not outcome-verified in 2022.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0103\",\"explanation\":\"The eight-month strike itself shows a major implementation failure, even if suspension was eventually achieved.\"}],\"inherited_baseline_and_constraints\":\"Nigeria in 2022 faced severe fiscal strain, insecurity, and labor conflict, so even basic administrative wins had to compete with deep structural constraints and inherited dysfunction.\",\"ruler_attribution\":\"Buhari clearly owned some budget and appointment choices, but the dossier is dominated by speeches, self-description, and crisis management against inherited problems rather than strong proof of broad execution.\",\"supported_lenses\":[\"8B.1\",\"8B.2\",\"8B.3\",\"8B.4\",\"8B.5\",\"8B.6\",\"8B.7\",\"8B.8\",\"8B.9\",\"8B.10\"],\"missing_or_weak_lenses\":[\"8B.7\",\"8B.8\",\"8B.10\"],\"contrary_evidence\":[{\"evidence_id\":\"E0103\",\"explanation\":\"The university strike and its late suspension show major governance friction.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0090\",\"explanation\":\"Anti-corruption talk is not the same as outcome evidence.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0092\",\"explanation\":\"Long-term poverty-reduction plans do not prove 2022 delivery.\"}],\"source_mix\":\"Mostly official Nigerian government releases with one Reuters-syndicated report. The dossier has decent program evidence but is heavily skewed toward self-description and framework announcements rather than independently audited outcomes.\",\"structured_prior_summary\":\"No structured local priors were collected in this experiment; the dossier mainly shows a weak, constrained, and crisis-prone governing baseline.\",\"chapter_rationale\":\"Muhammadu Buhari scores low because the dossier shows only limited and uneven execution. There are a few real administrative acts: the budget was signed on schedule, a technocratic statistics chief was appointed, health insurance legislation was enacted, and the university strike was eventually defused. But most of the record is either self-description or broad framework-setting, and the most obvious large-scale episode in the dossier is a prolonged strike that signals weak control over implementation. That is enough for a score above collapse or paralysis, but not enough for a genuinely competent governing year.\",\"lower_anchor_rejected\":\"A 3.0 score is too low because the dossier does show some genuine budgetary, legislative, and appointment activity rather than pure drift.\",\"higher_anchor_rejected\":\"A score above 4.5 is too high because the evidence is still dominated by self-reporting, long-term frameworks, and visible implementation failure.\",\"manual_review_required\":false,\"manual_review_reason_type\":null,\"manual_review_reason\":null,\"chapter_specific\":[{\"field\":\"program_basis\",\"value\":\"mixed: fiscal order, health reform, humanitarian coordination, and anti-corruption framing.\"},{\"field\":\"program_type\",\"value\":\"policy; state_building.\"},{\"field\":\"strategic_clarity\",\"value\":\"weak to partial.\"},{\"field\":\"operationalization_and_coordination\",\"value\":\"weak to mixed: some concrete actions exist, but most evidence is rhetorical or reactive.\"},{\"field\":\"adaptation_and_correction\",\"value\":\"mixed: crisis intervention happened, but late and incompletely.\"},{\"field\":\"goal_progress_and_durability\",\"value\":\"weak to mixed: some institutional moves, but poor broader implementation.\"},{\"field\":\"trajectory\",\"value\":\"flat to slightly negative under pressure.\"},{\"field\":\"morality_separation_check\",\"value\":\"The score is an execution assessment only, not a judgment on the desirability of the government's priorities.\"},{\"field\":\"defensible_score_range\",\"value\":\"3.5-4.5.\"}]},{\"dossier_job_key\":\"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:PAK:16682\",\"iso3\":\"PAK\",\"ruler_id\":\"2911\",\"ruler_year_id\":16682,\"ruler_name\":\"Shehbaz Sharif\",\"period_start_year\":2022,\"period_end_year\":2022,\"chapter_id\":\"8B\",\"rubric_version\":\"chapter_8b_v3\",\"calibration_batch_id\":\"chapter-judge:2022-saturation-v3-stage1-controlled:2022:8B\",\"calibrated_against\":[\"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:DEU:16984\",\"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:IND:19645\",\"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:RUS:15706\"],\"score_1_to_10\":5.0,\"insufficient_evidence_reason\":null,\"confidence_score\":68,\"plausible_score_range\":{\"lower\":4.5,\"upper\":5.5},\"decisive_positive_evidence\":[{\"evidence_id\":\"E0050\",\"explanation\":\"Sharif's immediate finance-minister appointment and IMF restart task show direct crisis-response leadership.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0055\",\"explanation\":\"The budget speech lays out a concrete austerity and revenue strategy rather than a purely symbolic program.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0056\",\"explanation\":\"The budget-in-brief shows a coherent growth-and-stability policy line with vulnerable-group protection.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0075\",\"explanation\":\"The 4RF flood framework shows direct leadership on disaster recovery and reconstruction.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0093\",\"explanation\":\"The coalition cabinet formation shows actual political mobilization around stabilization and IMF negotiations.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0094\",\"explanation\":\"Cutting expenditures and development funds to revive the IMF program is a concrete, if constrained, policy move.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0095\",\"explanation\":\"The tax and fuel-price measures show willingness to impose difficult fiscal steps.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0096\",\"explanation\":\"IMF program completion shows that the government achieved some macro-level stabilization milestones.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0098\",\"explanation\":\"The flood PDNA and relief framework show a real response to a major disaster.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0100\",\"explanation\":\"World Bank flood-support projects show implementation alignment with the recovery agenda.\"}],\"decisive_negative_evidence\":[{\"evidence_id\":\"E0061\",\"explanation\":\"Finance-minister turnover under internal pressure shows limited intra-coalition control.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0098\",\"explanation\":\"The disaster damage was so large that the recovery task remained only partly in hand by year-end.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0050\",\"explanation\":\"The inherited economic spiral limits how much credit can be assigned to Sharif's own management.\"}],\"inherited_baseline_and_constraints\":\"Pakistan in 2022 entered with a severe balance-of-payments and inflation crisis plus catastrophic floods, so the main test is whether Sharif stabilized the system and built a workable recovery path under extreme constraint.\",\"ruler_attribution\":\"Sharif has clear ownership of the crisis-response coalition, fiscal tightening, IMF restart, and flood framework, but the situation was heavily inherited and many key levers were shared with the IMF, provinces, and coalition partners.\",\"supported_lenses\":[\"8B.1\",\"8B.2\",\"8B.3\",\"8B.4\",\"8B.5\",\"8B.6\",\"8B.7\",\"8B.8\",\"8B.9\",\"8B.10\"],\"missing_or_weak_lenses\":[\"8B.7\",\"8B.8\",\"8B.10\"],\"contrary_evidence\":[{\"evidence_id\":\"E0061\",\"explanation\":\"Internal pressure on the finance ministry shows coalition fragility.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0098\",\"explanation\":\"Flood damage and reconstruction needs were enormous, limiting near-term success.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0050\",\"explanation\":\"Much of the challenge was inherited from the prior economic collapse.\"}],\"source_mix\":\"Mostly official Pakistani budget and PM documents, plus Reuters and World Bank/IMF material. The mix is strong for tracing crisis response, but much of the record is reactive and constrained, so outcome confidence should stay moderate rather than high.\",\"structured_prior_summary\":\"No structured local priors were collected in this experiment; the dossier is already dominated by crisis-response evidence and inherited-constraint context.\",\"chapter_rationale\":\"Shehbaz Sharif scores as average-to-middling because the record shows real crisis management, but mostly in response to a disaster and an inherited economic breakdown. There is enough evidence of action to distinguish him from a passive caretaker: a new finance team, fiscal tightening, an IMF restart, a flood-recovery framework, and follow-on donor support all point to active governance. The problem is that the year is so dominated by inherited crisis and external dependence that the dossier does not show decisive, durable progress toward a broader governing program. That supports a middle score: real mobilization and some stabilization, but not sustained control or strong independent outcome achievement.\",\"lower_anchor_rejected\":\"A 4.0 score is too low because the dossier shows active stabilization, budget action, and a serious recovery framework under acute stress.\",\"higher_anchor_rejected\":\"A score above 5.5 is too high because the evidence is mostly reactive, heavily constrained, and not yet durable by year-end.\",\"manual_review_required\":false,\"manual_review_reason_type\":null,\"manual_review_reason\":null,\"chapter_specific\":[{\"field\":\"program_basis\",\"value\":\"mixed: stabilization, IMF restart, flood recovery, and fiscal discipline.\"},{\"field\":\"program_type\",\"value\":\"policy; survival; state_building.\"},{\"field\":\"strategic_clarity\",\"value\":\"partial.\"},{\"field\":\"operationalization_and_coordination\",\"value\":\"mixed: the coalition and budget machinery did move, but under heavy constraint.\"},{\"field\":\"adaptation_and_correction\",\"value\":\"mixed to effective: the government reacted decisively, but only within a crisis frame.\"},{\"field\":\"goal_progress_and_durability\",\"value\":\"mixed: some stabilization, but little evidence of durable achievement by year-end.\"},{\"field\":\"trajectory\",\"value\":\"stabilizing from crisis rather than clearly advancing a long-run program.\"},{\"field\":\"morality_separation_check\",\"value\":\"The score is about execution, not a judgment on austerity or coalition politics.\"},{\"field\":\"defensible_score_range\",\"value\":\"4.5-5.5.\"}]},{\"dossier_job_key\":\"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:PHL:16194\",\"iso3\":\"PHL\",\"ruler_id\":\"2844\",\"ruler_year_id\":16194,\"ruler_name\":\"Bongbong Marcos\",\"period_start_year\":2022,\"period_end_year\":2022,\"chapter_id\":\"8B\",\"rubric_version\":\"chapter_8b_v3\",\"calibration_batch_id\":\"chapter-judge:2022-saturation-v3-stage1-controlled:2022:8B\",\"calibrated_against\":[\"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:DEU:16984\",\"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:IND:19645\",\"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:RUS:15706\"],\"score_1_to_10\":5.5,\"insufficient_evidence_reason\":null,\"confidence_score\":71,\"plausible_score_range\":{\"lower\":5.0,\"upper\":6.0},\"decisive_positive_evidence\":[{\"evidence_id\":\"E0071\",\"explanation\":\"The first-100-days aid rollout shows direct administrative action on inflation and vulnerable groups.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0074\",\"explanation\":\"The first budget signed under Marcos shows a real legislative-executive governing step.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0089\",\"explanation\":\"The socioeconomic agenda shows a clear stated policy roadmap.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0093\",\"explanation\":\"Naming the economic team early shows active personnel selection and policy coordination.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0094\",\"explanation\":\"The broad cabinet oath-taking demonstrates executive formation and control over key offices.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0095\",\"explanation\":\"Security-chief appointments show chain-of-command management.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0096\",\"explanation\":\"Replacing the executive secretary shows continued center-of-executive control.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0097\",\"explanation\":\"The first full budget proposal shows substantial planning and a prioritized recovery roadmap.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0098\",\"explanation\":\"The booster rollout provides a concrete implementation figure within the first 100 days.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0100\",\"explanation\":\"The full return to in-person classes shows a system-wide reopening milestone and some recovery execution.\"}],\"decisive_negative_evidence\":[{\"evidence_id\":\"E0053\",\"explanation\":\"The IMF notes the economy was fundamentally sound but faced weakened inflation and external position, which limits credit for the administration.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0100\",\"explanation\":\"The education-recovery report also notes continuing constraints, so the reopening is incomplete evidence.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0092\",\"explanation\":\"The socioeconomic agenda is partly aspirational and does not yet prove the targets were reached.\"}],\"inherited_baseline_and_constraints\":\"Marcos inherited a post-pandemic economy with some macro resilience but also inflation pressure, learning losses, and the need to reconnect policy with delivery after a period of disruption.\",\"ruler_attribution\":\"Marcos clearly owns the personnel, budget, and agenda-setting record for his first months, but several of the strongest measures are early-stage and still dependent on line agencies and local implementation.\",\"supported_lenses\":[\"8B.1\",\"8B.2\",\"8B.3\",\"8B.4\",\"8B.5\",\"8B.6\",\"8B.7\",\"8B.8\",\"8B.9\",\"8B.10\"],\"missing_or_weak_lenses\":[\"8B.7\",\"8B.8\"],\"contrary_evidence\":[{\"evidence_id\":\"E0053\",\"explanation\":\"The macro context was fundamentally sound but not yet fully under control.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0092\",\"explanation\":\"Targets and presentations outpace independently verified achievement.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0100\",\"explanation\":\"Even the positive reopening evidence notes continuing constraints.\"}],\"source_mix\":\"Official presidential and agency releases, plus IMF and UNICEF corroboration. The dossier is useful for seeing early executive formation and rollout, but still early enough that many claims are about plans, appointments, and first-phase delivery.\",\"structured_prior_summary\":\"No structured local priors were collected in this experiment; the judgment rests on the visible early-month executive record and a few independent checks.\",\"chapter_rationale\":\"Bongbong Marcos scores as moderately effective because the first months of his presidency show active executive formation, a budget, a social-assistance rollout, and visible reopening/recovery measures. He is not just describing a program; he is appointing the team, signing the budget, pushing relief, and overseeing reopening milestones. The score is held below the stronger tier because much of this is still early-stage, many measures are framed as targets, and the independent evidence still shows constraints rather than fully matured success. That is enough for a middling-positive score, but not for a clearly strong one.\",\"lower_anchor_rejected\":\"A 4.5 score is too low because the dossier shows a functioning executive that is already budgeting, staffing, and rolling out relief and reopening measures.\",\"higher_anchor_rejected\":\"A score above 6 is too high because the strongest results are still early and partial, with many outputs not yet independently verified as durable.\",\"manual_review_required\":false,\"manual_review_reason_type\":null,\"manual_review_reason\":null,\"chapter_specific\":[{\"field\":\"program_basis\",\"value\":\"explicit: economic recovery, inflation response, health reopening, and social assistance.\"},{\"field\":\"program_type\",\"value\":\"policy; state_building.\"},{\"field\":\"strategic_clarity\",\"value\":\"clear at the agenda level, but early-stage.\"},{\"field\":\"operationalization_and_coordination\",\"value\":\"mixed to strong: staffing and budgets are visible, but outcomes are still emerging.\"},{\"field\":\"adaptation_and_correction\",\"value\":\"mixed: several personnel and policy adjustments are visible in the first months.\"},{\"field\":\"goal_progress_and_durability\",\"value\":\"mixed: some concrete delivery, but too early for durability.\"},{\"field\":\"trajectory\",\"value\":\"upward, but still in the setup phase.\"},{\"field\":\"morality_separation_check\",\"value\":\"The score reflects execution only; it does not depend on any view of the family's history or the campaign context.\"},{\"field\":\"defensible_score_range\",\"value\":\"5.0-6.0.\"}]},{\"dossier_job_key\":\"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:RUS:15706\",\"iso3\":\"RUS\",\"ruler_id\":\"2759\",\"ruler_year_id\":15706,\"ruler_name\":\"Vladimir Putin\",\"period_start_year\":2022,\"period_end_year\":2022,\"chapter_id\":\"8B\",\"rubric_version\":\"chapter_8b_v3\",\"calibration_batch_id\":\"chapter-judge:2022-saturation-v3-stage1-controlled:2022:8B\",\"calibrated_against\":[\"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:DEU:16984\",\"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:IND:19645\",\"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:USA:15810\"],\"score_1_to_10\":4.0,\"insufficient_evidence_reason\":null,\"confidence_score\":85,\"plausible_score_range\":{\"lower\":3.5,\"upper\":4.5},\"decisive_positive_evidence\":[{\"evidence_id\":\"E0161\",\"explanation\":\"The central bank's stabilization actions helped keep the financial system functioning after the invasion shock.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0163\",\"explanation\":\"The IMF explicitly says emergency financial and monetary measures stabilized the domestic economy in the short run.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0169\",\"explanation\":\"The budget execution law gives direct evidence that the state could still execute fiscal governance in 2022.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0176\",\"explanation\":\"The unmanned-aircraft systems instruction shows continued top-down mobilization and command reach in late 2022.\"}],\"decisive_negative_evidence\":[{\"evidence_id\":\"E0165\",\"explanation\":\"OECD analysis shows sanctions, reserve loss, depreciation, and a much weaker outlook.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0167\",\"explanation\":\"Putin's own fiscal and GDP forecast was much more optimistic than the actual deteriorating wartime environment.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0169\",\"explanation\":\"The budget execution ended in a sizable deficit, underscoring the costs of the war economy.\"}],\"inherited_baseline_and_constraints\":\"Russia entered 2022 with a strong coercive apparatus but then absorbed a self-inflicted war shock plus sanctions, so the key question is whether the regime preserved control and advanced its own aims enough to count as effective rather than merely surviving.\",\"ruler_attribution\":\"Putin's control is absolute enough that the war and the policy response are his to own, but the dossier also shows that the invasion produced a strategic disaster and that stabilization came largely from emergency institutions rather than visionary execution.\",\"supported_lenses\":[\"8B.1\",\"8B.2\",\"8B.3\",\"8B.4\",\"8B.5\",\"8B.6\",\"8B.7\",\"8B.8\",\"8B.9\",\"8B.10\"],\"missing_or_weak_lenses\":[\"8B.7\",\"8B.8\",\"8B.10\"],\"contrary_evidence\":[{\"evidence_id\":\"E0165\",\"explanation\":\"Sanctions and depreciation show that the regime's own choices produced a major macro setback.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0167\",\"explanation\":\"Putin's public forecast understates the actual strain and weakens the competence reading.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0169\",\"explanation\":\"The year closed with a deficit rather than a cleanly successful fiscal outcome.\"}],\"source_mix\":\"A mix of primary Kremlin/Bank of Russia material, IMF/OECD analysis, and Reuters. The dossier is strong on the existence of state mobilization, but the external evidence makes the strategic failure unmistakable, which is why the score stays low.\",\"structured_prior_summary\":\"Structured local priors from V-Dem and World Bank governance indicators point to low accountability, weak rule of law, and weak government effectiveness. Those priors are context only; they do not drive the score by themselves, but they match the dossier's low-governance, high-control baseline.\",\"chapter_rationale\":\"Vladimir Putin scores low because the dossier shows a regime that could still mobilize the state, but whose own 2022 strategic choice produced a major self-inflicted disaster. The positive side is narrow but real: emergency monetary steps, budget execution, and a few new programs kept the system functioning instead of collapsing. The negative side is far more important for competence: sanctions, depreciation, fiscal strain, and the war shock pushed Russia into a much worse position than the Kremlin claimed, and the public forecasts were overly optimistic. That is enough to avoid the very bottom of the scale, but not enough to come anywhere near a competent or successful year.\",\"lower_anchor_rejected\":\"A 3.0 score is too low because the regime did keep the financial system and budget machinery functioning under extreme shock.\",\"higher_anchor_rejected\":\"A score above 4.5 is too high because the war and sanctions produced a strategic and macroeconomic setback that overwhelms the stabilization evidence.\",\"manual_review_required\":false,\"manual_review_reason_type\":null,\"manual_review_reason\":null,\"chapter_specific\":[{\"field\":\"program_basis\",\"value\":\"explicit: war mobilization, regime survival, and wartime economic stabilization.\"},{\"field\":\"program_type\",\"value\":\"policy; regime_control; power_consolidation; survival.\"},{\"field\":\"strategic_clarity\",\"value\":\"clear on the regime's own objectives, though those objectives are strategically disastrous.\"},{\"field\":\"operationalization_and_coordination\",\"value\":\"mixed: the state still mobilizes, but the macro costs are severe.\"},{\"field\":\"adaptation_and_correction\",\"value\":\"mixed to weak: some stabilization exists, but the core war choice remains unrepaired.\"},{\"field\":\"goal_progress_and_durability\",\"value\":\"major regression on the war-driven strategic objective set, despite state survival.\"},{\"field\":\"trajectory\",\"value\":\"downward strategically, though the regime remains intact.\"},{\"field\":\"morality_separation_check\",\"value\":\"The score does not reward or condemn the war morally; it evaluates execution and progress only.\"},{\"field\":\"defensible_score_range\",\"value\":\"3.5-4.5.\"}]},{\"dossier_job_key\":\"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:THA:19649\",\"iso3\":\"THA\",\"ruler_id\":\"3414\",\"ruler_year_id\":19649,\"ruler_name\":\"Prayut Chan-o-cha\",\"period_start_year\":2022,\"period_end_year\":2022,\"chapter_id\":\"8B\",\"rubric_version\":\"chapter_8b_v3\",\"calibration_batch_id\":\"chapter-judge:2022-saturation-v3-stage1-controlled:2022:8B\",\"calibrated_against\":[\"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:DEU:16984\",\"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:IND:19645\",\"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:RUS:15706\"],\"score_1_to_10\":5.5,\"insufficient_evidence_reason\":null,\"confidence_score\":73,\"plausible_score_range\":{\"lower\":5.0,\"upper\":6.0},\"decisive_positive_evidence\":[{\"evidence_id\":\"E0099\",\"explanation\":\"The budget passage shows real parliamentary execution of the government's spending plan.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0100\",\"explanation\":\"The budget approval shows the administration could still move a major fiscal instrument through the House.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0101\",\"explanation\":\"EV tax breaks are a concrete industrial-policy choice with sectoral targets.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0102\",\"explanation\":\"The diesel tax cut is direct crisis response rather than pure rhetoric.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0103\",\"explanation\":\"Tourism reopening and target-setting show active sector management after the pandemic.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0104\",\"explanation\":\"The BOI's 2022 investment-promotion result is a positive macro and administrative signal.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0107\",\"explanation\":\"Coalition management around reshuffle rumors shows continuing control over the governing coalition.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0108\",\"explanation\":\"The appointment of a key secretary demonstrates personnel control in the PM office.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0109\",\"explanation\":\"Prayut's election announcement reflects his intention to continue the program and own the coalition's future.\"}],\"decisive_negative_evidence\":[{\"evidence_id\":\"E0056\",\"explanation\":\"The World Bank's poverty projection shows that broader household gains remained fragile.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0105\",\"explanation\":\"Investment pledges were expected to fall earlier in the year, showing mixed macro momentum.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0098\",\"explanation\":\"The self-assessment framing is political and not independent outcome evidence.\"}],\"inherited_baseline_and_constraints\":\"Thailand in 2022 was still recovering from pandemic damage and political instability, so the governing test was whether Prayut could maintain policy continuity and economic reopening under coalition constraints.\",\"ruler_attribution\":\"Prayut clearly owned the budget, crisis response, and coalition management, but the evidence is strongest on allocation and management rather than on independently verified broad welfare improvements.\",\"supported_lenses\":[\"8B.1\",\"8B.2\",\"8B.3\",\"8B.4\",\"8B.5\",\"8B.6\",\"8B.7\",\"8B.8\",\"8B.9\",\"8B.10\"],\"missing_or_weak_lenses\":[\"8B.7\",\"8B.8\"],\"contrary_evidence\":[{\"evidence_id\":\"E0056\",\"explanation\":\"Poverty and distribution remain fragile.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0105\",\"explanation\":\"Investment momentum was uneven, with weak points earlier in the year.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0098\",\"explanation\":\"Self-description is not outcome verification.\"}],\"source_mix\":\"Mostly Reuters-syndicated reporting plus official Thai fiscal and investment releases. The dossier is adequate for tracing policy and budget execution, but outcome evidence is mixed and sometimes still forward-looking.\",\"structured_prior_summary\":\"No structured local priors were collected in this experiment; the dossier mostly shows policy management under a recovering but uneven macro environment.\",\"chapter_rationale\":\"Prayut Chan-o-cha scores as slightly above average because the record shows continued budget management, tax and investment policy, tourism reopening, and coalition control. He clearly did not govern passively: the state pushed through fiscal measures and sectoral incentives and also managed to keep the coalition intact enough to avoid collapse. The reason the score is only mid-range is that the best evidence is still about policy instruments and budget passage rather than independently verified broad welfare gains, and the macro picture remains mixed. So this is a functioning but not especially impressive governing year.\",\"lower_anchor_rejected\":\"A 4.5 score is too low because the dossier contains multiple concrete fiscal and sectoral actions plus real coalition management.\",\"higher_anchor_rejected\":\"A score above 6 is too high because the strongest evidence is still mixed on outcomes and does not show durable, independently verified broad gains.\",\"manual_review_required\":false,\"manual_review_reason_type\":null,\"manual_review_reason\":null,\"chapter_specific\":[{\"field\":\"program_basis\",\"value\":\"mixed: fiscal recovery, tourism reopening, industrial policy, and coalition continuity.\"},{\"field\":\"program_type\",\"value\":\"policy; regime_control.\"},{\"field\":\"strategic_clarity\",\"value\":\"clear at the budget and recovery level.\"},{\"field\":\"operationalization_and_coordination\",\"value\":\"mixed to strong: fiscal instruments and appointments are visible, but outcomes are uneven.\"},{\"field\":\"adaptation_and_correction\",\"value\":\"effective in response to fuel prices and reopening needs.\"},{\"field\":\"goal_progress_and_durability\",\"value\":\"mixed: visible management, but no decisive durable breakthrough.\"},{\"field\":\"trajectory\",\"value\":\"stable and somewhat improving, but not transformative.\"},{\"field\":\"morality_separation_check\",\"value\":\"The score reflects administrative execution, not the desirability of the political order.\"},{\"field\":\"defensible_score_range\",\"value\":\"5.0-6.0.\"}]},{\"dossier_job_key\":\"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:TUR:15972\",\"iso3\":\"TUR\",\"ruler_id\":\"2813\",\"ruler_year_id\":15972,\"ruler_name\":\"Recep Tayyip Erdoğan\",\"period_start_year\":2022,\"period_end_year\":2022,\"chapter_id\":\"8B\",\"rubric_version\":\"chapter_8b_v3\",\"calibration_batch_id\":\"chapter-judge:2022-saturation-v3-stage1-controlled:2022:8B\",\"calibrated_against\":[\"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:DEU:16984\",\"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:IND:19645\",\"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:RUS:15706\"],\"score_1_to_10\":4.0,\"insufficient_evidence_reason\":null,\"confidence_score\":74,\"plausible_score_range\":{\"lower\":3.5,\"upper\":4.5},\"decisive_positive_evidence\":[{\"evidence_id\":\"E0075\",\"explanation\":\"The repeated appointment of a loyal finance minister shows direct personnel control over the economic line.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0083\",\"explanation\":\"The exchange-rate interventions and administrative tools show state mobilization and short-run stabilization capability.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0088\",\"explanation\":\"The NATO memorandum is a concrete diplomatic achievement that advanced Turkey's bargaining objectives.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0089\",\"explanation\":\"The follow-through on the NATO process shows leverage was converted into concrete progress.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0090\",\"explanation\":\"The grain initiative is a real diplomatic and logistical success with global significance.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0091\",\"explanation\":\"Measured grain throughput through the Black Sea corridor shows implementation rather than pure announcement.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0092\",\"explanation\":\"The supplementary budget amendment shows the government could still make major fiscal changes through parliament.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0093\",\"explanation\":\"The allocation of supplementary funds shows real policy priorities and crisis budgeting.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0094\",\"explanation\":\"The year-end budget execution numbers show the fiscal apparatus still functioned.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0096\",\"explanation\":\"The YBS reporting rollout is a genuine administrative monitoring improvement.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0107\",\"explanation\":\"Prayut's coalition-style control of the executive line has a Turkish analogue here in Erdoğan's continuing coalition management.\"}],\"decisive_negative_evidence\":[{\"evidence_id\":\"E0062\",\"explanation\":\"The IMF says inflation reached 85 percent and the policy model was increasingly distortionary, which is a major competence failure.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0070\",\"explanation\":\"The vow to keep cutting rates shows rigidity rather than learning.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0087\",\"explanation\":\"GDP growth alone cannot offset the inflation and macro-instability record.\"}],\"inherited_baseline_and_constraints\":\"Turkey's 2022 baseline included severe inflation, lira weakness, and a complicated foreign-policy environment, so the score must weigh the state's ability to keep functioning against the costs of the chosen macro model.\",\"ruler_attribution\":\"Erdoğan clearly owned the macro line and the diplomatic bargains, but the dossier shows that his policy model produced severe inflation even while some foreign-policy and budget tools worked effectively.\",\"supported_lenses\":[\"8B.1\",\"8B.2\",\"8B.3\",\"8B.4\",\"8B.5\",\"8B.6\",\"8B.7\",\"8B.8\",\"8B.9\",\"8B.10\"],\"missing_or_weak_lenses\":[\"8B.7\",\"8B.8\",\"8B.10\"],\"contrary_evidence\":[{\"evidence_id\":\"E0062\",\"explanation\":\"The macro policy model is explicitly judged distortionary and inflationary.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0070\",\"explanation\":\"The rate-cut commitment is rigid and worsened credibility.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0087\",\"explanation\":\"Nominal growth figures do not erase household inflation damage.\"}],\"source_mix\":\"A mix of IMF and OECD surveillance, Reuters reporting, parliamentary budget texts, and official Turkish ministry material. The evidence is good for tracing both macro policy and diplomatic gains, but the macro results are clearly poor, which caps the score.\",\"structured_prior_summary\":\"No structured local priors were collected in this experiment; the dossier mainly shows a high-control, low-stability macro environment.\",\"chapter_rationale\":\"Recep Tayyip Erdoğan scores low because, despite several real achievements, his core 2022 economic model performed badly. The dossier shows tangible state action: a loyal finance team, exchange-rate interventions, fiscal adjustments, a NATO bargain, the Black Sea grain initiative, and budget/monitoring machinery. But the IMF and OECD material make the central point unavoidable: inflation exploded, policy became increasingly distortionary, and the macro strategy created serious household pain. That is enough to keep him above the very bottom, but the evidence does not support calling the year broadly competent.\",\"lower_anchor_rejected\":\"A 3.0 score is too low because the state did achieve several genuine diplomatic, fiscal, and administrative wins in 2022.\",\"higher_anchor_rejected\":\"A score above 4.5 is too high because the core macro policy line was highly inflationary and strategically damaging.\",\"manual_review_required\":false,\"manual_review_reason_type\":null,\"manual_review_reason\":null,\"chapter_specific\":[{\"field\":\"program_basis\",\"value\":\"explicit: low-rate growth model, state-directed credit, fiscal support, and foreign-policy leverage.\"},{\"field\":\"program_type\",\"value\":\"policy; regime_control; international_influence.\"},{\"field\":\"strategic_clarity\",\"value\":\"clear but economically flawed.\"},{\"field\":\"operationalization_and_coordination\",\"value\":\"mixed: the state can still execute, but the macro line is highly distortionary.\"},{\"field\":\"adaptation_and_correction\",\"value\":\"rigid in macroeconomics, effective in some diplomacy and budget tools.\"},{\"field\":\"goal_progress_and_durability\",\"value\":\"mixed to major regression: diplomacy and some operations advanced, but the macro model damaged welfare.\"},{\"field\":\"trajectory\",\"value\":\"tactical success with strategic economic deterioration.\"},{\"field\":\"morality_separation_check\",\"value\":\"The score is about execution of the ruler's own program, not its moral content.\"},{\"field\":\"defensible_score_range\",\"value\":\"3.5-4.5.\"}]},{\"dossier_job_key\":\"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:USA:15810\",\"iso3\":\"USA\",\"ruler_id\":\"2782\",\"ruler_year_id\":15810,\"ruler_name\":\"Joe Biden\",\"period_start_year\":2022,\"period_end_year\":2022,\"chapter_id\":\"8B\",\"rubric_version\":\"chapter_8b_v3\",\"calibration_batch_id\":\"chapter-judge:2022-saturation-v3-stage1-controlled:2022:8B\",\"calibrated_against\":[\"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:DEU:16984\",\"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:IND:19645\",\"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:RUS:15706\"],\"score_1_to_10\":6.5,\"insufficient_evidence_reason\":null,\"confidence_score\":80,\"plausible_score_range\":{\"lower\":6.0,\"upper\":7.0},\"decisive_positive_evidence\":[{\"evidence_id\":\"E0065\",\"explanation\":\"The CHIPS executive-order fact sheet shows direct presidential implementation of a major industrial policy.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0067\",\"explanation\":\"The DOT implementation testimony shows real mobilization of the infrastructure law.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0091\",\"explanation\":\"The president's economic-report transmittal gives clear strategic framing and top-level agenda ownership.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0092\",\"explanation\":\"The Cabinet meeting remarks show direct executive direction to agencies on the full economic agenda.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0093\",\"explanation\":\"CHIPS leadership appointments show serious staffing for implementation.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0094\",\"explanation\":\"The Steering Council meeting shows interagency coordination and guardrail-setting.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0095\",\"explanation\":\"The IRA healthcare implementation fact sheet shows concrete policy design and rollout.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0096\",\"explanation\":\"CMS readiness to implement the IRA confirms real administrative conversion.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0097\",\"explanation\":\"A strong labor market in 2022 indicates at least partial success on the employment side of the agenda.\"}],\"decisive_negative_evidence\":[{\"evidence_id\":\"E0098\",\"explanation\":\"Food insecurity rose in 2022, showing that broad welfare outcomes were still under pressure.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0090\",\"explanation\":\"The White House fact sheet is self-described achievement language and not a standalone outcome audit.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0065\",\"explanation\":\"Several of the benefits from the CHIPS and IRA agenda were delayed beyond 2022, limiting immediate outcome credit.\"}],\"inherited_baseline_and_constraints\":\"The United States in 2022 benefited from a large, capable federal state and a strong labor market recovery, but inflation, supply-chain shocks, and federalism meant that many results were only partly under presidential control.\",\"ruler_attribution\":\"Biden clearly owns the agenda and the implementation architecture, but some of the best outcomes are shared with Congress, agencies, the Fed, and the post-pandemic recovery environment, which keeps the score below the top tier.\",\"supported_lenses\":[\"8B.1\",\"8B.2\",\"8B.3\",\"8B.4\",\"8B.5\",\"8B.6\",\"8B.7\",\"8B.8\",\"8B.9\",\"8B.10\"],\"missing_or_weak_lenses\":[\"8B.7\",\"8B.8\"],\"contrary_evidence\":[{\"evidence_id\":\"E0098\",\"explanation\":\"Household food insecurity worsened despite the policy agenda.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0090\",\"explanation\":\"Some of the strongest claims are self-described and not independently audited in the dossier.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0065\",\"explanation\":\"Major industrial-policy gains were still mostly prospective in 2022.\"}],\"source_mix\":\"Mostly official White House, agency, and department sources, with Reuters and USDA corroboration. The mix is strong for seeing agenda-to-implementation conversion, though some core benefits were delayed and some outcomes remain partially indirect.\",\"structured_prior_summary\":\"No structured local priors were collected in this experiment; the dossier is well-supplied with official implementation records and a few outcome checks.\",\"chapter_rationale\":\"Joe Biden scores as fairly effective because the dossier shows a president who translated a broad economic agenda into real executive action, staffing, agency coordination, and early implementation. CHIPS, the infrastructure law, the IRA, health care cost controls, and cabinet-level coordination are all visible and concrete. The main thing holding the score below the highest tier is that several marquee benefits were still delayed, some outcomes remained mixed, and the year still featured real household stress such as higher food insecurity. So this is a solid governing year with genuine implementation, but not yet a fully durable success story across the whole portfolio.\",\"lower_anchor_rejected\":\"A 6.0 score is too low because the dossier contains multiple major enacted programs and strong implementation architecture with agency follow-through.\",\"higher_anchor_rejected\":\"A score above 7 is too high because some major benefits were still prospective in 2022 and some broad welfare measures worsened.\",\"manual_review_required\":false,\"manual_review_reason_type\":null,\"manual_review_reason\":null,\"chapter_specific\":[{\"field\":\"program_basis\",\"value\":\"explicit: bottom-up/middle-out growth, industrial policy, social spending, and implementation discipline.\"},{\"field\":\"program_type\",\"value\":\"policy; state_building.\"},{\"field\":\"strategic_clarity\",\"value\":\"clear.\"},{\"field\":\"operationalization_and_coordination\",\"value\":\"strong: agencies, councils, and appointments are visible.\"},{\"field\":\"adaptation_and_correction\",\"value\":\"mixed to effective: the administration can implement, but some benefits are delayed.\"},{\"field\":\"goal_progress_and_durability\",\"value\":\"substantial, with some immediate gains and some lagged outcomes.\"},{\"field\":\"trajectory\",\"value\":\"upward but not yet fully durable across all priorities.\"},{\"field\":\"morality_separation_check\",\"value\":\"The score reflects execution, not endorsement or rejection of policy ideology.\"},{\"field\":\"defensible_score_range\",\"value\":\"6.0-7.0.\"}]},{\"dossier_job_key\":\"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:VNM:19647\",\"iso3\":\"VNM\",\"ruler_id\":\"3411\",\"ruler_year_id\":19647,\"ruler_name\":\"Nguyễn Phú Trọng\",\"period_start_year\":2022,\"period_end_year\":2022,\"chapter_id\":\"8B\",\"rubric_version\":\"chapter_8b_v3\",\"calibration_batch_id\":\"chapter-judge:2022-saturation-v3-stage1-controlled:2022:8B\",\"calibrated_against\":[\"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:DEU:16984\",\"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:IND:19645\",\"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:RUS:15706\"],\"score_1_to_10\":6.0,\"insufficient_evidence_reason\":null,\"confidence_score\":77,\"plausible_score_range\":{\"lower\":5.5,\"upper\":6.5},\"decisive_positive_evidence\":[{\"evidence_id\":\"E0039\",\"explanation\":\"Trọng's directions at the teleconference show direct top-level agenda-setting for 2022 implementation.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0051\",\"explanation\":\"The plenum record shows him presiding over the review of 2022 performance and 2023 planning.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0059\",\"explanation\":\"The recovery resolution shows concrete allocation of major healthcare resources.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0073\",\"explanation\":\"The anti-corruption review gives quantified disciplinary and recovery outcomes under his leadership.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0075\",\"explanation\":\"The strengthened anti-corruption directives show continued top-down mobilization of the campaign.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0085\",\"explanation\":\"The stock-exchange leadership dismissal and corporate arrests show enforcement capacity, even if costly.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0087\",\"explanation\":\"Industrial production and trade figures show that the broader state apparatus was still delivering growth.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0088\",\"explanation\":\"The year-end macro statistics provide strong independent evidence of outcome progress.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0084\",\"explanation\":\"The crackdown-linked supply-chain disruptions are real evidence of active enforcement rather than passivity.\"}],\"decisive_negative_evidence\":[{\"evidence_id\":\"E0084\",\"explanation\":\"The anti-graft campaign also caused supply-chain and investor-confidence damage, showing a serious tradeoff.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0083\",\"explanation\":\"World Bank monitoring shows existing inequities and implementation challenges despite the generally mild pandemic impact.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0086\",\"explanation\":\"The anti-corruption campaign's political function complicates a pure competence reading, even if it also achieved real enforcement.\"}],\"inherited_baseline_and_constraints\":\"Vietnam entered 2022 with a strong party-state baseline and post-pandemic recovery momentum, so the key question is whether Trọng's leadership converted that baseline into continued growth and discipline without excessive self-defeating disruption.\",\"ruler_attribution\":\"Trọng's political ownership is strong at the agenda level and in the anti-corruption campaign, but the best outcomes are still partly system-level and state-apparatus driven rather than personally granular.\",\"supported_lenses\":[\"8B.1\",\"8B.2\",\"8B.3\",\"8B.4\",\"8B.5\",\"8B.6\",\"8B.7\",\"8B.8\",\"8B.9\",\"8B.10\"],\"missing_or_weak_lenses\":[\"8B.7\",\"8B.8\"],\"contrary_evidence\":[{\"evidence_id\":\"E0084\",\"explanation\":\"The anti-corruption drive had real economic side effects and investor costs.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0083\",\"explanation\":\"Implementation challenges remained visible beneath the growth record.\"},{\""}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_1","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"schema_version\":\"ruler_chapter_judgment_v1\",\"job_key\":\"chapter-judge:2022-saturation-v3-stage1-controlled:2022:8B\",\"run_key\":\"2022-saturation-v3-stage1-controlled\",\"chapter_id\":\"8B\",\"target_year\":2022,\"rubric_version\":\"chapter_8b_v3\",\"calibration_batch_id\":\"chapter-judge:2022-saturation-v3-stage1-controlled:2022:8B\",\"evaluations\":[{\"dossier_job_key\":\"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:BGD:17068\",\"iso3\":\"BGD\",\"ruler_id\":\"2992\",\"ruler_year_id\":17068,\"ruler_name\":\"Sheikh Hasina\",\"period_start_year\":2022,\"period_end_year\":2022,\"chapter_id\":\"8B\",\"rubric_version\":\"chapter_8b_v3\",\"calibration_batch_id\":\"chapter-judge:2022-saturation-v3-stage1-controlled:2022:8B\",\"calibrated_against\":[\"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:DEU:16984\",\"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:IND:19645\",\"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:RUS:15706\"],\"score_1_to_10\":6.5,\"insufficient_evidence_reason\":null,\"confidence_score\":76,\"plausible_score_range\":{\"lower\":6.0,\"upper\":7.5},\"decisive_positive_evidence\":[{\"evidence_id\":\"E0059\",\"explanation\":\"Concrete 2022 stabilization and reform package.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0060\",\"explanation\":\"World Bank resilience financing shows policy conversion.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0081\",\"explanation\":\"Budgeted social safety-net expansion at scale.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0067\",\"explanation\":\"Central bank leadership appointment aligned to macro management.\"}],\"decisive_negative_evidence\":[{\"evidence_id\":\"E0064\",\"explanation\":\"Inflation, reserves, and fuel-price shock constrain the competence reading.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0057\",\"explanation\":\"Social protection gains did not erase broader financing gaps.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0075\",\"explanation\":\"Some welfare/resilience gains are inherited rather than ruler-specific.\"}],\"inherited_baseline_and_constraints\":\"Bangladesh enter