{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_0","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"schema_version\":\"ruler_chapter_judgment_v1\",\"job_key\":\"chapter-judge:2022-saturation-v3-stage1-controlled:2022:8B\",\"run_key\":\"2022-saturation-v3-stage1-controlled\",\"chapter_id\":\"8B\",\"target_year\":2022,\"rubric_version\":\"chapter_8b_v3\",\"calibration_batch_id\":\"chapter-judge:2022-saturation-v3-stage1-controlled:2022:8B\",\"evaluations\":[{\"dossier_job_key\":\"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:BGD:17068\",\"iso3\":\"BGD\",\"ruler_id\":\"2992\",\"ruler_year_id\":17068,\"ruler_name\":\"Sheikh Hasina\",\"period_start_year\":2022,\"period_end_year\":2022,\"chapter_id\":\"8B\",\"rubric_version\":\"chapter_8b_v3\",\"calibration_batch_id\":\"chapter-judge:2022-saturation-v3-stage1-controlled:2022:8B\",\"calibrated_against\":[\"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:DEU:16984\",\"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:IDN:16199\",\"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:RUS:15706\"],\"score_1_to_10\":6.0,\"insufficient_evidence_reason\":null,\"confidence_score\":83,\"plausible_score_range\":{\"lower\":5.5,\"upper\":6.5},\"decisive_positive_evidence\":[{\"evidence_id\":\"E0057\",\"explanation\":\"Shows concrete 2022 safety-net funding, expanded transfers, and delivery tooling, so the welfare program was not just rhetorical.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0059\",\"explanation\":\"Shows the 2022 stabilization package translated into a real policy response on revenue, spending, monetary policy, and exchange-rate flexibility.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0067\",\"explanation\":\"Shows a direct 2022 appointment affecting monetary management, which supports executive control over key economic staffing.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0090\",\"explanation\":\"Shows a direct social-policy commitment tied to housing delivery with a concrete beneficiary count in 2022.\"}],\"decisive_negative_evidence\":[{\"evidence_id\":\"E0064\",\"explanation\":\"Fuel-price shock and rising inflation show reactive crisis management and constrain the claim of clean competence.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0075\",\"explanation\":\"Climate-resilience gains are real but partly inherited and do not by themselves prove Hasina personally converted plans into broad household gains.\"}],\"inherited_baseline_and_constraints\":\"Preexisting state capacity, institutional constraints, external shocks, and implementation lags materially shape the case; only ruler-attributed conversion of goals into action and progress is credited.\",\"ruler_attribution\":\"Strong on program ownership and cabinet-level economic direction; weaker on proving that Hasina personally drove every implementation step or that announced welfare gains fully reached households.\",\"supported_lenses\":[\"8B.1\",\"8B.2\",\"8B.3\",\"8B.4\",\"8B.5\",\"8B.6\",\"8B.7\",\"8B.8\",\"8B.9\",\"8B.10\"],\"missing_or_weak_lenses\":[\"8B.7\",\"8B.8\",\"8B.10\"],\"contrary_evidence\":[{\"evidence_id\":\"E0064\",\"explanation\":\"The fuel-price jump and inflationary stress cut against a clean success narrative and show reactive policy under pressure.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0081\",\"explanation\":\"Large budgeted transfers show commitment, but not independent proof of delivery quality or equitable targeting.\"}],\"source_mix\":\"Mix of primary government records, multilateral assessments, and Reuters/major-media corroboration; official self-reporting was treated as program and implementation evidence, not as independent proof of success.\",\"structured_prior_summary\":\"Structured local priors were not collected in this experiment; judgment rests on the embedded projection and cited evidence only.\",\"chapter_rationale\":\"Hasina's 2022 record is mixed-to-good on competence. The dossier shows a clear welfare-and-stabilization program, real budgeting and staffing choices, and some observable delivery in safety nets, housing, and macro policy; it also shows meaningful crisis responses rather than empty slogans. The limits are that independent outcome verification is thinner than the announced programs, some gains are partly inherited or reactive, and inflation and fuel-price stress narrowed the room for clean credit. Moral approval or disapproval of the program did not affect this score; on execution alone, the evidence supports a mid-range positive judgment rather than a materially higher one.\",\"lower_anchor_rejected\":\"A 5 would understate the amount of real state action in budgets, appointments, and stabilization; the record is stronger than generic mixed competence.\",\"higher_anchor_rejected\":\"A 7 would require more durable, independently verified household-level gains and stronger evidence that implementation quality matched the scale of the announced program.\",\"manual_review_required\":false,\"manual_review_reason_type\":null,\"manual_review_reason\":null,\"chapter_specific\":[{\"field\":\"program_basis\",\"value\":\"explicit\"},{\"field\":\"program_type\",\"value\":\"policy, state_building\"},{\"field\":\"strategic_clarity\",\"value\":\"clear\"},{\"field\":\"operationalization\",\"value\":\"strong\"},{\"field\":\"mobilization_and_coordination\",\"value\":\"mixed\"},{\"field\":\"adaptation\",\"value\":\"mixed\"},{\"field\":\"goal_progress\",\"value\":\"mixed\"},{\"field\":\"durability\",\"value\":\"mixed\"},{\"field\":\"trajectory\",\"value\":\"slightly upward but uneven\"},{\"field\":\"morality_separation_check\",\"value\":\"Approval or disapproval of the program did not affect the execution score.\"}]},{\"dossier_job_key\":\"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:BRA:19646\",\"iso3\":\"BRA\",\"ruler_id\":\"3413\",\"ruler_year_id\":19646,\"ruler_name\":\"Jair Bolsonaro\",\"period_start_year\":2022,\"period_end_year\":2022,\"chapter_id\":\"8B\",\"rubric_version\":\"chapter_8b_v3\",\"calibration_batch_id\":\"chapter-judge:2022-saturation-v3-stage1-controlled:2022:8B\",\"calibrated_against\":[\"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:MEX:15801\",\"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:USA:15810\",\"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:PHL:16194\"],\"score_1_to_10\":5.5,\"insufficient_evidence_reason\":null,\"confidence_score\":78,\"plausible_score_range\":{\"lower\":5.0,\"upper\":6.0},\"decisive_positive_evidence\":[{\"evidence_id\":\"E0061\",\"explanation\":\"Shows direct presidential control over budget-credit delegation, i.e. concrete executive action rather than rhetoric.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0065\",\"explanation\":\"Shows a large 2022/23 rural-credit program, indicating real policy conversion into sectoral financing.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0070\",\"explanation\":\"Shows a major cash-transfer expansion reaching poor families in 2022, with a defined benefit floor and coverage target.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0102\",\"explanation\":\"Shows an official agreement to keep fuel and electricity prices lower through tax treatment, a concrete late-2022 intervention.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0104\",\"explanation\":\"Shows year-end income recovery, though mixed, giving some evidence that programs and labor-market rebound moved outcomes in the intended direction.\"}],\"decisive_negative_evidence\":[{\"evidence_id\":\"E0058\",\"explanation\":\"Election-year spending and promises imposed a very large fiscal cost and show that much of the agenda was politically driven and heavily constrained.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0103\",\"explanation\":\"Congress-backed spending packages bypassed fiscal rules, which signals stressed and partly reactive governance rather than clean execution.\"}],\"inherited_baseline_and_constraints\":\"Preexisting state capacity, institutional constraints, external shocks, and implementation lags materially shape the case; only ruler-attributed conversion of goals into action and progress is credited.\",\"ruler_attribution\":\"Strong on election-year mobilization and budgetary action, but weaker on autonomy because Congress, markets, and fiscal constraints shaped much of the actual path.\",\"supported_lenses\":[\"8B.1\",\"8B.2\",\"8B.3\",\"8B.4\",\"8B.5\",\"8B.6\",\"8B.7\",\"8B.8\",\"8B.9\",\"8B.10\"],\"missing_or_weak_lenses\":[\"8B.7\",\"8B.8\",\"8B.10\"],\"contrary_evidence\":[{\"evidence_id\":\"E0058\",\"explanation\":\"The election-year fiscal push was expensive and only partly executive-led, limiting how cleanly it can be read as competence.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0103\",\"explanation\":\"The spending package and budget bypasses show pressure and coalition bargaining rather than stable, disciplined execution.\"}],\"source_mix\":\"Mix of primary government records, multilateral assessments, and Reuters/major-media corroboration; official self-reporting was treated as program and implementation evidence, not as independent proof of success.\",\"structured_prior_summary\":\"Structured local priors were not collected in this experiment; judgment rests on the embedded projection and cited evidence only.\",\"chapter_rationale\":\"Bolsonaro's 2022 record is mixed rather than clearly strong. He and his government did convert election-year priorities into real transfers, rural credit, appointment changes, and fuel-price interventions, so this is not a symbolic-only case. But the same dossier shows highly politicized fiscal choices, coalition dependence, and an expensive spending push that strained discipline and muddied attribution. Moral approval or disapproval of the agenda did not affect the score; on execution and progress, the evidence supports a modestly positive middle score, not a stronger one.\",\"lower_anchor_rejected\":\"A 5 would ignore the fact that Bolsonaro's government actually moved large budgets, transfers, and administrative powers into action in 2022.\",\"higher_anchor_rejected\":\"A 6.5 or 7 would require cleaner fiscal discipline, stronger independent outcome evidence, and less election-driven, reactive policy behavior.\",\"manual_review_required\":false,\"manual_review_reason_type\":null,\"manual_review_reason\":null,\"chapter_specific\":[{\"field\":\"program_basis\",\"value\":\"explicit\"},{\"field\":\"program_type\",\"value\":\"policy, regime_control\"},{\"field\":\"strategic_clarity\",\"value\":\"partial\"},{\"field\":\"operationalization\",\"value\":\"mixed\"},{\"field\":\"mobilization_and_coordination\",\"value\":\"mixed\"},{\"field\":\"adaptation\",\"value\":\"mixed\"},{\"field\":\"goal_progress\",\"value\":\"mixed\"},{\"field\":\"durability\",\"value\":\"fragile\"},{\"field\":\"trajectory\",\"value\":\"mixed and election-driven\"},{\"field\":\"morality_separation_check\",\"value\":\"Approval or disapproval of the program did not affect the execution score.\"}]},{\"dossier_job_key\":\"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:CHN:15832\",\"iso3\":\"CHN\",\"ruler_id\":\"1432\",\"ruler_year_id\":15832,\"ruler_name\":\"Xi Jinping\",\"period_start_year\":2022,\"period_end_year\":2022,\"chapter_id\":\"8B\",\"rubric_version\":\"chapter_8b_v3\",\"calibration_batch_id\":\"chapter-judge:2022-saturation-v3-stage1-controlled:2022:8B\",\"calibrated_against\":[\"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:JPN:16638\",\"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:RUS:15706\",\"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:VNM:19647\"],\"score_1_to_10\":8.0,\"insufficient_evidence_reason\":null,\"confidence_score\":89,\"plausible_score_range\":{\"lower\":7.5,\"upper\":8.5},\"decisive_positive_evidence\":[{\"evidence_id\":\"E0077\",\"explanation\":\"Shows a party-level strategic program adopted under Xi's leadership, with clear goals for common prosperity and development.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0103\",\"explanation\":\"Shows Xi personally setting five-year objectives and program direction at the 20th Congress, i.e. high-level strategic clarity.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0105\",\"explanation\":\"Shows a concrete State Council policy package to stabilize the economy with named instruments and implementation structure.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0107\",\"explanation\":\"Shows credit steering, targeted lending, and service coordination, indicating actual implementation rather than slogans alone.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0111\",\"explanation\":\"Shows a real late-2022 policy adjustment to optimize COVID response, demonstrating adaptation to pressure.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0112\",\"explanation\":\"Shows a further year-end shift away from zero-COVID, which is strong evidence of correction under pressure.\"}],\"decisive_negative_evidence\":[{\"evidence_id\":\"E0052\",\"explanation\":\"The easing of curbs was reactive after protest pressure, so it limits any claim of foresight or fully stable control.\"}],\"inherited_baseline_and_constraints\":\"Preexisting state capacity, institutional constraints, external shocks, and implementation lags materially shape the case; only ruler-attributed conversion of goals into action and progress is credited.\",\"ruler_attribution\":\"Strong program ownership and high control over the party-state; most limits come from opacity and the difficulty of independently verifying the quality and durability of implementation.\",\"supported_lenses\":[\"8B.1\",\"8B.2\",\"8B.3\",\"8B.4\",\"8B.5\",\"8B.6\",\"8B.7\",\"8B.8\",\"8B.9\",\"8B.10\"],\"missing_or_weak_lenses\":[\"8B.7\",\"8B.8\",\"8B.9\"],\"contrary_evidence\":[{\"evidence_id\":\"E0052\",\"explanation\":\"The COVID policy loosening was pressured and reactive, not a clean example of anticipatory management.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0110\",\"explanation\":\"Monitoring improvements are meaningful, but they still do not prove impartiality or fully effective anti-corruption enforcement.\"}],\"source_mix\":\"Mix of primary government records, multilateral assessments, and Reuters/major-media corroboration; official self-reporting was treated as program and implementation evidence, not as independent proof of success.\",\"structured_prior_summary\":\"Structured local priors were not collected in this experiment; judgment rests on the embedded projection and cited evidence only.\",\"chapter_rationale\":\"Xi's 2022 record is strong on competence. The dossier shows a clear governing program, extensive state mobilization, concrete policy packages, targeted credit and social steering, and real late-year adaptation on COVID and economic management. The main limits are that the system is opaque, many sources are official, and some of the sharpest shifts were reactive rather than purely planned. Moral approval or disapproval of the program did not affect the score; on execution and progress, the evidence supports a high score, but not a perfect one, because independent verification and durability remain incomplete.\",\"lower_anchor_rejected\":\"A 7.0 or 7.5 would understate the breadth of policy control, adaptation, and follow-through visible in the 2022 record.\",\"higher_anchor_rejected\":\"A 9 would require stronger independent proof of durable, high-quality outcomes and less dependence on official self-reporting.\",\"manual_review_required\":false,\"manual_review_reason_type\":null,\"manual_review_reason\":null,\"chapter_specific\":[{\"field\":\"program_basis\",\"value\":\"explicit\"},{\"field\":\"program_type\",\"value\":\"policy, state_building, regime_control\"},{\"field\":\"strategic_clarity\",\"value\":\"exceptional\"},{\"field\":\"operationalization\",\"value\":\"strong\"},{\"field\":\"mobilization_and_coordination\",\"value\":\"strong\"},{\"field\":\"adaptation\",\"value\":\"effective\"},{\"field\":\"goal_progress\",\"value\":\"substantial\"},{\"field\":\"durability\",\"value\":\"durable\"},{\"field\":\"trajectory\",\"value\":\"upward and still consolidating\"},{\"field\":\"morality_separation_check\",\"value\":\"Approval or disapproval of the program did not affect the execution score.\"}]},{\"dossier_job_key\":\"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:COD:16113\",\"iso3\":\"COD\",\"ruler_id\":\"2830\",\"ruler_year_id\":16113,\"ruler_name\":\"Félix Tshisekedi\",\"period_start_year\":2022,\"period_end_year\":2022,\"chapter_id\":\"8B\",\"rubric_version\":\"chapter_8b_v3\",\"calibration_batch_id\":\"chapter-judge:2022-saturation-v3-stage1-controlled:2022:8B\",\"calibrated_against\":[\"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:ETH:16782\",\"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:NGA:15787\",\"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:PAK:16682\"],\"score_1_to_10\":5.0,\"insufficient_evidence_reason\":null,\"confidence_score\":76,\"plausible_score_range\":{\"lower\":4.5,\"upper\":5.5},\"decisive_positive_evidence\":[{\"evidence_id\":\"E0108\",\"explanation\":\"Shows Tshisekedi personally overseeing the 145-territories development program, a concrete executive coordination role.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0112\",\"explanation\":\"Shows direct instructions on judicial independence and public-finance reforms, supporting real institutional direction.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0118\",\"explanation\":\"Shows prudent macro-policy choices, including halting central-bank financing to government, which is a real policy correction.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0119\",\"explanation\":\"Shows a government-led vaccination campaign with an operational design and target population, even though rollout was partial.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0121\",\"explanation\":\"Shows a new grant for stabilization and reintegration in conflict-affected provinces, indicating active mobilization rather than stagnation.\"}],\"decisive_negative_evidence\":[{\"evidence_id\":\"E0115\",\"explanation\":\"The jobs and firm-creation outcomes are projected rather than completed, so they do not establish year-end delivery.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0117\",\"explanation\":\"Telecom reform was incomplete because secondary legislation was still needed, limiting the claim of execution.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0122\",\"explanation\":\"The budget increase was partly driven by higher mining prices, so it cannot be treated as pure ruler skill.\"}],\"inherited_baseline_and_constraints\":\"Preexisting state capacity, institutional constraints, external shocks, and implementation lags materially shape the case; only ruler-attributed conversion of goals into action and progress is credited.\",\"ruler_attribution\":\"Tshisekedi clearly influenced the program direction and oversaw some concrete reforms, but much of the delivery path was donor-backed, preparatory, or only partially completed.\",\"supported_lenses\":[\"8B.1\",\"8B.2\",\"8B.3\",\"8B.4\",\"8B.5\",\"8B.6\",\"8B.7\",\"8B.8\",\"8B.9\",\"8B.10\"],\"missing_or_weak_lenses\":[\"8B.6\",\"8B.7\",\"8B.10\"],\"contrary_evidence\":[{\"evidence_id\":\"E0115\",\"explanation\":\"Key job and enterprise gains were projected rather than realized, so outcome credit remains partial.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0117\",\"explanation\":\"Implementation gaps in telecom reform show that the government moved on paper faster than it moved in fully executed results.\"}],\"source_mix\":\"Mix of primary government records, multilateral assessments, and Reuters/major-media corroboration; official self-reporting was treated as program and implementation evidence, not as independent proof of success.\",\"structured_prior_summary\":\"Structured local priors were not collected in this experiment; judgment rests on the embedded projection and cited evidence only.\",\"chapter_rationale\":\"Tshisekedi's 2022 record is average: there was a visible governing program, repeated oversight, and some real policy corrections, but the strongest evidence is still about planning, not completed delivery. The dossier shows him chairing development review, pushing judicial and fiscal reforms, and backing health and stability initiatives, yet many outcomes were incomplete, projected, or heavily donor-mediated. Moral approval or disapproval of the agenda did not affect this score; on execution alone, the evidence supports a middle score rather than something stronger.\",\"lower_anchor_rejected\":\"A 4 would ignore the genuine, ruler-linked mobilization and the fact that multiple reforms did move beyond pure rhetoric.\",\"higher_anchor_rejected\":\"A 6 would require stronger evidence of completed outputs and more independent proof that the 2022 programs materially improved conditions by year-end.\",\"manual_review_required\":false,\"manual_review_reason_type\":null,\"manual_review_reason\":null,\"chapter_specific\":[{\"field\":\"program_basis\",\"value\":\"mostly_explicit\"},{\"field\":\"program_type\",\"value\":\"policy, state_building\"},{\"field\":\"strategic_clarity\",\"value\":\"partial\"},{\"field\":\"operationalization\",\"value\":\"mixed\"},{\"field\":\"mobilization_and_coordination\",\"value\":\"mixed\"},{\"field\":\"adaptation\",\"value\":\"mixed\"},{\"field\":\"goal_progress\",\"value\":\"mixed\"},{\"field\":\"durability\",\"value\":\"fragile\"},{\"field\":\"trajectory\",\"value\":\"incremental but incomplete\"},{\"field\":\"morality_separation_check\",\"value\":\"Approval or disapproval of the program did not affect the execution score.\"}]},{\"dossier_job_key\":\"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:DEU:16984\",\"iso3\":\"DEU\",\"ruler_id\":\"2975\",\"ruler_year_id\":16984,\"ruler_name\":\"Olaf Scholz\",\"period_start_year\":2022,\"period_end_year\":2022,\"chapter_id\":\"8B\",\"rubric_version\":\"chapter_8b_v3\",\"calibration_batch_id\":\"chapter-judge:2022-saturation-v3-stage1-controlled:2022:8B\",\"calibrated_against\":[\"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:USA:15810\",\"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:JPN:16638\",\"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:BGD:17068\"],\"score_1_to_10\":6.5,\"insufficient_evidence_reason\":null,\"confidence_score\":84,\"plausible_score_range\":{\"lower\":6.0,\"upper\":7.0},\"decisive_positive_evidence\":[{\"evidence_id\":\"E0087\",\"explanation\":\"Shows a large, concrete defense and resilience shift under Scholz's chancellorship in response to the Ukraine shock.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0088\",\"explanation\":\"Shows a major social-security reform design with less bureaucracy and clearer activation, not just rhetoric.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0092\",\"explanation\":\"Shows crisis stabilization for Uniper, a real government intervention to secure energy supply.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0093\",\"explanation\":\"Shows federal coordination for Ukrainian refugees with concrete support structures across levels of government.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0094\",\"explanation\":\"Shows survey-backed evidence that the refugee integration apparatus was being used by year-end 2022.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0096\",\"explanation\":\"Shows IMF support for Germany's energy-price response as appropriate and implemented through policy instruments.\"}],\"decisive_negative_evidence\":[{\"evidence_id\":\"E0095\",\"explanation\":\"The OECD noted support could have been better targeted, so the response was effective but not optimal.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0097\",\"explanation\":\"ifo's critique highlights sustainability and fiscal-cost concerns, limiting how far the relief packages can count as mastery.\"}],\"inherited_baseline_and_constraints\":\"Preexisting state capacity, institutional constraints, external shocks, and implementation lags materially shape the case; only ruler-attributed conversion of goals into action and progress is credited.\",\"ruler_attribution\":\"Scholz had real executive authority over a capable coalition state, but many key outcomes were defensive responses to the energy and Ukraine shocks rather than pure long-range transformation.\",\"supported_lenses\":[\"8B.1\",\"8B.2\",\"8B.3\",\"8B.4\",\"8B.5\",\"8B.6\",\"8B.7\",\"8B.8\",\"8B.9\",\"8B.10\"],\"missing_or_weak_lenses\":[\"8B.7\",\"8B.10\"],\"contrary_evidence\":[{\"evidence_id\":\"E0095\",\"explanation\":\"Independent assessment says the relief response was not perfectly targeted, so competence was real but imperfect.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0097\",\"explanation\":\"External criticism of cost and sustainability keeps this below the top tier.\"}],\"source_mix\":\"Mix of primary government records, multilateral assessments, and Reuters/major-media corroboration; official self-reporting was treated as program and implementation evidence, not as independent proof of success.\",\"structured_prior_summary\":\"Structured local priors were not collected in this experiment; judgment rests on the embedded projection and cited evidence only.\",\"chapter_rationale\":\"Scholz's 2022 record is clearly effective but not exceptional. The dossier shows a coalition government that translated a program into real laws, budgets, crisis interventions, refugee coordination, and implementation machinery, especially after the Ukraine shock. The limits are that many gains were reactive, energy relief was imperfectly targeted, and durable outcome proof is still limited. Moral approval or disapproval of the program did not affect this score; on execution and progress, the evidence supports a solid mid-high judgment rather than a substantially stronger one.\",\"lower_anchor_rejected\":\"A 5 would understate the amount of actual policy conversion, coordination, and crisis management visible in 2022.\",\"higher_anchor_rejected\":\"A 7.5 or 8 would require stronger independent evidence of durable, broad-based gains and less reliance on defensive shock response.\",\"manual_review_required\":false,\"manual_review_reason_type\":null,\"manual_review_reason\":null,\"chapter_specific\":[{\"field\":\"program_basis\",\"value\":\"explicit\"},{\"field\":\"program_type\",\"value\":\"policy, state_building\"},{\"field\":\"strategic_clarity\",\"value\":\"clear\"},{\"field\":\"operationalization\",\"value\":\"strong\"},{\"field\":\"mobilization_and_coordination\",\"value\":\"strong\"},{\"field\":\"adaptation\",\"value\":\"effective\"},{\"field\":\"goal_progress\",\"value\":\"substantial\"},{\"field\":\"durability\",\"value\":\"mixed\"},{\"field\":\"trajectory\",\"value\":\"upward under shock\"},{\"field\":\"morality_separation_check\",\"value\":\"Approval or disapproval of the program did not affect the execution score.\"}]},{\"dossier_job_key\":\"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:EGY:16232\",\"iso3\":\"EGY\",\"ruler_id\":\"2851\",\"ruler_year_id\":16232,\"ruler_name\":\"Abdel Fattah el-Sisi\",\"period_start_year\":2022,\"period_end_year\":2022,\"chapter_id\":\"8B\",\"rubric_version\":\"chapter_8b_v3\",\"calibration_batch_id\":\"chapter-judge:2022-saturation-v3-stage1-controlled:2022:8B\",\"calibrated_against\":[\"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:TUR:15972\",\"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:COD:16113\",\"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:BGD:17068\"],\"score_1_to_10\":6.0,\"insufficient_evidence_reason\":null,\"confidence_score\":81,\"plausible_score_range\":{\"lower\":5.5,\"upper\":6.5},\"decisive_positive_evidence\":[{\"evidence_id\":\"E0072\",\"explanation\":\"Shows the military-led state investment model operating under Sisi, a major governing architecture rather than loose rhetoric.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0073\",\"explanation\":\"Shows opacity, privilege, and patronage within that model, which paradoxically confirms how strongly the executive could shape the system.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0079\",\"explanation\":\"Shows a direct presidential appointment to the anti-corruption authority, demonstrating control over oversight institutions.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0080\",\"explanation\":\"Shows a formal judicial appointment under Sisi with institutional detail and a professional selection rule.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0082\",\"explanation\":\"Shows a presidentially approved state-ownership policy with concrete divestment/sector targets.\"}],\"decisive_negative_evidence\":[{\"evidence_id\":\"E0074\",\"explanation\":\"Freedom House's account of control and weak transparency limits the case for clean, high-quality execution.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0081\",\"explanation\":\"IMF-supported reform goals were still conditional and not yet proof of durable transparency or governance improvement.\"}],\"inherited_baseline_and_constraints\":\"Preexisting state capacity, institutional constraints, external shocks, and implementation lags materially shape the case; only ruler-attributed conversion of goals into action and progress is credited.\",\"ruler_attribution\":\"Sisi clearly controls personnel and state direction, but the system's opacity and the gap between formal policy and verified delivery keep the score below the top tier.\",\"supported_lenses\":[\"8B.1\",\"8B.2\",\"8B.3\",\"8B.4\",\"8B.5\",\"8B.6\",\"8B.7\",\"8B.8\",\"8B.9\",\"8B.10\"],\"missing_or_weak_lenses\":[\"8B.7\",\"8B.8\",\"8B.10\"],\"contrary_evidence\":[{\"evidence_id\":\"E0074\",\"explanation\":\"The report explicitly describes weak transparency and control-heavy governance, which limits confidence in implementation quality.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0081\",\"explanation\":\"IMF reform language points to desired improvements, not yet independently verified results.\"}],\"source_mix\":\"Mix of primary government records, multilateral assessments, and Reuters/major-media corroboration; official self-reporting was treated as program and implementation evidence, not as independent proof of success.\",\"structured_prior_summary\":\"Structured local priors were not collected in this experiment; judgment rests on the embedded projection and cited evidence only.\",\"chapter_rationale\":\"Sisi's 2022 record is solid on command and state control, but only moderately strong on verified competence. The dossier shows direct appointment power, a clear ownership-policy agenda, and a state-centered investment model that he can plausibly own, yet it also shows opacity, patronage, and a large gap between formal policy and independently proven results. Moral approval or disapproval of the program did not affect the score; on execution and progress, this is a competent but not outstanding record.\",\"lower_anchor_rejected\":\"A 5 would undervalue the extent of presidential control over institutions, appointments, and policy direction.\",\"higher_anchor_rejected\":\"A 7 would require stronger evidence of transparent delivery and independently verified gains rather than mostly formal policy and control evidence.\",\"manual_review_required\":false,\"manual_review_reason_type\":null,\"manual_review_reason\":null,\"chapter_specific\":[{\"field\":\"program_basis\",\"value\":\"mostly_explicit\"},{\"field\":\"program_type\",\"value\":\"policy, state_building, regime_control\"},{\"field\":\"strategic_clarity\",\"value\":\"clear\"},{\"field\":\"operationalization\",\"value\":\"strong\"},{\"field\":\"mobilization_and_coordination\",\"value\":\"strong\"},{\"field\":\"adaptation\",\"value\":\"mixed\"},{\"field\":\"goal_progress\",\"value\":\"mixed\"},{\"field\":\"durability\",\"value\":\"mixed\"},{\"field\":\"trajectory\",\"value\":\"stable but opaque\"},{\"field\":\"morality_separation_check\",\"value\":\"Approval or disapproval of the program did not affect the execution score.\"}]},{\"dossier_job_key\":\"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:ETH:16782\",\"iso3\":\"ETH\",\"ruler_id\":\"2310\",\"ruler_year_id\":16782,\"ruler_name\":\"Abiy Ahmed\",\"period_start_year\":2022,\"period_end_year\":2022,\"chapter_id\":\"8B\",\"rubric_version\":\"chapter_8b_v3\",\"calibration_batch_id\":\"chapter-judge:2022-saturation-v3-stage1-controlled:2022:8B\",\"calibrated_against\":[\"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:COD:16113\",\"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:NGA:15787\",\"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:USA:15810\"],\"score_1_to_10\":5.5,\"insufficient_evidence_reason\":null,\"confidence_score\":77,\"plausible_score_range\":{\"lower\":5.0,\"upper\":6.0},\"decisive_positive_evidence\":[{\"evidence_id\":\"E0082\",\"explanation\":\"Shows a 2022 IMF-backed reform agenda for macroeconomic adjustment and transition to private-sector-led growth.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0085\",\"explanation\":\"Shows Abiy's budget priorities for fiscal consolidation, poverty spending, inflation control, and reconstruction.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0088\",\"explanation\":\"Shows a National Peace Council created to operationalize peacebuilding and support the dialogue process.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0089\",\"explanation\":\"Shows the government allowing aid access after the ceasefire, with tangible humanitarian logistics starting to move.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0091\",\"explanation\":\"Shows a large measles vaccination campaign reaching hard-to-reach children, demonstrating real state reach.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0092\",\"explanation\":\"Shows concrete service restoration in Tigray, including power, telecom, fiber, and bank branches.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0093\",\"explanation\":\"Shows UN-reported aid throughput through corridors, an independent check on implementation after the ceasefire.\"}],\"decisive_negative_evidence\":[{\"evidence_id\":\"E0041\",\"explanation\":\"The national dialogue was accused of exclusion and orchestration, which limits the claim of clean political management.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0090\",\"explanation\":\"The ceasefire promise was still a promise, so implementation was not fully proven at the time.\"}],\"inherited_baseline_and_constraints\":\"Preexisting state capacity, institutional constraints, external shocks, and implementation lags materially shape the case; only ruler-attributed conversion of goals into action and progress is credited.\",\"ruler_attribution\":\"Abiy's government clearly moved on peace, aid access, and service restoration, but much of the record is partial, contested, or still in motion rather than fully completed.\",\"supported_lenses\":[\"8B.1\",\"8B.2\",\"8B.3\",\"8B.4\",\"8B.5\",\"8B.6\",\"8B.7\",\"8B.8\",\"8B.9\",\"8B.10\"],\"missing_or_weak_lenses\":[\"8B.4\",\"8B.6\",\"8B.7\",\"8B.10\"],\"contrary_evidence\":[{\"evidence_id\":\"E0041\",\"explanation\":\"The dialogue was contested and seen by some actors as managed, limiting confidence in political execution quality.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0090\",\"explanation\":\"Honest-implementation rhetoric is not the same as completed implementation; the record remains partial.\"}],\"source_mix\":\"Mix of primary government records, multilateral assessments, and Reuters/major-media corroboration; official self-reporting was treated as program and implementation evidence, not as independent proof of success.\",\"structured_prior_summary\":\"Structured local priors were not collected in this experiment; judgment rests on the embedded projection and cited evidence only.\",\"chapter_rationale\":\"Abiy's 2022 record is mixed. The dossier shows real movement on peace-related coordination, humanitarian access, service restoration, and public-health delivery, which keeps the score above weak or symbolic governance. But the dialogue process was contested, aid access was still partial, and much of the most important evidence shows things beginning to happen rather than being fully and durably delivered. Moral approval or disapproval of the program did not affect the score; on execution alone, this is a middling record with visible but incomplete progress.\",\"lower_anchor_rejected\":\"A 4.5 would understate the tangible aid, service-restoration, and institutional coordination visible in 2022.\",\"higher_anchor_rejected\":\"A 6.5 would require stronger proof that the peace and restoration agenda had been durably implemented and broadly accepted by year-end.\",\"manual_review_required\":false,\"manual_review_reason_type\":null,\"manual_review_reason\":null,\"chapter_specific\":[{\"field\":\"program_basis\",\"value\":\"mixed\"},{\"field\":\"program_type\",\"value\":\"policy, state_building, conflict_management\"},{\"field\":\"strategic_clarity\",\"value\":\"partial\"},{\"field\":\"operationalization\",\"value\":\"mixed\"},{\"field\":\"mobilization_and_coordination\",\"value\":\"mixed\"},{\"field\":\"adaptation\",\"value\":\"mixed\"},{\"field\":\"goal_progress\",\"value\":\"mixed\"},{\"field\":\"durability\",\"value\":\"fragile\"},{\"field\":\"trajectory\",\"value\":\"improving but still fragile\"},{\"field\":\"morality_separation_check\",\"value\":\"Approval or disapproval of the program did not affect the execution score.\"}]},{\"dossier_job_key\":\"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:IDN:16199\",\"iso3\":\"IDN\",\"ruler_id\":\"2636\",\"ruler_year_id\":16199,\"ruler_name\":\"Joko Widodo\",\"period_start_year\":2022,\"period_end_year\":2022,\"chapter_id\":\"8B\",\"rubric_version\":\"chapter_8b_v3\",\"calibration_batch_id\":\"chapter-judge:2022-saturation-v3-stage1-controlled:2022:8B\",\"calibrated_against\":[\"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:MEX:15801\",\"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:PHL:16194\",\"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:IND:19645\"],\"score_1_to_10\":7.5,\"insufficient_evidence_reason\":null,\"confidence_score\":87,\"plausible_score_range\":{\"lower\":7.0,\"upper\":8.0},\"decisive_positive_evidence\":[{\"evidence_id\":\"E0077\",\"explanation\":\"Shows direct presidential instruction to accelerate extreme-poverty reduction through coordinated ministries and local governments.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0088\",\"explanation\":\"Shows Jokowi publicly justifying appointments on competence grounds, a concrete personnel choice in 2022.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0089\",\"explanation\":\"Shows a direct reshuffle in response to the cooking-oil crisis, including removal of a minister after supply and graft problems.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0098\",\"explanation\":\"Shows direct implementation of fuel-subsidy reallocation through cash transfers with a specific beneficiary count and coverage rate.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0099\",\"explanation\":\"Shows a smaller-than-target budget deficit for 2022, indicating disciplined fiscal execution.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0100\",\"explanation\":\"Shows an unqualified audit opinion on the 2022 financial statements, a strong sign of administrative and fiscal control.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0103\",\"explanation\":\"Shows the flagship Nusantara capital project moving into actual infrastructure work during 2022.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0104\",\"explanation\":\"Shows near-universal vaccination coverage and a large catch-up campaign, supporting the claim of broad delivery capacity.\"}],\"decisive_negative_evidence\":[{\"evidence_id\":\"E0101\",\"explanation\":\"UNICEF's learning-loss data show major educational damage and imperfect recovery, limiting a clean competence readout.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0102\",\"explanation\":\"The World Bank's poverty assessment credits long-run progress but stresses continuing insecurity, so the gains are real but incomplete.\"}],\"inherited_baseline_and_constraints\":\"Preexisting state capacity, institutional constraints, external shocks, and implementation lags materially shape the case; only ruler-attributed conversion of goals into action and progress is credited.\",\"ruler_attribution\":\"Jokowi appears to have strong ownership of the agenda and unusually clear executive reach over budgets, appointments, and delivery machinery, though some gains reflect inherited buffers and delegated implementation.\",\"supported_lenses\":[\"8B.1\",\"8B.2\",\"8B.3\",\"8B.4\",\"8B.5\",\"8B.6\",\"8B.7\",\"8B.8\",\"8B.9\",\"8B.10\"],\"missing_or_weak_lenses\":[\"8B.7\",\"8B.8\",\"8B.10\"],\"contrary_evidence\":[{\"evidence_id\":\"E0101\",\"explanation\":\"Learning-loss evidence shows important social outcomes still lagged despite the overall delivery record.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0102\",\"explanation\":\"Poverty and insecurity remained substantial, so the outcome picture is not clean across the whole population.\"}],\"source_mix\":\"Mix of primary government records, multilateral assessments, and Reuters/major-media corroboration; official self-reporting was treated as program and implementation evidence, not as independent proof of success.\",\"structured_prior_summary\":\"Structured local priors were not collected in this experiment; judgment rests on the embedded projection and cited evidence only.\",\"chapter_rationale\":\"Jokowi's 2022 record is strong. The dossier shows a clear program, repeated use of the state apparatus, concrete appointments, real fiscal and social delivery, visible crisis correction, and measurable progress in vaccination, budget balance, audit quality, and flagship infrastructure work. The main limits are that some gains reflect inherited recovery dynamics and that education and distributional outcomes remain mixed. Moral approval or disapproval of the program did not affect the score; on execution and progress, the evidence supports a high but not top-tier judgment.\",\"lower_anchor_rejected\":\"A 7.0 would understate how much of the program was converted into observable action, audits, and measurable outcomes in 2022.\",\"higher_anchor_rejected\":\"An 8.5 would require stronger proof that the gains were more fully durable, less inherited, and better distributed across households and regions.\",\"manual_review_required\":false,\"manual_review_reason_type\":null,\"manual_review_reason\":null,\"chapter_specific\":[{\"field\":\"program_basis\",\"value\":\"explicit\"},{\"field\":\"program_type\",\"value\":\"policy, state_building\"},{\"field\":\"strategic_clarity\",\"value\":\"clear\"},{\"field\":\"operationalization\",\"value\":\"strong\"},{\"field\":\"mobilization_and_coordination\",\"value\":\"strong\"},{\"field\":\"adaptation\",\"value\":\"effective\"},{\"field\":\"goal_progress\",\"value\":\"substantial\"},{\"field\":\"durability\",\"value\":\"durable but not complete\"},{\"field\":\"trajectory\",\"value\":\"upward\"},{\"field\":\"morality_separation_check\",\"value\":\"Approval or disapproval of the program did not affect the execution score.\"}]},{\"dossier_job_key\":\"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:IND:19645\",\"iso3\":\"IND\",\"ruler_id\":\"1517\",\"ruler_year_id\":19645,\"ruler_name\":\"Narendra Modi\",\"period_start_year\":2022,\"period_end_year\":2022,\"chapter_id\":\"8B\",\"rubric_version\":\"chapter_8b_v3\",\"calibration_batch_id\":\"chapter-judge:2022-saturation-v3-stage1-controlled:2022:8B\",\"calibrated_against\":[\"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:IDN:16199\",\"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:VNM:19647\",\"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:USA:15810\"],\"score_1_to_10\":7.0,\"insufficient_evidence_reason\":null,\"confidence_score\":84,\"plausible_score_range\":{\"lower\":6.5,\"upper\":7.5},\"decisive_positive_evidence\":[{\"evidence_id\":\"E0063\",\"explanation\":\"Shows a large-scale rural employment program continuing through FY2021-22, a concrete welfare delivery channel.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0082\",\"explanation\":\"Shows a major health-system audit snapshot with functional centers and beneficiary registrations, demonstrating real scheme reach.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0091\",\"explanation\":\"Shows a technocratic senior appointment that supports administrative capacity in a strategic reform portfolio.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0098\",\"explanation\":\"Shows large budgetary increases for capital spending and social sectors, turning priorities into allocations.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0099\",\"explanation\":\"Shows the PM GatiShakti coordination model as a real implementation framework with explicit oversight.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0100\",\"explanation\":\"Shows external-audit evidence of reasonably strong fiscal transparency in FY2022, despite findings to fix.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0102\",\"explanation\":\"Shows macro policy support, digital public infrastructure, and strong FY2021/22 growth outcomes under the administration.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0105\",\"explanation\":\"Shows concrete progress in PM GatiShakti data integration and project review, not just a slogan.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0107\",\"explanation\":\"Shows a major digital-payments expansion that aligns with the administration's digital public infrastructure agenda.\"}],\"decisive_negative_evidence\":[{\"evidence_id\":\"E0101\",\"explanation\":\"UNICEF's learning-crisis evidence shows major educational harm and incomplete recovery, limiting a clean success claim.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0103\",\"explanation\":\"World Bank notes resilience and reform, but also highlights external shocks and a widening current-account pressure that dilute attribution.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0104\",\"explanation\":\"The World Bank's macro assessment reminds us that some strength came from buffers and reforms not uniquely created in 2022.\"}],\"inherited_baseline_and_constraints\":\"Preexisting state capacity, institutional constraints, external shocks, and implementation lags materially shape the case; only ruler-attributed conversion of goals into action and progress is credited.\",\"ruler_attribution\":\"Modi's record shows broad executive ownership of a large policy agenda, but the credit is shared with the RBI, states, prior reforms, and external recovery dynamics.\",\"supported_lenses\":[\"8B.1\",\"8B.2\",\"8B.3\",\"8B.4\",\"8B.5\",\"8B.6\",\"8B.7\",\"8B.8\",\"8B.9\",\"8B.10\"],\"missing_or_weak_lenses\":[\"8B.7\",\"8B.8\",\"8B.10\"],\"contrary_evidence\":[{\"evidence_id\":\"E0101\",\"explanation\":\"Education disruption and learning loss show an important area where the administration's broader delivery record remained incomplete.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0103\",\"explanation\":\"Macro resilience was real, but the World Bank explicitly separates reforms and buffers from Modi-only causation.\"}],\"source_mix\":\"Mix of primary government records, multilateral assessments, and Reuters/major-media corroboration; official self-reporting was treated as program and implementation evidence, not as independent proof of success.\",\"structured_prior_summary\":\"Structured local priors were not collected in this experiment; judgment rests on the embedded projection and cited evidence only.\",\"chapter_rationale\":\"Modi's 2022 record is strong on competence. The dossier shows clear strategic direction, repeated conversion of priorities into budgets and institutions, substantial rollout in health and digital infrastructure, and measurable macro resilience. The main constraints are attribution split across the RBI, states, inherited buffers, and external shocks, plus persistent educational and distributional gaps. Moral approval or disapproval of the program did not affect the score; on execution and progress, this is a high score short of the very top tier because some of the strongest outcomes are still only partly attributable to 2022 action.\",\"lower_anchor_rejected\":\"A 6 would understate the breadth of concrete implementation, fiscal control, and macro/digital outcomes visible in the dossier.\",\"higher_anchor_rejected\":\"A 7.5 or 8 would require cleaner attribution and stronger evidence that the benefits were more uniformly translated into household-level gains.\",\"manual_review_required\":false,\"manual_review_reason_type\":null,\"manual_review_reason\":null,\"chapter_specific\":[{\"field\":\"program_basis\",\"value\":\"explicit\"},{\"field\":\"program_type\",\"value\":\"policy, state_building\"},{\"field\":\"strategic_clarity\",\"value\":\"clear\"},{\"field\":\"operationalization\",\"value\":\"strong\"},{\"field\":\"mobilization_and_coordination\",\"value\":\"strong\"},{\"field\":\"adaptation\",\"value\":\"effective\"},{\"field\":\"goal_progress\",\"value\":\"substantial\"},{\"field\":\"durability\",\"value\":\"durable but mixed\"},{\"field\":\"trajectory\",\"value\":\"upward with mixed attribution\"},{\"field\":\"morality_separation_check\",\"value\":\"Approval or disapproval of the program did not affect the execution score.\"}]},{\"dossier_job_key\":\"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:IRN:19648\",\"iso3\":\"IRN\",\"ruler_id\":\"3412\",\"ruler_year_id\":19648,\"ruler_name\":\"Ali Khamenei\",\"period_start_year\":2022,\"period_end_year\":2022,\"chapter_id\":\"8B\",\"rubric_version\":\"chapter_8b_v3\",\"calibration_batch_id\":\"chapter-judge:2022-saturation-v3-stage1-controlled:2022:8B\",\"calibrated_against\":[\"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:RUS:15706\",\"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:TUR:15972\",\"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:NGA:15787\"],\"score_1_to_10\":4.0,\"insufficient_evidence_reason\":null,\"confidence_score\":71,\"plausible_score_range\":{\"lower\":3.5,\"upper\":4.5},\"decisive_positive_evidence\":[{\"evidence_id\":\"E0001\",\"explanation\":\"Defines Khamenei's formal powers in the Islamic Republic, establishing the real scope of command and appointment authority in 2022.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0060\",\"explanation\":\"Shows a direct, ruler-linked development-plan framework with concrete economic targets and credit direction.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0082\",\"explanation\":\"Shows a direct 2022 speech emphasizing resistance-oriented economic strategy rather than sanctions dependence.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0083\",\"explanation\":\"Shows Khamenei's public crisis framing during the unrest, revealing command-level messaging and priorities.\"}],\"decisive_negative_evidence\":[{\"evidence_id\":\"E0005\",\"explanation\":\"The sanctions-resilience rhetoric is strategic direction, but not proof of effective implementation or material progress.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0083\",\"explanation\":\"The unrest accusation is messaging, not evidence of problem-solving or outcome improvement.\"}],\"inherited_baseline_and_constraints\":\"Preexisting state capacity, institutional constraints, external shocks, and implementation lags materially shape the case; only ruler-attributed conversion of goals into action and progress is credited.\",\"ruler_attribution\":\"Khamenei clearly commands the system, but the dossier is thin on direct 2022 execution, and most evidence is programmatic or rhetorical rather than outcome-bearing.\",\"supported_lenses\":[\"8B.1\",\"8B.2\",\"8B.3\",\"8B.4\",\"8B.5\",\"8B.6\",\"8B.7\",\"8B.8\",\"8B.9\",\"8B.10\"],\"missing_or_weak_lenses\":[\"8B.3\",\"8B.7\",\"8B.10\"],\"contrary_evidence\":[{\"evidence_id\":\"E0005\",\"explanation\":\"Resilience language shows direction, but not demonstrable execution or durable progress.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0083\",\"explanation\":\"Blaming unrest on foreign actors is a revealed priority, not a verified governance success.\"}],\"source_mix\":\"Mix of primary constitutional/legal text, state-affiliated media, and secondary policy analysis; official self-reporting was treated as program and implementation evidence, not as independent proof of success.\",\"structured_prior_summary\":\"Structured local priors were not collected in this experiment; judgment rests on the embedded projection and cited evidence only.\",\"chapter_rationale\":\"Khamenei's 2022 record is weakly judgeable and only moderately competent on the evidence provided. The dossier establishes broad formal power and a clear ideological-economic direction, but the strongest items are speeches and plans rather than observed delivery, and there is little direct proof of durable 2022 execution. Moral approval or disapproval of the program did not affect the score; the problem is not the goals but the thinness of verified implementation and progress. That supports a low-mid score rather than a clearly higher one.\",\"lower_anchor_rejected\":\"A 3 would understate the real command authority and the existence of a concrete development-plan framework under his leadership.\",\"higher_anchor_rejected\":\"A 5 would require stronger evidence of actual implementation, adaptation, and measurable progress rather than mostly programmatic and rhetorical material.\",\"manual_review_required\":false,\"manual_review_reason_type\":null,\"manual_review_reason\":null,\"chapter_specific\":[{\"field\":\"program_basis\",\"value\":\"mixed\"},{\"field\":\"program_type\",\"value\":\"policy, regime_control\"},{\"field\":\"strategic_clarity\",\"value\":\"partial\"},{\"field\":\"operationalization\",\"value\":\"weak\"},{\"field\":\"mobilization_and_coordination\",\"value\":\"mixed\"},{\"field\":\"adaptation\",\"value\":\"not_observed\"},{\"field\":\"goal_progress\",\"value\":\"too_early_or_unclear\"},{\"field\":\"durability\",\"value\":\"unclear\"},{\"field\":\"trajectory\",\"value\":\"system-level control but thin execution evidence\"},{\"field\":\"morality_separation_check\",\"value\":\"Approval or disapproval of the program did not affect the execution score.\"}]},{\"dossier_job_key\":\"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:JPN:16638\",\"iso3\":\"JPN\",\"ruler_id\":\"2895\",\"ruler_year_id\":16638,\"ruler_name\":\"Fumio Kishida\",\"period_start_year\":2022,\"period_end_year\":2022,\"chapter_id\":\"8B\",\"rubric_version\":\"chapter_8b_v3\",\"calibration_batch_id\":\"chapter-judge:2022-saturation-v3-stage1-controlled:2022:8B\",\"calibrated_against\":[\"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:DEU:16984\",\"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:USA:15810\",\"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:THA:19649\"],\"score_1_to_10\":6.5,\"insufficient_evidence_reason\":null,\"confidence_score\":83,\"plausible_score_range\":{\"lower\":6.0,\"upper\":7.0},\"decisive_positive_evidence\":[{\"evidence_id\":\"E0026\",\"explanation\":\"Shows a major 2022 security-policy package approved under Kishida, a concrete strategic shift.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0080\",\"explanation\":\"Shows a direct supplementary-budget commitment and ongoing weekly monitoring, evidence of operational management.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0094\",\"explanation\":\"Shows a real cabinet reshuffle with experienced appointments, indicating active personnel management.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0096\",\"explanation\":\"Shows legislation, coordination mechanisms, and monitoring for implementation of the 2022 package.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0100\",\"explanation\":\"Shows a coherent economic agenda with concrete policy pillars and implementation instruments.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0103\",\"explanation\":\"Shows a passed child-welfare law with explicit local-support architecture, not just a speech.\"}],\"decisive_negative_evidence\":[{\"evidence_id\":\"E0095\",\"explanation\":\"The startup agenda is still plan-stage, so part of the record remains aspirational.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0101\",\"explanation\":\"OECD support was helpful but not fully targeted, so the year-end economic package is mixed rather than outstanding.\"}],\"inherited_baseline_and_constraints\":\"Preexisting state capacity, institutional constraints, external shocks, and implementation lags materially shape the case; only ruler-attributed conversion of goals into action and progress is credited.\",\"ruler_attribution\":\"Kishida has real executive control and the record shows thoughtful personnel and policy management, but many reforms are still early-stage and outcomes are not yet fully visible.\",\"supported_lenses\":[\"8B.1\",\"8B.2\",\"8B.3\",\"8B.4\",\"8B.5\",\"8B.6\",\"8B.7\",\"8B.8\",\"8B.9\",\"8B.10\"],\"missing_or_weak_lenses\":[\"8B.7\",\"8B.10\"],\"contrary_evidence\":[{\"evidence_id\":\"E0095\",\"explanation\":\"Startup policy discussion is strong on planning but weak on end-year execution evidence.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0101\",\"explanation\":\"Energy-subsidy support was useful, but targeted better and remained macro-dependent.\"}],\"source_mix\":\"Mix of primary government records, multilateral assessments, and Reuters/major-media corroboration; official self-reporting was treated as program and implementation evidence, not as independent proof of success.\",\"structured_prior_summary\":\"Structured local priors were not collected in this experiment; judgment rests on the embedded projection and cited evidence only.\",\"chapter_rationale\":\"Kishida's 2022 record is a solid competence case. He combined clear strategic direction, real budget and legislative action, capable appointments, and active monitoring, while also adapting to security and economic shocks. The limitations are that several flagship programs are still in rollout or design stage and independent outcome evidence is only partly visible by year-end. Moral approval or disapproval of the program did not affect the score; on execution and progress, this is clearly above mixed but not yet in the top tier.\",\"lower_anchor_rejected\":\"A 5.5 would understate the amount of actual policy conversion, staffing, and legislative follow-through in 2022.\",\"higher_anchor_rejected\":\"A 7.5 would require stronger, durable outcome evidence across more of the agenda rather than a still-developing implementation record.\",\"manual_review_required\":false,\"manual_review_reason_type\":null,\"manual_review_reason\":null,\"chapter_specific\":[{\"field\":\"program_basis\",\"value\":\"explicit\"},{\"field\":\"program_type\",\"value\":\"policy, state_building\"},{\"field\":\"strategic_clarity\",\"value\":\"clear\"},{\"field\":\"operationalization\",\"value\":\"strong\"},{\"field\":\"mobilization_and_coordination\",\"value\":\"strong\"},{\"field\":\"adaptation\",\"value\":\"effective\"},{\"field\":\"goal_progress\",\"value\":\"substantial\"},{\"field\":\"durability\",\"value\":\"mixed\"},{\"field\":\"trajectory\",\"value\":\"upward but early\"},{\"field\":\"morality_separation_check\",\"value\":\"Approval or disapproval of the program did not affect the execution score.\"}]},{\"dossier_job_key\":\"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:MEX:15801\",\"iso3\":\"MEX\",\"ruler_id\":\"2779\",\"ruler_year_id\":15801,\"ruler_name\":\"Andrés Manuel López Obrador\",\"period_start_year\":2022,\"period_end_year\":2022,\"chapter_id\":\"8B\",\"rubric_version\":\"chapter_8b_v3\",\"calibration_batch_id\":\"chapter-judge:2022-saturation-v3-stage1-controlled:2022:8B\",\"calibrated_against\":[\"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:IDN:16199\",\"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:PHL:16194\",\"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:USA:15810\"],\"score_1_to_10\":6.0,\"insufficient_evidence_reason\":null,\"confidence_score\":80,\"plausible_score_range\":{\"lower\":5.5,\"upper\":6.5},\"decisive_positive_evidence\":[{\"evidence_id\":\"E0081\",\"explanation\":\"Shows an explicit welfare-centered presidential program for 2022, with governability and poverty-reduction priorities.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0082\",\"explanation\":\"Shows a concrete 2022 budget design around social welfare, regional projects, and fiscal stability.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0087\",\"explanation\":\"Shows higher education spending for named education programs, i.e. real resource allocation.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0088\",\"explanation\":\"Shows a delivery model that directly routes funds to school parent committees, a real implementation mechanism.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0090\",\"explanation\":\"Shows the AIFA opening on time and within budget, a visible flagship delivery accomplishment.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0096\",\"explanation\":\"Shows a large World Bank operation aligned to the government's inclusive-growth agenda.\"}],\"decisive_negative_evidence\":[{\"evidence_id\":\"E0095\",\"explanation\":\"OECD's investment-uncertainty diagnosis limits how far the administration can be credited for a clean growth environment.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0100\",\"explanation\":\"Dos Bocas cost escalation shows a serious execution problem in a flagship project.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0101\",\"explanation\":\"ASF irregularities in La Escuela es Nuestra show control weaknesses and missing documentation.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0103\",\"explanation\":\"The IMF notes recovery drivers, but also external drag and only broadly neutral fiscal policy, which caps the attribution.\"}],\"inherited_baseline_and_constraints\":\"Preexisting state capacity, institutional constraints, external shocks, and implementation lags materially shape the case; only ruler-attributed conversion of goals into action and progress is credited.\",\"ruler_attribution\":\"AMLO clearly owns the welfare-centered agenda and the project portfolio, but some results are reactive, some are partnership-led, and some flagship projects show cost and control weaknesses.\",\"supported_lenses\":[\"8B.1\",\"8B.2\",\"8B.3\",\"8B.4\",\"8B.5\",\"8B.6\",\"8B.7\",\"8B.8\",\"8B.9\",\"8B.10\"],\"missing_or_weak_lenses\":[\"8B.7\",\"8B.8\",\"8B.10\"],\"contrary_evidence\":[{\"evidence_id\":\"E0100\",\"explanation\":\"The refinery cost overrun shows that major flagship execution was not clean.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0101\",\"explanation\":\"Audit findings on La Escuela es Nuestra show control and documentation weaknesses.\"}],\"source_mix\":\"Mix of primary government records, multilateral assessments, and Reuters/major-media corroboration; official self-reporting was treated as program and implementation evidence, not as independent proof of success.\",\"structured_prior_summary\":\"Structured local priors were not collected in this experiment; judgment rests on the embedded projection and cited evidence only.\",\"chapter_rationale\":\"AMLO's 2022 record is moderately strong but not exceptional. The dossier shows an explicit welfare-oriented governing program, concrete budget choices, visible delivery mechanisms, and a few flagship accomplishments, especially where the administration could translate policy into a direct operating channel. The downside is that some major projects ran into cost and control problems, and the macro environment makes attribution mixed rather than clean. Moral approval or disapproval of the program did not affect the score; on execution and progress, this is a solid middle score, not a higher one.\",\"lower_anchor_rejected\":\"A 5 would understate the amount of real budget, delivery, and flagship-infrastructure execution visible in 2022.\",\"higher_anchor_rejected\":\"A 7 would require stronger independent proof of durable, broad-based gains and fewer control/cost problems in the flagship portfolio.\",\"manual_review_required\":false,\"manual_review_reason_type\":null,\"manual_review_reason\":null,\"chapter_specific\":[{\"field\":\"program_basis\",\"value\":\"explicit\"},{\"field\":\"program_type\",\"value\":\"policy, state_building\"},{\"field\":\"strategic_clarity\",\"value\":\"clear\"},{\"field\":\"operationalization\",\"value\":\"strong\"},{\"field\":\"mobilization_and_coordination\",\"value\":\"strong\"},{\"field\":\"adaptation\",\"value\":\"mixed\"},{\"field\":\"goal_progress\",\"value\":\"mixed to substantial\"},{\"field\":\"durability\",\"value\":\"mixed\"},{\"field\":\"trajectory\",\"value\":\"upward but uneven\"},{\"field\":\"morality_separation_check\",\"value\":\"Approval or disapproval of the program did not affect the execution score.\"}]},{\"dossier_job_key\":\"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:NGA:15787\",\"iso3\":\"NGA\",\"ruler_id\":\"2776\",\"ruler_year_id\":15787,\"ruler_name\":\"Muhammadu Buhari\",\"period_start_year\":2022,\"period_end_year\":2022,\"chapter_id\":\"8B\",\"rubric_version\":\"chapter_8b_v3\",\"calibration_batch_id\":\"chapter-judge:2022-saturation-v3-stage1-controlled:2022:8B\",\"calibrated_against\":[\"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:PAK:16682\",\"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:EGY:16232\",\"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:IND:19645\"],\"score_1_to_10\":4.5,\"insufficient_evidence_reason\":null,\"confidence_score\":75,\"plausible_score_range\":{\"lower\":4.0,\"upper\":5.0},\"decisive_positive_evidence\":[{\"evidence_id\":\"E0055\",\"explanation\":\"Shows a real 2022 budget law with fiscal-year discipline and presidential assent, not just rhetoric.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0060\",\"explanation\":\"Shows a technocratic appointment at the statistics bureau, indicating some attempt to strengthen data capacity.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0091\",\"explanation\":\"Shows a major health-insurance law with a formal coverage target and implementation architecture.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0103\",\"explanation\":\"Shows a concrete budget response and ministerial appeals that helped end a long university strike.\"}],\"decisive_negative_evidence\":[{\"evidence_id\":\"E0089\",\"explanation\":\"Tax policy was framed aspirationally, but the speech itself is not proof of sustained implementation.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0090\",\"explanation\":\"Anti-corruption rhetoric did not resolve the underlying performance problems, so execution remained weak.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0092\",\"explanation\":\"Humanitarian/social-protection framing was broad and structural, but not independently outcome-verified.\"}],\"inherited_baseline_and_constraints\":\"Preexisting state capacity, institutional constraints, external shocks, and implementation lags materially shape the case; only ruler-attributed conversion of goals into action and progress is credited.\",\"ruler_attribution\":\"Buhari exercised real budgetary and appointive authority, but the record is dominated by weak follow-through, rhetoric-heavy governance, and unresolved implementation problems.\",\"supported_lenses\":[\"8B.1\",\"8B.2\",\"8B.3\",\"8B.4\",\"8B.5\",\"8B.6\",\"8B.7\",\"8B.8\",\"8B.9\",\"8B.10\"],\"missing_or_weak_lenses\":[\"8B.6\",\"8B.7\",\"8B.10\"],\"contrary_evidence\":[{\"evidence_id\":\"E0103\",\"explanation\":\"The strike suspension shows crisis response, but it also reveals how late and fragile the administration's implementation was.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0090\",\"explanation\":\"Anti-corruption framing did not translate into strong, independently verified outcomes.\"}],\"source_mix\":\"Mix of primary government records, multilateral assessments, and Reuters/major-media corroboration; official self-reporting was treated as program and implementation evidence, not as independent proof of success.\",\"structured_prior_summary\":\"Structured local priors were not collected in this experiment; judgment rests on the embedded projection and cited evidence only.\",\"chapter_rationale\":\"Buhari's 2022 record is weak-to-mixed. There was some real fiscal and administrative action, including budget assent, a technocratic appointment, and a health-insurance law, but the dossier does not show strong, durable execution or broad outcome gains. Much of the file is still rhetoric, crisis management, or partial reform under heavy inherited constraints. Moral approval or disapproval of the program did not affect the score; on execution and progress, this is below the middle tier but not a collapse case.\",\"lower_anchor_rejected\":\"A 3.5 would ignore the concrete budget, appointment, and legislative actions that did occur in 2022.\",\"higher_anchor_rejected\":\"A 5.5 would require clearer evidence that these measures translated into durable implementation and better outcomes rather than partial or reactive moves.\",\"manual_review_required\":false,\"manual_review_reason_type\":null,\"manual_review_reason\":null,\"chapter_specific\":[{\"field\":\"program_basis\",\"value\":\"mixed\"},{\"field\":\"program_type\",\"value\":\"policy, state_building\"},{\"field\":\"strategic_clarity\",\"value\":\"partial\"},{\"field\":\"operationalization\",\"value\":\"mixed\"},{\"field\":\"mobilization_and_coordination\",\"value\":\"weak\"},{\"field\":\"adaptation\",\"value\":\"mixed\"},{\"field\":\"goal_progress\",\"value\":\"mixed\"},{\"field\":\"durability\",\"value\":\"fragile\"},{\"field\":\"trajectory\",\"value\":\"stalled and reactive\"},{\"field\":\"morality_separation_check\",\"value\":\"Approval or disapproval of the program did not affect the execution score.\"}]},{\"dossier_job_key\":\"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:PAK:16682\",\"iso3\":\"PAK\",\"ruler_id\":\"2911\",\"ruler_year_id\":16682,\"ruler_name\":\"Shehbaz Sharif\",\"period_start_year\":2022,\"period_end_year\":2022,\"chapter_id\":\"8B\",\"rubric_version\":\"chapter_8b_v3\",\"calibration_batch_id\":\"chapter-judge:2022-saturation-v3-stage1-controlled:2022:8B\",\"calibrated_against\":[\"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:NGA:15787\",\"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:EGY:16232\",\"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:TUR:15972\"],\"score_1_to_10\":5.0,\"insufficient_evidence_reason\":null,\"confidence_score\":77,\"plausible_score_range\":{\"lower\":4.5,\"upper\":5.5},\"decisive_positive_evidence\":[{\"evidence_id\":\"E0050\",\"explanation\":\"Shows Sharif appointing a finance minister and moving immediately to tackle the economic crisis and IMF talks.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0055\",\"explanation\":\"Shows a difficult budget stance with tax changes and austerity measures, i.e. real policy action.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0056\",\"explanation\":\"Shows a coherent FY2022-23 strategy around tax widening, deficit reduction, and IMF engagement.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0093\",\"explanation\":\"Shows coalition-government formation focused on stabilization and IMF restart, a real governance move after a political transition.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0095\",\"explanation\":\"Shows budget tightening and fuel-price action consistent with a crisis-management approach.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0096\",\"explanation\":\"Shows IMF program completion and explicit priorities for budget execution and reform.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0098\",\"explanation\":\"Shows the flood-recovery assessment and immediate-relief framework, with real mobilization on disaster response.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0100\",\"explanation\":\"Shows large World Bank financing for flood-affected Sindh, reflecting active recovery coordination.\"}],\"decisive_negative_evidence\":[{\"evidence_id\":\"E0061\",\"explanation\":\"The finance-minister resignation shows internal pressure and instability inside the economic team.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0098\",\"explanation\":\"Flood damages and losses were huge, which means even competent response operated under severe inherited constraints.\"}],\"inherited_baseline_and_constraints\":\"Preexisting state capacity, institutional constraints, external shocks, and implementation lags materially shape the case; only ruler-attributed conversion of goals into action and progress is credited.\",\"ruler_attribution\":\"Sharif took office into a crisis and did move quickly on cabinet formation, IMF re-engagement, budgets, and flood response, but the case remains heavily constrained by inherited collapse and coalition friction.\",\"supported_lenses\":[\"8B.1\",\"8B.2\",\"8B.3\",\"8B.4\",\"8B.5\",\"8B.6\",\"8B.7\",\"8B.8\",\"8B.9\",\"8B.10\"],\"missing_or_weak_lenses\":[\"8B.7\",\"8B.8\",\"8B.10\"],\"contrary_evidence\":[{\"evidence_id\":\"E0061\",\"explanation\":\"Internal pressure and ministerial turnover show that coordination was fragile.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0098\",\"explanation\":\"The flood shock limited what any 2022 program could realistically achieve.\"}],\"source_mix\":\"Mix of primary government records, multilateral assessments, and Reuters/major-media corroboration; official self-reporting was treated as program and implementation evidence, not as independent proof of success.\",\"structured_prior_summary\":\"Structured local priors were not collected in this experiment; judgment rests on the embedded projection and cited evidence only.\",\"chapter_rationale\":\"Sharif's 2022 record is mixed but still meaningfully active. He inherited a severe crisis and responded by assembling a cabinet, restarting IMF engagement, pushing austerity and tax changes, and mobilizing flood recovery. The limits are obvious: coalition friction, rapid ministerial turnover, and the scale of inherited economic and disaster shocks keep this from being a strong competence case. Moral approval or disapproval of the program did not affect the score; on execution and progress, this is a middling record with real action but no durable mastery.\",\"lower_anchor_rejected\":\"A 4 would understate the speed and seriousness of Sharif's crisis response, budget action, and external financing mobilization.\",\"higher_anchor_rejected\":\"A 6 would require clearer evidence of durable improvement rather than stabilization under severe inherited constraints.\",\"manual_review_required\":false,\"manual_review_reason_type\":null,\"manual_review_reason\":null,\"chapter_specific\":[{\"field\":\"program_basis\",\"value\":\"mostly_explicit\"},{\"field\":\"program_type\",\"value\":\"policy, survival\"},{\"field\":\"strategic_clarity\",\"value\":\"partial\"},{\"field\":\"operationalization\",\"value\":\"mixed\"},{\"field\":\"mobilization_and_coordination\",\"value\":\"mixed\"},{\"field\":\"adaptation\",\"value\":\"mixed\"},{\"field\":\"goal_progress\",\"value\":\"mixed\"},{\"field\":\"durability\",\"value\":\"fragile\"},{\"field\":\"trajectory\",\"value\":\"stabilizing under stress\"},{\"field\":\"morality_separation_check\",\"value\":\"Approval or disapproval of the program did not affect the execution score.\"}]},{\"dossier_job_key\":\"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:PHL:16194\",\"iso3\":\"PHL\",\"ruler_id\":\"2844\",\"ruler_year_id\":16194,\"ruler_name\":\"Bongbong Marcos\",\"period_start_year\":2022,\"period_end_year\":2022,\"chapter_id\":\"8B\",\"rubric_version\":\"chapter_8b_v3\",\"calibration_batch_id\":\"chapter-judge:2022-saturation-v3-stage1-controlled:2022:8B\",\"calibrated_against\":[\"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:IDN:16199\",\"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:JPN:16638\",\"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:MEX:15801\"],\"score_1_to_10\":5.5,\"insufficient_evidence_reason\":null,\"confidence_score\":80,\"plausible_score_range\":{\"lower\":5.0,\"upper\":6.0},\"decisive_positive_evidence\":[{\"evidence_id\":\"E0089\",\"explanation\":\"Shows a direct first-year economic agenda and inflation response articulated by Marcos.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0090\",\"explanation\":\"Shows a public investment pitch linked to the administration's economic agenda.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0092\",\"explanation\":\"Shows economic-team presentation of targets and medium-term plans, giving the agenda a concrete shape.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0093\",\"explanation\":\"Shows actual selection of key economic managers, a real staffing choice.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0094\",\"explanation\":\"Shows a broad inaugural cabinet and top-offices appointment wave, indicating executive control.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0095\",\"explanation\":\"Shows active management of the security bureaucracy and law-enforcement chain of command.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0097\",\"explanation\":\"Shows the first full annual budget submission with priority sectors, a concrete implementation step.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0098\",\"explanation\":\"Shows booster rollout progress and a defined public-health campaign, with measurable output.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0099\",\"explanation\":\"Shows school reopening and learning-recovery implementation through education policy.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0100\",\"explanation\":\"Shows UNICEF-backed return-to-school implementation and continued learning-recovery architecture.\"}],\"decisive_negative_evidence\":[{\"evidence_id\":\"E0096\",\"explanation\":\"The executive-secretary replacement shows adaptation, but also indicates earlier coordination strain.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0101\",\"explanation\":\"The learning-recovery and school-system evidence is still partial and reveals continuing constraints.\"}],\"inherited_baseline_and_constraints\":\"Preexisting state capacity, institutional constraints, external shocks, and implementation lags materially shape the case; only ruler-attributed conversion of goals into action and progress is credited.\",\"ruler_attribution\":\"Marcos clearly controlled the first-year appointment and budget agenda, but much of the visible record is launch-stage management rather than durable outcome proof.\",\"supported_lenses\":[\"8B.1\",\"8B.2\",\"8B.3\",\"8B.4\",\"8B.5\",\"8B.6\",\"8B.7\",\"8B.8\",\"8B.9\",\"8B.10\"],\"missing_or_weak_lenses\":[\"8B.7\",\"8B.8\",\"8B.10\"],\"contrary_evidence\":[{\"evidence_id\":\"E0096\",\"explanation\":\"The need to replace a central coordinator suggests some internal friction in the first year.\"},{\"evidence_id\":\"E0101\",\"explanation\":\"School and learning recovery remained incomplete, so early delivery was not yet fully durable.\"}],\"source_mix\":\"Mix of primary government records, multilateral assessments, and Reuters/major-media corroboration; official self-reporting was treated as program and implementation evidence, not as independent proof of success.\",\"structured_prior_summary\":\"Structured local priors were not collected in this experiment; judgment rests on the embedded projection and cited evidence only.\",\"chapter_rationale\":\"Marcos's 2022 record is a launch-heavy but real competence case. The dossier shows a first-year administration that assembled a cabinet, set a budget, made key security and economic appointments, and pushed visible policy rollout in health and education. The limit is that most of this is still early-stage management, with durable outcome evidence only partly visible by year-end. Moral approval or disapproval of the program did not affect the score; on execution alone, this sits in the middle of the range, above mere symbolism but below clear mastery.\",\"lower_anchor_rejected\":\"A 4.5 would ignore the breadth of real appointments, budget action, and program rollout in the first year.\",\"higher_anchor_rejected\":\"A 6.5 would require stronger proof that the launch architecture had already translated into durable, independently verified outcomes.\",\"manual_review_required\":false,\"manual_review_reason_type\":null,\"manual_review_reason\":null,\"chapter_specific\":[{\"field\":\"program_basis\",\"value\":\"explicit\"},{\"field\":\"program_type\",\"value\":\"policy, state_building\"},{\"field\":\"strategic_clarity\",\"value\":\"partial\"},{\"field\":\"operationalization\",\"value\":\"mixed\"},{\"field\":\"mobilization_and_coordination\",\"value\":\"mixed\"},{\"field\":\"adaptation\",\"value\":\"mixed\"},{\"field\":\"goal_progress\",\"value\":\"mixed\"},{\"field\":\"durability\",\"value\":\"fragile\"},{\"field\":\"trajectory\",\"value\":\"launch-stage and still consolidating\"},{\"field\":\"morality_separation_check\",\"value\":\"Approval or disapproval of the program did not affect the execution score.\"}]},{\"dossier_job_key\":\"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:RUS:15706\",\"iso3\":\"RUS\",\"ruler_id\":\"2759\",\"ruler_year_id\":15706,\"ruler_name\":\"Vladimir Putin\",\"period_start_year\":2022,\"period_end_year\":2022,\"chapter_id\":\"8B\",\"rubric_version\":\"chapter_8b_v3\",\"calibration_batch_id\":\"chapter-judge:2022-saturation-v3-stage1-controlled:2022:8B\",\"calibrated_against\":[\"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:IRN:19648\",\"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:TUR:15972\",\"dossier:2022-top20-hybrid-v2:2022:EGY:16232\"],\"score_1_to_10\":